/* 黄鈺茜 · 文章（中/英） */
window.ESSAYS=[{"id":"W-2024-01","n":10,"title":{"zh":"金老师《中国思想史》课程感想","en":"Reflections on Professor Jin’s Course History of Chinese Thought"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2024-11-17","genre":"随笔","summary":{"zh":"我总有一种感觉，觉得天地宽阔任我游，可这天地的边界在哪？这是一直被悬置起来的问题。","en":"I have always had a feeling that heaven and earth are wide and I may roam them freely — but where are the edges of this heaven and earth? This is a question I have always left suspended."},"words":2688,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"我总有一种感觉，觉得天地宽阔任我游，可这天地的边界在哪？这是一直被悬置起来的问题。在您的课上和《轴心文明与现代社会》这本书中，我有了很多新的感悟体会。在历史的长河里，人们的变与不变，想要找到自己的位置是一件庞大的、需要很多的时间的一件事。","en":"I have always had a feeling that heaven and earth are wide and I may roam them freely — but where are the edges of this heaven and earth? This is a question I have always left suspended. In your class and in the book Axial Civilizations and Modern Society, I came to many new insights and understandings. In the long river of history, amid all that changes and all that stays the same in people, finding one’s own place is an enormous undertaking, one that takes a great deal of time."},{"t":"p","zh":"我的专业是水彩画绘画，也喜欢读一些哲学、美术史类的书。初选这门课的目的是觉得自己对中国的历史文化民族不了解，而我想用水彩这一西画工具画出中国人画出的画，用中国人的立场写出好的文章。所以修《中国思想史》这门课一开始是为了知识的查漏补缺。在您的这门课的这段时间，我感到有很多认知又一次打破后重建，也反思了许多以前那些旧的、脆弱的观念。我审视以往所知的历史，多了一些真伪历史的判断和整体历史的大局视角。对于我们社会的理解多了一些深刻。把很多事情放在更大、也更具体的框架下重新认识。","en":"My major is watercolor painting, and I also like to read books on philosophy and art history. I first chose this course because I felt I did not understand China’s history, culture and people, while I want to use watercolor, a Western painting medium, to paint pictures that a Chinese person would paint, and to write good essays from a Chinese standpoint. So at the start, taking History of Chinese Thought was a way to fill the gaps in my knowledge. Over the time of your course, I felt many of my understandings being broken down and rebuilt once again, and I reflected on many old, fragile ideas I used to hold. Examining the history I knew before, I gained more ability to tell true history from false and more of a big-picture view of history as a whole. My understanding of our society became somewhat deeper. I came to understand many things anew, placing them within a larger and also more concrete framework."},{"t":"p","zh":"有一个具体的事例：在旅行时，我感到了旅游景点的各类图像拼凑。这个事情之前我一直想弄明白，以下是我在一次旅行所思所想的一段文字：","en":"Here is a concrete example: while traveling, I sensed the patchwork of all kinds of images that makes up tourist sites. This was something I had long wanted to figure out. Below is a passage I wrote about what I thought and felt on one trip:"},{"t":"p","zh":"进入乌镇划分的园区，好多东西一下子塞到眼睛里。景观园林图式的步行区、住宿饮食区、乌镇镇民生活区、购物纪念品的间隔分布，一切都是那么的鳞次栉比。它是仿照了江南生活这样的符号来拼凑出的、表面的一些演员班子，一个度假村，一个舞台场景。在西栅的进门左侧，有着一个酒家，每到一定时间就要让演员到室外靠河的一片空地到外面表演。一个手推式小音箱播放着戏曲，演员穿着戏服在上面对口型，时不时的再摆弄两下胳膊，做出个演员的样子。商铺的老板也不是自己拥有这家店铺完全自负盈亏，而是扮演店主的店主…这片江南小镇像是一个工具，现成地呈现给观者。甚至每一个砖瓦都是展销会的展品，我带着感受风土人情的目的来到这里，想深入了解这个古镇，品味、感受它和它背后的意蕴。可那玻璃罩子拒绝着我，推搡着我的身体，我就和这砖墙一样，麻木的重复的，向前踏步。","en":"Entering the zoned park of Wuzhen, a great many things are stuffed into your eyes all at once. The pedestrian areas laid out like landscaped gardens, the lodging and dining areas, the living quarters of Wuzhen’s townspeople, the shopping and souvenir areas, spaced out at intervals — everything is packed closely together, row upon row. It is a superficial troupe of performers pieced together by imitating the symbols of Jiangnan life: a resort, a stage set. On the left as you enter Xizha there is a tavern, and at set times performers are sent outdoors to an open space by the river to perform. A small push-cart speaker plays opera while the performers, in costume, lip-sync on top of it, now and then waving their arms a little to look the part. The shopkeepers do not own their shops and bear their own profits and losses either; they are shopkeepers playing shopkeepers… This little Jiangnan town is like a tool, presented ready-made to the viewer. Even every brick and tile is an exhibit at a trade fair. I came here intending to experience the local customs and character, wanting to understand this ancient town deeply, to savor and feel it and the meaning behind it. But that glass case rejected me and shoved my body along, and I, like these brick walls, numbly and repetitively marched forward."},{"t":"p","zh":"当一个个旅行主体的游客旅者，抱着身心更换场域状态的期待、希望打破日常重复状态和获得新的体验来到这里，却成了另一重复方式的可替换机械零件，反倒是加强了自己的这种“被变成机器”的感觉。来到一个新的地方，想去感受，深深呼吸，观察体会人文地理的细微差异…但是在这数个相同的景区模式里，人的感受封闭的。就好像处于一个个圆环中，从一个圆环到另一个圆环，通向圆环外的缺口总是打不开。","en":"Tourists and travelers, each the subject of their own journey, come here expecting body and mind to change fields and states, hoping to break the repetition of daily life and gain new experiences — yet they become replaceable mechanical parts in another mode of repetition, which only strengthens their sense of “being turned into a machine.” Coming to a new place, you want to feel, to breathe deeply, to observe and savor the subtle differences of culture and geography… but within these several identical scenic-area templates, people’s feelings are closed off. It is as if you were inside ring after ring, passing from one ring to the next, and the gap that leads out of the ring never opens."},{"t":"p","zh":"这样的旅游地作为一个舞台布景是很美的：江南的屋瓦望上去一层叠着一层的，高高低低，上面是浅浅的一溜瓦片，下面是斑迹驳驳的白墙；加以爬墙虎、红叶、还有小桥、流水这些江南刻板印象的物性符号…实在是相得益彰，是很美的一幅图景。可惜这不是一个舞台场景，而是有着历史的、实用功能的建筑群，本质上是人所生活的聚落群。可现在成了一个为放大物性吸引游客而牺牲事性的“表演场地”。作为一个历史的、这种人一代又一代绵延继承下来的气息、生活的人气儿，它的灵韵已经没有了。它留下的只是外表空空的图像。","en":"As a stage set, a tourist place like this is very beautiful: the roof tiles of Jiangnan, looked at from below, are stacked layer upon layer, high and low, a pale strip of tiles above and mottled white walls below; add Boston ivy, red leaves, little bridges and flowing water — the material symbols of the Jiangnan stereotype… they truly set one another off, a very beautiful picture. Unfortunately this is not a stage set but a group of buildings with a history and practical functions — in essence, a cluster of settlements where people live. Yet now it has become a “performance venue” that sacrifices its eventness in order to amplify its thingness and attract tourists. As something historical — the atmosphere handed down and inherited generation after generation, the human warmth of lived life — its aura is gone. What it leaves behind is only an outward, empty image."},{"t":"p","zh":"本雅明说，本真性是物性与事性的统一，两者缺一不可，机械复制导致了事性的丧失，也就是灵韵的丧失。人的心灵无法栖息在这种只有物性而没有事性的商品上。这或许也是我们现在这个社会倦怠感的来源之一，人们那如同普罗米修斯一般，天天被秃鹰啄食，我们倦怠、心灵无处安放。","en":"Benjamin said that authenticity is the unity of thingness and eventness, and neither can be missing; mechanical reproduction leads to the loss of eventness, that is, the loss of aura. The human soul cannot dwell in commodities like these that have only thingness and no eventness. Perhaps this is also one of the sources of the weariness of our society today: people are like Prometheus, pecked at by the vulture every day; we are weary, and our souls have nowhere to rest."},{"t":"p","zh":"而同时值得被考虑的一点是，机械时代，事性和物性本身就是割裂的。如这个经典的例子：“我们亲手制作的一个布娃娃与我们购买的一个芭比娃娃是有区别的。前者我们投入了情感，制作过程本身就是布娃娃的一部分；而对后者，我们只投入了金钱，很难像对待自己亲手制作的东西那样向它投入“意愿和感情”。因此，对后者而言，膜拜价值已经消失，只剩下展示价值。“","en":"At the same time, one point worth considering is that in the mechanical age, eventness and thingness are already split apart in themselves. Take this classic example: “There is a difference between a rag doll we make with our own hands and a Barbie doll we buy. Into the former we have put our feelings, and the process of making it is itself part of the doll; into the latter we have put only money, and it is hard to invest ‘will and feeling’ in it the way we do in something we made ourselves. Therefore, for the latter, cult value has disappeared, and only exhibition value remains.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"也就是说这不仅是一个文化继承的方式问题，也是作为生产者和使用者，生产者“消失不可见”的问题。我觉得文化一定要有人、个人的参与，与之产生关系，才可以真的被接纳。可当文化遗产变成了日常的“物”，变成了一个有隔阂的展品，那么此局何破？","en":"That is to say, this is not only a question of how culture is passed down, but also — between producer and user — a question of the producer “disappearing from view.” I think culture must have people, individuals, taking part in it and forming a relationship with it before it can truly be embraced. But when cultural heritage turns into an everyday “object,” an exhibit held at a distance, how can this impasse be broken?"},{"t":"p","zh":"一个个景点像是一个个旅行场，经济为主导，其余一切都成了被物化的零件。如此类似的‘旅行场‘还有很多。中国不同地区文化的面貌不尽相同，可以被进行商业包装出售的也有很多，因此对传统文化、环境资源的’贱卖‘也已经成为一个广泛普遍的事情。“","en":"Each scenic spot is like a “travel field” where the economy dominates and everything else has become an objectified part. There are many more ‘travel fields’ like this. The cultures of China’s different regions vary in their features, and much of them can be commercially packaged and sold, so the ‘selling off cheap’ of traditional culture and environmental resources has already become something widespread and common.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"每每看到这些被贱卖的文化历史甚至是大自然，我就感到很难受、很排斥。不愿意接受。我觉得有一种无力感，好像这些被糟蹋了的精华会真的再也站不起来了。","en":"Every time I see culture and history, even nature itself, sold off cheap like this, I feel upset and repelled. I don’t want to accept it. I feel a kind of powerlessness, as if these treasures that have been ruined will truly never stand up again."},{"t":"p","zh":"但现在我似乎有了一些新的视角。或许这不是一个现代社会才有的事件类型—人们有着很长的伪造历史的历史。我所说的这个不能被破解的局，是不是并不真的存在，或者说是由于片面放大了此刻的一个方面，使事实看上去很沉重无力。其实或许历史向来如此，我应该再少一些自己的主观意愿。我们真正要改变和促成的，不仅仅是上述的一个在历史长河中短暂的一个事件，更应当是一代人又一代人更加的求真严谨的态度。","en":"But now I seem to have gained some new perspectives. Perhaps this is not a kind of event that only modern society has — people have a long history of forging history. Perhaps the impasse I called unbreakable does not really exist; or perhaps, by one-sidedly magnifying one aspect of the present moment, I made the facts look heavy and hopeless. In fact, perhaps history has always been this way, and I should bring less of my own subjective wishes to it. What we really need to change and bring about is not merely the event described above, a brief moment in the long river of history, but rather a more truth-seeking and rigorous attitude, generation after generation."},{"t":"p","zh":"但好像虽然道理是这样，可如果落实下去就发现，谎言其实才是事情运行下去的前提和动力。所以求真严谨真的被实现，似乎就像是信奉犹太教的人真的得到了救赎。","en":"But it seems that although this is right in principle, once you try to put it into practice you find that lies are actually the precondition and driving force that keep things running. So for truth-seeking and rigor to truly be realized would seem to be like believers in Judaism truly receiving redemption."},{"t":"p","zh":"但也好像不是求真性的问题，历史都是建构在人们的话语中的。但是我们把真的和假的说明白会对大众和后代有一个更好的引领，但是这个引领体现在哪个方面呢？但其实我所讲的乌镇的这件事情和求真的事情，应该是两个范畴的事儿，一个是大历史的事儿，一个生活的事儿，今天在的东西一百年后真的不一定就会在了，所以我所纠结的这个点，不是在纠结生活中的点，而是在思想这种在别的领域的这种点，我把它又带入到生活中，所以感觉解释不通。并且民间的事情在官方过去也没怎么记载，我所说的这个范畴的事情也无从查起。研究历史、记录历史、创造历史的人们，在今天这个道德丧失的年代，应该揽起重建道德的责任吗？还是应该不干预，令其顺其自然的发展。","en":"But it also doesn’t seem to be a question of truthfulness; history is always constructed within people’s discourse. Still, if we make clear what is true and what is false, it will give better guidance to the public and to later generations — but in what respect would this guidance show itself? In fact, the Wuzhen matter I described and the matter of seeking truth probably belong to two different categories: one is a matter of grand history, the other a matter of life. What exists today may well not exist a hundred years from now. So the point I am struggling with is not a point in life, but a point from another domain, that of thought, which I then carried into life — and that is why it feels as if it can’t be explained. Moreover, folk matters were never much recorded by officials in the past, so matters of the kind I am talking about cannot be looked up anyway. In today’s age of lost morality, should the people who study history, record history and make history take on the responsibility of rebuilding morality? Or should they not interfere, and let things develop as they naturally will?"},{"t":"p","zh":"就算我们建立了新的道德，也会出现新的问题，如此反复。","en":"Even if we built a new morality, new problems would arise, and so on, over and over."},{"t":"p","zh":"我突然想到解构、历史观消失带来的虚无。我发现我想的这些问题有些没有意义。或许在方法论上有些问题、或许是一些系统胡乱串在一起、或许是滥用误用了一些概念，所以，我觉得这个问题我可以先让它过去，等能更宏观的看待历史、社会问题，有更好的哲学、思想史的思路之后，再重新拾起看看会不会有新的发现。","en":"I suddenly thought of deconstruction, and of the nihilism brought on by the disappearance of a view of history. I realized that some of the questions I’ve been thinking about are rather meaningless. Perhaps there is something wrong with my methodology, perhaps I have strung several systems together haphazardly, perhaps I have misused or abused some concepts. So I think I can let this question pass for now, and once I can look at history and social problems from a broader perspective and have better approaches from philosophy and the history of thought, I will pick it up again and see whether I find anything new."},{"t":"p","zh":"我特别喜欢听您的课，脑子被代入进去一直在跟着转，也有特别多的转变和收获。我觉得您在课上和书上很多事情都讲得很明白了，所以我一时也想不到提出什么针对性的问题，然后用思想史的方法论去解决它。我对历史还不甚了解，只是一个知道皮毛的入门者，不知道我今后会做多大程度的思想史研究，但是您讲的内容我受益终身。再次感谢您，愿您身体健康、桃李满园、春晖四方。","en":"I really love listening to your lectures; my mind gets drawn in and keeps turning along with them, and I have gone through a great many changes and gained a great deal. I feel you have already explained many things very clearly in class and in the book, so for now I can’t think of a specific question to raise and then work through with the methodology of the history of thought. I still know little about history — I am only a beginner who knows the surface — and I don’t know how far I will go in researching the history of thought in the future, but what you taught will benefit me all my life. Thank you again. I wish you good health, a garden full of flourishing students, and your spring warmth shining in every direction."}]},{"id":"W-2024-02","n":9,"title":{"zh":"潘天寿与20世纪中国绘画课程感悟小结","en":"Reflections on the Course “Pan Tianshou and Twentieth-Century Chinese Painting”"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2024-12-16","genre":"随笔","summary":{"zh":"我是绘画学院水性综合材料绘画的一年级研究生，从刚刚开始学习绘画就接受的西方的体系。","en":"I am a first-year graduate student in water-based mixed-media painting at the School of Painting, and from the moment I began learning to paint I was trained in the Western system."},"words":3002,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"我是绘画学院水性综合材料绘画的一年级研究生，从刚刚开始学习绘画就接受的西方的体系。西洋的造型、色彩、构图，成体系的训练。我对中国画的了解只停留在很表层的绘画分类，甚至连流派、朝代…这些都搞不清楚。而对于潘天寿先生也只是停留在，知道潘老师是大师，这样非常粗浅的认识。","en":"I am a first-year graduate student in water-based mixed-media painting at the School of Painting, and from the moment I began learning to paint I was trained in the Western system: Western modelling, colour and composition, in systematic training. My knowledge of Chinese painting stayed at the most superficial level of the categories of painting; I couldn’t even keep the schools and dynasties straight… As for Mr Pan Tianshou, my understanding stopped at knowing that Mr Pan was a great master—a very crude level of understanding."},{"t":"p","zh":"我的专业虽然是水彩—西洋画，但水彩和中国水墨却也有着千丝万缕的联系，水色产生的反应，纸面带来的质感，软笔线条的灵动活变…它们可以互相交融。我的导师曾经说，中国想要走向国际舞台，非得从水彩走。在当时的语境下，老师是稍带夸张的去陈述的，但我是同意老师的观点的。油画这一舶来之物，在中国的历史仅仅一百年之久，它还是一个新生儿，需要更长的生长周期去发展成熟。并且油画在西方，不仅历史深厚积淀，且话语权主导权都在西方。西方的人似乎是生来就带这种基因的。而中国的文化在输出上，一直都有些，依赖于它者体系，有些费力与无奈，尽管我们有这么好的文化基因，博大精深的艺术体系和历史积淀，可当我们想让别人也了解、接受的时候，却发现有一道隐形的屏障。尽管我们进入到了全球化时代、信息、政经…紧密的联系在一起，可不同文化、语言之间，除去文化霸权这些当下状况，就艺术本身上，也缺少可以让观者进入的一个通道。水彩，在西方，一直都是作为小稿或是为油画完成稿来打底这样一种辅助性能的甚至不能称之为画种的一种存在。到了两百年前威廉透纳那时，水彩才独立成为一个画种，在西学东渐那会儿被传入中国。但也只是被人称之为小情调，根本就不敢妄想与国油板雕并为一谈。但随着一代又一代的前辈们去继承发展发扬，中国的水彩生命力越来越强盛了，我们的技法也在更成熟的发展，我们的画面呈现也有着震撼人心的力量。水彩既可以融入油画的浓烈鲜艳，又可以有着国画的勾勒皴叠…而对于西方来说，水彩有着可以被接受的基础，所以我们可以借助这一平台，让一些东西在明在暗地在水彩这一载体上呈现出来，让中国的一些元素、精神可以缓缓流入别人的世界。关于我的专业我说了挺多的，有一点点贩卖情怀，现在我想说说我自己选这门课的所思所想。每周三上潘天寿与20世纪中国美术，每周四上中国思想史。选这两门课我的初衷是一样的：我觉得自己对中国的历史文化民族太不了解，而我想用水彩这一西画工具画出中国人画出的画，用中国人的立场写出好的文章，所以算是开始着手研究中国的艺术、文化、精神、历史。","en":"Although my major is watercolour—a Western form of painting—watercolour and Chinese ink are bound together in countless ways: the reactions between water and colour, the texture the paper brings, the lively, changeable lines of the soft brush… they can blend into one another. My supervisor once said that if China wants to step onto the international stage, it has to go by way of watercolour. In the context of that moment my teacher was exaggerating a little, but I agree with that view. Oil painting, an import, has a history of only about a hundred years in China; it is still a newborn and needs a longer period of growth to mature. Moreover, oil painting in the West not only has deep historical accumulation, but the West also holds the power of discourse and the leading role. Westerners seem to be born with it in their genes. Chinese culture, by contrast, has always been somewhat dependent on other systems when it comes to cultural export, which makes it laborious and leaves us somewhat helpless. Although we have such fine cultural genes, an artistic system and historical accumulation so broad and profound, when we want others to understand and accept them too, we find an invisible barrier. Although we have entered the age of globalisation, with information, politics and economics… tightly linked together, between different cultures and languages—setting aside present conditions such as cultural hegemony—art itself also lacks a passage through which viewers can enter. In the West, watercolour long existed only in an auxiliary role, as small sketches or as underpainting for finished oil paintings, something that could not even be called a genre of painting. Only some two hundred years ago, in William Turner’s time, did watercolour become an independent genre, and it was brought to China when Western learning spread east. But even then it was dismissed as a pleasant little diversion, and no one dared dream of mentioning it in the same breath as Chinese painting, oil painting, printmaking and sculpture. Yet as generation after generation of predecessors have inherited, developed and carried it forward, Chinese watercolour has grown ever more vital; our techniques keep maturing, and our pictures have a power that can move people deeply. Watercolour can take in the intensity and vividness of oil painting and also the outlining and layered texture strokes of Chinese painting… And for the West, watercolour has a basis on which it can be accepted, so we can use this platform to let certain things appear, openly or subtly, through the vehicle of watercolour, and let some Chinese elements and spirit flow slowly into other people’s worlds. I have said quite a lot about my major, with a touch of sentimentality; now I want to talk about my own thoughts on choosing this course. Every Wednesday I take Pan Tianshou and Twentieth-Century Chinese Art, and every Thursday Chinese Intellectual History. My reason for choosing these two courses was the same: I felt I knew far too little about China’s history, culture and people, and I want to use watercolour, a Western painting tool, to paint pictures that a Chinese person would paint, and to write good essays from a Chinese standpoint. So I have begun, in a way, to study Chinese art, culture, spirit and history."},{"t":"h","zh":"一· 关于《听天阁谈随笔》摘抄及观后感悟","en":"I. Excerpts from Casual Notes on Painting from the Tingtian Pavilion, and My Reflections"},{"t":"quote","zh":"\"画事需有天资、功力、学养、品德四者兼备，不可有高低先后。\"","en":"“The practice of painting requires talent, skill, learning and moral character, all four together; none may be ranked higher or lower, earlier or later.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"这段话我读后很有感触。一个人只有真实的面对自己的内心、严肃的对待目光所及的每件事，才能够真的看到事情的发生，而只有有了大量的阅读、学识，才能够更全面的认识到这件事情的不同方面，将事情放在不同的框架来去把握。而良好的品德就像是明镜，映射着自我内心真实的选择。天资的发现离不开一个艺术家对自我的深刻剖析、不停打碎重建的自我人格，寻找自我的变与不变，对世界的看法、与世界的关系、与自我的关系及认知。而功力和学养我认为是两面一体的。两者的本质都是时间。在艺术这一条道路上，我们有多少比例的时间用于学术、艺术？我们是否开阔心胸广集知识而不是作茧自缚固步自封，我们是否孜孜不倦严于利己迎难而上。如果对天资的认识是宏观的、细微的，那对品德的认识应该是更全面的、客观的。道德、品德离不开文明文化的历史和当下的社会建构，品德便是一个人在这个社会上所处的位置及所谋之事。正如前文所说品德如同明镜，它所映射的不仅是我们选择去看到的，我们真实的选择本身，还包含的一个人、一个艺术家的社会责任、传承发扬之义务。我们不仅是我们本身，还是不同线的交点。我觉得不仅是画事如此，这世间的万事万物皆离不开这四点。我觉得我们作画不仅是为了作画，其实也是观照自身的过程，如果一个人连自己是谁都不知道，那这个人还能上哪？去观照什么？","en":"This passage moved me deeply when I read it. Only when a person faces their own heart truthfully and treats seriously everything within their sight can they really see things as they happen; and only with wide reading and learning can they understand the different sides of a matter more fully and grasp it within different frameworks. Good character is like a bright mirror, reflecting the true choices of one’s inner self. Discovering one’s talent is inseparable from an artist’s deep self-analysis, from a self that is continually broken and rebuilt, from searching for what in oneself changes and what does not, for one’s view of the world, one’s relationship with the world, and one’s relationship with and understanding of oneself. Skill and learning, I think, are two sides of one whole. The essence of both is time. On the path of art, what proportion of our time do we give to scholarship and to art? Do we open our minds and gather knowledge widely, rather than spinning a cocoon around ourselves and standing still? Are we tireless, strict with ourselves, ready to meet difficulty head-on? If our understanding of talent should be both broad and fine-grained, our understanding of character should be still more comprehensive and objective. Morality and character are inseparable from the history of civilisation and culture and from the present construction of society; character is the position a person occupies in society and the things they set out to do. As I said above, character is like a bright mirror: what it reflects is not only what we choose to see and our true choices themselves, but also the social responsibility of a person, of an artist, and the duty to pass things on and carry them forward. We are not only ourselves; we are also the point where different lines intersect. I think it is not only painting that is like this: nothing in this world can do without these four. I feel we paint not only for the sake of painting; it is actually also a process of reflecting on ourselves. If a person doesn’t even know who they are, where can they go? What is there for them to reflect on?"},{"t":"p","zh":"\"接受优良传统，倘不起开今作用，则所受之传统死传统也。学术固须接受传统，以为发展之动力。然外来之传统，易须细心吸取，丰富营养。中国人从事中画，如一意摹拟古人，无丝毫推陈出新，足以光宗耀祖者，是一笨子孙。中国人从事西画，如一意摹拟西人，无点滴之自己特点为为民族增光彩者，是一洋奴隶。民族之艺术，即为一民族精神之结晶。故振兴民族艺术与振兴民族精神有密切关系。\"在近百年前潘先生说出的这番话，这个话题，也是我们近百年一直在讨论的。","en":"“To receive a fine tradition without letting it open up the present is to receive a dead tradition. Scholarship must of course receive tradition as the driving force of its development. Yet foreign traditions, too, must be carefully absorbed to enrich our nourishment. A Chinese who practises Chinese painting and does nothing but imitate the ancients, without the slightest renewal that could bring honour to his forebears, is a foolish descendant. A Chinese who practises Western painting and does nothing but imitate Westerners, without a drop of his own character to add lustre to his nation, is a foreign slave. A nation’s art is the crystallisation of that nation’s spirit. Therefore reviving national art is closely bound up with reviving the national spirit.” Mr Pan said these words nearly a hundred years ago, and this topic is one we have been debating for nearly a century."},{"t":"h","zh":"二·潘先生与20世纪中国绘画","en":"II. Mr Pan and Twentieth-Century Chinese Painting"},{"t":"p","zh":"新浙派绘画，老师在课堂上讲新浙派代表人物的艺术经历：他们的素描功底、油画绘画经历以及他们对于素描造型和国画的塑造方式之间的一些推敲、取舍、转化···","en":"On the New Zhejiang School of painting: in class the teacher talked about the artistic careers of the school’s leading figures—their grounding in drawing, their experience of oil painting, and their deliberations, choices and transformations between the modelling of academic drawing and the ways forms are built in Chinese painting···"},{"t":"p","zh":"我个人在浅浅看了新浙派的一些画家的其中的一点作品之后，觉得跟潘天寿先生的简直没法比。在人物造型上新浙派的画家们扎实、厉害。但在整个画面的气势、画面的那种凝聚的感觉，和那种创造的世界的扩散的感觉。潘先生依托现代的说法、画面的评论的角度和方式，为中西结合寻找道路。但中国的纯粹的艺术，气韵神韵，我觉得在新浙派的身上没有体现出来。也没有很好的继承潘先生的画，延续的那种精髓。在那个时代，或许人们想办法对传统进行转换、继承。可或许真的是山穷水尽了。所以我不是说仗着自己年轻无知而大放厥词，而是心里的一种不甘不舍与失落。再往后的中国绘画我没了解过，之后一定会好好了解。","en":"Having taken a brief look at a few works by some of the New Zhejiang School painters, I personally felt they simply could not compare with Mr Pan Tianshou. In figure modelling the New Zhejiang painters are solid and impressive. But in the overall momentum of the picture, that sense of concentration in the picture, and that sense of a created world spreading outward… Mr Pan drew on modern terms and on the angles and methods of pictorial criticism to seek a path for combining Chinese and Western painting. But the pure art of China, its qiyun and shenyun (spirit resonance and spiritual charm), I feel is not embodied in the New Zhejiang School. Nor did they properly inherit the essence that Mr Pan’s painting carried on. In that era, perhaps people were looking for ways to transform and inherit tradition. But perhaps they really had come to the end of the road. So I am not, trading on being young and ignorant, making wild pronouncements; it is a kind of reluctance, an unwillingness to let go, and a disappointment in my heart. I haven’t yet studied Chinese painting after that period, and I will certainly study it properly later."},{"t":"h","zh":"三·《关于潘天寿美术文集》","en":"III. On Pan Tianshou’s Collected Writings on Art"},{"t":"p","zh":"我粗略的通读了这本书。潘先生从绘画本身、篆刻一直到用笔制笔、装裱….将金石学、艺理…都从头梳理，查找大量的文献考证，编著。我没看之前没想过潘先生是这么写这本书的，我以为会是像《苦瓜先生画语录》那样的画论合辑。潘先生作为一校之长，行政事务繁忙，同时作为画家，又很多产。在学术上又是博览群书、严谨考究，这便是潘先生所说的天资、功力、学养、品德四者兼备了吧。","en":"I read through this book roughly. From painting itself and seal carving all the way to using and making brushes and mounting…., Mr Pan sorted out epigraphy, the principles of art… from the ground up, consulting a large body of literature for evidence as he compiled and wrote. Before reading it I had never imagined Mr Pan wrote the book like this; I thought it would be a compilation of painting theory like the Sayings on Painting of Mr Bitter Melon. As head of a school, Mr Pan was busy with administrative affairs; as a painter, he was also very prolific; and in scholarship he read widely and was rigorous and meticulous. This, I suppose, is what Mr Pan meant by having talent, skill, learning and character all together."},{"t":"img","src":"e09-01.png"},{"t":"img","src":"e09-02.png"},{"t":"p","zh":"潘先生的这本文集中\"关于构图问题\"这一章有大量的配图，是那种亲手画的，步骤图一样的图。我之前也看过一些比如芥子兰画谱这种入门者要学着画的，但没有语言的讲解，就觉得看完了跟没看一样，云里雾里。但在这一章里面我的收获真的很大很大，关于构图、关于画面的势，疏密，线条的组织···就是那些抽象的概念都有了一个简单的形象、一个指示","en":"In this collection, the chapter “On Problems of Composition” has a great many illustrations, drawn by Mr Pan’s own hand, like step-by-step diagrams. I had looked before at things like the Mustard Seed Garden Manual of Painting, which beginners have to learn to copy from, but with no explanation in words, it felt as if I hadn’t looked at all—I was lost in clouds and mist. But from this chapter I really gained a great, great deal: about composition, about the shi (momentum) of the picture, density and sparseness, the organisation of lines···all those abstract concepts were given a simple image, a pointer"},{"t":"h","zh":"关于指头画","en":"On Finger Painting"},{"t":"p","zh":"之前没有听说过指头画。我有时也会用手指在画面上抹来抹去，有时会加入一些综合材料比如糊精，这种粘稠的膏状材料，这样可以在纸本材料的绘画上留下一些微凸起的痕迹。我觉得是一种技法吧，在潘先生这里我第一次了解到还有指头画专门的画种。指头画出现起源的比较晚，作画需用到指甲、指肚。虽然指头不能像毛笔那样蓄墨，但却易于发挥枯墨、泼墨、误墨法…指头画虽然很巧妙、也很有乐趣，但潘先生说：要学指头画，还得从毛笔的基础入手，我们必须从内容出发，下功夫去创作。如石涛言：凡是有经必有权，一知其法，即工于化。“我觉得我在画画的时候也应该秉持这个观念，千百种技法，离不开的是画面的基本的框架。功力要有，从建立起来到熟练运用，再到不显于象。而不显并不代表真的没有，而是更高级、更含蓄、更大气的有。","en":"I had never heard of finger painting before. Sometimes I smear things around on the picture with my fingers too, and sometimes I add mixed materials such as dextrin, a thick, paste-like material that can leave slightly raised marks on paintings on paper. I thought of it as just a technique; it was through Mr Pan that I first learned there is a whole genre devoted to finger painting. Finger painting arose relatively late; painting this way uses the fingernail and the pad of the finger. Although a finger cannot hold ink the way a brush can, it readily brings out the dry-ink, splashed-ink and accidental-ink methods… Finger painting is ingenious and great fun, but Mr Pan says: to learn finger painting you must still start from a foundation in the brush; we must begin from content and put real effort into creating. As Shitao says: wherever there is a constant rule there must be adaptation; once you know the method, you become skilled at transformation.” I think I should hold to this idea when I paint as well: for all the hundreds and thousands of techniques, what you cannot do without is the basic framework of the picture. Skill is a must—from building it up, to using it fluently, to the point where it no longer shows in the image. And not showing doesn’t mean it is really absent; it is a higher, subtler, grander kind of presence."},{"t":"h","zh":"结尾","en":"Conclusion"},{"t":"p","zh":"潘先生于我如钥匙或打向某条道路的那束光。我觉得对我而言，读懂中国画按时间顺序有些困难，我觉得太久远的绘画我难以进入他们的世界，只能研究流派或者技法。但读潘先生的画，我一开始也进不去，但现在我觉得可以感受到一些了。所以我觉得或许我再深入了解中国绘画史的时候，倒着去研究，会不会可以更利于理解呢。","en":"To me, Mr Pan is like a key, or the beam of light cast onto a certain road. For me, I think, understanding Chinese painting in chronological order is rather difficult: with painting from too long ago I find it hard to enter its world, and can only study schools or techniques. With Mr Pan’s paintings I couldn’t get in at first either, but now I feel I can sense something. So I wonder whether, when I go deeper into the history of Chinese painting, studying it backwards might make it easier to understand."},{"t":"p","zh":"本次的课受益匪浅，感谢老师。","en":"I have benefited greatly from this course. Thank you, teacher."}]},{"id":"W-2025-01","n":5,"title":{"zh":"从罗伯特·莱曼理解绘画中的身体、痕迹与在场","en":"Understanding Body, Trace and Presence in Painting through Robert Ryman"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2025-06-15","genre":"论文","summary":{"zh":"文章首先引用了艺术家本人所表达的三个艺术理念，指出艺术家创作所持的态度。","en":"The article begins by citing three artistic ideas expressed by the artist himself, pointing out the attitude with which he approached his work."},"words":10509,"blocks":[{"t":"label","zh":"摘要","en":"Abstract"},{"t":"p","zh":"文章首先引用了艺术家本人所表达的三个艺术理念，指出艺术家创作所持的态度。而后，文章引入艺术家的生活轨迹，并由此以其画作为论述对象，按照艺术家绘画发展的线性时间顺序，从中分别抽离出三个进入艺术家世界的视角。这部分聚焦于具体的画面。文章第三部分名为“‘身体’‘在这里’留下了‘痕迹’”，从“一个艺术品在场”和“观看中的流动状态”这两个方面分别分析艺术家的创作理念。最后，文章将讨论放入更大范围内的境遇里，指出从莱曼的艺术实践中可以获得启发的可能。","en":"The article begins by citing three artistic ideas expressed by the artist himself, pointing out the attitude with which he approached his work. It then introduces the artist’s life trajectory and, taking his paintings as the object of discussion and following the linear chronology of his development as a painter, extracts from them three perspectives for entering the artist’s world. This part focuses on the concrete pictures. The third part of the article, titled “The ‘Body’ Leaves ‘Traces’ ‘Here’,” analyses the artist’s creative ideas from two aspects: “the presence of an artwork” and “the fluid state of looking.” Finally, the article places the discussion in a broader situation and points to the possibilities of inspiration that can be drawn from Ryman’s artistic practice."},{"t":"p","zh":"关键词：罗伯特莱曼；物质性；身体；材料","en":"Keywords: Robert Ryman; materiality; body; materials"},{"t":"label","zh":"Abstract","en":"Abstract"},{"t":"p","zh":"The article begins by citing three artistic philosophies articulated by the artists themselves, thereby highlighting the attitudes that guide their creative endeavors. It then introduces the trajectory of the artist's life and, taking their paintings as the primary objects of analysis, traces the linear chronological development of their work to distill three distinct perspectives for entering the artist's world. This section focuses specifically on the visual imagery of the artworks. The third section of the article, titled \"The 'Body' Leaves 'Traces' 'Here,'\" analyzes the artist's creative philosophy through two distinct lenses: \"the presence of the artwork\" and \"the state of flux inherent in the act of viewing.\" Finally, the article situates this discussion within a broader contextual framework, pointing out the potential for drawing inspiration from the artist's artistic practice.","en":"The article begins by citing three artistic philosophies articulated by the artists themselves, thereby highlighting the attitudes that guide their creative endeavors. It then introduces the trajectory of the artist's life and, taking their paintings as the primary objects of analysis, traces the linear chronological development of their work to distill three distinct perspectives for entering the artist's world. This section focuses specifically on the visual imagery of the artworks. The third section of the article, titled \"The 'Body' Leaves 'Traces' 'Here,'\" analyzes the artist's creative philosophy through two distinct lenses: \"the presence of the artwork\" and \"the state of flux inherent in the act of viewing.\" Finally, the article situates this discussion within a broader contextual framework, pointing out the potential for drawing inspiration from the artist's artistic practice."},{"t":"p","zh":"Keywords: Robert Ryman; Materiality; Body; Materials","en":"Keywords: Robert Ryman; Materiality; Body; Materials"},{"t":"h","zh":"引言","en":"Introduction"},{"t":"p","zh":"如果说莱曼自己设定的实践主题，是拒绝被指向的。而我去写这样一篇有结尾的“解析‘拒绝被指向’”的文章，这本身在逻辑上就是相悖的。因此，我只能先提前说明，我的论文，写作主要目的是提供“进入莱曼艺术世界的方式”。重要的不是那个被整合出的看上去闭合的理论，而是“启发的可能”。在莱曼的生命结束后，他作为公共世界“档案”里的人，使写作上是难以避免“指向的终点”的。但这是写作的逻辑，并不指向罗伯特莱曼的艺术实践。","en":"If the theme of practice that Ryman set for himself is one that refuses to be pointed toward anything, then for me to write an essay with an ending, one that “analyses ‘the refusal to be pointed toward’,” is in itself logically contradictory. I can therefore only state at the outset that the main purpose of my thesis is to offer “ways of entering Ryman’s artistic world.” What matters is not a theory pieced together into a seemingly closed whole, but “the possibility of inspiration.” Now that Ryman’s life has ended, he exists as a figure in the “archive” of the public world, which makes it hard for writing to avoid “an endpoint it points toward.” But that is the logic of writing; it does not point to Robert Ryman’s artistic practice."},{"t":"p","zh":"第一次站在罗伯特·莱曼的画前时，我几乎不知道该看什么。没有人物，没有事件，没有象征，没有叙事。白色覆盖着白色，笔触覆盖着笔触。它似乎什么都没有提供给我，却又让我无法迅速离开。","en":"The first time I stood before a painting by Robert Ryman, I hardly knew what to look at. No figures, no events, no symbols, no narrative. White covering white, brushstroke covering brushstroke. It seemed to offer me nothing, and yet it would not let me leave quickly."},{"t":"p","zh":"我们的观看早已习惯于寻找意义：寻找被描绘的对象、寻找艺术家的意图、寻找隐藏在作品背后的观念。然而在莱曼的绘画面前，这些寻找常常失效。视线开始在画布、边缘、钉子、墙面和光线之间游移。观看不再是一种解读，而更像是一种停留。","en":"Our looking has long been accustomed to searching for meaning: searching for the object depicted, for the artist’s intention, for the idea hidden behind the work. Yet before Ryman’s paintings these searches often fail. The gaze begins to drift between canvas, edges, nails, wall and light. Looking is no longer a kind of interpretation; it is more like a kind of lingering."},{"t":"p","zh":"它与中国传统绘画有着共通之处。白色并非空无，恰恰相反，它让许多原本被忽略的东西显现出来：颜料的厚薄、表面的起伏、光线的变化，以及身体与空间之间不断发生的关系。","en":"In this it shares something with traditional Chinese painting. White is not emptiness; on the contrary, it lets many things that would otherwise be overlooked appear: the thickness or thinness of the paint, the undulations of the surface, the changes of light, and the relationship continually taking place between body and space."},{"t":"p","zh":"这篇论文便从这样一次停留开始。","en":"This thesis begins from just such a moment of lingering."},{"t":"h","zh":"艺术家本人所传达的绘画理念","en":"The Ideas about Painting Conveyed by the Artist Himself"},{"t":"p","zh":"莱曼常常被归类于极简主义（但他本人并不这样认为），他那大片的白色绘画似乎藏着一些玄妙高深的神秘理论。莱曼于20世纪八九十年代职业生涯开始进入高峰期，一直到2019年他的职业生涯结尾。在这个时间段发生着一个无法被忽视的语境和话题，那就是“绘画灭亡”。在这个前提下去谈作为艺术家，他个人的绘画理念就不仅仅是表层的绘画理念罗列，同时也指向这个大语境下艺术家对这个问题的回应和思考。笔者根据艺术所接受的采访，根据论文主题列举了他的三个观点：","en":"Ryman is often classified as a Minimalist (though he himself did not see it that way), and his large white paintings seem to conceal some arcane and mysterious theory. Ryman’s career entered its peak in the 1980s and 1990s and continued until its close in 2019. During this period a context and topic unfolded that cannot be ignored: the “death of painting.” Against this backdrop, to speak of an artist’s personal ideas about painting is not merely to list surface-level principles; it also points to the artist’s response to, and reflection on, this question within the larger context. Drawing on interviews the artist gave, and in line with the theme of this thesis, I list three of his views:"},{"t":"h","zh":"2.1“绘画在于带来愉悦”","en":"2.1 “Painting Is About Bringing Pleasure”"},{"t":"p","zh":"绘画在于带来愉悦（pleasure）。而这种愉悦是即刻的、不假思索的。莱曼说：“就像倾听交响乐，你不需要知道乐谱，你可以仅仅听到声音，欣赏声音。”","en":"Painting is about bringing pleasure. And this pleasure is immediate and unreflective. Ryman said: “It’s like listening to a symphony: you don’t need to know the score; you can simply hear the sound and enjoy the sound.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"我们可以看到画布上的笔触、色彩。它们引导着我们的视线。我们可以把这幅画、这位画家或者观看画作的过程，放在心理学、历史学、美学、艺术史、哲学、精神科学、色彩原理、观者的个人文化背景生活背景等等这些体系、结构中，分析这幅画带给观者的“神奇的化学反应”的原因、过程......","en":"We can see the brushstrokes and colours on the canvas. They guide our gaze. We can place this painting, this painter, or the process of looking at the painting within systems and structures such as psychology, history, aesthetics, art history, philosophy, the human sciences, colour theory, and the viewer’s own cultural and personal background, and analyse the causes and the process of the “magical chemical reaction” the painting produces in the viewer……"},{"t":"p","zh":"但构成那一瞬间的所有原因本身与个体感到的愉悦感受却不是因果关系。我愉悦就是我愉悦。逻辑的魔爪伸不到愉悦本身。","en":"But all the causes that make up that instant do not stand in a relation of cause and effect to the pleasure the individual feels. I am pleased because I am pleased. The clutches of logic cannot reach pleasure itself."},{"t":"p","zh":"绘画、音乐.....都是这样“愉悦”。","en":"Painting, music…… all “please” in this way."},{"t":"h","zh":"2.2“绘画在于创造视觉经验”","en":"2.2 “Painting Is About Creating Visual Experience”"},{"t":"p","zh":"许多评论家认为莱曼是哲学家式的艺术家，对于这个问题，莱曼也有所回应：“我不是学者、历史学家，对我而言 绘画是用来解决问题，创造视觉经验的。”","en":"Many critics regard Ryman as a philosopher-artist, and Ryman responded to this: “I am not a scholar or a historian; for me, painting is for solving problems and creating visual experience.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"如果一定要表达个人的理念、思想，用语言文字来描述会更加清晰，而不是在创作之前借用文字来为自己的绘画创作寻找来源与合理性。站在一张绘画前，我们可以用不同的方式去进行分析，可以是在哲学系统中寻找语言，或是在艺术史的系统中寻找来源…但是对于我们而言，这本就处于语言符号所构成的意义世界之中了。而视觉形象是我们未形成复杂语言之前更直接更本能的认识世界的方式。“在学会用语言去描述我们的世界很久以前，我们一定已经学会用视觉来区分和辨别它。”。艺术家用语言思考，但绘画不需要语言先入为主地替自己发言；观众跟着路标——文字与符号，来到一场展览；但展览中的绘画并不是展前导览的插图。","en":"If one insists on expressing personal ideas and thoughts, describing them in words would be clearer, rather than borrowing words before making a work in order to find sources and justification for one’s painting. Standing before a painting, we can analyse it in different ways: we can look for a language within philosophical systems, or look for sources within the system of art history… but for us, this already lies within a world of meaning constituted by linguistic signs. Visual images, by contrast, are a more direct and more instinctive way of knowing the world, one that comes before we form complex language. “Long before we learned to describe our world in words, we must have learned to distinguish and recognise it by sight.” The artist thinks in language, but a painting does not need language to speak for it in advance; the audience follows the signposts—words and signs—to arrive at an exhibition, but the paintings in the exhibition are not illustrations for the pre-show guide."},{"t":"h","zh":"2.3“不存在画什么的问题、只有怎么画的问题”","en":"2.3 “There Is No Question of What to Paint, Only of How to Paint”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在广泛的共识里，绘画有画什么和怎么画这两个问题。甚至，如罗伯特·莱曼所言：“没有画什么的问题，要考虑的只有‘怎么画’这一个问题。”在绘画的过程中、绘画本身的重要性要远远大于它的主题。","en":"By broad consensus, painting involves two questions: what to paint and how to paint. Indeed, as Robert Ryman put it: “There is no question of what to paint; the only thing to consider is ‘how’ to paint.” In the process of painting, the importance of painting itself far exceeds that of its subject."},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术作品中的真理性存在和创作过程中创作者去主体化密切相关——也就是这个过程中就是借由艺术家本人但却不是有意所流露出来的本真性存在。这是一种并不直接显现出重量的轻盈。对此，我想参照米兰.昆德拉的著作《生命不可承受之轻》的情节：当特蕾莎返回捷克时，托马斯感受到了一种“存在性的眩晕”。个体的存在因个体存在之外的存在而展开意义。当特蕾莎回到匈牙利时，对于托马斯来说，这不仅是他的伴侣离开了他，他的责任、意义的锚点也离开了他。存在的重量从他的身上抽离。所以他如行尸走肉四处消磨时间，躲避生命处于自由之轻的虚无。最终他放弃了在匈牙利的一切，回到了正处在战争中的祖国，特蕾莎的身边。而对于萨比娜，她一生都在逃离、追寻无媚俗的自由。可我们不是超人，媚俗避无可避。人活着需要一个有确定性的锚点、一个生命之重。艺术也是如此，它可以允许有更多“未定、悬置”的存在，它给予事情发生方向敞开的可能性；但当它真正发生的时候，也需要有意义的锚点。","en":"The truthful existence in a work of art is closely bound up with the creator’s de-subjectification in the process of making—that is, in this process it is an authentic existence that flows out through the artist, yet not by the artist’s intention. This is a lightness that does not directly show its weight. Here I would like to refer to the plot of Milan Kundera’s The Unbearable Lightness of Being: when Tereza returns to Czechoslovakia, Tomas feels a kind of “existential vertigo.” An individual’s existence unfolds its meaning through an existence outside the individual. When Tereza went back to Hungary, for Tomas it was not only that his partner had left him; his responsibility, his anchor of meaning, had left him too. The weight of existence was drawn out of him. So he wandered about like a walking corpse, killing time, hiding from the nothingness of a life in the lightness of freedom. In the end he gave up everything he had in Hungary and returned to his homeland, then at war, to Tereza’s side. As for Sabina, she spent her whole life fleeing, pursuing a freedom without kitsch. But we are not supermen; kitsch cannot be avoided. To live, a person needs an anchor of certainty, a weight of life. Art is the same: it can allow more “undetermined, suspended” existence, opening up possibilities for the direction in which things happen; but when something truly happens, it also needs an anchor of meaning."},{"t":"p","zh":"从这个角度来切入，我认为对于莱曼来说，他要捕捉的就是重量下与世界交融却不留主体意识的“轻”。他用绘画和空间想呈现给观者的就是这种被剥离后的轻，还原到存在本身的丰富。","en":"Approaching it from this angle, I think what Ryman wanted to capture was a “lightness” that, beneath the weight, merges with the world yet leaves no trace of subjective consciousness. What he wanted to present to the viewer through painting and space was this lightness that remains once everything is stripped away, a return to the richness of existence itself."},{"t":"p","zh":"所以，不存在画什么的问题，只有怎么画的这一过程性问题。","en":"Therefore, there is no question of what to paint, only the processual question of how to paint."},{"t":"h","zh":"罗伯特·莱曼的早期经历与其艺术的核心主题","en":"Robert Ryman’s Early Life and the Core Themes of His Art"},{"t":"h","zh":"2.1在从事艺术创作以前","en":"2.1 Before Taking Up Art"},{"t":"p","zh":"开始去研究一个艺术家时，我对这位艺术家早期经历的资料会尤为注意，因为想了解各种外部因素对这位艺术家成长道路的影响。想根据他的个人经历分析他的个人特质、个人风格的形成、艺术实践的倾向等，了解它们是如何发生和发展的。在MOMA为艺术家制作的catalog中，有一些简要的信息：他出生于美国田纳西州，在高中时开始学习萨克斯，大学时希望成为一名爵士乐手。但至于更细节的信息，莱曼并不愿向外界透露：“我的画关于光、表面和结构，与我的过去无关。”(1985)","en":"When I begin to study an artist, I pay particular attention to material on the artist’s early life, because I want to understand how various external factors shaped the artist’s path. I want to analyse, on the basis of personal experience, the formation of the artist’s personal traits and style, the tendencies of their artistic practice, and so on, and to understand how these arose and developed. The catalogue MoMA produced for the artist contains some brief information: he was born in Tennessee, began learning the saxophone in high school, and in college hoped to become a jazz musician. As for more detailed information, Ryman was unwilling to disclose it: “My paintings are about light, surface and structure; they have nothing to do with my past.” (1985)"},{"t":"p","zh":"在朝鲜战争后备军服役后不久，莱曼于1953年移居纽约，并在纽约现代艺术博物馆（MoMA）担任保安工作了七年，就这样与绘画产生了接触。在20世纪40-60年代，抽象表现绘画方兴未艾。行动绘画、色域绘画、极简主义都正在发生。在一些采访莱曼的资料中，我们可以知道他当时被德库宁、罗斯科、马蒂斯、克莱因等艺术家所深深吸引、影响。","en":"Shortly after serving in the Army reserve during the Korean War, Ryman moved to New York in 1953 and worked as a security guard at the Museum of Modern Art (MoMA) for seven years, and in this way came into contact with painting. From the 1940s to the 1960s, Abstract Expressionist painting was in full swing. Action painting, Colour Field painting and Minimalism were all taking place. From some interviews with Ryman we know that at the time he was deeply drawn to and influenced by artists such as de Kooning, Rothko, Matisse and Klein."},{"t":"p","zh":"此外，根据与他一同长期生活过的艺术评论家露西.利帕德提供的信息，我们知道艺术家最喜欢的书是亨利米勒的《北回归线》。并且他深深受到了存在主义哲学的影响。","en":"In addition, according to information provided by the art critic Lucy Lippard, who lived with him for a long time, we know that the artist’s favourite book was Henry Miller’s Tropic of Cancer, and that he was deeply influenced by existentialist philosophy."},{"t":"p","zh":"关于艺术家的生平介绍就止于此了，这也让我们在进入作品时被迫绕开“传记式”的那种解释，而直接进入材料、笔触、支撑物与墙面之间的关系结构等等。在观看他的作品时与产出作品的作者也因此相互隔开了一段距离，这个距离带我们更直接地靠近画作本身。","en":"The account of the artist’s life ends here, which forces us, when approaching the works, to bypass “biographical” interpretation and go directly into the materials, the brushstrokes, the relational structure between support and wall, and so on. In looking at his works we are thereby also kept at a certain distance from the author who produced them, and this distance brings us more directly close to the paintings themselves."},{"t":"h","zh":"2.2艺术家作品的核心主题","en":"2.2 The Core Themes of the Artist’s Work"},{"t":"p","zh":"策展人罗伯特斯托尔在1993年首次梳理了艺术家的艺术探索轨迹，再到2019年艺术家去世，他职业生涯被划分为四个阶段。本部分我将参考这个按照线性时间的划分，尝试提取出几个核心的主题，分散地解读艺术家的探索过程。","en":"In 1993 the curator Robert Storr first traced the trajectory of the artist’s explorations; through to the artist’s death in 2019, his career has been divided into four phases. In this section I will refer to this linear chronological division and try to extract several core themes, interpreting the artist’s process of exploration piece by piece."},{"t":"h","zh":"2.2.1-绘画在平面内部-材料与结构的发生","en":"2.2.1 Painting Within the Plane: The Emergence of Material and Structure"},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术家处于初步探索阶段时的作品，尽管与他后期的画作存在潜在的和直接的联系，但就这一较早时期而言，艺术实践总的来说还是在平面内的实验。许多画作甚至直接以“实验+编号”为题","en":"Although the works of the artist’s initial exploratory phase have latent and direct connections with his later paintings, during this earlier period his practice was, on the whole, still experimentation within the plane. Many paintings were even titled simply “Experiment + number”"},{"t":"p","zh":"这一阶段他关注：画面的结构、色彩的占比、绘画工具的特性。","en":"In this phase his concerns were the structure of the picture, the proportions of colour, and the properties of painting tools."},{"t":"p","zh":"想要从莱曼的画面中解读出他的“绘之所思”，就不得不提到他深受启发的塞尚和马蒂斯。","en":"To read Ryman’s “thinking in painting” from his pictures, one has to mention Cézanne and Matisse, by whom he was deeply inspired."},{"t":"p","zh":"他认为塞尚、马蒂斯十分了解颜料的特性。在这两位艺术家的油画、水彩画、铅笔炭笔画等当中，我们都可以发现艺术家对不同材料展现的明晰的、相互勾嵌式的运用。——不是艺术家用绘画工具在绘画的承载物上描绘、堆叠的一个“目的-结果”的线性累加。而是每一个动作和各个零碎的落在平面上的结果似乎都是打破了时间，相互抓扣、影响的。","en":"He believed that Cézanne and Matisse understood the properties of paint thoroughly. In these two artists’ oil paintings, watercolours, pencil and charcoal drawings, we can find a clear, interlocking use of different materials. —It is not a linear “purpose–result” accumulation in which the artist uses tools to depict and build up layers on a support. Rather, each movement, and each fragmentary result that lands on the plane, seems to break through time, gripping and affecting one another."},{"t":"p","zh":"同种关系不仅在材料中体现，在画面的结构这方面，也是同理。","en":"The same relationship is reflected not only in materials; the same holds for the structure of the picture."},{"t":"p","zh":"莱曼在访谈中提及塞尚用笔触构建画面。塞尚的每一个色块、笔触都相互呼应咬合并建构着画面结构。色彩、画面结构、构成、构图，这些使画面之为画面的 根本 相辅相成。这很大影响了莱曼对自身作品的呈现的思考——他用单纯的白色、简化色彩、暴露出原本可能会被掩盖掉的因素，对画面进行拆解与建构。","en":"In interviews Ryman mentioned that Cézanne built his pictures with brushstrokes. Each of Cézanne’s patches of colour and brushstrokes echo and interlock with one another and construct the structure of the picture. Colour, pictorial structure, composition, arrangement—these fundamentals that make a picture a picture complement one another. This greatly influenced Ryman’s thinking about how to present his own works: using pure white, simplifying colour, and exposing factors that might otherwise be concealed, he took the picture apart and built it up."},{"t":"img","src":"e05-01.jpeg"},{"t":"cap","zh":"图 1","en":"Figure 1"},{"t":"h","zh":"2.2.2绘画与场域-绘画作为物本身-从“画内”向外延申","en":"2.2.2 Painting and Site: Painting as an Object in Itself, Extending Outward from “Within the Picture”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在莱曼艺术生涯的中后期，他开始关注绘画作品与其周边环境的关系。有时他会在展览的现场根据展览所处的光线墙面等环境进行绘画。并且在这一阶段，他做了一些大型的绘画“装置”。","en":"In the middle and later periods of his career, Ryman began to attend to the relationship between paintings and their surroundings. Sometimes he would paint on site at an exhibition, according to the light, walls and other conditions of the venue. And in this phase he made some large painting “installations.”"},{"t":"img","src":"e05-02.jpeg"},{"t":"cap","zh":"图 2","en":"Figure 2"},{"t":"p","zh":"对这一阶段的莱曼而言，展览的空间和画作本身都很重要。","en":"For Ryman in this phase, both the exhibition space and the painting itself were important."},{"t":"quote","zh":"“墙面本身就是绘画的一部分。我所关注的是真实的空间、场域本身、真实的光线，以及真实的物质表面。”","en":"“The wall itself is part of the painting. What I am concerned with is real space, the site itself, real light, and real material surfaces.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"首先，我们先抽离出“观看一幅绘画”行为本身。就简单的说人、墙上物、空间这三者之间的关系，我们站在一幅画面前，环境、包裹画作的墙面也会进入到我们的观看和感受中。进一步缩小范围：一幅画挂在墙上，它作为“墙上的画”是被凝固的、与我们有所阻断的一个平面，但它同时也是这个空间里的异物，这个异样的物将它自身的“异”对外部空间进行延伸，当站在、处在这张画作面前、在它在的空间里时，观者也是这一场域中的一环。","en":"First, let us isolate the act of “looking at a painting” itself. Put simply, in terms of the relationship among person, object on the wall and space: when we stand before a painting, the environment and the wall surrounding the work also enter our looking and feeling. Narrowing further: a painting hangs on a wall; as a “painting on the wall” it is a congealed plane, set apart from us, yet at the same time it is a foreign object in this space, and this foreign object extends its own “foreignness” into the surrounding space. When standing and being before the painting, in the space where it is, the viewer too becomes a link in this field."},{"t":"p","zh":"莱曼说：“关键在于让画面表面充满生命力，赋予其动态与活力。”","en":"Ryman said: “The key is to fill the surface of the picture with life, to give it movement and vitality.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"生命力不仅通过厚重的笔触和浓稠的颜料来实现，也借助那些在白色基底中若隐若现的微妙变化的色彩、和不同位置的光线变化来推动。在莱曼的画前，观看者的视线很难保持一个“稳定焦点”、画面中的笔触和结构并不直白的诱导到整张画面的某个部分：动态与活力是与观看动作本身共生的：观众的视线往往会在画面的边缘游移、在画布、钉子、墙面之间跳转，观者要不断调整观看的位置和距离。换句话说也就是，作品没有一个“正确观看点”、一个聚集性的“中心”或“终点”——与图像式的“解码”不同，在莱曼的画面上，观看是“过程，是一种身体的定位行为。","en":"Vitality is achieved not only through thick brushstrokes and dense paint, but is also driven by subtly shifting colours that flicker within the white ground and by changes of light at different positions. Before Ryman’s paintings, it is hard for the viewer’s gaze to keep a “stable focus”; the brushstrokes and structure do not plainly lead the eye to any one part of the picture. Movement and vitality coexist with the act of looking itself: the viewer’s gaze often drifts along the edges of the picture and jumps between canvas, nails and wall, and the viewer must keep adjusting position and distance. In other words, the work has no “correct viewing point,” no converging “centre” or “endpoint”—unlike image-like “decoding,” on Ryman’s surfaces looking is “a process, an act of bodily positioning."},{"t":"h","zh":"“身体”“在这里”留下了“痕迹”","en":"The “Body” Leaves “Traces” “Here”"},{"t":"h","zh":"3.1“在这里”——“在场”","en":"3.1 “Here”: “Presence”"},{"t":"p","zh":"“在场”这一词语的范畴很广，在不同的解释方式、不同语境里，“在场”这一词语的内容和指向会引导读者走入完全不同的理解。因此在运用这个词语来进行分析前，我想先作范围的限定与澄清：本文使用的“在场”，小范围的指一种“作品在当下时间空间依照自己本身的“材料、结构和节奏等”成立，观者在“理解”上并不先于“遇见”的“在场”。","en":"The term “presence” (zaichang) covers a wide range; under different interpretations and in different contexts, its content and reference can lead readers into entirely different understandings. So before using the term for analysis, I want to delimit and clarify its scope: “presence” as used in this thesis refers, narrowly, to a “presence” in which “the work stands in the present time and space according to its own ‘materials, structure, rhythm and so on’, and the viewer’s ‘understanding’ does not come before the ‘encounter’."},{"t":"p","zh":"莱曼说：“i don't think of my painting as abstract ,because I don't abstract from anything.”（我不认为我的绘画是抽象绘画，因为我不对一个具体的东西进行抽象）。将“图像”这一因素、画面的存在方式，从绘画整体中暂时地抽离；或引入图像学的方式；我们可以在抽象与具象之间做一个横轴来回调节，使其在视觉上形成不同的形象可识别程度，根据这个“可识别度”给一幅画下“抽象”或是“具象”的定义。可对于具体的画面本身来说，每个笔触都是实实在在存在着的。它在画布上单独成立或与其他笔触相融合，这并不抽象。就算仅仅只有白色，每一个白色的形状、厚薄和画面上被光线所捕捉到的细微色差也都是十分具象的。颜料本身就已经是颜料，是一个此在的物。在“本真地生存上的可能性的见证”问题上，海德格尔写道：“随着丧失于常人之中的境况，此在切近的实际能在——诸种任务、规则、措施、操劳在世和操持在世的紧迫性与广度——总已被决定好了。常人总已经从此在那里取走了对那种种存在可能性的掌握。......由于它的耽搁，此在曾丧失于非本真状态中。从常人中收回〔zurickholen〕自己就是从常人自身的生存方式转为本真的自己存在的生存方式；而这必定以补做〔nachholen〕某种选择的方式来进行。补做选择却意味着对这一补做的选择进行选择，意味着决定要从本己的自己方面来能在。借助对选择进行选择，此在才使自已本真的能在成为可能。”  在绘画中也是这个道理，它可以作为图像的侍从、为叙事服务；也可作为视觉的附庸，激发心灵的共颤；作为“常人”——作为装饰、作为除了自己之外的其他目的的承担者。但作为本真性存在，意味着在涌现和遮蔽中有可以被定格到它“本身、本真”的可能。“再次补做选择，让物成为自身。”正是如此，每一方白色的笔触、与莱曼相互支配。","en":"Ryman said: “I don’t think of my painting as abstract, because I don’t abstract from anything.” (That is: I do not consider my painting abstract painting, because I do not abstract from any concrete thing.) If we temporarily extract the factor of the “image”—the way the picture exists—from painting as a whole, or bring in an iconographic approach, we can set up a horizontal axis between abstraction and figuration and adjust back and forth along it, producing different degrees of visual recognisability of form, and on the basis of this “recognisability” define a painting as “abstract” or “figurative.” Yet for the concrete picture itself, every brushstroke really and truly exists. It stands on its own on the canvas or merges with other brushstrokes; this is not abstract. Even if there is only white, the shape and thickness of every white, and the slight differences of colour caught by the light on the surface, are all thoroughly concrete. Paint is already paint, a thing that is there (Dasein). On the question of “the attestation of an authentic potentiality-for-being,” Heidegger writes: “With Dasein’s lostness in the ‘they’, that factical potentiality-for-being which is closest to it—its tasks, rules, measures, the urgency and extent of concernful and solicitous being-in-the-world—has always already been decided. The ‘they’ has always already taken from Dasein the grasp of these possibilities of being. …… Because of this neglect, Dasein has been lost in inauthenticity. Bringing itself back [zurickholen] from the ‘they’ means turning from the way of existing of the they-self to the way of existing of authentically being-one’s-self; and this must be done by way of making up [nachholen] for a choice. But making up for the choice means choosing to make this choice, deciding for a potentiality-for-being from one’s own self. Only in choosing to make this choice does Dasein make its authentic potentiality-for-being possible.” The same holds in painting: it can serve as the attendant of the image, in the service of narrative; it can be an appendage of vision, stirring a resonant tremor of the soul; it can be one of the “they”—decoration, the bearer of purposes other than itself. But to exist authentically means that, within emergence and concealment, there is a possibility of being fixed in “itself, its own authentic being.” “Make up the choice once more, and let the thing become itself.” Precisely so: each patch of white brushstroke and Ryman govern one another."},{"t":"p","zh":"在这样的绘画面前，抽象具象问题争论就像是地上的两粒尘埃，它们仅仅短暂经过、无法留下痕迹，轻轻的空气流动就将其带走了。","en":"Before such paintings, the dispute over abstraction and figuration is like two specks of dust on the ground: they only pass by briefly, unable to leave a trace, and a light movement of air carries them away."},{"t":"img","src":"e05-03.jpeg"},{"t":"cap","zh":"图 3","en":"Figure 3"},{"t":"p","zh":"莱曼绝大多数的作品都使用白色来进行绘画，因为他认为白色具有彰显所有事物的能力，让观者看到的更多。在访谈中，莱曼说：“如果那些画面是黑色或蓝色、红色，那它们就会完全变成另一件事。你会看见色彩，而那些画面会变得更像物件本身，也更关乎具体的色彩。但白色提供了一种如此中立的情境，以至于当你看到它时，你不会把它想成是“白色”。你就能看到事物的本来面目了。”与罗斯科的大块彩色绘画共置对比，对于莱曼而言，他感兴趣的不是色彩带来的幽密幻觉、以及对观者接受反应的控制，相反，他希望排除掉颜色的“干扰”-让颜料：材料、质地、以及组合的结构本身的语言“被看到”，在未有人进入到艺术品所处之处之前，作品就完整地、自洽地处在那里。","en":"The vast majority of Ryman’s works are painted in white, because he believed white has the capacity to make all things manifest, letting the viewer see more. In an interview Ryman said: “If those paintings were black or blue or red, they would become something else entirely. You would see colour, and the paintings would become more like objects themselves, and more about the particular colour. But white provides such a neutral situation that when you see it, you don’t think of it as ‘white.’ You can see things as they are.” Set beside Rothko’s large colour paintings by comparison, what interested Ryman was not the mysterious illusions colour brings, or control over how the viewer receives and reacts; on the contrary, he wanted to remove the “interference” of colour, letting the paint—its material, its texture, and the structure of its combinations—have its own language “be seen.” Before anyone enters the place where the artwork is, the work is already there, complete and self-consistent."},{"t":"quote","zh":"依本源而居者  终难离其原位。","en":"Whoever dwells near the origin / in the end can hardly leave the place."},{"t":"quote","zh":"——荷尔德林","en":"—Hölderlin"},{"t":"h","zh":"3.2“身体”与“痕迹”：","en":"3.2 “Body” and “Trace”:"},{"t":"p","zh":"上部分是对于画面本身的分析，这部分将侧重于对观看过程的分析。","en":"The previous section was an analysis of the picture itself; this section will focus on an analysis of the process of looking."},{"t":"p","zh":"第二章第二节提到，在莱曼的画面上，观看是“过程，是一种身体的定位行为。这与我们所接受的中国山水画的观看方式有相通之处。各个文化文明产生的艺术作品，当到达了一定的高度，将相互贯通。罗伯特莱曼画面中的精神可以作为桥梁，带我们回到中国古代山水的世界。在此我想选择王蒙的山水画，将其放在一种“生成的状态”中来阐释。","en":"Section 2 of Chapter 2 noted that on Ryman’s surfaces looking is “a process, an act of bodily positioning. This has something in common with the way of looking at Chinese shanshui (landscape) painting that has come down to us. When the artworks produced by different cultures and civilisations reach a certain height, they connect with one another. The spirit in Robert Ryman’s paintings can serve as a bridge that takes us back to the world of ancient Chinese landscape painting. Here I choose the landscapes of Wang Meng and interpret them within a “state of becoming.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"首先我想先探讨的是，在一幅作品完成前，在两位艺术家都是如何创作的。我不能自创空中楼阁，而后将两者的绘画放在这个虚壳中、班门弄斧地自证其合理性。因此，在此引入“感兴”一词。但不是将两者放在“感兴”的发生框架里，而是讲述这个框架，以期达到一种“意会”的效果。","en":"What I first want to explore is how the two artists each worked before a work was completed. I cannot build a castle in the air, and then place the two painters’ work inside this empty shell and presumptuously prove its validity. Therefore I introduce here the term ganxing (感兴, “being moved and roused”). But rather than placing the two within the framework of how ganxing occurs, I describe this framework, in the hope of reaching a kind of tacit understanding."},{"t":"p","zh":"“感兴”一词的词源可以被追溯至先秦时期，之后又随时代发展被重新阐释。依照初始时先秦对“感”与“兴”的编录，感兴是：“‘主体’在承接、面临某事物时，内在被‘触动’。这时，‘主体’与外部发生了一种相融，从而在符号世界产生的‘对语言和其内涵进行的选择和运用’的呈现。”感兴常被简单指向一种情绪状态、或是一种“感”加“兴”的单向过程。感兴是：“能量出现，方向尚未依此被调配。”因为方向是有指向的，而能量是敞开、悬而未决的。","en":"The origins of the term ganxing can be traced back to the pre-Qin period, and it was later reinterpreted as the ages went on. According to the original pre-Qin records of gan (感, to be moved) and xing (兴, to rise, to be roused), ganxing is: “when the ‘subject’ receives or faces something, it is inwardly ‘touched.’ At this moment the ‘subject’ enters into a kind of fusion with what is outside, giving rise in the symbolic world to the presentation of ‘a selection and use of language and its connotations’.” Ganxing is often simply taken to mean an emotional state, or a one-way process of gan plus xing. Ganxing is: “energy appears, while its direction has not yet been allotted accordingly.” For a direction points somewhere, whereas energy is open and unresolved."},{"t":"p","zh":"“兴”字所暗示的感兴之意，也包含了外物对内心的感发作用。“感兴”一词并不是一个在古典文献中被严格界定的哲学术语，而是由“兴”的诗学传统与中国思想中的感应观念长期叠合而形成的一种经验结构。它并非指向某种明确的概念体系，而是描述一种意义在行动过程尚未被完全概念化之前的生成状态。","en":"The sense of ganxing implied by the character xing also includes the stirring effect of external things upon the heart. “Ganxing” is not a philosophical term strictly defined in the classical texts, but an experiential structure formed through the long overlapping of the poetic tradition of xing with the idea of resonance (ganying) in Chinese thought. It does not point to any explicit conceptual system; rather, it describes a state of becoming in which meaning, in the course of action, has not yet been fully conceptualised."},{"t":"p","zh":"在中国以笔墨书写为核心的文人绘画实践传统中，这种状态往往通过身体行动得以呈现。“皴”、“擦”、“勾”、“描”...这些我们耳熟能详的绘画技法，放在实践过程的语境中，实则是作画者的呼吸节律、身体重心的游动以及手腕握笔带来的笔触节奏，通过水与墨的流动在纸面之上所留下的痕迹。在绘画的整体上，进一步形成了我们常言的“气”“势”“迹”。这些痕迹既是物质性的，同时又承载着作画者行动发生时的时间经验。这些痕迹进一步以人的视觉为载体，通过人与人之间相同的身体构造和呼吸节律，进一步构建出一种作画者与观画者可共同交流的世界。","en":"In the Chinese tradition of literati painting, centred on writing with brush and ink, this state is often presented through bodily action. Techniques we know so well—cun (texturing strokes), ca (rubbing), gou (outlining), miao (tracing)…—when placed in the context of practice, are in fact the traces left on the paper, through the flow of water and ink, by the painter’s rhythm of breathing, the shifting of the body’s centre of gravity, and the rhythm of strokes produced by the wrist holding the brush. Across the painting as a whole, they further form what we commonly call qi (vital breath), shi (momentum) and ji (trace). These traces are material, and at the same time they carry the experience of time from the moment the painter’s action took place. With human vision as their carrier, and through the bodily structure and breathing rhythms that people share, these traces go on to build a world in which painter and viewer can communicate."},{"t":"p","zh":"在感兴的过程中，后发生的也在指向、定义着前发生的，单向流动的时间并不决定这一作品内部的时间结构。在这种生成状态中，作品不是一个封闭的整体，而是储存了一种“尚未完成”的力场，这个力场使得观者处于其前，随着创作者的身体运动、而被触动——观看成为新的“感兴事件”，另一具身体在这个生成过程中被重新开启。","en":"In the process of ganxing, what happens later also points to and defines what happened earlier; time flowing in one direction does not determine the temporal structure within the work. In this state of becoming, the work is not a closed whole but holds an “unfinished” force field. This force field places the viewer before it, to be touched along with the movements of the creator’s body—looking becomes a new “event of ganxing,” and another body is opened anew within this process of becoming."},{"t":"p","zh":"现在，我们聚焦于“触动”本身，来去仔细拆解艺术作品在这一瞬间带给观者的感受。对于不同的观者而言，不同的作品会带来不可复制的、独特经验的“触动”。从这个节点开始，人们会在这个节点上延伸出很多个人的记忆或感想。在这里用笔者的个人观画感受来举例：在观看王蒙的山水画时，画面中“牛毛皴”的那种“毛茸茸”的视觉触感在一瞬间、会在身体上发生感受：“身体感到轻微的、被抓挠过的感觉，就好像是有一股微弱的电流穿过了身体。鼻根处似乎有一种淡淡的烧焦了的味道。”瞬间随后发生的，是在这具身体过去发生过的某个片段涌入脑中。于此同时，这种“触动”在不同的作品和观看者处是有着“强度”差异的。尽管有的艺术作品“使观者发生触动”更具普遍性，但在不同个体所面对这同一个艺术作品时，所带来的情感体验是不同的。","en":"Now let us focus on “being touched” itself, and carefully take apart what the artwork gives the viewer in that instant. For different viewers, different works bring an unrepeatable “touch” of unique experience. From this node, people extend many personal memories or thoughts. Let me take my own experience of looking at paintings as an example: when I look at Wang Meng’s landscapes, the “fuzzy” visual tactility of the “ox-hair texture strokes” (niumao cun) in the picture produces, in an instant, a sensation in the body: “The body feels something slight, as if it had been scratched, as though a faint electric current had passed through it. At the root of the nose there seems to be a faint smell of burning.” What follows in that instant is some fragment from this body’s past flooding into the mind. At the same time, this “touch” differs in “intensity” from work to work and viewer to viewer. Although some artworks are more universal in “touching the viewer,” the emotional experience they bring differs when different individuals face the same artwork."},{"t":"cap","zh":"图 4 元 王蒙 松下著书图（局部）|纸本水墨","en":"Figure 4. Wang Meng (Yuan dynasty), Writing Books under the Pine Trees (detail) | ink on paper"},{"t":"img","src":"e05-04.webp"},{"t":"cap","zh":"466.7x70.5厘米 克利夫兰艺术博物馆藏","en":"466.7 × 70.5 cm, Cleveland Museum of Art"},{"t":"p","zh":"在“触动”的一瞬间后，语言、记忆、知识慢慢追随其后。这个过程看起来像是个人经验在前，而后记忆被唤起，强度是由记忆决定。但若是真的如此，这种艺术作品对人的身体发生的反应就将会停留在个体内部，无法产生交汇。实际上，正如“感兴”的发生过程，强度本身就是展开的、潜在被连接的。而在特定的场域中，个体的记忆、经验只是在遭遇强度展开扩散的“场”时，在个体身体场内部的在“关系已经在先”了的条件中，被强度所吸取、摄引的部分。","en":"After the instant of “being touched,” language, memory and knowledge slowly follow. This process looks as if personal experience comes first, memory is then called up, and intensity is determined by memory. But if that were really so, the reaction an artwork produces in a person’s body would stay inside the individual and could never meet anyone else’s. In fact, just as in the occurrence of ganxing, intensity itself is unfolding and potentially connected. And in a particular field, an individual’s memories and experiences are only the parts that, on encountering the “field” in which intensity unfolds and spreads, are drawn in and absorbed by intensity, under conditions within the individual’s bodily field in which “relations already come first.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"虽然对观者身体发生作用的强度一定程度上是与观者过去相关的，但并不是完全和个人经验挂钩。与此相同的逻辑，艺术作品中的痕迹的强度也并不和它承载的历史记忆或传统意义完全挂钩。不是记忆触发强度，而是强度在某些情况下以“记忆”的形式显现。古代的山水画在当下——与作画时完全不同的现代生活条件下仍能够触动我们；王蒙的山水画可以通过牛毛皴的痕迹击中我，莱曼的白色绘画通过笔触留下的痕迹触发我。也正是因为它们并不完全要求我们和他们了解、共享一种历史、文化经验，它要求的是一种艺术品自身具备的强度和观者的“身体配置”。人类的身体在一些基础层面上是高度相似的，比如：呼吸的频率；节律的区间。通过这些生物共性，人与人越过语言，建立起联系。","en":"Although the intensity acting on the viewer’s body is related to some extent to the viewer’s past, it is not wholly tied to personal experience. By the same logic, the intensity of the traces in an artwork is not wholly tied to the historical memory or traditional meaning it carries. It is not memory that triggers intensity; rather, in certain circumstances intensity appears in the form of “memory.” Ancient landscape paintings can still move us today, under modern living conditions entirely different from those in which they were painted; Wang Meng’s landscapes can strike me through the traces of ox-hair texture strokes, and Ryman’s white paintings set me off through the traces left by the brushstrokes. This is precisely because they do not wholly require us to know them and share a historical or cultural experience with them; what they require is an intensity that the artwork itself possesses and the viewer’s “bodily configuration.” Human bodies are highly similar at certain basic levels: for example, the frequency of breathing, the range of rhythms. Through these biological commonalities, people reach past language and form connections."},{"t":"h","zh":"拒绝“让观看指向完成”的绘画","en":"Painting That Refuses to “Let Looking Point Toward Completion”"},{"t":"h","zh":"4.1共同的客体-作为“协商平台”的白色","en":"4.1 A Common Object: White as a “Platform for Negotiation”"},{"t":"p","zh":"西方的古典肖像绘画是在代表性公共领域以及封建制度下闲暇带来的文化生活中产生的。西方贵族身为契约分封的领主、几乎在自己的领土之内自治，有相当大的自主权。同时，由于他们是文化生活的主导者，在他们的具体艺术品中，这种代表性公共领域的运行逻辑也是同步的。其中，一个核心的词就是-“展示”。而我们去观看一些古代贵族的绘画肖像时，就已经不由自主地处在他们的逻辑结构当中了。这要怎么解释呢？按照汉娜阿伦特的说法，一个人是没有政治的，而两个人就可以有政治了。换句话说：总有一个说话的人和倾听的人——讲述者和被讲述者，权力就开始从这当中浮现。同样，在观看绘画时也是这样：代表型公共领域，贵族们通过展示，来构建权力，于是，这件艺术品被创造时本身就有着这样的潜在内涵，粗糙一点来讲就是：“我高、我好，我要向你们来展示了”，也即布迪厄的“符号暴力”。所以观看者看似是主动地选择去观看，但实则在更深层的逻辑中，已经在这个被观看的对象前被剥夺了主体性。同样的关系在今天的生活中也处处可见——对观者的操控和潜移默化的殖民。","en":"Classical Western portraiture arose within the representative public sphere and the cultural life made possible by leisure under the feudal system. Western aristocrats, as lords enfeoffed by contract, were almost self-governing within their own territories and had considerable autonomy. At the same time, because they led cultural life, the operating logic of the representative public sphere ran in parallel in their artworks. One core word here is—“display.” And when we look at the painted portraits of aristocrats of the past, we are already, involuntarily, inside their logical structure. How can this be explained? According to Hannah Arendt, one person alone has no politics, but two people can have politics. In other words: there is always someone who speaks and someone who listens—the narrator and the narrated—and power begins to emerge from this. It is the same with looking at paintings: in the representative public sphere, aristocrats constructed power through display, so the artwork already carried this latent meaning when it was created—put crudely: “I am high, I am good, and I am going to put myself on display for you,” which is Bourdieu’s “symbolic violence.” So the viewer seems to choose actively to look, but at a deeper logical level has already been stripped of subjectivity before the object being looked at. The same relationship can be seen everywhere in life today—the manipulation of viewers and a colonisation that works imperceptibly."},{"t":"p","zh":"把“莱曼的绘画”放入这个前提和语境中，回应前文所讨论的、他所关注的主题以及他让他的绘画作品呈现的方式。他的艺术作品不再是那种“展示”语境的，悬挂在墙面上的那个被叙事包围的更高位者，而是溶于观者所处的空间，与之形成一种共生的、相互缠绕的关系。画面中那些有干燥时间、有堆积、刮擦的白，不会自动生产出意义、并不指向外在叙事，而是停留在了材料留下的痕迹，使自己无法被指涉。在这里，颜料、笔触就是其所是的是其本身--它们是无指向的媒介。","en":"Let us place “Ryman’s paintings” within this premise and context, in response to the themes he attended to, discussed above, and the way he let his paintings present themselves. His artworks no longer belong to the context of “display”—the superior hanging on the wall, surrounded by narrative—but dissolve into the space the viewer is in, forming a symbiotic, mutually entwined relationship with it. The whites in the pictures, with their drying times, their build-ups and scrapings, do not automatically produce meaning and do not point to an external narrative; they remain with the traces the material has left, making themselves impossible to refer to. Here paint and brushstroke are what they are, themselves—they are media that point to nothing."},{"t":"h","zh":"4.2工作到行动*——意义的转移","en":"4.2 From Work to Action*: The Shift of Meaning"},{"t":"quote","zh":"“不存在那个被设定的目的地，有的只是动作。（There is no destination, only movement.)”","en":"“There is no destination, only movement.”"},{"t":"quote","zh":"——亨利.米勒《北回归线》","en":"—Henry Miller, Tropic of Cancer"},{"t":"p","zh":"在过去，制度、传统、宗教替人们承担意义。可自现代以来，意义已不再是自动成立的了。有人选择自己为自己的行为赋予意义，也有人说自由的人要为自己的每一步寻找正当性...工具理性已经取代了终极关怀。过去沿袭下来的宏大叙事框架在伦理逻辑上是站不住的。在具体的生活语境里，也就是说，一个具体的个体无法作为一个个体真的去拯救或者改变任何人、去承担承担不了的责任。","en":"In the past, institutions, traditions and religion carried meaning on people’s behalf. But since the advent of modernity, meaning no longer holds automatically. Some choose to give meaning to their own actions; others say that a free person must seek justification for every step they take… Instrumental rationality has replaced ultimate concern. The grand narrative frameworks handed down from the past cannot stand up in terms of ethical logic. In concrete life situations, that is to say, a concrete individual cannot, as an individual, truly save or change anyone, or take on responsibilities that cannot be borne."},{"t":"p","zh":"而在具体的行为里，人能做只剩下了：找出问题、做出判断；而在具体的态度上，似乎只剩下了不说谎。","en":"And in concrete action, all that is left for a person to do is to identify problems and make judgments; and in concrete attitude, all that seems to be left is not lying."},{"t":"p","zh":"我们用语言交流，但这中间总是存在着歧义、错位；语言想要诉说真理，但它总是容易自我指涉，作为存在者遮蔽着真理。并且有时尽管改变叙事的语境和框架，但实际上并没有新的内容出现。在今天，思想是如此容易被语言切割成碎片，以至于其被再次加工成为一个个提供合法性的装置。","en":"We communicate in language, but there is always ambiguity and misalignment in between; language wants to tell the truth, but it easily becomes self-referential and, as a being, conceals the truth. And sometimes, although the context and framework of a narrative are changed, no new content actually appears. Today thought is so easily cut into fragments by language that it gets reprocessed into one device after another for supplying legitimacy."},{"t":"p","zh":"作为一个主体，在这样一个工具理性的结构中，当需要脱离自己、进入到社会结构去讲述宏大叙事时，会产生一种切换感、分裂感。因为涉及到用语言传播的问题就也触碰到了语言的真实性、伦理性的问题。比如：我有怎样的资格去这样说/做？我该如何将个人的观念理念转述出去？这种转述怎样不算是对他人的操控？我创造的价值是对于谁而言是有意义的？....","en":"As a subject in such a structure of instrumental rationality, when one has to leave oneself and enter the social structure to tell a grand narrative, a sense of switching, of being split, arises. For whatever involves dissemination through language also touches on the truthfulness and the ethics of language. For example: What standing do I have to say or do this? How should I convey my personal ideas to others? How can this conveying not be a manipulation of others? For whom is the value I create meaningful?…."},{"t":"p","zh":"而罗伯特.莱曼几乎不谈这个维度的问题。他喜欢亨利米勒的《北回归线》、仔细研究过存在主义哲学。所以据此我们可以推断，存在、伦理、意义问题对他而言是深思熟虑过后沉重、沉默、内敛。他不谈，或许是因为他把“行动”范围内的问题当成了工作的前提条件。他只活动在：“支撑、颜料、表面、在场。”这些设定的限制中。他不试图解决意义危机、作出立场判断......而是让这些问题被放在前面，成为了前提。这些问题不再直接连接自己的工作，而是被嵌入进了材料关系。当创作变成：对材料的耐心、对空间的回应、对时间的承担...艺术的伦理就不再依赖观众。","en":"Robert Ryman hardly ever talks about questions of this dimension. He loved Henry Miller’s Tropic of Cancer and studied existentialist philosophy carefully. From this we can infer that, for him, questions of existence, ethics and meaning were heavy, silent and held within, after long deliberation. He did not talk about them, perhaps because he treated questions within the scope of “action” as the preconditions of his work. He moved only within the limits he had set: “support, paint, surface, presence.” He did not try to resolve the crisis of meaning or to take a position…… instead he let these questions be placed first, so that they became premises. These questions no longer connect directly to his work but are embedded in the relations of materials. When making art becomes patience with materials, response to space, and bearing the weight of time… the ethics of art no longer depends on the audience."},{"t":"p","zh":"“需要知道”这一循环停止，一个答案并不需要被他整合出来而后被确认：我是不是可以继续。在他的艺术世界中，他只判断：“这一步是否符合我设定的限制。”这不是进入乌托邦的解放、也不是犬儒主义的避世，而是在设定的范围里说实话——一种在逻辑上可以不自欺的可能。","en":"The cycle of “needing to know” stops; no answer needs to be pieced together by him and then confirmed: whether I may go on. In his artistic world he judges only: “Does this step keep to the limits I have set?” This is neither a liberation into utopia nor a cynic’s withdrawal from the world, but telling the truth within a set range—a possibility, logically, of not deceiving oneself."},{"t":"h","zh":"致谢","en":"Acknowledgements"},{"t":"quote","zh":"凡已死者，永不再死。 What is dead may never die.","en":"What is dead may never die."},{"t":"quote","zh":"——谨致敬那些作者们和作品们。","en":"—In tribute to those authors and those works."},{"t":"p","zh":"感谢家人们在生活中所有的爱、守护与支持。感谢朋友们的理解与挂念。感谢学姐们的关爱与照顾，感谢同学们在无意中流露出的全部善意。","en":"Thank you to my family for all their love, protection and support in life. Thank you to my friends for their understanding and concern. Thank you to the senior students for their care and looking after me, and to my classmates for all the kindness they showed without meaning to."},{"t":"p","zh":"感谢陈坚导师的倾听、鼓励与教导。老师强调，要练好色彩关系和人物造型，而这些都逐渐成为了我进行艺术表达的地基。“做人要靠谱”，老师常对我讲。“自我表达”和“做学生的职责、做艺术家的职责”会产生碰撞，但作为社会中的人，要认清自己的能力，还有自己所在的位置和责任。","en":"Thank you to my supervisor, Chen Jian, for his listening, encouragement and teaching. He stressed practising colour relationships and figure modelling, and these have gradually become the foundation of my artistic expression. “Be someone people can count on,” he often told me. “Self-expression” and “the duties of a student, the duties of an artist” may collide, but as a person in society one has to recognise one’s own abilities, as well as one’s position and responsibilities."},{"t":"p","zh":"每个时代都有每个时代的艺术，可我们的艺术之路还正处于这个前期阶段，我们也不知道自己的“创造”是否真的是时代的产物，还是说只是一时脑热。老师说，要从体系中而出。这是艺术和生存的锚点。在没有足够的阅历和沉淀之前，我们需要脚踏实地。","en":"Every age has its own art, but our path in art is still at this early stage, and we do not know whether our “creation” is truly a product of the times or only a passing fever. My teacher said that one has to come out of a system. This is the anchor of art and of living. Until we have enough experience and depth, we need to keep our feet on the ground."},{"t":"p","zh":"谢谢LLM作为快速检索、概括信息的好助手，作为对话者和生发生成机制，让混乱的思考可以快速被多种已经存在的更高的思想所牵引。也感谢其作为生活中的好同伴。","en":"Thank you to LLMs, as good assistants for quickly searching and summarising information, and as interlocutors and generative mechanisms that let muddled thinking be quickly drawn along by the many higher thoughts that already exist. Thank you as well for being good companions in life."},{"t":"p","zh":"感谢学校所建立的学习平台、传道授业解惑的老师们和在生活中友好的教职工们。","en":"Thank you to the school for the learning platform it has built, to the teachers who passed on knowledge and answered our doubts, and to the staff who were friendly in everyday life."},{"t":"p","zh":"学生时代结束了。这一路上，有很多的转变和感慨。从最亲密和熟悉的人，到路上仅对视一秒的陌生人，再到互联网上我从未谋面的人。在这里，谨向我遇到的所有人致谢。感谢那些不同程度上启发和鼓舞着我的人们。","en":"My student days are over. Along the way there have been many changes and many feelings. From the people closest and most familiar to me, to strangers whose eyes I met for a single second on the street, to people on the internet I have never met. Here I offer my thanks to everyone I have encountered. Thank you to those who, in different ways and degrees, have inspired and encouraged me."},{"t":"h","zh":"参考文献","en":"References"},{"t":"ref","zh":"1.Robert Ryman - Artworks & Biography\". David Zwirner. Retrieved June 30, 2024.","en":"1.Robert Ryman - Artworks & Biography\". David Zwirner. Retrieved June 30, 2024."},{"t":"ref","zh":"2.《Robert Ryman 》 Tate Gallery Publications,Copyright 1993 Tate Gallery.","en":"2.《Robert Ryman 》 Tate Gallery Publications,Copyright 1993 Tate Gallery."},{"t":"ref","zh":"瓦尔特.本雅明， 2019，《机械复制时代的艺术作品》，载于《本雅明经典作品六种》，王涌 译，北京：北京日报出版社，","en":"Walter Benjamin, 2019, “The Work of Art in the Age of Mechanical Reproduction,” in Six Classic Works by Benjamin, trans. Wang Yong, Beijing: Beijing Daily Press,"},{"t":"ref","zh":"阿瑟.丹托·C.， 2012，《寻常物的嬗变：一种艺术的哲学》，陈岸瑛 译，南京：江苏人民出版社。","en":"Arthur C. Danto, 2012, The Transfiguration of the Commonplace: A Philosophy of Art, trans. Chen Anying, Nanjing: Jiangsu People’s Publishing House."},{"t":"ref","zh":"马丁.海德格尔， 2014，《存在与时间》（修订译本），陈嘉映、王庆节 译，北京：生活·读书·新知三联书店。","en":"Martin Heidegger, 2014, Being and Time (revised translation), trans. Chen Jiaying and Wang Qingjie, Beijing: SDX Joint Publishing Company."},{"t":"ref","zh":"贡布里希.E.H.， 2012，《艺术与错觉：图画再现的心理学研究》，林夕、李本正、范景中 译，桂林：广西美术出版社。","en":"E. H. Gombrich, 2012, Art and Illusion: A Study in the Psychology of Pictorial Representation, trans. Lin Xi, Li Benzheng and Fan Jingzhong, Guilin: Guangxi Fine Arts Publishing House."},{"t":"ref","zh":"米歇尔.福柯，2017《这不是一只烟斗》，刑克超 译，漓江出版社。","en":"Michel Foucault, 2017, This Is Not a Pipe, trans. Xing Kechao, Lijiang Publishing House."},{"t":"ref","zh":"徐小虎，《被遗忘的真迹-吴镇书画重鉴》","en":"Hsu Hsiao-hu (Joan Stanley-Baker), The Forgotten Authentic Works: A Re-examination of the Calligraphy and Painting of Wu Zhen"},{"t":"ref","zh":"克莱门特.格林伯格， 2015，《艺术与文化》，沈语冰 译，广西师范大学出版社。","en":"Clement Greenberg, 2015, Art and Culture, trans. Shen Yubing, Guangxi Normal University Press."},{"t":"ref","zh":"安瑟姆.基弗，2014 《艺术在没落中升起》梅宁、孙周兴 译。北京：商务印书馆","en":"Anselm Kiefer, 2014, Art Will Survive Its Ruins, trans. Mei Ning and Sun Zhouxing. Beijing: The Commercial Press"},{"t":"ref","zh":"巫鸿，2017《重屏：中国绘画中的媒材与再现》，文丹 译，上海：上海人民出版社","en":"Wu Hung, 2017, The Double Screen: Medium and Representation in Chinese Painting, trans. Wen Dan, Shanghai: Shanghai People’s Publishing House"},{"t":"ref","zh":"米兰.昆德拉， 2004，《生命中不能承受之轻》，许钧 译，上海：上海译文出版社。","en":"Milan Kundera, 2004, The Unbearable Lightness of Being, trans. Xu Jun, Shanghai: Shanghai Translation Publishing House."},{"t":"ref","zh":"海德格尔，2010《艺术作品的本源》、弗里德里希-威廉姆.冯.海尔曼 编，孙周兴译。北京：商务印书馆","en":"Martin Heidegger, 2010, The Origin of the Work of Art, ed. Friedrich-Wilhelm von Herrmann, trans. Sun Zhouxing. Beijing: The Commercial Press"},{"t":"ref","zh":"韩炳哲，2019《精神政治学》关玉红 译，中信出版集团","en":"Byung-Chul Han, 2019, Psychopolitics, trans. Guan Yuhong, CITIC Press Group"},{"t":"ref","zh":"马克思韦伯，2019《新教伦理与资本主义精神》，康乐 简惠美 译，上海三联书店","en":"Max Weber, 2019, The Protestant Ethic and the Spirit of Capitalism, trans. Kang Le and Jian Huimei, Shanghai Joint Publishing"},{"t":"ref","zh":"哈耶克 《通往奴役之路》王明毅，冯兴元 译，中国社会科学出版社","en":"Friedrich A. Hayek, The Road to Serfdom, trans. Wang Mingyi and Feng Xingyuan, China Social Sciences Press"},{"t":"ref","zh":"亨利.米勒，2024，《北回归线》，袁洪庚 译，江苏：江苏译林出版社。","en":"Henry Miller, 2024, Tropic of Cancer, trans. Yuan Honggeng, Jiangsu: Yilin Press."},{"t":"ref","zh":"汉娜.阿伦特，2017，《人的境况》，王寅丽 译，上海：上海人民出版社。","en":"Hannah Arendt, 2017, The Human Condition, trans. Wang Yinli, Shanghai: Shanghai People’s Publishing House."},{"t":"ref","zh":"汉娜.阿伦特著，杰罗姆.科恩编，2016，《政治的应许》，张琳 译，上海：上海人民出版社。","en":"Hannah Arendt, ed. Jerome Kohn, 2016, The Promise of Politics, trans. Zhang Lin, Shanghai: Shanghai People’s Publishing House."},{"t":"ref","zh":"齐格蒙.鲍曼《现代性与大屠杀》，2002，杨渝东 史建华 译 译林出版社","en":"Zygmunt Bauman, Modernity and the Holocaust, 2002, trans. Yang Yudong and Shi Jianhua, Yilin Press"},{"t":"ref","zh":"尤尔根.哈贝马斯，1999，《公共领域的结构转型》，曹卫东等译，上海：学林出版社。","en":"Jürgen Habermas, 1999, The Structural Transformation of the Public Sphere, trans. Cao Weidong et al., Shanghai: Xuelin Press."},{"t":"ref","zh":"尤尔根.哈贝马斯，2025《公共领域的新结构转型》，蓝江 译，中信出版集团。","en":"Jürgen Habermas, 2025, A New Structural Transformation of the Public Sphere, trans. Lan Jiang, CITIC Press Group."},{"t":"ref","zh":"金观涛《轴心文明与现代社会》，北京：东方出版社，2021","en":"Jin Guantao, Axial Civilisations and Modern Society, Beijing: Oriental Press, 2021"},{"t":"ref","zh":"德勒兹 ，《普鲁斯特与符号》姜宇辉 译，2008上海：上海世纪出版有限公司","en":"Gilles Deleuze, Proust and Signs, trans. Jiang Yuhui, 2008, Shanghai: Shanghai Century Publishing Co., Ltd."},{"t":"ref","zh":"本尼迪克.安德森《想象的共同体》 吴叡人 译，2016，上海人民出版社","en":"Benedict Anderson, Imagined Communities, trans. Wu Rwei-ren, 2016, Shanghai People’s Publishing House"},{"t":"ref","zh":"亨利.米勒《北回归线》袁洪庚 译 2024 译林出版社","en":"Henry Miller, Tropic of Cancer, trans. Yuan Honggeng, 2024, Yilin Press"}]},{"id":"W-2025-02","n":15,"title":{"zh":"士大夫的乌托邦","en":"The Utopia of the Shidafu"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2025-11-18","genre":"评论","summary":{"zh":"在展览的开幕式上、在演讲中、文章中...人们反反复复提起“文人、和谐、大同”。将其作为传统绘画的根基、独特的价值之处，试图在这个基础上构建起文化自信。","en":"At exhibition openings, in speeches and in articles... people bring up “the literati, harmony, datong” again and again, treating them as the foundation and the distinctive value of traditional painting and trying to build cultural confidence on that basis."},"words":7045,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"在展览的开幕式上、在演讲中、文章中...人们反反复复提起“文人、和谐、大同”。将其作为传统绘画的根基、独特的价值之处，试图在这个基础上构建起文化自信。而生活中，也有人将其贴在自己身上作为一种身份和标签，满足自身需求，与此同时将这些概念所承载的历史慢慢削弱并增加了负面含义。","en":"At exhibition openings, in speeches and in articles... people bring up “the literati, harmony, datong 大同 (the Great Unity, the ideal world of universal concord)” again and again, treating them as the foundation and the distinctive value of traditional painting and trying to build cultural confidence on that basis. In everyday life, too, some people stick these labels on themselves as an identity and a tag to meet their own needs, while gradually weakening the history these concepts carry and adding negative connotations to them."},{"t":"p","zh":"这些概念本身就是乌托邦的构想，因为它如果真的合理的存在，就不会这样被重复、被向往、被构建。如果它真的是存在的，那么人们只会习以为常，这将会是一种常识和久而久之形成的偏见。我们宣扬自己的历史文化中所产出的图像词汇。对摆脱文化他者身份做了很多的尝试。但对于身份认同的寻找，不应以不假思索的重复和自我欺骗为基础。","en":"These concepts are themselves utopian conceptions, because if they really and reasonably existed, they would not be repeated, longed for and constructed in this way. If they really existed, people would simply take them for granted; they would be common sense, and prejudices formed over time. We promote the pictorial vocabulary produced by our own history and culture, and have made many attempts to shake off our status as the cultural Other. But the search for identity should not be founded on unthinking repetition and self-deception."},{"t":"p","zh":"我想先以我们沉浸其中的娱乐世界中常被消费的“贵族形象”来引出对于这种中西不同的对比，重点放在对“主体性”的论述。并作一些中立视角的尝试。","en":"I want first to use the “aristocratic image” so often consumed in the entertainment world we are immersed in to introduce this contrast between China and the West, with the focus on a discussion of “subjectivity,” and to make some attempts at a neutral perspective."},{"t":"h","zh":"一.与士大夫形象相对的欧洲贵族形象","en":"I. The European Aristocratic Image as Counterpart to the Image of the Shidafu"},{"t":"p","zh":"西方各类媒体展现、编织了众多欧洲贵族的形象与生活，比如唐顿庄园等各类历史名人传记电影、电视剧等等。而作为我们，也沉浸在这些泛滥的图像、影视当中。我们对于欧洲贵族的态度，很多时候会被迫处在低其一等的气氛中，并常言行上邯郸学步、自我殖民。一个原因是因为现代社会是由西方文明演变而来，所以在他们的逻辑框架下，我们确实是属于更下等的位置。再一个就是我们自己历史的一些图像有太多的负面的形象，我们的皇室贵族的摄影作品以及影视作品都带着一股被凝视的猎奇的视角，很少带着那种自我展示的态度和出发点，而是一种迎合式的消费。这和我们从业者及受众的接受度有关、与我们的行业发展阶段与经济水平有关、也与我们的“自省基因”有关。主观来讲，这些视觉记忆对我个人而言，会使我感到对我们的传统、旧贵族...有很大的排斥心理。这也是这篇文章切入点选择的原因。那么这种低人一等的情绪从何而来？下面就到了我们的第二部分：","en":"Western media of all kinds have displayed and woven together a great many images of European aristocrats and their lives, such as Downton Abbey and all sorts of biographical films and television dramas about historical figures. And we, too, are immersed in this flood of images and screen works. Our attitude toward the European aristocracy is often forced into an atmosphere of being one rung below them, and in word and deed we often clumsily imitate, colonising ourselves. One reason is that modern society evolved out of Western civilisation, so within their logical framework we really do occupy a lower position. Another is that so many of the images from our own history are negative: the photographs and screen works of our imperial family and aristocracy carry a gazed-upon, curiosity-seeking perspective, seldom an attitude or starting point of self-presentation, but rather a pandering kind of consumption. This has to do with the receptiveness of our practitioners and audiences, with our industry’s stage of development and economic level, and also with our “gene of self-examination.” Subjectively speaking, for me personally these visual memories make me feel a strong aversion toward our tradition, our old aristocracy... This is also why I chose this entry point for the essay. So where does this feeling of inferiority come from? This brings us to the second part:"},{"t":"h","zh":"二．自我展示的符号暴力。","en":"II. The Symbolic Violence of Self-Presentation."},{"t":"p","zh":"西方的贵族文化是建立在代表性公共领域以及封建制度下闲暇带来的文化生活。西方贵族身为契约分封的领主。文化的主导者，也就是各个贵族几乎在自己的领土之内自治，有相当大的自主权。","en":"Western aristocratic culture was built on the representative public sphere and on the cultural life afforded by leisure under the feudal system. Western aristocrats were lords enfeoffed by contract. The leaders of culture, that is, the various aristocrats, were nearly self-governing within their own territories and had considerable autonomy."},{"t":"p","zh":"在中国唯一符合“封建”本意的时期是周代，特别是西周，实行“封邦建国”。自秦始皇之后，主体政治制度是“郡县制”，皇权高度集中。作为特权精英阶层的中国的士大夫则为皇权授予的官僚。","en":"In China the only period that fits the original meaning of “feudalism” (fengjian) is the Zhou dynasty, especially the Western Zhou, which practised “enfeoffing states and establishing domains.” From the First Emperor of Qin onward, the main political system was the “commandery-county system,” with imperial power highly centralised. China’s shidafu 士大夫 (scholar-officials), as a privileged elite stratum, were bureaucrats appointed by imperial power."},{"t":"p","zh":"而这种代表性公共领域的运行逻辑也深深地嵌入到他们的文化中。一个核心的词就是-“展示”。比如，我们去观看一些古代贵族的绘画肖像，这时不由自主地本身就已经在他们的场域中了。这要怎么理解？我们常说一个人是没有政治的，而两个人就可以有政治了。换句话说：总有一个说话的人和倾听的人——讲述者和被讲述者，权力就开始从这当中浮现。同样，在观看绘画时也是这样：代表性公共领域，贵族们通过展示，来构建权力，于是，这件艺术品被创造时本身就有着这样的潜在内涵，即“我高于你们，我要向你们来展示了”，也即布迪厄的“符号暴力”。所以观看者看似是主动的、主导的，但实则潜在的已经被剥夺了主体性。","en":"And the operating logic of this representative public sphere was deeply embedded in their culture. One core word is “display.” For example, when we go to look at painted portraits of aristocrats from the past, we are already, without realising it, in their field. How should this be understood? We often say that one person alone has no politics, but two people can have politics. In other words, there is always one who speaks and one who listens—the narrator and the narrated—and power begins to emerge from this. The same is true of looking at a painting: in the representative public sphere, aristocrats construct power through display, so the artwork, when created, already carries this latent meaning, namely “I am above you, and I am going to display myself to you,” which is Bourdieu’s “symbolic violence.” So the viewer seems active and in control, but has in fact already been latently deprived of subjectivity."},{"t":"p","zh":"这是一种粗糙的平行比较，如果先悬置起来这种现代文明中的中西碰撞，我想先谈一谈士大夫这一群体的艺术表达的创作动机、即他们的多重身份的内在张力。","en":"This is a rough parallel comparison. If I first suspend this Sino-Western collision within modern civilisation, I want to talk about the creative motives of the shidafu as a group in their artistic expression, that is, the internal tension of their multiple identities."},{"t":"h","zh":"三.入世的轴心文化进入到了现代文明","en":"III. A This-Worldly Axial Culture Enters Modern Civilisation"},{"t":"p","zh":"家国同构文化下的君主的权利极大。文人和官员是一个人的两个方面、但并不完全绑定在一起。政治和文化表达也相互交融、联系紧密。诗词、书画常常是政治生活的延申、补充、或失意时候的寄托。“ 修身、齐家、治国、平天下”的儒家价值理念和政治生活本身有着内在巨大的张力。我认为“失意时候的寄托”这一点很重要，因为这是一种“在世的逃避”。我们不需要对更高的存在（例如上帝）示忠、负责，这种排除在外的负担就又转头回到了“此世”。","en":"In a culture where family and state share the same structure, the ruler’s power was enormous. The man of letters and the official were two sides of one person, but not wholly bound together. Politics and cultural expression blended with each other and were closely linked. Poetry, calligraphy and painting were often an extension of or supplement to political life, or a refuge in times of disappointment. The Confucian value of “cultivating oneself, regulating the family, governing the state and bringing peace to all under heaven” carried an enormous internal tension with political life itself. I think “a refuge in times of disappointment” is very important, because it is an “escape within the world.” We do not need to pledge loyalty or be accountable to a higher being (such as God); this burden, being excluded, turns back to “this world.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"这种在此世的状态使得士大夫对“尘嚣缰锁”厌倦而向往“猿声鸟鸣”。这本质是出世的、但是是个人的、他的出发点是一种对被压制境况的反抗与排解。","en":"This state of being in this world made the shidafu weary of “the clamour and fetters of the dusty world” and long for “the cries of gibbons and the songs of birds.” This is in essence a withdrawal from the world, but a personal one; its starting point is resistance to and release from a condition of being suppressed."},{"t":"p","zh":"让我来将用1.山水画与表现主义绘画作共置；2.“中世纪盛期”的西欧骑士与“宋明以降”的中国士大夫，这两个方面通过对比来作说明。","en":"Let me explain this through comparison on two fronts: 1. juxtaposing landscape painting with Expressionist painting; 2. the Western European knight of the “High Middle Ages” and the Chinese shidafu “from the Song and Ming onward.”"},{"t":"h","zh":"1.山水画与表现主义绘画","en":"1. Landscape Painting and Expressionist Painting"},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"zh":"","en":"","span":1},{"zh":"山水画","en":"Landscape painting (shanshui)","span":1},{"zh":"表现主义绘画","en":"Expressionist painting","span":1}],[{"zh":"创作动机","en":"Creative motive","span":1},{"zh":"在现实政治中受挫后，需要通过艺术来重新构建一个内在的、有序的、永恒的精神世界。","en":"After setbacks in real politics, the need to rebuild through art an inner, ordered and eternal spiritual world.","span":1},{"zh":"工业社会下个人的异化、第一次世界大战的创伤，以及对虚伪社会规范的反抗。","en":"The alienation of the individual in industrial society, the trauma of the First World War, and revolt against hypocritical social norms.","span":1}],[{"zh":"情感诉求","en":"Emotional aim","span":1},{"zh":"它追求的是 “澄怀观道”，即洗涤内心的烦扰，去体悟和表现宇宙自然的根本规律（“道”）。以此修身、悟道。","en":"It pursues “clearing the heart to contemplate the Dao,” that is, washing away inner disturbance to apprehend and express the fundamental law of the cosmos and nature (the “Dao”), and thereby cultivating oneself and awakening to the Way.","span":1},{"zh":"如表现主义者所言：“不是描绘可见的，而是制造可见的”——即把内心激烈的、扭曲的、痛苦的情感状态变得可见。","en":"As the Expressionists said: “Not to depict the visible, but to make visible”—that is, to make visible inner emotional states that are violent, distorted and painful.","span":1}],[{"zh":"情感表达方式","en":"Mode of emotional expression","span":1},{"zh":"含蓄的、程式化的、借助笔法的。\n情感通过构图、笔墨和意境来含蓄传达。运用笔法的轻重缓急等来传达情绪节奏。情感被蒸馏、提纯、宇宙化了，个人的悲伤转换为对天地永恒的慨叹。","en":"Restrained, formulaic, relying on brushwork.\nEmotion is conveyed implicitly through composition, brush and ink, and mood (yijing). The rhythm of emotion is conveyed through the weight and speed of the brush. Emotion is distilled, purified and made cosmic; personal sorrow is turned into a lament for the eternity of heaven and earth.","span":1},{"zh":"直接的、感官的、借助色彩与形变的。\n情感直接诉诸于强烈对比的色彩、粗犷的笔触和扭曲的形体。情感是原始的、未加修饰的、个人主义的，追求的是瞬间的视觉与心理冲击力。","en":"Direct, sensory, relying on colour and deformation.\nEmotion appeals directly to strongly contrasting colour, rough brushstrokes and distorted forms. Emotion is primal, unadorned and individualistic, seeking instantaneous visual and psychological impact.","span":1}],[{"zh":"对世界的态度","en":"Attitude toward the world","span":1},{"zh":"来自道家的“道法自然”和禅宗的“明心见性”，认为世界本质上是和谐的，人需要做的是去体认这种和谐。艺术是通往“虚静”状态的路径。","en":"Derived from the Daoist “the Dao follows what is natural” and the Chan (Zen) “seeing one’s nature by illuminating the mind,” it holds that the world is in essence harmonious and that what one must do is recognise this harmony. Art is a path to the state of “emptiness and stillness.”","span":1},{"zh":"来源于近代哲学对个体内在性的发掘，对理性的怀疑与叛变。认为世界本质上是冲突的、病态的，艺术是个人对抗异化世界的武器。","en":"Derived from modern philosophy’s excavation of individual interiority and its doubt of, and revolt against, reason. It holds that the world is in essence conflicted and sick, and that art is the individual’s weapon against an alienated world.","span":1}]]},{"t":"p","zh":"（注：用山水这样一个大的范畴和处于一定历史节点的表现主义来作直接对比，或许会被认为不够严谨。但在我的世界观里，在我们的网状信息获取与处理的认知方式的前提下，这些线性历史的平行对比无法满足我对这些不同信息要素加工处理。并且我从理念上用来做对比的这两个典型，与我个人以及观察经验范围内的很多人所面临的文化转变、身份认同的撕裂感的内核，体现出了较为清晰的原因。）","en":"(Note: Directly comparing a broad category like landscape painting with Expressionism, which belongs to a particular historical moment, may be considered insufficiently rigorous. But in my worldview, given our networked way of acquiring and processing information, parallel comparisons along linear history cannot satisfy the way I process these different elements of information. Moreover, the two types I compare at the level of ideas show fairly clearly the reasons behind the core of the sense of tearing—of cultural transformation and identity—faced by me and by many people within the range of my observation.)"},{"t":"h","zh":"2.骑士和士大夫的身份","en":"2. The Identities of the Knight and the Shidafu"},{"t":"p","zh":"（范围集中在“中世纪盛期”的西欧骑士与“宋明以降”的中国士大夫。）","en":"(The scope is limited to the Western European knight of the “High Middle Ages” and the Chinese shidafu “from the Song and Ming onward.”)"},{"t":"p","zh":"在代表制公共领域中，骑士受封于国王或贵族领主，而后者主导文化生活。而文人士大夫官爵掌握在集中皇权中，身为文人、主导文人画发展。所以将这两者共置并不平行，但在身份、社会阶级中有共通之处，所以借此说明多重身份的内在张力。","en":"In the representative public sphere, knights were enfeoffed by the king or by aristocratic lords, and the latter led cultural life. The ranks and offices of the literati shidafu, by contrast, were held within centralised imperial power, and as men of letters they led the development of literati painting. So setting the two side by side is not a parallel, but they have something in common in identity and social class, so I use this to illustrate the internal tension of multiple identities."},{"t":"h","zh":"①.两者的身份对比","en":"① Comparison of the two identities"},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"zh":"","en":"","span":1},{"zh":"骑士","en":"Knight","span":1},{"zh":"士大夫","en":"Shidafu","span":1}],[{"zh":"权力来源","en":"Source of power","span":1},{"zh":"血统、土地、军事义务。\n与领主的双向契约（我的附庸的附庸不是我的附庸）","en":"Lineage, land, military obligation.\nA two-way contract with the lord (“the vassal of my vassal is not my vassal”)","span":1},{"zh":"学识、德行、科举功名。\n权力来自皇权授予（率土之滨，莫非王臣）","en":"Learning, virtue, success in the imperial examinations.\nPower conferred by imperial authority (“to the shores of all the land, there is none who is not the king’s subject”)","span":1}],[{"zh":"个体内在张力核心","en":"Core of the individual’s internal tension","span":1},{"zh":"契约内部的忠诚与领土自治的张力","en":"The tension between loyalty within the contract and territorial autonomy","span":1},{"zh":"现实政治与自身内部儒家道德理想的张力（从道&从君）","en":"The tension between real politics and one’s own inner Confucian moral ideals (following the Way vs. following the ruler)","span":1}],[{"zh":"价值观","en":"Values","span":1},{"zh":"骑士精神：勇敢、忠诚、虔诚、保护弱小、荣誉。","en":"Chivalry: courage, loyalty, piety, protecting the weak, honour.","span":1},{"zh":"君子之道：仁、义、礼、智、信、中庸、修身养性。","en":"The way of the junzi (gentleman): benevolence, righteousness, ritual propriety, wisdom, trustworthiness, the doctrine of the mean, self-cultivation.","span":1}],[{"zh":"处事行为导向","en":"Orientation of conduct","span":1},{"zh":"外向的、展示的。价值需要通过外在行动证明和捍卫。荣誉是第二生命。","en":"Outward, demonstrative. Value must be proved and defended through outward action. Honour is a second life.","span":1},{"zh":"内向的、自省的。价值需要通过内在修养达成。追求内心平和与道德完善。","en":"Inward, introspective. Value must be attained through inner cultivation. Pursuit of inner peace and moral perfection.","span":1}],[{"zh":"成功路径","en":"Path to success","span":1},{"zh":"武力、军事建功，\n以得在世封赏与荣耀","en":"Force of arms, military achievement,\nto win worldly rewards and glory","span":1},{"zh":"科举入仕、考试和政绩，\n以得青史留名","en":"Entering office through the imperial examinations, examinations and achievements in office,\nto leave one’s name in history","span":1}],[{"zh":"失意应对","en":"Response to disappointment","span":1},{"zh":"冒险与征服","en":"Adventure and conquest","span":1},{"zh":"隐逸与内化","en":"Reclusion and internalisation","span":1}]]},{"t":"h","zh":"②.两者终极追求的差异","en":"② Differences in the ultimate pursuits of the two"},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"zh":"","en":"","span":1},{"zh":"骑士","en":"Knight","span":1},{"zh":"士大夫","en":"Shidafu","span":1}],[{"zh":"世俗上的追求","en":"Worldly pursuits","span":1},{"zh":"维护、扩大 领地与家族荣耀\n追求实体的传承：城堡、血缘、领地、纹章...\n家族、荣耀体现在个人中","en":"Maintaining and expanding territory and family honour\nPursuing material inheritance: castles, bloodlines, territory, coats of arms...\nFamily and honour embodied in the individual","span":1},{"zh":"治国平天下、光宗耀祖\n追求文本的传承：史书记载功业、文章传承后世。\n个人体现在家族、集体中","en":"Governing the state and bringing peace to all under heaven, bringing glory to one’s ancestors\nPursuing textual inheritance: deeds recorded in the histories, writings handed down to later ages.\nThe individual embodied in the family and the collective","span":1}],[{"zh":"精神追求","en":"Spiritual pursuits","span":1},{"zh":"灵魂救赎与上帝认可。其行为最终要向上帝负责","en":"Salvation of the soul and God’s approval. His conduct is ultimately accountable to God","span":1},{"zh":"内在“圣人”境界与天人合一。其行为最终向自己的良知和“道”负责。","en":"The inner realm of the “sage” and the unity of heaven and humanity. His conduct is ultimately accountable to his own conscience and to the “Dao.”","span":1}],[{"zh":"理想人格","en":"Ideal personality","span":1},{"zh":"信仰的捍卫者、领主的忠诚封臣、弱者的保护人、宫廷中风度翩翩的情人","en":"Defender of the faith, loyal vassal of his lord, protector of the weak, gallant lover at court","span":1},{"zh":"道德完满的圣贤、治国安邦的能臣","en":"A sage of complete virtue, an able minister who governs and secures the state","span":1}]]},{"t":"p","zh":"在反思自己时，我发现我的很多出发点和结果导向都是典型的儒生思想，而对于我个人的内在张力在于，在个人主义的现代竞争中，我的这种修身治国齐家平天下就成了一种自我内在的、个人化、封闭的东西。这种世界观所产出的行为无法投射在整个世界中，因为两者既不平行也不接轨。这件事的性质不再是思维导向行为，而后众人一同构建起这种文化影响行动。而是思维和行动之间出现了断裂。并且，这种内部理想和政治现实之间的冲突在当下社会运行的逻辑中，没有安放之地。作为千禧年之后出生的我，在新自由主义社会中成长，与其说一切都被体系收编，倒不如说是这个体系的运行逻辑包罗万象。既然一切都是为了经济，脱贫、军事、文化、环境...都需要强大的经济支撑，那么道德、伦理自然就降级为了一种个人选择。","en":"Reflecting on myself, I find that many of my starting points and outcome orientations are typically those of a Confucian scholar, and my personal internal tension lies in this: in the individualistic competition of modernity, my “cultivating oneself, governing the state, regulating the family and bringing peace to all under heaven” has become something internal, personalised and closed within me. The conduct produced by this worldview cannot be projected onto the world as a whole, because the two neither run parallel nor connect. The nature of the matter is no longer thought guiding conduct, after which many people together build up this culture to shape action. Rather, a rupture has opened between thought and action. Moreover, the conflict between inner ideals and political reality has no place to rest within the logic by which society now runs. Born after the millennium and raised in a neoliberal society, I would say not so much that everything has been absorbed by the system as that the operating logic of this system encompasses everything. Since everything is for the economy—poverty alleviation, the military, culture, the environment... all need strong economic support—morality and ethics are naturally demoted to a personal choice."},{"t":"p","zh":"好像又回到了那个死循环、那个我所批判的乌托邦式的自我欺骗。","en":"It seems I have come back to that vicious circle, that utopian self-deception I was criticising."},{"t":"p","zh":"传统文化与皇权-士大夫的中央集权帝国制度是共生体。科举制是维系这个体系的核心。近代，与【过去范畴的精英】交融的【生产系统和价值评判体系】崩溃。我们今天的政治制度、法律体系、国家概念，都是【西方轴心文明的衍生物-现代文明】的产出物。我经常看到人说”中西结合、辨证取舍”,但我怀疑这种“中西”结合、取舍的可能性。为什么？","en":"Traditional culture and the centralised imperial system of emperor and shidafu were a symbiosis. The imperial examination system was the core that held this system together. In modern times, the [production system and system of value judgement] that was fused with [the elite in the old sense] collapsed. Our political system, legal system and concept of the state today are all products of [modern civilisation, a derivative of the Western Axial civilisation]. I often see people say “combine Chinese and Western, take and discard dialectically,” but I doubt the possibility of such “Chinese-Western” combining and selecting. Why?"},{"t":"p","zh":"因为这就像是一个骑在牛背上的牧童想坐在牛身上替牛把草给吃了。","en":"Because it is like a cowherd boy riding on an ox’s back who wants to eat the grass for the ox while sitting on it."},{"t":"p","zh":"想要作为牧童吃草，就得从牛背上下来，但牧童也吃不了草。","en":"If the cowherd wants to eat grass, he has to get down off the ox’s back, but the cowherd cannot eat grass either."},{"t":"p","zh":"这是我们的困境，我们必须得坐在牛背上。","en":"This is our predicament: we have to sit on the ox’s back."},{"t":"p","zh":"守着过去走不出困境，但走出困境又必须要回溯过去。说句八卦性质的话：走出困境得靠诗人，简单直接、拥有与生俱来的直觉和创造力。","en":"Holding on to the past we cannot get out of the predicament, yet to get out of it we must go back to the past. To say something gossipy: getting out of the predicament will depend on poets—simple, direct, possessed of innate intuition and creativity."},{"t":"p","zh":"我本来想梳理一下脑子里对于这种困境的理解，以至于别让它们是一锅粥。但现在梳理完了发现，就算我这样写下来了，这件事本身在我这里还是一团乱麻。","en":"I originally wanted to sort out my understanding of this predicament in my head so that it wouldn’t be a muddle. But now that I have sorted it out, I find that even though I have written it down like this, the matter itself is still a tangle for me."},{"t":"p","zh":"既有中西碰撞的两者间的张力带来身份、文化焦虑；又有个人对于个体解放、个人权利、自由与责任、家国、道德之间的内在撕扯。","en":"There is both the identity and cultural anxiety brought by the tension of the Sino-Western collision, and the individual’s inner tearing among individual liberation, personal rights, freedom and responsibility, family and nation, and morality."},{"t":"p","zh":"讲道理是讲不清楚了。那在具体的艺术创作表达上呢？下面引入第四个部分。","en":"Reasoning it out won’t make it clear. What about concrete artistic creation and expression, then? This brings in the fourth part."},{"t":"h","zh":"四.日本动画","en":"IV. Japanese Animation"},{"t":"p","zh":"下面我将把侯孝贤导演的《刺客聂隐娘》与宫崎骏导演的《千与千寻》作共置。借这个小范畴的对比侧面说明我对这件事的看法。两者相比之下，日本的影视作品有相当的主体性。","en":"Below I will juxtapose Hou Hsiao-hsien’s The Assassin with Hayao Miyazaki’s Spirited Away, using this small-scale comparison to illustrate obliquely my view on this matter. By comparison, Japanese screen works have considerable subjectivity."},{"t":"p","zh":"在刺客聂隐娘这部电影中，每一个画面都极其精致考究，活脱脱的是一个关于东方的、极度精美的“艺术装置。但与此同时这份完美也带给了我们极大的疏离感，就像玻璃罩里的珍宝，我们承认其价值，却难以与之产生血脉的共鸣。它在一定程度上，依然是一种被（艺术家）高度凝练后的“他者”视角，即便是给我们自己看的。在叙事上，人与人之间的对话也是在去带有目的地讲述、解释。《刺客聂隐娘》的创作是挪用传统、传统是外部元素，是单独在外部悬浮的。","en":"In The Assassin, every frame is extremely refined and meticulous; it is a veritable, exquisitely beautiful “art installation” about the East. But at the same time this perfection also gives us a great sense of distance, like a treasure under a glass dome: we acknowledge its value but find it hard to feel a blood-deep resonance with it. To some extent it is still an “Other’s” perspective, highly condensed by the artist, even if it is made for us to watch ourselves. In the narrative, too, the dialogue between people tells and explains with a purpose. The making of The Assassin appropriates tradition; tradition is an external element, floating separately outside."},{"t":"p","zh":"在千与千寻这部电影中，神道教的宗教理念、元素...处处都在却不刻意彰显。正如在他们的生活、旅游业、城市等当中，这些从历史延续的精神和集体的无意识是其所是的存在于他们的世界。传统是他们看待世界的内在视角，所以传统在它的创作中是由内向外发散的。这导致日本的文化表达有一种理所当然的出发点，而我们总带着慌张与局促。","en":"In Spirited Away, the religious ideas and elements of Shinto... are everywhere yet never deliberately displayed. Just as in their lives, their tourism, their cities and so on, this spirit and collective unconscious continued from history exist in their world as what they are. Tradition is their inner perspective for viewing the world, so in their creation tradition radiates outward from within. This gives Japanese cultural expression a starting point it takes for granted, whereas we always carry a flustered unease."},{"t":"p","zh":"下面的这个小表格是deepseek生成的中日现代化进程中，精英阶级改造的异同：","en":"The small table below, generated by DeepSeek, shows the similarities and differences in the reshaping of the elite class in the modernisation of China and Japan:"},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"zh":"","en":"","span":1},{"zh":"日本废除武士阶级，转化其灵魂。 通过“废刀令”、“征兵令”等法律手段剥夺武士特权，但将其“忠勇、克己、奉献”的武士道精神灌输给新国家的官僚、军人和企业员工，实现了精英精神的平移与传承。","en":"Japan abolished the samurai class but transformed its soul. Through legal measures such as the “Sword Abolishment Edict” and the “Conscription Ordinance,” it stripped the samurai of their privileges, but instilled their bushido spirit of “loyalty and courage, self-restraint, devotion” into the bureaucrats, soldiers and company employees of the new state, achieving a lateral transfer and inheritance of the elite spirit.","span":1},{"zh":"中国彻底打倒士大夫阶级。 科举制被废除，作为传统社会支柱的士绅阶级在革命和土改中被彻底消灭。儒家学说（士大夫的思想根基）被猛烈批判，出现了 “断根式”的精英更替。","en":"China completely overthrew the shidafu class. The imperial examination system was abolished, and the gentry class, a pillar of traditional society, was entirely eliminated in revolution and land reform. Confucian doctrine (the intellectual foundation of the shidafu) was fiercely criticised, and a “root-severing” replacement of elites took place.","span":1}]]},{"t":"p","zh":"我们的现代化建立在暴力的、快速的对传统全盘否定的革命的基础上，但“革命”的历史和精神也并不根植于我们的文化之中。我们决绝地和过去说了再见，在面对西方时，容易陷入 “我们曾经是什么？我们应该是谁？” 的深刻焦虑，表现为时而极度自卑，时而极度自负的摇摆。","en":"Our modernisation was built on a violent, rapid revolution that negated tradition wholesale, but the history and spirit of “revolution” are not rooted in our culture either. We said goodbye to the past resolutely, and when facing the West we easily fall into a deep anxiety of “What were we once? Who should we be?”, which shows itself as a swing between extreme inferiority at times and extreme arrogance at others."},{"t":"p","zh":"日本在现代化进程中，缓慢的把传统嫁接在其中，这种传统、历史有所缓冲和延续的。而中国在一些重要的历史节点里把传统视为“需要克服的障碍”，我们在打开国门时，这种历史传统和现代化是对立抗争的、转变是更为瞬间的。我们的传统在时间线上，中间是有断裂的。我们无法设想，在危亡之时，我们的知识分子们是肩负着怎样的纠结痛苦与压力，也无法设想，如果他们当时慢一点、一点一点地去嫁接，会不会让事情有所不同。从心理的角度来讲，中国原本是东亚文化中心的“天朝上国”，文化自信根深蒂固。当被自己眼中的“蛮夷”击败时，产生的自信崩塌是毁灭性的。为了生存，不得不彻底的自我否定，其过程自然也更为痛苦和剧烈。","en":"In its modernisation, Japan slowly grafted tradition into it; this tradition and history had a buffer and a continuity. China, at some important historical junctures, regarded tradition as “an obstacle to be overcome”; when we opened our doors, this historical tradition and modernisation stood in opposition and struggle, and the transformation was far more abrupt. Our tradition has a break in the middle of its timeline. We cannot imagine with what conflicted pain and pressure our intellectuals were burdened in the hour of national peril, nor can we imagine whether, had they gone a little slower and grafted things on bit by bit, it would have made any difference. Psychologically speaking, China had originally been the “Celestial Empire” at the centre of East Asian culture, with deep-rooted cultural confidence. When defeated by those it regarded as “barbarians,” the resulting collapse of confidence was devastating. To survive, it had to negate itself completely, and the process was naturally more painful and violent."},{"t":"p","zh":"我们无法用现代语言自然地去讲述传统故事。有的是像《刺客聂隐娘》那样，罩着一层博物馆的玻璃，近在眼前却陌生疏离；还有的是像商业古装剧那样，披着一层古装式的服装迎合特定群体的价值观和情感内核...","en":"We cannot tell traditional stories naturally in a modern language. Some, like The Assassin, are covered by a layer of museum glass, close at hand yet strange and distant; others, like commercial costume dramas, wear a layer of period costume to cater to the values and emotional core of particular audiences..."},{"t":"p","zh":"在饮食男女中，李安导演用了一个慈悲的视角来去解读父亲的这个身份、作为父权制主导者的个体境遇中的这样一种身份困境。在结尾，当他剥去了社会锁链的枷锁时，他的味觉也恢复了。无论这是不是导演自己的有意设计，但在我看来这是对传统与现代伦理转换的一种探索。","en":"In Eat Drink Man Woman, director Ang Lee uses a compassionate perspective to interpret the identity of the father, an identity predicament within the individual situation of one who presides over patriarchy. At the end, when he has stripped off the shackles of social chains, his sense of taste returns too. Whether or not this was the director’s deliberate design, to me it is an exploration of the transition between traditional and modern ethics."},{"t":"p","zh":"很多国际舞台上的文化宣传时的场景常让我幻视：一个满脸是土的小孩而从打了补丁的棉衣口袋中掏出玻璃珠，高高举起，睁着水汪汪的大眼睛讲：“你看，我们也有好东西”。一群群人们像是一个时常遭到批评、心中有很多的创伤的小孩，捧着隐隐作痛的心脏仍期望被认可。","en":"Many scenes of cultural promotion on the international stage often make me picture this: a child with a face covered in dirt pulls a glass marble out of the pocket of a patched cotton coat, holds it up high, and says with big, watery eyes, “Look, we have good things too.” Crowds of people are like a child who is often criticised and carries many wounds in the heart, holding a dully aching heart and still hoping to be recognised."},{"t":"p","zh":"最后这一篇，写了一大顿也没写出逻辑清晰的论证、也带着这种情绪化的文化焦虑。想把一些东西想扯开了讲，但却像是在扯一个钢丝球一样，越扯越乱。但得出了一个小小的直觉，重点还是，要创造，要带着主体性。","en":"This final piece: I have written a great deal and still not produced a logically clear argument, and it too carries this emotional cultural anxiety. I wanted to pull some things apart and lay them out, but it was like pulling at a steel-wool ball—the more I pulled, the more tangled it got. But I arrived at a small intuition: the point, still, is to create, and to create with subjectivity."},{"t":"p","zh":"还有一点需要被认识清楚：儒、道、法、佛，士大夫文化、民间习俗、地域文化……这些彼此之间常有矛盾的传统，哪一个才算“传统”？到底什么是传统？","en":"There is one more thing that needs to be clearly recognised: Confucianism, Daoism, Legalism, Buddhism, shidafu culture, folk customs, regional cultures... among these traditions, which often contradict one another, which one counts as “tradition”? What, after all, is tradition?"},{"t":"h","zh":"五.中国的传统","en":"V. China’s Tradition"},{"t":"h","zh":"1.对于“传统”这一词语的词源考据","en":"1. Etymological research on the word “chuantong” (tradition)"},{"t":"p","zh":"①传：本义： 古代篆文像人手持物相递，本义是递交、传送。引申为转授、延续。","en":"① Chuan 传: Original meaning: in ancient seal script the character resembles a person holding an object and passing it on; the original meaning is to hand over, to transmit. Extended to mean to pass on, to continue."},{"t":"p","zh":"核心： 强调一个在时间中纵向移动的动作过程，如“传承”、“传递”。","en":"Core: it emphasises a process of action moving vertically through time, as in “chuancheng” (inheritance) and “chuandi” (transmission)."},{"t":"p","zh":"②统：本义： 与丝线有关，指丝的头绪。找到了“统”，就能理清整束丝。引申为一脉相承的系统、纲领、根本。","en":"② Tong 统: Original meaning: related to silk thread, it refers to the leading end of silk. Once you find the “tong,” you can straighten out the whole skein. Extended to mean a system passed down in one line, a guiding principle, a root."},{"t":"p","zh":"核心： 强调一个在空间中横向统领的体系、一个正统的脉络，如“系统”、“血统”、“道统”。","en":"Core: it emphasises a system that governs horizontally in space, an orthodox lineage, as in “xitong” (system), “xuetong” (bloodline) and “daotong” (orthodox transmission of the Way)."},{"t":"p","zh":"③传统：二字连用，最早见于《后汉书》，其内涵是 “世代相传的、具有根本性的系统” 。它描述的不仅是“传”这个动作，更是“统”这个被传递的核心内容——一套正统的学说、技艺、法度或血脉。","en":"③ Chuantong 传统: the two characters used together first appear in the Book of the Later Han; its connotation is “a fundamental system handed down from generation to generation.” It describes not only the act of “chuan” but, even more, the core content “tong” that is transmitted—an orthodox body of doctrine, craft, law or bloodline."},{"t":"h","zh":"2.“传统”这一词语含义的转变（含AI生成内容）","en":"2. Changes in the meaning of the word “tradition” (includes AI-generated content)"},{"t":"p","zh":"第一阶段：19世纪以前的帝制时期，传统的重点在于“统”，“传”是不言自明的。“传统”是社会运作和知识体系的“默认状态”。“传统”被视为权威、智慧和合法性的来源，是必须遵循和延续的范式。","en":"Stage one: in the imperial period before the nineteenth century, the emphasis of tradition lay on “tong”; “chuan” went without saying. “Tradition” was the “default state” of social operation and the knowledge system. “Tradition” was regarded as the source of authority, wisdom and legitimacy, a paradigm that had to be followed and continued."},{"t":"p","zh":"那么，什么“统”该被“传”？","en":"So, which “tong” should be “chuan” (transmitted)?"},{"t":"p","zh":"①儒家道统论： 从韩愈到宋明理学家，构建了一个从尧、舜、禹、文、武、周公直至孔、孟的“道统”谱系。传承此“道统*”是士大夫的核心使命。","en":"① The Confucian theory of daotong: from Han Yu to the Song-Ming Neo-Confucians, a genealogy of the “daotong” was constructed running from Yao, Shun, Yu, King Wen, King Wu and the Duke of Zhou down to Confucius and Mencius. Transmitting this “daotong*” was the core mission of the shidafu."},{"t":"p","zh":"②皇统/血统： 皇位的继承，强调血脉的正统性。","en":"② Imperial lineage/bloodline: succession to the throne, emphasising the orthodoxy of the bloodline."},{"t":"p","zh":"③学统/艺统： 学术流派（如程朱理学、陆王心学）和手工技艺的衣钵传承。","en":"③ Scholarly lineage/artistic lineage: the handing down of the mantle in scholarly schools (such as the Cheng-Zhu school of principle and the Lu-Wang school of mind) and in handicraft skills."},{"t":"h","zh":"第二阶段：近代转型期（晚清民国）；“传统”的“问题化”","en":"Stage two: the modern transition (late Qing and Republic); the “problematisation” of “tradition”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在“三千年未有之大变局”的遭遇下，面对强大异质的西方文明，中国的“统”第一次出现了整体性危机，其内涵发生了巨变：","en":"Faced with “a great change unseen in three thousand years,” and confronted with a powerful and alien Western civilisation, China’s “tong” for the first time underwent a total crisis, and its connotation changed dramatically:"},{"t":"p","zh":"1.它从主体变成了客体：“传统”不再是不言自明的好东西，而是被审视、被批判的对象。","en":"1. It turned from subject into object: “tradition” was no longer a self-evidently good thing, but an object to be scrutinised and criticised."},{"t":"p","zh":"2.它成了需要被克服的障碍：知识分子们为迅速救亡图存将“传统”与“现代”对立，在“五四”新文化运动的旗帜下，“传统”（特别是儒家礼教）被等同于“落后”、“封建”、“迷信”，而“现代”（德先生、赛先生）被等同于“进步”、“光明”。“反传统”成为新的思潮“传统”的内涵在此刻发生了根本性的逆转，从褒义词变成了贬义词。","en":"2. It became an obstacle to be overcome: to save the nation from peril swiftly, intellectuals set “tradition” against “modernity.” Under the banner of the May Fourth New Culture Movement, “tradition” (especially Confucian ritual teaching) was equated with “backwardness,” “feudalism” and “superstition,” while “modernity” (Mr Democracy and Mr Science) was equated with “progress” and “light.” “Anti-traditionalism” became the new current of thought. The meaning of “tradition” underwent a fundamental reversal at this moment, turning from a commendatory word into a pejorative one."},{"t":"h","zh":"第三阶段：当代（1949年后至今）；“传统”的复杂回归与重构","en":"Stage three: the contemporary period (from 1949 to the present); the complex return and reconstruction of “tradition”"},{"t":"p","zh":"1.毛泽东时代“传统”继续被视为“封建残余”，是革命需要扫除的对象，尤其在“破四旧”等运动中达到顶峰。","en":"1. In the Mao Zedong era, “tradition” continued to be regarded as “feudal remnants,” an object the revolution needed to sweep away, reaching its peak in campaigns such as “Destroy the Four Olds.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"2.改革开放以来：","en":"2. Since Reform and Opening-up:"},{"t":"p","zh":"①战略制定：随着经济发展，传统被作为“文化资源”。它不再被武断地视为负面，而是被重新定义为“中华民族的优秀文化遗产”，是文化认同和软实力的重要资源。","en":"① Strategic formulation: with economic development, tradition was treated as a “cultural resource.” It was no longer arbitrarily regarded as negative, but redefined as “the excellent cultural heritage of the Chinese nation,” an important resource for cultural identity and soft power."},{"t":"p","zh":"②选择性的复兴：社交媒体兴起的“国学热”、汉服热、传统节日复兴等。但此时的“传统”是被筛选过的，例如，更强调其审美、伦理（如孝道）、身心健康（如太极拳、中医）等方面，而选择性地屏蔽掉其政治性方面。","en":"② Selective revival: the “National Studies craze,” the Hanfu craze and the revival of traditional festivals that arose with social media. But the “tradition” of this moment has been filtered: for example, it emphasises aesthetics, ethics (such as filial piety) and physical and mental health (such as taijiquan and Chinese medicine), while selectively screening out its political aspects."},{"t":"p","zh":"③消费主义的“传统”：“传统”也被商品化，成为旅游、影视、文创产品的卖点。","en":"③ Consumerist “tradition”: “tradition” has also been commodified, becoming a selling point for tourism, film and television, and cultural-creative products."},{"t":"p","zh":"结语：我们总是在发明传统。对于当下的我们来说，“传统”取决于我们眼光和需求。传统从来不是一个和谐统一的整体，它内部本身有着各种制衡、互补。我们的近代之前，“统”的内涵构建就是一个不断被争夺、被定义的意义场域。 而到了近代以后，西方文明的冲击、以及现代社会的生存方式、各个民族国家之间的紧密联系与博弈、互联网时代的文化同质化...这些让“传统”处境变得更为挤压。按照我的个人经验与观察，还要专门去把传统拎出来梳理、重新注入到我们的生活中，核心问题就是身份认同焦虑、以及民族自信与创新的融合这两个问题我们绕不过去、也不可能等待其自然进化。","en":"Concluding remarks: we are always inventing tradition. For us today, “tradition” depends on our vision and our needs. Tradition has never been a harmonious, unified whole; internally it contains all kinds of checks and complementarities. Before our modern era, the construction of the meaning of “tong” was a field of meaning continually contested and defined. After the modern era began, the impact of Western civilisation, the way of life of modern society, the close ties and rivalries among nation-states, the cultural homogenisation of the internet age... all these have squeezed the situation of “tradition” further. In my personal experience and observation, the reason we still have to single out tradition deliberately, sort it out and inject it back into our lives is that the core problems—the anxiety of identity, and the fusion of national confidence with innovation—are two problems we cannot get around, nor can we wait for them to evolve naturally."},{"t":"p","zh":"写到此，我的观念有了转变：j我们今天的任务，不是去寻找一个“纯粹”的传统，而是认清其复杂源流后，带着主体性，万分斟酌与急切地参与这场意义的建构与传递。","en":"Having written this far, my view has changed: our task today is not to look for a “pure” tradition, but, having recognised its complex sources and currents, to take part with subjectivity, with the utmost deliberation and urgency, in this construction and transmission of meaning."},{"t":"h","zh":"*关于“道统”：（含AI生成内容）","en":"*On the “daotong”: (includes AI-generated content)"},{"t":"h","zh":"一.溯源","en":"I. Origins"},{"t":"p","zh":"由孟子最先提出从尧、舜、禹、汤、文王、孔子到自己的传承线索，并自认是孔子正统的继承者。再到韩愈在《原道》中，面对佛教强大的“法统”传承体系，明确构建了儒家的道统谱系：“尧、舜、禹、汤、文、武、周公、孔、孟。” 他明确指出孟子之后道统中断，而自己的使命就是接续道统，排斥佛老。到宋明理学深化，朱熹将韩愈的道统说进一步神圣化、精细化。他将“十六字心传”： “人心惟危，道心惟微，惟精惟一，允执厥中”定为道统的核心，并将程颢、程颐（和他自己）接续到孟子之后，确立了 “孔—孟—程—朱” 的理学道统谱系。通过编纂《四书章句集注》，使之成为科举标准，这套道统观从此成为中国后期帝制时代的官方正统思想。","en":"Mencius was the first to propose a line of transmission from Yao, Shun, Yu, Tang, King Wen and Confucius down to himself, and regarded himself as Confucius’s orthodox successor. Then Han Yu, in “On the Origin of the Way” (Yuan Dao), facing Buddhism’s powerful system of “dharma lineage” transmission, explicitly constructed the Confucian genealogy of the daotong: “Yao, Shun, Yu, Tang, Wen, Wu, the Duke of Zhou, Confucius, Mencius.” He stated explicitly that the daotong was broken after Mencius and that his own mission was to continue it and reject Buddhism and Daoism. With the deepening of Song-Ming Neo-Confucianism, Zhu Xi further sanctified and refined Han Yu’s theory of the daotong. He made the “sixteen-character transmission of the mind”—“The human mind is precarious, the mind of the Way is subtle; be discerning and single-minded, and hold fast to the mean”—the core of the daotong, and joined Cheng Hao and Cheng Yi (and himself) after Mencius, establishing the Neo-Confucian genealogy of the daotong as “Confucius—Mencius—the Chengs—Zhu.” Through compiling the Collected Commentaries on the Four Books, which became the standard for the imperial examinations, this view of the daotong became from then on the official orthodox thought of China’s late imperial era."},{"t":"h","zh":"二.内涵","en":"II. Connotations"},{"t":"p","zh":"强调三个方面：1.对内：讲个人內圣修身。2.对外即治国平天下之道，倡导仁政王道。3.文化和价值的正统，这也是我们华夏文明和“蛮夷”的区分之道","en":"It emphasises three aspects: 1. inwardly: the individual’s inner sageliness and self-cultivation. 2. outwardly: the way of governing the state and bringing peace to all under heaven, advocating benevolent government and the kingly way. 3. the orthodoxy of culture and values, which is also how our Huaxia civilisation distinguished itself from the “barbarians”"},{"t":"h","zh":"三.与治统的核心矛盾","en":"III. The Core Contradiction with the Zhitong"},{"t":"p","zh":"治统： 指现实的政治权力传承谱系，即“皇统”。","en":"Zhitong 治统 (the line of rule): refers to the genealogy of the transmission of real political power, that is, the “imperial line.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"道统： 指超越现实的道德与真理谱系。","en":"Daotong 道统: refers to the genealogy of morality and truth that transcends reality."},{"t":"p","zh":"理想状态下，道统与治统合一，即“圣君贤相”，君主既是权力掌握者，也是道德楷模（如尧舜禹）。二而更常见的现实是治道相互分离，士大夫（道统持有者）与皇权（治统持有者）形成一种微妙的制衡：","en":"Ideally, the daotong and the zhitong are united, that is, “a sage ruler and worthy ministers,” with the ruler being both the holder of power and a moral exemplar (like Yao, Shun and Yu). But the more common reality was that rule and the Way were separated from each other, and the shidafu (holders of the daotong) and imperial power (holder of the zhitong) formed a subtle balance:"},{"t":"p","zh":"士大夫用“道统”来批判、规训甚至否定不理想的“治统”。当皇帝昏庸时，士大夫可以依据“道统”进行谏诤，宣称自己代表的是更高的“道”。","en":"The shidafu used the “daotong” to criticise, discipline and even reject an unsatisfactory “zhitong.” When the emperor was benighted, the shidafu could remonstrate on the basis of the “daotong,” declaring that they represented a higher “Dao.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"皇帝也深知“道统”的重要性，因此通过推崇孔子、举办祭孔大典、将理学定为官学等方式，试图将“道统”纳入“治统”的管辖之下，成为统治的工具。","en":"Emperors, too, knew well the importance of the “daotong,” and therefore, by venerating Confucius, holding grand ceremonies of sacrifice to Confucius, making Neo-Confucianism the official learning and so on, tried to bring the “daotong” under the jurisdiction of the “zhitong” as a tool of rule."},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"zh":"时代","en":"Era","span":1},{"zh":"关系状态","en":"State of the relationship","span":1},{"zh":"制衡基础","en":"Basis of the balance","span":1},{"zh":"皇权策略","en":"Imperial strategy","span":1},{"zh":"士大夫策略","en":"Shidafu strategy","span":1},{"zh":"最终结果","en":"Final outcome","span":1}],[{"zh":"宋代","en":"Song dynasty","span":1},{"zh":"共治","en":"Co-governance","span":1},{"zh":"制度保障与共识","en":"Institutional guarantees and consensus","span":1},{"zh":"尊重、协商、纳谏","en":"Respect, consultation, accepting remonstrance","span":1},{"zh":"积极参与治理、制度内谏诤","en":"Active participation in governance, remonstrance within the system","span":1},{"zh":"相对稳定，文治昌盛","en":"Relatively stable, civil governance flourished","span":1}],[{"zh":"明代","en":"Ming dynasty","span":1},{"zh":"对抗","en":"Confrontation","span":1},{"zh":"道统气节与群体抗争","en":"Integrity grounded in the daotong and collective resistance","span":1},{"zh":"暴力镇压、权术分化","en":"Violent suppression, divide-and-rule manipulation","span":1},{"zh":"以死谏捍卫礼法、集体抗议","en":"Defending ritual law through remonstrance unto death, collective protest","span":1},{"zh":"激烈冲突，消耗巨大","en":"Fierce conflict, enormous costs","span":1}],[{"zh":"清代","en":"Qing dynasty","span":1},{"zh":"压制","en":"Suppression","span":1},{"zh":"皇权绝对优势下的有限规劝","en":"Limited admonition under the absolute superiority of imperial power","span":1},{"zh":"思想监控、恐怖威慑、收编","en":"Thought surveillance, intimidation by terror, co-optation","span":1},{"zh":"个体道德劝谏、谨慎避祸","en":"Individual moral admonition, cautious avoidance of disaster","span":1},{"zh":"士大夫独立性丧失，制衡虚化","en":"Loss of shidafu independence, the balance rendered hollow","span":1}],[{"zh":"晚清","en":"Late Qing","span":1},{"zh":"崩溃","en":"Collapse","span":1},{"zh":"旧制度完全失效","en":"The old system entirely ineffective","span":1},{"zh":"内部倾轧、顽固守旧","en":"Internal strife, stubborn conservatism","span":1},{"zh":"激进改革或顽固守旧，严重分裂","en":"Radical reform or stubborn conservatism, severe division","span":1},{"zh":"体系瓦解，革命兴起","en":"Disintegration of the system, rise of revolution","span":1}]]},{"t":"p","zh":"总而言之，“道统”是古代士大夫阶层赖以保持独立性、批判现实政治、并维系文化认同的精神支柱和权力话语。","en":"In sum, the “daotong” was the spiritual pillar and discourse of power on which the ancient shidafu stratum relied to maintain its independence, criticise real politics and sustain cultural identity."},{"t":"h","zh":"四.近代以来的形态","en":"IV. Its Forms Since Modern Times"},{"t":"p","zh":"进入20世纪，随着帝制崩溃和儒家思想的官方地位瓦解，“道统”在制度上已彻底断裂。","en":"Entering the twentieth century, with the collapse of the imperial system and the disintegration of Confucianism’s official status, the “daotong” was completely severed institutionally."},{"t":"p","zh":"但其思维模式和深层影响犹在：","en":"But its mode of thinking and deep influence remain:"},{"t":"p","zh":"1.文化心理： 中国人潜意识中仍有一种对“正统”和“传承”的执着，以及知识分子（或文化精英）应承担“为往圣继绝学，为万世开太平”的使命感。","en":"1. Cultural psychology: in the Chinese unconscious there is still an attachment to “orthodoxy” and “transmission,” and a sense of mission that intellectuals (or cultural elites) should take on “continuing the lost learning of past sages and opening an age of peace for all generations.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"2.政治话语： 现代中国在建构合法性时，虽然语言是全新的（如马克思主义中国化），但其叙事结构有时会隐约呼应“道统”逻辑——即强调自身是一个伟大真理和正确道路的当代继承者与践行者。","en":"2. Political discourse: when modern China constructs legitimacy, although the language is entirely new (such as the Sinicisation of Marxism), its narrative structure sometimes faintly echoes the logic of the “daotong”—that is, it emphasises that it is the contemporary inheritor and practitioner of a great truth and a correct path."},{"t":"p","zh":"理解“道统”可以更好的带我们理解：权力与真理博弈、历史书写、文化认同塑造。","en":"Understanding the “daotong” can better help us understand the contest between power and truth, the writing of history, and the shaping of cultural identity."},{"t":"p","zh":"对于传统的梳理，我发现要从很多的方面去寻找答案，我决定开启新的系列，不然这个“士大夫的乌托邦”就太多了。我将专门开启“中国传统”这一系列，虽然不知道要写多久，但一个一个问题来写，我相信我会对这个问题有更深入、更少情绪化的见解。探索那个老生常谈的主题：“传”“统”、取其精华去其糟粕，创造性转化创新性发展。","en":"In sorting out tradition, I have found that answers must be sought from many directions, so I have decided to start a new series, or else this “Utopia of the Shidafu” would grow too large. I will start a dedicated series, “Chinese Tradition.” Although I do not know how long it will take, by writing about one question at a time I believe I will arrive at deeper and less emotional views on this problem, exploring that well-worn theme: “chuan” and “tong,” taking the essence and discarding the dross, creative transformation and innovative development."},{"t":"h","zh":"1.时间观念","en":"1. Conceptions of time"},{"t":"p","zh":"四大轴心文明对比","en":"Comparison of the four Axial civilisations"},{"t":"p","zh":"从女蜗补天---我们的创世、我们起源的世界观","en":"From Nüwa mending the sky—our creation, the worldview of our origins"},{"t":"p","zh":"到","en":"to"},{"t":"p","zh":"破四旧、文革带来的伤害","en":"the harm brought by Destroy the Four Olds and the Cultural Revolution"},{"t":"h","zh":"各时期学者们的尝试","en":"Attempts by scholars of various periods"},{"t":"p","zh":"民国时期、","en":"The Republican period,"},{"t":"p","zh":"毛泽东时代、","en":"the Mao Zedong era,"},{"t":"p","zh":"改革开放后、","en":"after Reform and Opening-up,"},{"t":"p","zh":"全球化时代","en":"the age of globalisation"},{"t":"h","zh":"金观涛","en":"Jin Guantao"},{"t":"p","zh":"现代的起源","en":"The origins of the modern"},{"t":"p","zh":"现代的特征（金观涛《轴心文明与现代社会》p246）","en":"Features of the modern (Jin Guantao, Axial Civilisations and Modern Society, p. 246)"},{"t":"p","zh":"1.市场可无限扩张（相比于传统社会市场嵌入其中、现代市场甚至可以形成独立的市场社会）","en":"1. The market can expand without limit (compared with traditional society, in which the market is embedded; the modern market can even form an independent market society)"},{"t":"p","zh":"2.科学技术革命和市场机制一起引发生产力超增长。","en":"2. The scientific and technological revolution, together with the market mechanism, triggers super-growth of productive forces."},{"t":"p","zh":"3.民族国家成为人类社会的基本形态。","en":"3. The nation-state becomes the basic form of human society."},{"t":"p","zh":"中国现代的转型","en":"China’s modern transformation"},{"t":"p","zh":"宋明理学","en":"Song-Ming Neo-Confucianism"},{"t":"h","zh":"陈来","en":"Chen Lai"},{"t":"p","zh":"论李泽厚","en":"On Li Zehou"},{"t":"p","zh":"论冯友兰","en":"On Feng Youlan"},{"t":"p","zh":"论《中庸》","en":"On the Doctrine of the Mean (Zhongyong)"},{"t":"p","zh":"个人主义与集体主义","en":"Individualism and collectivism"},{"t":"p","zh":"情绪：对上级的强烈恐惧（封建时期的潜意识残留）","en":"Emotion: intense fear of superiors (an unconscious residue of the feudal period)"}]},{"id":"W-2025-03","n":13,"title":{"zh":"一只小牛虻","en":"A Little Gadfly"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2025-11-21","genre":"评论","summary":{"zh":"本篇旨在对回溯艺术承载社会批判性的历史，就“艺术家”这个词语，发表个人观点。","en":"This piece sets out to look back on the history of art as a bearer of social critique, and to offer my personal view on the word “artist.”"},"words":1828,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"本篇旨在对回溯艺术承载社会批判性的历史，就“艺术家”这个词语，发表个人观点。","en":"This piece sets out to look back on the history of art as a bearer of social critique, and to offer my personal view on the word “artist.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"尽管在漫不经心的重复和爆炸的信息中，一个词语的定义和它的历史内涵会被拆解或颠倒。但如果关照自身、反思自身存在的锚点，那么就要自己去赋予这些词语重量。","en":"In careless repetition and the explosion of information, the definition of a word and its historical meaning can be taken apart or turned upside down. But if we attend to ourselves and reflect on the anchor of our own existence, then we have to give these words weight ourselves."},{"t":"p","zh":"汉娜阿伦特认为：“哲学家和艺术家是现代社会荒漠中绿洲的守护者。”以期在主流价值之外，保留一片进行深度、无功利思考的空间，以对抗“极权主义”、“大众”等现代生活的“荒漠”。这种对抗所保留的绿洲，为被异化的人提供逃逸的路线和可能。","en":"Hannah Arendt held that “philosophers and artists are the guardians of the oases in the desert of modern society.” The hope is to preserve, outside mainstream values, a space for deep, disinterested thinking, in order to resist the “deserts” of modern life such as “totalitarianism” and “the masses.” The oases preserved by this resistance offer alienated people lines and possibilities of escape."},{"t":"p","zh":"那么这种对主流的反思、对“牛虻”之存在的批判态度从何沿袭而来？艺术又是何时开始承担起这种牛虻的身份？","en":"So where does this reflection on the mainstream, this critical attitude of the “gadfly,” come down to us from? And when did art begin to take on this identity of the gadfly?"},{"t":"p","zh":"这首先从遥远的古希腊开始谈起。","en":"This has to begin with distant ancient Greece."},{"t":"p","zh":"用“牛虻”作比喻最早出自苏格拉底，记录在柏拉图所著的《苏格拉底申辩篇》中。公元前399年，苏格拉底因“不敬神”和“腐蚀青年”的罪名受审。在法庭上，他为自己进行了著名的申辩。苏格拉底将自己比作雅典城邦这匹“高大、高贵但因肥大而懒惰迟钝的骏马”身上的一只牛虻。他说，他的职责就是不断地叮咬、刺激、批评雅典城和其公民，迫使他们对真理、正义和美德进行自我反省，从麻木和自满中惊醒，从而保持活力与健康。“批判者作为牛虻”这一角色的哲学原型，在苏格拉底处确立。","en":"The metaphor of the “gadfly” first comes from Socrates, as recorded in Plato’s Apology of Socrates. In 399 BC Socrates was tried on charges of “impiety” and “corrupting the youth.” In court he made his famous defence. Socrates compared himself to a gadfly on the city of Athens, a “great and noble horse, but sluggish and slow on account of its size.” His duty, he said, was to keep biting, stinging and criticising the city and its citizens, forcing them to examine themselves with regard to truth, justice and virtue, to wake from numbness and complacency, and so to stay vigorous and healthy. The philosophical prototype of the role of “the critic as gadfly” was established in Socrates."},{"t":"p","zh":"经历了启蒙运动到了近代，19c，现实主义的文学、艺术大规模地、自觉地将视角投向社会的“阴暗面”、主流文化的“边缘者”，并明确承担起社会记录与批判者的角色。艺术作为“社会牛虻”的形象由此变得清晰可见。而到了20c，有了法兰克福学派等现代理论的加持，使得艺术的批判性更被推到我们眼前，众多艺术家们也视其为核心信条。","en":"After the Enlightenment, in the modern era of the nineteenth century, realist literature and art turned their gaze, on a large scale and deliberately, to the “dark side” of society and to the “marginal people” of mainstream culture, and explicitly took on the role of recorder and critic of society. The image of art as a “social gadfly” thus became clearly visible. By the twentieth century, backed by modern theory such as the Frankfurt School, the critical nature of art was pushed even further before our eyes, and many artists took it as a core creed."},{"t":"p","zh":"从黑格尔到丹托的艺术终结论再到今天，“艺术”一词的内涵和范畴不停地在转变，而如果艺术家和哲学家作为现代生活的牛虻，他们的存在方式与其说是牛虻，倒不如说是接种的疫苗。先产生一点抗体、而后我们融入一体。","en":"From Hegel to Danto’s theses on the end of art and on to today, the meaning and scope of the word “art” have kept changing. And if artists and philosophers are the gadflies of modern life, their mode of existence is less that of a gadfly than that of a vaccine: first a few antibodies are produced, and then we merge into one."},{"t":"p","zh":"从牛虻到疫苗，什么变了？","en":"From gadfly to vaccine—what has changed?"},{"t":"p","zh":"不同艺术形式的生态不能以偏概全，下面我就以我自己更熟悉一点的绘画为代表的体系来讨论。","en":"The ecologies of different art forms cannot all be judged by one part, so below I will discuss the system represented by painting, which I know a little better."},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术生态与经济系统紧密相连。","en":"The ecology of art is closely tied to the economic system."},{"t":"p","zh":"我们强大的系统高速运转，我们的权力高度集中，我们不再反对批判者、不再无视试图创造新的价值者，而是收编他们、消费他们。激进的、批判性的艺术、文学，被博物馆收藏、被富豪买下、在艺博会展出、获得顶级奖项.....它的尖锐刺刀就变成了证明这个系统“包容、开放、自由”的装饰品。系统通过展示它的“批判”与“创新”来证明自己的“健康”、掩盖自己的腐朽，同时借用宣传使其成为消费的噱头。","en":"Our powerful system runs at high speed, and our power is highly concentrated; we no longer oppose critics or ignore those who try to create new values—instead we absorb them and consume them. Radical, critical art and literature are collected by museums, bought by the rich, shown at art fairs, given top prizes….. and their sharp bayonet becomes an ornament proving that the system is “tolerant, open and free.” The system proves its “health” and covers up its decay by displaying its “critique” and “innovation,” while using publicity to turn them into a selling point for consumption."},{"t":"p","zh":"以至于消费的逻辑代替、吞噬了批判的逻辑，批判成为一种为彰显独特性的猎奇。","en":"So much so that the logic of consumption replaces and swallows the logic of critique, and critique becomes a hunt for novelty in order to flaunt uniqueness."},{"t":"p","zh":"同时，它伪造了一个绿洲，就好像是带上了VR眼镜，我们就看到了少数艺术家“为艺术而艺术”地活着的幻觉，给人一种“自由仍在”的幻觉。像城市中心保留的那片精心打理的自然公园，它是现代化的一种点缀和补充，让人们暂时喘口气，然后更好地投入下一轮异化劳动。这些艺术品就是那片公园。而VR眼镜却不是视网膜。","en":"At the same time, it fakes an oasis. It is as if we had put on VR goggles and saw the illusion of a few artists living “art for art’s sake,” an illusion that “freedom still exists.” Like the carefully tended nature park kept in the city centre, it is an ornament and a supplement to modernisation, letting people catch their breath for a moment so that they can throw themselves better into the next round of alienated labour. These artworks are that park. And VR goggles are not retinas."},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术的批判性、如何建设性的介入到社会生活中？这是我时常纠结的的，这也是对于“艺术无用”的无奈与不甘。可现实就是，对于“异化”，人们适得其所。这使得谈及“异化”这两个字都很堂吉诃德。要么就是用这个词语来自我标榜。","en":"How can art’s critical nature intervene constructively in social life? This is something I often agonise over, and it is also my helplessness and unwillingness to accept that “art is useless.” But the reality is that, as for “alienation,” people are quite at home in it. This makes even mentioning the word “alienation” seem quixotic—or else the word is used for self-promotion."},{"t":"p","zh":"总之，异化似乎已经过时，说出这两个字仿佛只是在嘴里嚼着过去残烛的蜡汁。","en":"In short, alienation seems to be out of date; saying the word feels like chewing the wax drippings of a candle from the past."},{"t":"p","zh":"比较焦灼的时候脑子里总浮现一句话：“什么是真的？”","en":"When I am most anxious, one question always comes to mind: “What is real?”"},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术学院生产出艺术品生产者，艺术品进入到资本中作为金融衍生品。这是一个庞大的经济生态，有着巨大的现金流。因此不断地有人参与其中。艺术品的艺术水平可以被悬置起来，重要的是，要有这样的一个承载物来承接一些人的投资、一些人的社交、一些人的生存。","en":"Art academies produce producers of artworks, and artworks enter capital as financial derivatives. This is a huge economic ecology with enormous cash flow, so people keep joining it. The artistic quality of the artworks can be set aside; what matters is that there be such a vehicle to take in some people’s investments, some people’s socialising, some people’s livelihoods."},{"t":"p","zh":"人们的阶层、人性的虚荣、这些是真的。","en":"People’s social classes, human vanity—these are real."},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术家的欲望、独特的视角、这些也是真的。","en":"Artists’ desires, their unique perspectives—these are real too."},{"t":"p","zh":"尽管在这个巨大的车轮中，我们还是要时刻提醒一下自己这些无奈的事实。不过总要乐观的看问题，那么或许有新的时代产生，我们可以找到一个更实体的绿洲。但如果我们一直要必须这样生存、生活，那么至少可以为后来保存火种。","en":"Even inside this huge wheel, we still have to keep reminding ourselves of these helpless facts. But one should always look at things optimistically, and so perhaps a new era will come and we can find a more solid oasis. And if we must go on surviving and living like this, then at least we can keep the fire alive for those who come after."},{"t":"p","zh":"用那个经典的话题来做结尾：“to be or not to be”。","en":"Let me end with that classic question: “To be or not to be.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"选择不去选not to be，意味着在存在性虚无后，你主动选择的那个to be。包含着你的立场、你要做的具体的事情。那么、你是否会想让世界变得更好？哪怕只有一点点。 但不是说批判就是让世界变得更好，不批判就不是。我们不能、也没有必要作“革命性”的态度，因为我们都从系统中获益太多。但一定可以有一些小的推动、改进，与系统或许有一点点的殊途，但却同归。","en":"Choosing not to choose “not to be” means the “to be” you actively choose after existential nothingness. It contains your position and the concrete things you will do. So, would you want to make the world better? Even just a little. But this is not to say that critique makes the world better and the absence of critique does not. We cannot, and need not, take a “revolutionary” attitude, because we have all benefited too much from the system. But there can certainly be some small pushes and improvements—perhaps by a slightly different road from the system, yet arriving at the same place."}]},{"id":"W-2025-04","n":11,"title":{"zh":"见山仍是山","en":"Seeing the Mountain Still as a Mountain"},"subtitle":{"zh":"赵无极的中西融合三变","en":"Zao Wou-Ki’s Three Transformations in Fusing China and the West"},"date":"2025-11-26","genre":"评论","summary":{"zh":"赵无极就是这样的一位艺术家。可以谈的太多，这篇文章我想就仅从中西文化融合的视角来谈赵无极。","en":"Zao Wou-Ki is just such an artist. There is too much one could talk about; in this essay I want to discuss Zao Wou-Ki only from the perspective of the fusion of Chinese and Western cultures."},"words":1386,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"关于中国传统与西方绘画的融合，一代又一代的画家做出了很多的尝试，留下很多经典，文化宝藏。一个大师级的艺术家他的作品之经典，可以从不同的角度切入，不同的语境来赏析，无论时间地域变换，总是有新的东西被挖掘出，令人启发与感动。赵无极就是这样的一位艺术家。可以谈的太多，这篇文章我想就仅从中西文化融合的视角来谈赵无极。","en":"Generation after generation of painters have made many attempts at fusing Chinese tradition with Western painting, leaving behind many classics and cultural treasures. The classic quality of a master artist’s work can be approached from different angles and appreciated in different contexts; no matter how time and place change, something new is always unearthed that inspires and moves us. Zao Wou-Ki is just such an artist. There is too much one could talk about; in this essay I want to discuss Zao Wou-Ki only from the perspective of the fusion of Chinese and Western cultures."},{"t":"p","zh":"按照时间顺序来看赵无极的作品，第一时期，20c40—60年代，在这时他对甲骨文有着浓烈的兴趣，受到米罗.胡安的启发。他收藏了一些中国古代青铜器，也有很多研究甲骨文的书籍。这个时期对于中西结合，中国传统文化的引入，更多是古代人物造型的图像式的、符号式的直接引入。这一时期整个画面的背景结合着油画的（笔触、糅合、过度等）在画的周围做了重色的处理：是更黑、更暗的一圈。呈现出一种“天地初开、混沌一片,黄土云雾中透着光”的大气蓬勃的氛围，仿佛是一个梦境，是历史的回忆，是遥远的观看。近看时，才注意到的微观的国画造型的树、人、马车、庭院…同时期还可以看到“马蒂斯式”的中国田园生活图景等等。在部分佛教一铺造像中，菩萨静静的坐在最上方，下面是一层叠一层的天兵、神将，肃穆镇定。这类造像大小大概是人的两三。向上仰去，给人遥不可及、只可远观的感叹。这一时期晚期的画，就是给观者这种感觉的：黑黑的无色凡尘之中光束透过云雾，那片白、那束光在视觉上离我们很遥远、神圣。画面同时带给我们视觉震撼和宗教震慑感。这一时期的画，可谓是巧妙地中西握手：各种因素的提取、拼接融合。","en":"Looking at Zao Wou-Ki’s work in chronological order, the first period runs from the 1940s to the 1960s. At this time he had an intense interest in oracle-bone script and was inspired by Joan Miró. He collected some ancient Chinese bronzes and owned many books on the study of oracle-bone script. In this period, the fusion of China and the West—the bringing-in of traditional Chinese culture—was mostly a direct, pictorial, symbolic borrowing of the forms of ancient figures. The background of the whole picture, combined with the means of oil painting (brushwork, blending, transitions and so on), was given a dark treatment around the edges of the canvas: a blacker, darker ring. It presents a grand and vigorous atmosphere of “heaven and earth newly parted, all in chaos, light shining through yellow earth and cloud and mist,” as if it were a dream, a memory of history, a gazing from far away. Only on looking closely does one notice the tiny trees, figures, carriages and courtyards drawn in the forms of Chinese painting… In the same period one can also see “Matisse-like” scenes of Chinese pastoral life, and so on. In some Buddhist sculptural ensembles, the bodhisattva sits quietly at the very top, and below are layer upon layer of heavenly soldiers and divine generals, solemn and composed. Such statues are roughly two or three times human size. Looking up at them, one sighs at something out of reach, to be admired only from afar. The late paintings of this period give the viewer exactly this feeling: in the black, colourless mortal dust a beam of light pierces the clouds and mist, and that patch of white, that beam of light, seems visually very far from us, and sacred. The painting gives us at once a visual shock and a sense of religious awe. The paintings of this period can be called a clever handshake between China and the West: the extraction, splicing and fusion of all kinds of elements."},{"t":"p","zh":"第二个时期，70-90年代。这一时期，画面在色彩上饱和度拉高处理，与前一时期的较为直接不同，这一时期对于中国传统因素的引入更为隐晦，虽无却有。赵无极十分看重推崇书法和宋代山水。这一时期间，赵无极接受了水墨画和书法的训练。多是采用熟宣，是水与墨的泼溅、相互沁染还有拓印等等，他做了很多水墨实验。在画面意境气息上与唐宋山水更为贴近，用笔和墨迹分配上令人看到徐渭和八大对他的影响。水墨葡萄、晶莹剔透、飞水豪放。在水墨之后的油画，更多时候，四周的暗圈消失了。四周的暗圈不仅是氛围上的影响，在观感上也是有距离的。而这一时期取之的是水墨画训练后的大面留白的作画方式，与此同时，观看感受的距离被拉进。如果五六十年代的画是历史的回看，那么这一时期的画便是作者自己的回忆、他在向观者讲述一个故事，深海的神话、漫天的金沙。这一时期他似乎回归了自己，他的情感、他的感慨、无尽冥思…比起历史的沉重，这一时期更为轻快。","en":"The second period runs from the 1970s to the 1990s. In this period the saturation of colour in the paintings was pushed higher. Unlike the relatively direct approach of the previous period, the bringing-in of traditional Chinese elements became more veiled—absent, yet present. Zao Wou-Ki greatly valued and admired calligraphy and Song-dynasty landscape painting. During this period he received training in ink painting and calligraphy. He mostly used sized xuan paper, with water and ink splashed, seeping and bleeding into each other, as well as rubbing and printing; he carried out many ink experiments. In mood and breath the pictures come closer to Tang and Song landscapes, and in the brushwork and the distribution of ink one can see the influence of Xu Wei and Bada Shanren on him. Ink grapes, crystal-clear and translucent; flying water, bold and unrestrained. In the oil paintings that followed the ink work, the dark ring around the edges mostly disappeared. That dark ring had not only been an effect of atmosphere; it also created distance in the viewing experience. What took its place in this period was a way of painting with large areas of blank space, learned through training in ink painting, and at the same time the distance of the viewing experience was drawn closer. If the paintings of the 1950s and 60s were a look back at history, then the paintings of this period are the artist’s own memories: he is telling the viewer a story—myths of the deep sea, gold sand filling the sky. In this period he seems to have returned to himself: his emotions, his sighs, his endless meditation… Compared with the weight of history, this period is lighter and brisker."},{"t":"p","zh":"第三个时期也是最后一个时期，20c90年代一直到赵无极先生过世。这一时期的画面，色彩饱和度都无比的高，鲜亮似乎甚至画面在发着荧光。比起一束光打在一幅画上那种舞台式的观看，这种极高色彩自身发光，更像是一种窥视、一种自身向外的展示、勾引。这鲜艳明亮的厚重材料中，水墨式的细的、有骨的、不刻意的笔画却总带人进入中国的传统、精神、意境、幻境。而那难以传达出的气韵、气、流动…也被自然地含在画中。这不禁令人想到石涛的“一画”。","en":"The third and final period runs from the 1990s until Mr Zao Wou-Ki’s death. In the paintings of this period the colour saturation is extraordinarily high, so bright that the canvas seems even to fluoresce. Compared with the stage-like viewing of a beam of light falling on a painting, this extremely saturated colour that gives off its own light is more like a kind of peeping, a display from the self outward, a seduction. Within these vivid, bright, heavy materials, the fine, bony, unforced ink-like strokes always lead one into Chinese tradition, spirit, mood and realms of illusion. And that qiyun (spirit resonance), that qi, that flow, so hard to convey… are also naturally contained in the paintings. One cannot help thinking of Shitao’s “one stroke” (yihua)."},{"t":"p","zh":"这早已不仅是中西融合的尝试，而是另一种高度，自发地流露。他的画是深沉的、似神话一样的，震慑着观者。绘画在最初承担着巫术神话的功能，它是语言、逻辑形成之前、人类直接、本能的与世界的联系。而赵无极先生的艺术探索道路，在数万年后、现代文明的今天，带我们凝练的走过了：见山是山，见山不是山，再见还是山、无所谓是山否。","en":"This has long ceased to be merely an attempt at fusing China and the West; it is another height, a spontaneous outpouring. His paintings are deep and myth-like, and they awe the viewer. Painting originally carried the function of magic and myth; before language and logic took shape, it was humanity’s direct, instinctive connection with the world. And Mr Zao Wou-Ki’s path of artistic exploration, tens of thousands of years later, in today’s modern civilization, has led us in condensed form through this: seeing the mountain as a mountain, seeing the mountain as not a mountain, seeing it again as still a mountain—and no longer caring whether it is a mountain or not."}]},{"id":"W-2025-05","n":12,"title":{"zh":"从“膝不能弯”到“丽水巴比松”","en":"From “Knees That Cannot Bend” to “Lishui Barbizon”"},"subtitle":{"zh":"未曾改变的文化焦虑","en":"A Cultural Anxiety That Has Never Changed"},"date":"2025-11-26","genre":"评论","summary":{"zh":"其实，今天我们在文化领域里津津乐道的那种“丽水巴比松”类型的称谓，在底层逻辑上，与那句“膝不能弯”何其相似。","en":"In fact, the “Lishui Barbizon” kind of label that we so relish in today’s cultural world is, in its underlying logic, strikingly similar to that old saying about “knees that cannot bend.”"},"words":1508,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"想想看，我们生活中这种对话太常见了。","en":"Think about it: this kind of conversation is all too common in our lives."},{"t":"p","zh":"“欸，你知道吗，丽水有艺术驻留项目，有个‘丽水巴比松’呢。”","en":"“Hey, did you know? Lishui has an artist residency programme—there’s a ‘Lishui Barbizon’.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"“是吗？听着挺像那么回事儿啊。”","en":"“Really? Sounds pretty impressive.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在这段闲聊里，“巴比松”三个字像一个勋章，别在了“丽水”的胸前。说话的人可能带着一丝自豪，但这份自豪里，总让人觉得有点不是滋味。仿佛“丽水”自己不够分量，必须借一个远在法国的名字，才能获得谈论的价值。","en":"In this bit of small talk, the word “Barbizon” is like a medal pinned on the chest of “Lishui.” The speaker may feel a touch of pride, but there is something in that pride that leaves a bad taste. It is as if “Lishui” on its own did not carry enough weight and had to borrow a name from faraway France before it became worth talking about."},{"t":"p","zh":"“丽水巴比松”——这一类型的称谓，让我想起一些更为久远的事。","en":"“Lishui Barbizon”—this kind of label reminds me of something from much longer ago."},{"t":"p","zh":"鸦片战争初期，清军和民众在面对英军完全陌生的坚船利炮时，在巨大的震撼与挫败之余，民间还有着这样的一种说法：这些金发碧眼的洋人“膝不能弯”，一旦倒下便难以起身。","en":"In the early days of the Opium War, when Qing soldiers and ordinary people faced the British forces’ completely unfamiliar “strong ships and powerful guns,” amid the enormous shock and defeat a saying went around among the common people: these blond, blue-eyed foreigners had “knees that cannot bend,” and once they fell down they could hardly get up again."},{"t":"p","zh":"这当然是无稽之谈，但它作为一种心理现象却无比真实：我们通过将无法理解的“强者”贬低为在身体结构上存在“缺陷”的怪异存在，以此来缓解那份面对绝对劣势而产生的、令人窒息的焦虑。其实，今天我们在文化领域里津津乐道的那种“丽水巴比松”类型的称谓，在底层逻辑上，与那句“膝不能弯”何其相似。","en":"This was nonsense, of course, but as a psychological phenomenon it was entirely real: by belittling the incomprehensible “strong” as strange beings with “defects” in their bodily structure, we eased the suffocating anxiety of facing absolute inferiority. In fact, the “Lishui Barbizon” kind of label that we so relish in today’s cultural world is, in its underlying logic, strikingly similar to that saying about “knees that cannot bend.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"我们如此热衷于为自己土地上生长出的文化现象，冠以一个西方艺术的“姓氏”。这看似是一种推崇——你看，我们也有了自己的“巴比松”。但深究下去，这种命名的背后，何尝不也是一种隐秘的自我贬低？我们不相信“丽水”二字本身能具备独立的艺术分量，必须借由“巴比松”这个光环，才能为其“正名”，才能让它进入一个可以被谈论、被理解的序列。这背后，是一种根深蒂固的文化自卑，一种自我嫌弃的愤怒。这种愤怒，本质上源于对“强者”的无力感。然而，“强”本身并不是一种错误，于是，这种无处安放的愤怒，便只能调转枪口，化为对我们自身、对我们自己人的苛责与贬低。在茶余饭后的闲聊、gossip 中，这种心态表现得最为赤裸。我们推崇西方的文化艺术明星，在重复的语言中保持自己低人一等的姿态。我们贬低自己土壤中产生出的明星。一是因为从内容上讲，属实是略逊一筹；二是因为处于文化自卑，一种自我嫌弃的愤怒。","en":"We are so keen to give the cultural phenomena that grow from our own soil the “surname” of Western art. It looks like a form of esteem—look, we have our own “Barbizon” too. But dig a little deeper, and isn’t there, behind this naming, a hidden self-belittlement as well? We do not believe that the word “Lishui” can carry independent artistic weight on its own; it has to borrow the halo of “Barbizon” to be “legitimized,” to enter a ranking in which it can be talked about and understood. Behind this lies a deep-rooted cultural inferiority, an anger of self-loathing. This anger comes, in essence, from a sense of powerlessness before the “strong.” Yet being “strong” is not itself a wrong, and so this anger, with nowhere to go, can only turn its guns around and become harsh criticism and belittlement of ourselves and of our own people. In after-dinner chat and gossip this mentality shows itself most nakedly. We exalt the stars of Western culture and art, and in repeated language we keep up our posture of being inferior. We belittle the stars who come out of our own soil—first, because in terms of content they really are a notch below; and second, because of cultural inferiority, an anger of self-loathing."},{"t":"p","zh":"然而，这种攻击自己人的行为，并不会因为我们“先知先觉”般的贬低，就掩盖掉我们在那个幻想中的“主流文化”面前的“他者”身份。它更像是一种精神上的自我边缘化。我们骂得越凶，越是证明我们内心认同了那套来自远方的评判标准。我们无法通过这种方式融入那个向往的世界，更无法借此获得一丝一毫的尊严。真正的尊严，来自于创造。而创造的前提，是放下这种自满与自卑交织的拧巴心态，回归到一种最为朴素的“畏惧之心”——承认自己的局限，认识到文明与艺术的海洋之浩瀚，从而保持一种谦逊和一无所知的态度，去持续地学习与反思。唯有如此，我们才能从徒劳的情绪发泄，转向扎实的价值创造。自满只会令人沉浸于自娱自乐的迷宫，而自卑的愤怒，则会将迷宫的墙壁越砌越高。","en":"But attacking our own people does not, by our belittling them as if we had seen it all coming, cover up our status as “the other” before that imagined “mainstream culture.” It is more like a spiritual self-marginalization. The harder we scold, the more we prove that deep down we have accepted that set of standards of judgment from far away. We cannot join the world we long for in this way, still less win the slightest bit of dignity from it. True dignity comes from creation. And the precondition for creation is to let go of this twisted mentality in which complacency and inferiority are knotted together, and to return to the plainest “heart of awe”—admitting our own limits, recognizing how vast the ocean of civilization and art is, and so keeping an attitude of humility, of knowing nothing, in order to go on learning and reflecting. Only in this way can we turn from futile venting of emotion to the solid creation of value. Complacency only sinks people into a maze of self-entertainment, while the anger of inferiority builds the walls of that maze ever higher."},{"t":"p","zh":"回过头看，文化焦虑的形态在变，但其内核依旧。我们每一个人，无论身处哪个行业、哪个阶层、哪个地区，都在以不同的形式参与着这场宏大的、关于文化自信的构建。我们的生命是紧紧联系在一起的，大众的言行往往在不自觉地重复着某种被设定的模式。因此，对大众的引领，便成了一项复杂而不可逃避的责任，这责任落在每一个有意识的个体肩上，尤其是那些掌握着话语权的人。","en":"Looking back, the forms of cultural anxiety have changed, but its core remains the same. Every one of us, whatever our industry, class or region, is taking part in different ways in this vast construction of cultural confidence. Our lives are tightly bound together, and the words and actions of the public often unconsciously repeat some pre-set pattern. Guiding the public therefore becomes a complex and inescapable responsibility, one that falls on the shoulders of every conscious individual, and above all of those who hold the power of discourse."},{"t":"p","zh":"当因一点小小的成就而得意地沾沾自喜时，要警惕掉入个人主义的陷阱中。","en":"When we grow smug and pleased with ourselves over some small achievement, we must beware of falling into the trap of individualism."},{"t":"p","zh":"当对现状不满而愤世嫉俗，想要放弃一切努力时，也要意识到，我们脚下还有很远的、需要共同去铺设的道路。","en":"When we become cynical out of dissatisfaction with the way things are and want to give up all effort, we must also realize that there is still a long road beneath our feet that we need to pave together."},{"t":"p","zh":"当感到不满想要抱怨时，更要提醒自己，这从来不是一个个人的、孤立的问题，而是我们所有人共同面对的时代课题。","en":"When we feel dissatisfied and want to complain, we should remind ourselves all the more that this has never been a personal, isolated problem, but a question of our time that all of us face together."},{"t":"p","zh":"一切的称谓与标签都是暂时的，唯有那真诚的、无需借名的谦虚、奋斗，才是我们尊严与希望 沉默而坚实的根基。我们的历史与传统、在今天，亟待被重新解读、重新挖掘，我们的文化自信的道路，最终是要通向那里。","en":"All names and labels are temporary; only sincere humility and striving that need no borrowed name are the silent and solid foundation of our dignity and hope. Our history and tradition urgently need, today, to be reinterpreted and rediscovered; the road of our cultural confidence must in the end lead there."}]},{"id":"W-2025-06","n":17,"title":{"zh":"塞巴斯蒂安萨尔加多Sebastião Salgado带给我的思考","en":"What Sebastião Salgado Has Made Me Think About"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2025-11-30","genre":"评论","summary":{"zh":"本篇的内容是关于 对“艺术表达、展示、传播苦难。”的探讨。","en":"This piece is a discussion of “art expressing, displaying and disseminating suffering.”"},"words":2563,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"本篇的内容是关于 对“艺术表达、展示、传播苦难。”的探讨。","en":"This piece is a discussion of “art expressing, displaying and disseminating suffering.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在最初筹备毕业论文时，塞巴斯蒂安萨尔加多也是我想写的艺术家之一","en":"When I first began preparing my graduation thesis, Sebastião Salgado was one of the artists I wanted to write about."},{"t":"p","zh":"大概两三年前，我第一次观看了由文德斯执导的关于塞巴斯蒂安的纪录片《地球之盐》。之后，又重复观看了很多次。纪录片很多条线，主线是萨尔加多摄影作品的几个重要的系列：塞拉佩拉达金矿、移民、劳动者、创世纪。副线有他的人生轨迹、社会实践。文德斯在纪录片中说，他最初看到萨尔加多的摄影作品时，被其中传达出的【艺术家对人类的爱】深深的感动。","en":"About two or three years ago, I watched for the first time The Salt of the Earth, the documentary about Sebastião directed by Wim Wenders. Afterwards I watched it again many times. The documentary has many threads. The main thread is several important series of Salgado’s photographs: the Serra Pelada gold mine, Migrations, Workers, Genesis. The secondary threads are the course of his life and his social practice. In the documentary Wenders says that when he first saw Salgado’s photographs, he was deeply moved by what they conveyed: [the artist’s love for humanity]."},{"t":"img","src":"e17-01.jpeg"},{"t":"p","zh":"我也被这位艺术家的作品深深打动，选择了几张他所摄制的人物形象画了下来。大概是十七八岁的时候，有一段时间很想做战地记者。而这部纪录片、这位艺术家的作品又重新燃起了曾经的那个热情：我希望我可以把战争、非洲挨饿的孩子们、瘦骨嶙峋的死亡....这些给运用绘画、摄影或者文字记录下来、传播出去。那时，使我产生这个想法的，可能更多的是无知和同情心。两三年前重燃这个想法时，有着更复杂的考虑，并且我也有着在作为一个绘画者带着一种“拟定创作主题”的态度。当时就已经意识到苦难美学化所带来的伦理问题，总之这个想法还是搁置了。现在的话，这个问题在我这里的状态可能还是pending。","en":"I too was deeply moved by this artist’s work, and I chose several of the figures he photographed and painted them. When I was about seventeen or eighteen, there was a period when I very much wanted to be a war correspondent. This documentary and this artist’s work rekindled that old passion: I hoped I could record war, starving children in Africa, emaciated death... through painting, photography or writing, and spread them out into the world. Back then, what gave me the idea was probably more ignorance and sympathy than anything else. When the idea was rekindled two or three years ago, my considerations were more complicated, and as a painter I also had the attitude of “settling on a creative theme.” I was already aware at the time of the ethical problems that come with aestheticizing suffering, and in the end I set the idea aside. As of now, the status of this question for me is probably still pending."},{"t":"p","zh":"“艺术表达、展示、传递 苦难”这件事情，确实本身是比较双刃的：","en":"“Art expressing, displaying and conveying suffering” is, in itself, really something of a double-edged sword:"},{"t":"p","zh":"一方面，这种（带着爱的视角与情感的）传播以及苦难本身，会带给观者很多心里的涟漪，我们会因同情、因为看到，而去对这件事情有多一些的关注与行动，也会带给我们观者自己个人很多反思。","en":"On the one hand, this kind of dissemination (with a loving perspective and feeling) and the suffering itself send many ripples through the viewer’s heart. Out of sympathy, and because we have seen it, we pay more attention to the matter and take more action, and it also prompts a great deal of personal reflection in us as viewers."},{"t":"p","zh":"而另一方面，当我们去在这个场所展示苦难时，是一种被过滤、被“艺术化”了的“苦难”，当我们对这个物件倾注情感的同时，对苦难本身大多数情况下是会忽略的-大多人只会作一种“良心安慰”式的自我感动。而苦难本身所带来的情感幅度也会转变成消费逻辑的标价。","en":"On the other hand, when we display suffering in such a venue, it is a filtered, “art-ified” “suffering.” While we pour our emotions into this object, in most cases we overlook the suffering itself — most people only feel a kind of self-congratulatory emotion that “soothes the conscience.” And the emotional range that suffering itself carries is also converted into a price tag in the logic of consumption."},{"t":"p","zh":"在流媒体上看到【一场在南法关于韩国画家姜明姬画展的开幕午餐会】的参与者所录制的，举办者法国的前总理德维尔潘的一段祝酒词，他表达了这样的一个观点：“在这样一个（他指的他们所在的场地，见图片）美丽的地方，人们是不会去想到苦难、战争的，美与和谐就是我们的解药。”先不管这段发言背后的偷换概念、何不食肉糜，还有他讲得有道理的可取之处。","en":"On a streaming platform I saw a recording, made by a participant in [an opening luncheon in the South of France for an exhibition by the Korean painter Kang Myung-hee], of a toast given by the host, former French Prime Minister Dominique de Villepin. He expressed this view: “In such a beautiful place (he meant the venue they were in; see the picture), people do not think of suffering or war; beauty and harmony are our antidote.” Leaving aside, for now, the sleight of hand and the “let them eat cake” obliviousness behind this remark, as well as the points where he does have a reasonable argument —"},{"t":"img","src":"e17-02.jpeg"},{"t":"p","zh":"就仅仅这个观点而论，结合塞巴斯蒂安萨尔加多的艺术作品。我想知道，与文学不同，一个视觉艺术，比如绘画，它的属性，都包含什么？","en":"Taking just this view on its own, together with Sebastião Salgado’s artworks, I want to know: unlike literature, what do the properties of a visual art, such as painting, include?"},{"t":"p","zh":"可能会有：1.绘画这件事情的历史、它的叙事性、它关注的主题、它的平面性...这些之后“绘画的组合的视觉可能性”2.它的观看者和接收者，作为多数资源掌握者，那么作为艺术家，一个艺术表达、传播者，要向这些接收者传达什么内容？这也是在本文提到的姜明姬和塞巴斯蒂安萨尔加多所代表的其中的两个不同的方向","en":"They might include: 1. the history of painting as a practice, its narrativity, the themes it attends to, its flatness... and, beyond these, “the visual possibilities of painting’s combinations”; 2. its viewers and recipients — who, for the most part, are the holders of resources. So, as an artist, a person who expresses and disseminates through art, what content should one convey to these recipients? These are also two of the different directions represented by Kang Myung-hee and Sebastião Salgado, both mentioned in this essay."},{"t":"h","zh":"先把艺术家和艺术品分离出来谈艺术家","en":"First, separating the artist from the artwork, to talk about the artist"},{"t":"p","zh":"作为艺术品，它可以作为一种砝码放在一个有社会功能的“人”身上，为这个人的行动和影响力增力。","en":"An artwork, as an artwork, can be placed like a weight on the scale of a “person” who has a social function, adding force to that person’s actions and influence."},{"t":"p","zh":"苦难、美与和谐，首先表达的内容，是这个艺术品所带给观者的，而作为艺术家，艺术家的属性，其实是他的作品的属性是交织但分离的。艺术家、或者说作为群体中的人，首先要意识到自己在社会结构的位置，为谁发言、立场是什么。这个立场的范围比较广，也有民族国家层面的立场、有文化立场、由代表的群体/阶级的立场、等等，这个是艺术家作为人，她/他的必然在其中的政治属性，不过这也不仅仅是艺术家，但凡是个人，都有政治属性，而作为上层建筑的构建参与者、维护者、传播者，在作为“个人”时也要意识到这一点。而作为文化工作者，假设这个工作者要解决的问题是“文化自信问题”，那么在作为某个文化中带着文化身份的人时，她/他就得带着这些意识和立场。比如，一个印度的艺术家要在法国举办展览，那么在哪里办展、说什么语言、发言讲什么话、将给谁听....这些都是要精心构建的；假设德维尔潘画廊要为他举办展览，那么，他在和画廊主交流时，就不简简单单的是两个个体之间的语言博弈了，比如德维尔潘之前在姜明姬个展的午餐会上还说道：“姜明姬从济州岛出生，是有着很多的努力和运气才能到南法那里举办展览”。客观事实讲当然没错，这位艺术家在艺术生涯中付出了很多努力，但介于他们二者一个是欧洲白人男性外交政治家、另一个是亚洲的黄人女艺术家，那么在这个场所、说这句话，就不仅仅是对一个身作为一个画廊主在艺术家的开幕餐会上的简单的发言。这其中先入为主的高姿态，还有隐含着对后者文化和国力的蔑视。这种发言太过常见，以至于绝大部分时候我们发言者和言论接收者都习以为常，可就是这种惯性，支配我们一直生活在这种“上下结构的氛围”中。","en":"Suffering, beauty and harmony — the content expressed comes first from what the artwork gives the viewer; whereas the properties of the artist, as an artist, and the properties of his work are in fact intertwined yet separate. An artist, or rather a person within a group, must first be aware of their position in the social structure: on whose behalf they speak, and what their standpoint is. The scope of this standpoint is fairly broad: there are standpoints at the level of the nation-state, cultural standpoints, the standpoints of the groups or classes one represents, and so on. This is the political dimension the artist, as a person, necessarily has. But this is not only true of artists — anyone who is a person has a political dimension, and those who help build, maintain and disseminate the superstructure must also be aware of it when acting as “individuals.” As a cultural worker — supposing the problem this worker wants to address is the “problem of cultural confidence” — when acting as a person carrying a cultural identity within a given culture, she or he must carry this awareness and this standpoint. For example, if an Indian artist is to hold an exhibition in France, then where to exhibit, what language to speak, what to say in a speech, whom it will be addressed to... all of this must be carefully constructed. Suppose the Villepin gallery were to hold an exhibition for him: then, when he communicates with the gallery owner, it is not simply a verbal game between two individuals. For instance, at the luncheon for Kang Myung-hee’s solo exhibition, de Villepin also said: “Kang Myung-hee was born on Jeju Island; it took a great deal of effort and luck for her to be able to come to the South of France to hold an exhibition.” As objective fact this is of course true — the artist has put a great deal of effort into her artistic career. But given that one of them is a white European male diplomat-politician and the other a yellow-skinned Asian woman artist, saying this sentence in this setting is not merely a simple remark by someone who, as a gallery owner, is speaking at an artist’s opening luncheon. It carries a presumptuous air of superiority, as well as an implicit contempt for the latter’s culture and national strength. Remarks like this are so common that most of the time both we who speak and we who receive the words take them for granted — yet it is precisely this inertia that keeps us living in this “atmosphere of hierarchical structure.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"一切都在被记录、传播的这种生活方式，在人与人交流互动的线上领域，我认为我们还是不能完全自由放任，还是要有一定的意识和引导，身份问题的构建。慢慢地把那种上下结构的、“分层”的氛围给一点一点平衡过来。所以那位印度艺术家，任重道远。他倒是不用发表海阔天空的大言论，把自己的雄才大略都发表出来，但在具体的人与人交往的权力微型博弈中、在生活的被记录的表演中，都要谨慎、放下个人，拾起背后的身份。可能有点夸张了，但意思就是这么个意思。","en":"In this way of life where everything is being recorded and disseminated, in the online sphere where people communicate and interact, I think we still cannot be entirely laissez-faire; there must still be a certain awareness and guidance, a construction around questions of identity — slowly, bit by bit, bringing that hierarchical, “stratified” atmosphere back into balance. So that Indian artist has a heavy burden and a long road ahead. He doesn’t need to make sweeping grand pronouncements and lay out all his great ambitions, but in the concrete micro-games of power in person-to-person dealings, and in the recorded performance of life, he must be careful, set aside the individual self, and take up the identity behind him. Perhaps this is a bit exaggerated, but that is the gist of it."},{"t":"p","zh":"就如我在一只小牛虻里说的，相比艺术品本身，它所承接的人与人的社会关系更为重要。因此艺术家也不能因市场运用的“个人崇拜”的叙事就沉浸其中，顺着单一的逻辑维护“个人品牌”。","en":"As I said in “A Little Gadfly,” compared with the artwork itself, the social relations between people that it carries are more important. Therefore artists also must not immerse themselves in the “personality cult” narrative the market makes use of, maintaining a “personal brand” by following a single logic."},{"t":"p","zh":"做艺术家做艺术，不直接等同于艺术家做一个艺术品；艺术家的位置有点特殊，而里面包含的东西也还挺多的。","en":"Being an artist and making art is not directly the same as an artist making an artwork; the artist’s position is somewhat special, and it contains quite a lot."},{"t":"p","zh":"现在定下了毕业论文的主题，我没有在继续进行塞巴斯蒂安萨尔加多的这个主题了。","en":"Now that the topic of my graduation thesis has been decided, I am no longer pursuing this topic of Sebastião Salgado."},{"t":"p","zh":"如果写可以怎么写？塞巴斯蒂安是纪实摄影的大师，在法国、一个来自巴西的经济学博士摄影师。他的视角，这个可以延申到殖民话题、经济学可能带来的那种全球的、结构性的观察方式...他的作品，可以用图像学分析、他拍摄的角度和姿态，里面的政治、社会元素，摄影风格...","en":"If I were to write it, how could it be written? Sebastião is a master of documentary photography — a photographer in France, from Brazil, with a doctorate in economics. His perspective: this could extend to colonial topics, and to the global, structural way of observing that economics might bring... His works could be analyzed iconologically: the angles and postures of his shots, the political and social elements in them, his photographic style..."},{"t":"p","zh":"还有一些主题性的话题：苦难艺术化和消解政治性，这两者之间天然就有矛盾，我们应该如何处理？是偏向其中一方？还是规避其中一方？这两者可否达到一种共处的平衡？还是说必须要围绕着一个特定的目的*来做取舍？","en":"There are also some thematic topics: the aestheticization of suffering and the dissolving of the political — there is an inherent contradiction between the two. How should we handle it? Lean toward one side? Or avoid one side? Can the two reach a balance of coexistence? Or must the trade-off be made around a specific purpose*?"},{"t":"p","zh":"*：如果把“摄影”-“传播”看作时间性的过程，那么图像必然要承担政治责任。我觉得这也是塞巴斯蒂安的作品令人们感动的原因之一：它不仅是一个被观看的对象，这个对象也呈现了一种持平的权力结构和指向的政治态度及行动号召。","en":"*: If “photography” – “dissemination” is seen as a temporal process, then the image must bear political responsibility. I think this is also one of the reasons Sebastião’s work moves people: it is not only an object to be looked at; this object also presents a level, balanced power structure, and points to a political attitude and a call to action."},{"t":"img","src":"e17-03.jpeg"}]},{"id":"W-2025-07","n":3,"title":{"zh":"名言皇帝","en":"The Emperor of Quotations"},"subtitle":{"zh":"犬儒主义的金盾牌","en":"The Golden Shield of Cynicism"},"date":"2025-12-28","genre":"评论","summary":{"zh":"在公共领域中，在社交媒体的加持下，“名人的话语”总是被从语境中截出来、片段地引用，然后被赋予一种真理地位，而“名人的标签”本身使这句话“合法”、使其免于被讨论。","en":"In the public sphere, amplified by social media, “the words of famous people” are constantly cut out of their context, quoted in fragments and then granted the status of truth, while the “famous person” label itself makes the sentence “legitimate” and exempts it from discussion."},"words":2419,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"在公共领域中，在社交媒体的加持下，“名人的话语”总是被从语境中截出来、片段地引用，然后被赋予一种真理地位，而“名人的标签”本身使这句话“合法”、使其免于被讨论。","en":"In the public sphere, amplified by social media, “the words of famous people” are constantly cut out of their context, quoted in fragments and then granted the status of truth, while the “famous person” label itself makes the sentence “legitimate” and exempts it from discussion."},{"t":"p","zh":"这是在生活世界里普遍的现象，我们生活在其中，这是我们的惯习。这类现象存在且盛行，本篇文章便是对这样一种现象的反思与分析。","en":"This is a common phenomenon in the lifeworld; we live within it, and it is our habitus. Phenomena of this kind exist and are widespread, and this essay is a reflection on and an analysis of one such phenomenon."},{"t":"p","zh":"首先我们先将这种讨论的范围限定在“中文世界”，这种现象是基于什么逻辑和历史原因？在英文世界中又是基于什么？其他语境又是怎样的？","en":"First, let us limit the scope of the discussion to the “Chinese-speaking world”: on what logic and what historical causes is this phenomenon based? And in the English-speaking world, on what is it based? What about other contexts?"},{"t":"p","zh":"先从一个来源于公共语境中的例子入手，对其作出批评分析溯源。","en":"Let us begin with an example taken from the public context, and offer a critical analysis of it and trace its origins."},{"t":"img","src":"e03-01.jpeg"},{"t":"p","zh":"如果先搁置这个句子的作者和出处，仅将其视为一个普通命题、一个被广泛传播的命令式句子。先来说明现象：","en":"Suppose we first set aside the author and source of this sentence and treat it simply as an ordinary proposition, a widely circulated imperative sentence. First, the phenomenon:"},{"t":"p","zh":"这句话：“只有源自内在呼唤的行动才是善的，其他行动均无价值。”","en":"The sentence: “Only action that springs from an inner calling is good; all other action is worthless.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"这是一个给定的解释框架，本应引发大量问题，比如：","en":"This is a given interpretive framework, which ought to raise a great many questions, for example:"},{"t":"p","zh":"“人”指的是“个人”还是“群体”？如果是群体、这个群体的范围是如何？什么是“内心的声音”？如何划定外力驱使？等待觉醒是否会导致责任悬置？“善”在这里的含义是什么？必要的行为是对谁而言？是否存在必须回应外在他者的情境？“其他的一切”又是在什么范畴里？......","en":"Does “a person” mean “an individual” or “a group”? If a group, how wide is that group? What is “the inner voice”? How do we draw the line at being driven by external forces? Does waiting to awaken lead to responsibility being suspended? What does “good” mean here? Necessary actions—necessary for whom? Are there not situations in which one must respond to an external other? And within what scope is “everything else”?……"},{"t":"p","zh":"然而，在这种视觉—情绪包装中，这句话不再是一个需要承担后果的思想、它也不需要被怀疑、讨论。它被改造成了：一种为当下心理状态提供合法性的装置。","en":"Yet in this visual-emotional packaging, the sentence is no longer a thought whose consequences must be borne; it does not need to be doubted or discussed. It has been turned into a device that supplies legitimacy to a present state of mind."},{"t":"p","zh":"被“名人”标签所过滤后的言论被用来证明读者理应“安于其位”。犬儒主义的金盾牌现身了：合法性的紧张被抹平，不行动、不回应、不承担，是“正确的”、“伟大的”决定。","en":"Filtered through the “famous person” label, the statement is used to prove that the reader ought to “stay content in their place.” The golden shield of cynicism appears: the tension over legitimacy is smoothed away, and not acting, not responding, not taking responsibility become the “right,” even “great,” decision."},{"t":"p","zh":"这是在公共语境中的流通机制，那么这其中反映了什么问题？","en":"This is the mechanism by which it circulates in the public context. So what problems does it reflect?"},{"t":"p","zh":"首先，为什么这类现象大量在社交媒体出现？——也就是说为什么它存在被接收的大量群体？——它的话语机制的畅通流行一定是和群体的需求、意识形态等有所呼应、重叠的，那么它是和什么重叠的？","en":"First, why do such phenomena appear in such numbers on social media? That is to say, why is there such a large audience to receive them? The smooth and popular circulation of this discursive mechanism must echo and overlap with the needs, ideologies and so on of a group. So what does it overlap with?"},{"t":"p","zh":"其次，这种现象在别的语言的语境中形态是怎样的？处于怎样的结构中？连接的集体意识指向哪里？","en":"Second, what form does this phenomenon take in the contexts of other languages? Within what structure does it sit? Where does the collective consciousness it connects to point?"},{"t":"h","zh":"一.名言皇帝","en":"1. The Emperor of Quotations"},{"t":"p","zh":"这种机制在中国可以成立，依赖三层文化/历史条件：","en":"That this mechanism can hold in China depends on three layers of cultural and historical conditions:"},{"t":"h","zh":"1.经学传统","en":"1. The Classicist Tradition"},{"t":"p","zh":"在中国的语境里，“话语”不是被讨论的，而是被继承的；“断章取义”在经学结构里是在预设正当性的前提下进行再解释的，这是一种被沿袭下来的“常态操作”——经学的训练核心是：证明经典永远是对的、把现实解释为“符合经典”。","en":"In the Chinese context, “discourse” is not something to be discussed but something to be inherited; “quoting out of context” (duanzhang quyi) is, within the structure of classical studies (jingxue), a reinterpretation carried out on the premise that legitimacy is presupposed. It is a “normal operation” that has been handed down—the core of training in classical studies is to prove that the classics are always right and to interpret reality as “conforming to the classics.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在惯常的思维里，经典不是假设，而是前提。也就是说“质疑”天然的在这种思维的回路之外。而当进入了回路也就进入了“这句话已经是对的了”的前提。","en":"In habitual thinking, the classics are not hypotheses but premises. That is, “questioning” lies naturally outside the circuit of this way of thinking. And once one enters the circuit, one has also entered the premise that “this sentence is already right.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"总之，话语的真理性并不通过论证展开，而是依附于被承认的“位置”。","en":"In short, the truth of discourse does not unfold through argument; it attaches to an acknowledged “position.”"},{"t":"h","zh":"2.政治结构","en":"2. Political Structure"},{"t":"p","zh":"在皇权社会中，权威是人格化的，抽象的原则是由人格承载。","en":"In imperial society, authority was personified, and abstract principles were borne by persons."},{"t":"p","zh":"法不是法，法是皇帝。道不是道，道是圣人。判断不是逻辑，“判断”是解释权威的工具。","en":"Law is not law; law is the emperor. The Way is not the Way; the Way is the sage. Judgment is not logic; “judgment” is a tool for interpreting authority."},{"t":"p","zh":"也就是说，真实的、在心里默认的话语重量及接受度及影响力是：","en":"That is to say, the real weight, acceptance and influence of discourse, as tacitly assumed in people’s minds, run:"},{"t":"p","zh":"“谁说”＞“说了什么”＞“为什么这么说”","en":"“Who says it” > “what is said” > “why it is said”"},{"t":"p","zh":"而这个“谁说”当中，本来是有一个前提的：这个“谁”，已经被预先承认为“不可被审问的主体”；“说的什么”本身就是被截取出的正确经典。这个正确的经典原本是来自于“为什么这么说”的判断结果。但当话语被重复的次数和时间久了，“话语”就变成了被共同承认的“图腾”。前面的步骤都被过滤掉了，只剩下了一个“常识”。","en":"And within this “who says it” there was originally a premise: this “who” has already been acknowledged in advance as “a subject that cannot be interrogated”; “what is said” is itself a correct classic extracted from a larger whole. This correct classic originally came from the result of a judgment about “why it is said.” But when a piece of discourse has been repeated often enough and for long enough, the “discourse” becomes a commonly acknowledged “totem.” All the earlier steps are filtered out, and only a piece of “common sense” remains."},{"t":"p","zh":"在政治中，已经形成的“图腾”使应当“思考”的东西被用来“表态、归队”，获得心理或道德安全。","en":"In politics, an established “totem” means that what ought to be “thought about” is used instead to “declare one’s position and fall in line,” gaining psychological or moral safety."},{"t":"p","zh":"PS：关于道统结构，我在《士大夫的乌托邦（四）》一文当中有详细说","en":"PS: I discuss the structure of the daotong (the orthodox transmission of the Way) in detail in my essay “The Utopia of the Scholar-Officials (IV)”"},{"t":"h","zh":"3.现代性断裂","en":"3. The Rupture of Modernity"},{"t":"p","zh":"这是老生常谈的问题：现代，我们逐步引入了西方思想、哲学、理论...","en":"This is a well-worn issue: in modern times we gradually brought in Western thought, philosophy, theory…"},{"t":"p","zh":"在本文所讨论的话题里，它是这样体现的：","en":"In the topic discussed in this essay, it shows itself like this:"},{"t":"p","zh":"名人的思想并非是放在西方的“可争论主体”架构里，而更多是放在了中国“主体不可被争论”的架构里。","en":"The thought of famous people has not been placed in the Western framework of “a subject open to dispute,” but far more often in the Chinese framework of “a subject that cannot be disputed.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"思想变成了“名言名集”、理论成了“护身符”。","en":"Thought has become “collections of famous sayings,” and theory has become an “amulet.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"于是，随处可见：","en":"And so, everywhere you look:"},{"t":"p","zh":"“马克思变成了马克思主义口号”、“尼采变成了金句尼采”、福柯 被剪成“权力无处不在”。","en":"“Marx has become Marxist slogans,” “Nietzsche has become Nietzsche the quotable one,” and Foucault has been clipped down to “power is everywhere.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"也就是说，这种西方的名人名言进入到这种话语机制当中，被放在一种“道统”的位置上，潜移默化地在人的心理结构中成了“新皇帝”。","en":"In other words, when these Western famous sayings enter this discursive mechanism, they are placed in a position of daotong, and imperceptibly become a “new emperor” in people’s psychological structure."},{"t":"p","zh":"不过，就“现象”这一层次而言，在英文世界中，“名言崇拜”同样广泛存在。但其根源并不主要来自权威政治，而来自另一种结构：个人经验的合法化。因此，我们引出下一部分：","en":"However, at the level of the “phenomenon,” the “cult of quotations” is just as widespread in the English-speaking world. But its roots lie mainly not in authoritarian politics but in another structure: the legitimation of personal experience. This leads us to the next part:"},{"t":"h","zh":"二.西方公共语境中的“名言化”：经验的神圣化","en":"2. “Quotationisation” in the Western Public Context: The Sanctification of Experience"},{"t":"p","zh":"在英文世界广泛存在的foundation，至少有下面三条：","en":"In the English-speaking world there are at least three widespread foundations:"},{"t":"h","zh":"1.新教传统","en":"1. The Protestant Tradition"},{"t":"p","zh":"在新教的伦理中，真理不再必须经由教会中介，而可以被个体直接“领受”。","en":"In Protestant ethics, truth no longer has to be mediated by the Church; it can be “received” directly by the individual."},{"t":"p","zh":"一句话之所以成立，不在于它是否得到了教会的权威证明，而在于它是否“击中我”。","en":"A sentence holds not because its authority has been certified by the Church, but because it “hits me.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"不是经验本身被神圣化，而是“不可被他者质疑的感受性”被神圣化。","en":"It is not experience itself that is sanctified, but a “sensibility that cannot be questioned by others.”"},{"t":"h","zh":"2.经验主义与反系统","en":"2. Empiricism and Anti-Systematic Thought"},{"t":"p","zh":"从洛克、休谟到尼采、维特根斯坦，哲学内部就存在对宏大体系的警惕，偏好格言、洞见、瞬间的澄明。","en":"From Locke and Hume to Nietzsche and Wittgenstein, there has been, within philosophy itself, a wariness of grand systems and a preference for aphorisms, insights, moments of sudden clarity."},{"t":"p","zh":"对柏拉图主义以来的“本质/理念/至高”的反抗及解构，有着很长时间的发展。","en":"Resistance to, and deconstruction of, the “essence/Idea/supreme” that has prevailed since Platonism has a long history of development."},{"t":"p","zh":"（但中国的情况还不太一样，中国的思想源头不是一个被架空了的形而上的“至高体”，而是万物相生、自行运行。所以不能完全照搬西方的机制，不能把他们的理论在本土语境里用作“反”权威。如此嫁接理论与方法论是错位的。这里先不详细讨论这一点，我将在《感兴与上帝之死》一文中展开）","en":"(But the situation in China is rather different. The source of Chinese thought is not a metaphysical “supreme being” suspended above everything, but the mutual generation of all things, running of their own accord. So the Western mechanism cannot be copied wholesale, and their theories cannot be used in the local context to be “anti”-authority. Grafting theory and methodology in this way is a misalignment. I will not discuss this point in detail here; I will develop it in my essay “Ganxing and the Death of God.”)"},{"t":"h","zh":"3.资本主义公共空间的运作逻辑","en":"3. The Operating Logic of Capitalist Public Space"},{"t":"p","zh":"商品化是出发点。（中国也是商品化的逻辑，但本土的“皇帝化”历史延续的思想机制是讨论的重点，所以我没有在上一部分涉及这一范畴。）","en":"Commodification is the starting point. (China also follows the logic of commodification, but the focus of the discussion is the mechanism of thought that continues from the local history of “emperorisation,” which is why I did not touch on this area in the previous part.)"},{"t":"p","zh":"意义需要被快速消费、被情绪识别、被转发。","en":"Meaning has to be consumed quickly, recognised emotionally, and shared."},{"t":"p","zh":"于是，一句话成为最小可流通的思想单位。","en":"And so a sentence becomes the smallest circulating unit of thought."},{"t":"p","zh":"因此，西方公共语境中的名言更接近于：“这句话对我是真的。”","en":"Thus quotations in the Western public context are closer to: “This sentence is true for me.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"它类似于一种共鸣机制，而非裁决机制。","en":"It is something like a mechanism of resonance, not a mechanism of adjudication."},{"t":"p","zh":"（在中国有一点的情况不同在于：哪怕是在看似“个人感受”的语境中，名言仍常暗中滑向一种准规范性判断。）","en":"(One way in which the situation in China differs is that, even in contexts that seem to be about “personal feeling,” quotations often still slide quietly toward a quasi-normative judgment.)"},{"t":"h","zh":"结尾：","en":"Conclusion:"},{"t":"p","zh":"这一随处可见的现象和传播机制，并不能单纯地归于“大众没读懂原著”，也不仅仅是误译或误读问题，而是思想被置入了一个不同的话语承载结构。","en":"This ubiquitous phenomenon and mechanism of transmission cannot simply be put down to “the public not having understood the original texts,” nor is it merely a matter of mistranslation or misreading; rather, thought has been placed into a different structure that carries discourse."},{"t":"p","zh":"而在中英两种语境中的“名言化”虽然并不相同，但它们都完成了一件相似的事情：将原本需要承担后果的判断，转化为无需回应他者的心理确定性。","en":"And although “quotationisation” differs between the Chinese and English contexts, both accomplish a similar thing: they turn judgments that ought to bear consequences into a psychological certainty that need not answer to others."}]},{"id":"W-2025-08","n":1,"title":{"zh":"一个青年人在继承传统文化时所遇到的问题","en":"Problems a Young Person Encounters in Inheriting Traditional Culture"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2025-12-30","genre":"论文","summary":{"zh":"从“修复断裂的传统”作为出发点，分析这其中所遇到的问题，最终落脚于对文化焦虑的分析。","en":"Taking “repairing a broken tradition” as its starting point, this essay analyses the problems encountered along the way and arrives finally at an analysis of cultural anxiety."},"words":6145,"blocks":[{"t":"label","zh":"摘要","en":"Abstract"},{"t":"p","zh":"从“修复断裂的传统”作为出发点，分析这其中所遇到的问题，最终落脚于对文化焦虑的分析。","en":"Taking “repairing a broken tradition” as its starting point, this essay analyses the problems encountered along the way and arrives finally at an analysis of cultural anxiety."},{"t":"p","zh":"文章主要由三个部分组成：1.快速现代化进程中，中国语境内部“主体性危机及代际差异、转移与积累”的梳理。2.对于当下青年一代，儒家结构中伦理位置的失效形态、“差序格局”中人情社会的成立条件的消解3.关于被延续和转嫁的文化焦虑及其引发的冲突。","en":"The essay consists mainly of three parts: 1. an account, within the Chinese context of rapid modernisation, of the “crisis of subjectivity and its generational differences, transfer and accumulation”; 2. for today’s young generation, the forms in which ethical positions within the Confucian structure have ceased to function, and the dissolution of the conditions under which the favour-based society of the “differential mode of association” (chaxu geju 差序格局) could exist; 3. cultural anxiety that has been prolonged and passed on, and the conflicts it provokes."},{"t":"p","zh":"经过对上述三点的讨论和梳理，试找到不同的主体性危机内在串联、传递的线索。心理问题或价值观问题的静止分析易由个体差异走向群体性对立。在分析时笔者尽量避免对某一现象或事件进行简单归类、定性，而是将一个个分析放入到一种敞开、流动的“现代化进程中行动—伦理—结构—话语多重机制错位”非封闭事件中“来回滑动”。","en":"Through discussing and sorting out these three points, the essay tries to find the threads by which different crises of subjectivity are internally linked and transmitted. Static analyses of psychological problems or problems of values easily slide from individual difference into group antagonism. In the analysis the author has tried to avoid simply classifying or labelling any one phenomenon or event, and instead places each analysis within an open, fluid, non-closed event—the “misalignment of multiple mechanisms of action, ethics, structure and discourse in the process of modernisation”—and lets it “slide back and forth.”"},{"t":"label","zh":"注：","en":"Notes:"},{"t":"p","zh":"本文中，比起具体的年龄段，青年划定的范围更贴近于结构中风险与意义断裂的前沿承载者。","en":"In this essay, rather than a specific age group, the scope of “youth” is closer to the front-line bearers of risk and of ruptures of meaning within the structure."},{"t":"p","zh":"本文不否认个体差异与反向案例，其关注的是经验背后的生成机制。","en":"This essay does not deny individual differences or counter-examples; its concern is the generative mechanisms behind experience."},{"t":"h","zh":"引言","en":"Introduction"},{"t":"p","zh":"意义塌陷常被指向“意义-虚无”的解释框架。","en":"The collapse of meaning is often referred to the explanatory framework of “meaning versus nihilism.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"意义、虚无主义，这些理念与讨论的初始，是从西方“反柏拉图主义”的思想脉络而来。现代社会起源于理性主义和基督教传统的西方轴心文明，在希伯来-希腊思想中，“前语言理解”在语言框架之外，两者分别以“理念”或“上帝”作为追问源头，意义是自动成立的。而关于原始直接的、混乱的“人与世界的关系”长期被放在讨论范围之外，到德国古典哲学时达到巅峰——从“物自体”到“绝对精神”。","en":"Meaning and nihilism: these ideas and the discussions around them originally come from the Western intellectual current of “anti-Platonism.” Modern society arose from the Western Axial civilisation of rationalism and the Christian tradition. In Hebrew-Greek thought, “pre-linguistic understanding” lies outside the framework of language; the two take the “Idea” or “God” respectively as the source of inquiry, and meaning holds automatically. The primordial, immediate and chaotic “relationship between person and world” was long kept outside the scope of discussion, reaching its peak in German classical philosophy—from the “thing-in-itself” to “Absolute Spirit.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在中国的思想长河中，“存在”在一开始并不是被回避的。终极意义没有被一个至高的“理念、上帝”提前架构，意义并非是先验，而是在行动中自行展开的、意义存在于君君臣臣父父子子之间相互交往的伦理道德中。现代性的问题对儒家思想脉络而言，事件发生的框架比起意义-虚无，更贴近于伦理-失序。在中国的历史、传统中，儒家的“成己—成人”、道家的“安身—顺化”、礼制的“行动—正当性”....它们之间有一个共同点：行动须被嵌入一个可讲述的人生秩序中。所以在中国的情况中，当行动失效时，若仅用西方的“意义缺失”作解释属于倒果为因。","en":"In the long river of Chinese thought, “being” was not avoided from the start. Ultimate meaning was not framed in advance by a supreme “Idea or God”; meaning was not a priori, but unfolded of itself in action, residing in the ethics and morality of mutual dealings in which the ruler is ruler, the minister minister, the father father and the son son. For the Confucian current of thought, the framework in which the problem of modernity occurs is closer to “ethics versus disorder” than to “meaning versus nihilism.” In Chinese history and tradition—the Confucian “perfecting oneself—perfecting others,” the Daoist “settling oneself—following transformation,” the ritual system’s “action—legitimacy”....—there is one thing in common: action must be embedded in a life order that can be narrated. So in the Chinese case, when action fails, explaining it solely by the Western “lack of meaning” mistakes effect for cause."},{"t":"p","zh":"近年来，对于年轻人“躺平”、“内卷”的讨论已从火热逐渐转向常态化。“中国的年轻人失去了意义感”是经常被指向的一个原因。而作为交织其中的因素：代际差异、不平等加剧、心理问题等也是高频率的讨论。","en":"In recent years, discussion of young people “lying flat” (tangping) and “involution” (neijuan) has gradually shifted from heated to routine. “China’s young people have lost a sense of meaning” is a frequently cited cause. Intertwined factors—generational difference, worsening inequality, psychological problems and so on—are also discussed with high frequency."},{"t":"h","zh":"一.行动和主体的断裂","en":"I. The Rupture Between Action and Subject"},{"t":"p","zh":"对于这一问题的讨论，通常包括但不限于以下几种：①归因于全球范围共有的人类所面临的现代性危机；②溯源至五四、改革开放...作“中-西、传统-现代”或“过去、当下”的二元对立从而指向身份认同危机；③互联网时代以来的新的社会结构、人与人之间相处方式的改变，由此所加深的身份与身体的分离.....","en":"Discussion of this issue typically includes, but is not limited to, the following: ① attributing it to the crisis of modernity faced by humanity worldwide; ② tracing it back to the May Fourth Movement, Reform and Opening-up..., setting up binary oppositions of “China–West, tradition–modernity” or “past–present” and thus pointing to a crisis of identity; ③ the new social structures since the internet era and changes in how people relate to one another, which have deepened the separation of identity and body....."},{"t":"h","zh":"1.现代性危机在中国的发生情况：","en":"1. How the crisis of modernity has occurred in China:"},{"t":"p","zh":"首先引用西方学者福柯的观点：“自20世纪60年代以来，主体性、身份认同和个体性构成了一个重大的政治问题”；因此，我们必须首先改变“我们的主体性，我们与自身的关系。”这种斗争不再是针对剥削或宏观经济结构，而是针对个人与自身结合的斗争。关于对现代性危机的分析，从马克斯韦伯到今天，这些对断裂的讨论在西方已经延续了相当长的时间，主体性的问题在西方，从传统社会“宗教”到现代“世俗伦理”、“职业精神”、“公民身份”的转变形态是层层递进的。","en":"Let me first cite the view of the Western scholar Foucault: “Since the 1960s, subjectivity, identity and individuality have constituted a major political problem”; therefore we must first change “our subjectivity, our relationship to ourselves.” This struggle is no longer directed against exploitation or macroeconomic structures, but is a struggle over the individual’s binding to the self. As for analyses of the crisis of modernity, from Max Weber to today these discussions of rupture have continued in the West for a considerable time; there, the problem of subjectivity has developed step by step, in the transformation from “religion” in traditional society to “secular ethics,” the “vocational ethos” and “citizenship” in modern society."},{"t":"p","zh":"而相比之下，在中国，自改革开放以来，传统社会结构的宗族、道德、伦理秩序并非“循序渐进地过渡到当今全球化的现代社会形态”，而是在战争后高度加速的政治—制度重构中被切断。费孝通先生基于血缘和地缘的熟人社会伦理提出的“差序格局”，在快速城市化中土崩瓦解。人们直接从被国家全面包裹的“单位、公社体制”，被抛入到讲究契约和利益的“全球化市场体制”中。这就解释了为什么当代中国在经历了经济奇迹的同时，常常伴随着道德焦虑、信任危机和伦理失范——因为我们跳过了建立现代公共精神和契约道德的“循序渐进”阶段。","en":"By contrast, in China, since Reform and Opening-up, the clan, moral and ethical order of the traditional social structure did not “transition gradually into today’s globalised form of modern society,” but was cut off amid the highly accelerated political and institutional reconstruction after the wars. The “differential mode of association” that Fei Xiaotong proposed on the basis of the acquaintance-society ethics of blood and locality crumbled in rapid urbanisation. People were thrown directly from the “work-unit and commune system,” in which the state enveloped them entirely, into a “globalised market system” governed by contract and interest. This explains why contemporary China’s economic miracle has often been accompanied by moral anxiety, crises of trust and ethical anomie—because we skipped the “gradual” stage of building a modern public spirit and contractual morality."},{"t":"p","zh":"这是放在宏观结构作讨论，那么对于微观的数个个体而言：个人与自身结合的斗争”又是怎样在中国的现实情况中发生的？","en":"This is a discussion at the level of macro-structure; what, then, of the many individuals at the micro level: how has “the struggle over the individual’s binding to the self” taken place in China’s actual circumstances?"},{"t":"h","zh":"2.主体性危机——改革开放以来的主体性分析：","en":"2. The crisis of subjectivity—an analysis of subjectivity since Reform and Opening-up:"},{"t":"h","zh":"1.第一阶段（约1980s–1990s）","en":"1. Stage one (c. 1980s–1990s)"},{"t":"p","zh":"由于改革开放，“个人”开始大量出现，但这时候“个人”仍然外在地指向生存、家庭、改善命运，“主体性”并未成为反思对象。也就是说，人在行动，但不需要回答“我是谁”，因为“我要活下去、我要改变命运”本身就是答案。这一时期，意义是高度外在的、目标明确。这一时期的社会结构使得“为自己负责”的主要承载人群较小，有：农民、工人、第一代城市流动人口、小个体经营者等。他们的辛苦并不紧密联系于“意义焦虑”。因为他们的行动和回报关系是相对清晰的，身份主要由角色而非自我认同构成。在这个意义上，主体性尚未被问题化为反思的对象。","en":"Because of Reform and Opening-up, the “individual” began to appear in large numbers, but at this point the “individual” still pointed outward, toward survival, family and changing one’s fate; “subjectivity” had not yet become an object of reflection. That is, people acted but did not need to answer “who am I,” because “I must survive, I must change my fate” was itself the answer. In this period meaning was highly external and goals were clear. The social structure of the time meant that the group mainly bearing the burden of “being responsible for oneself” was relatively small: peasants, workers, the first generation of urban migrants, small self-employed businesspeople and so on. Their hardship was not closely tied to “anxiety about meaning,” because the relation between their action and its reward was relatively clear, and identity was constituted mainly by role rather than by self-identification. In this sense, subjectivity had not yet been problematised as an object of reflection."},{"t":"h","zh":"2.第二阶段（约1995–2008）","en":"2. Stage two (c. 1995–2008)"},{"t":"p","zh":"这一时期，教育、就业、城市开始成为筛选主体的装置，使得“努力—回报”被制度化为可比较的路径。绩效化使得主体开始被要求对结果负责，这导致了一个关键变化：人不再只是“行动”，而开始被要求用结果证明自己是谁。意义仍然存在，但高度功利化。与此同时，一种思考方式与之同步：成功才能成为正当主体，而若失败则会被指向个体问题。","en":"In this period, education, employment and the city began to become devices for screening subjects, institutionalising “effort—reward” into comparable paths. Performance-orientation meant that subjects began to be required to answer for results, which led to a key change: people no longer merely “acted,” but began to be required to prove who they were through results. Meaning still existed, but was highly utilitarian. At the same time a way of thinking developed in step with this: only success makes one a legitimate subject, and failure is attributed to individual problems."},{"t":"p","zh":"这时候，主要承载人群开始扩大：主要有城镇青年、高校毕业生、技术工人、白领阶层等。主体性开始被内化，危机初露端倪。但由于仍有成功叙事和社会流动性流动作为缓冲，因此问题尚未爆发，因为未来仍然可以被想象为是“敞开的”。","en":"At this point the group bearing the burden began to expand, chiefly urban youth, university graduates, skilled workers, white-collar workers and so on. Subjectivity began to be internalised, and the crisis began to show itself. But because narratives of success and social mobility still served as a buffer, the problem had not yet erupted, for the future could still be imagined as “open.”"},{"t":"h","zh":"3.第三阶段（约2008–2018）","en":"3. Stage three (c. 2008–2018)"},{"t":"p","zh":"这一时期主体危机正式显化，由于上升路径开始变窄、成功标准高度单一，个体被要求为包括结构性失败的一切负责。此时，“压力变大”成为广泛的讨论话题，主体突然被完全内在化，但意义生成机制却没有同步完成。意义结构开始正式崩塌：行动仍被强烈要求，但行动不再指向明确未来。“你必须行动”与“行动的结果无明确指向”并存。意义的悬置作为原因开始主导经验。","en":"In this period the crisis of the subject became fully visible. As upward paths narrowed and the standard of success became highly uniform, individuals were required to answer for everything, including structural failure. At this point “growing pressure” became a widely discussed topic; the subject was suddenly wholly internalised, but the mechanism for generating meaning had not been completed in step. The structure of meaning formally began to collapse: action was still strongly demanded, but action no longer pointed toward a definite future. “You must act” coexisted with “the results of action point nowhere definite.” The suspension of meaning, as a cause, began to dominate experience."},{"t":"p","zh":"而承载不再只是“青年”，受影响人群开始显著扩大，比如：身份焦虑的中产阶层、位置冻结的城市中年、回报断裂的高学历群体等等，主体性危机也开始跨代际扩散。","en":"And those bearing the burden were no longer only “youth”; the affected population expanded markedly, for example: a middle class anxious about status, urban middle-aged people frozen in position, highly educated groups whose returns had been severed, and so on. The crisis of subjectivity also began to spread across generations."},{"t":"h","zh":"4.第四阶段（约2018–至今）","en":"4. Stage four (c. 2018–present)"},{"t":"p","zh":"社交媒体盛行进一步使主体成为全面“自我管理—自我剥削”的主体。在这个阶段，主体危机的焦虑与高效相挂钩，呈现出“高度自律、持续自我优化、完全自我负责”的形态，同时、缺乏稳定的意义锚点又使主体高度倦怠。","en":"The prevalence of social media has further made the subject a subject of total “self-management—self-exploitation.” At this stage, the anxiety of the subject’s crisis is tied to efficiency, taking the form of “high self-discipline, continuous self-optimisation, total self-responsibility,” while the lack of a stable anchor of meaning leaves the subject deeply exhausted."},{"t":"p","zh":"今天，我们所面临的问题已经不再是“长时间式的”与自身结合的斗争，而是“碎片时间”中的持续内耗、自我监控、将结构性困境归因为心理问题....","en":"Today, the problem we face is no longer a “long-duration” struggle over binding to the self, but continuous inner attrition within “fragmented time,” self-surveillance, the attribution of structural predicaments to psychological problems...."},{"t":"p","zh":"信息爆炸使承载的人群几乎交叉覆盖：Z世代、青年、中年、灵活就业者、知识劳动者、体制内边缘群体、高学历但无稳定路径者等等。","en":"The information explosion means that the groups bearing the burden overlap almost entirely: Generation Z, youth, the middle-aged, flexible workers, knowledge workers, marginal groups within the state system, the highly educated without stable paths, and so on."},{"t":"p","zh":"主体性危机成为普遍状态，跨越社会结构不同位置，交织于广泛的生命经验中。","en":"The crisis of subjectivity has become a universal condition, cutting across different positions in the social structure and interwoven with a wide range of life experience."},{"t":"p","zh":"我们现在将分析的主体聚焦于青年群体，引入近年来在公共讨论中反复被提起的“内卷”和“躺平”现象进行分析","en":"We now focus the subject of analysis on the youth group, and bring in the phenomena of “involution” and “lying flat,” repeatedly raised in public discussion in recent years, for analysis"},{"t":"p","zh":"青年人内卷和躺平，二者实际上都是由于意义和身份的缺席对“归属群体”的心理在形式上的呈现方式。内卷和躺平是对于同一社会结构的不同回应，“是否参与竞争”并不是现代以来才出现的新的选择。","en":"Young people’s involution and lying flat are, in fact, both formal manifestations of the psychology of “belonging to a group,” arising from the absence of meaning and identity. Involution and lying flat are different responses to the same social structure; “whether or not to take part in competition” is not a new choice that has appeared only in modern times."},{"t":"p","zh":"并不是：青年人要么选择躺平、不进入到这个“大型运行机器”；要么，跟上系统运转的速率，内卷以淘汰他人。","en":"It is not that young people either choose to lie flat and stay out of this “great running machine,” or keep pace with the system and involute to eliminate others."},{"t":"p","zh":"而是：内卷和躺平是“焦虑与虚无成为了行为发动机”的呈现形态，它们来源是共同的：“没有稳定的意义感和自我认知的来源”。也就是说，内卷和躺平是结果而不是原因，将结果现象作为一种诊断，并由此开出“药房”，直接去让青年人改变行动的方式和方向，这是不合逻辑也无法被实现的。","en":"Rather, involution and lying flat are forms in which “anxiety and nihilism have become the engine of behaviour”; their source is shared: “the lack of a stable source of meaning and self-understanding.” That is, involution and lying flat are results, not causes. To take the resulting phenomena as a diagnosis and prescribe a “remedy” from it, directly asking young people to change the manner and direction of their action, is illogical and cannot be achieved."},{"t":"p","zh":"绩效社会的高效数据使得整体看上去“积极”。但实则对于青年人来说，无论是与之同步的“内卷”还是滞留原地的“躺平”，“消极”的行动疲惫、精神退缩、道德冷却，都是两者无法避免的情况。","en":"The efficient data of the performance society make the whole look “positive.” But in reality, for young people, whether they keep pace through “involution” or stay put by “lying flat,” the “negative” fatigue of action, spiritual withdrawal and moral cooling are unavoidable in both."},{"t":"p","zh":"还有第三种情况：设定一种理想状态。理想状态并不真实存在，只是一种象征。比如，将未来的目标设定为地理位置上的迁移。这是一种广泛的状态设定：退出既定评价体系、暂停持续比较、逃离熟人社会的期待与羞耻。哪怕这是一种幻想的“彼岸”设定，在现实中并不更轻松，但它至少更陌生、可以远离“断裂的主要承受者”的结构性位置。当“改变这里”不可实现时，只剩“离开这里”。因为“离开”会成为唯一被想象为有效的行动。这是行动空间被压缩后的自然反应。","en":"There is also a third case: positing an ideal state. The ideal state does not really exist; it is only a symbol. For example, setting one’s future goal as a geographical move. This is a widespread setting of state: exiting the established evaluation system, pausing constant comparison, escaping the expectations and shame of the acquaintance society. Even if this is an imagined “other shore,” no easier in reality, it is at least more unfamiliar and allows one to get away from the structural position of “the main bearer of rupture.” When “changing this place” is impossible, only “leaving this place” remains, because “leaving” becomes the only action that can be imagined as effective. This is the natural reaction once the space for action has been compressed."},{"t":"h","zh":"二.伦理位置的失效和差序格局成立条件的消解","en":"II. The Failure of Ethical Positions and the Dissolution of the Conditions for the Differential Mode of Association"},{"t":"p","zh":"身份断裂，不能仅仅推向现代社会结构中的“行动消失”。在中国文化的语境中，还有一个切入点需要被考虑：儒家传统结构中伦理位置的缺席。","en":"The rupture of identity cannot be pushed solely onto the “disappearance of action” in modern social structure. In the context of Chinese culture there is another entry point to consider: the absence of ethical positions within the traditional Confucian structure."},{"t":"p","zh":"行动中的主体被省略为“可替换的非必要变量”，人与人之间难以建立联系，这是人的境况。在一些运行的系统中：行动有路径记录、秩序有指标要求、系统有目标设定....流程往往是严密严谨的。但如果作剖面分析，将行动和人之间的关系进行对应，就会发现，多数情况下：行动不指向价值、服从不等于认同、努力不成为叙事.....也就是说，事情虽然被很好的解决了，但解决事情的却不是人，而是“程序”本身。因此，人们将矛头指向程序中的其他主体、“形式主义”、“社会的冷漠化”，认为问题在于“道德素质的参差不齐”、“执行者与实际参与者沟通不足”、“治理机制需要优化”.....","en":"The subject in action is reduced to a “replaceable, non-essential variable,” and it is hard for people to form connections with one another: this is the human condition. In some running systems—action has a recorded path, order has required indicators, the system has set targets....—procedures are often rigorous and precise. But if one makes a cross-sectional analysis, matching action against the person, one finds that in most cases action does not point to value, obedience is not identification, effort does not become narrative..... That is, although things are well resolved, what resolves them is not people but the “procedure” itself. So people direct their criticism at other subjects in the procedure, at “formalism,” at “the growing coldness of society,” believing the problem lies in “uneven moral quality,” “insufficient communication between implementers and actual participants,” “governance mechanisms needing optimisation”....."},{"t":"p","zh":"而在技术、理性为逻辑核心的治理下意义生产被边缘化的同时，在中国儒家沿袭的伦理逻辑中，这种断裂进一步生发出代际冲突、人际关系等衍生问题。下面引入费孝通先生的“差序格局”，进一步分析其在互联网全球化条件下的断裂式转变。","en":"And while the production of meaning is marginalised under a governance whose logical core is technology and rationality, within the ethical logic inherited from Chinese Confucianism this rupture further gives rise to derivative problems such as intergenerational conflict and interpersonal relations. Below I bring in Fei Xiaotong’s “differential mode of association” to further analyse its ruptured transformation under conditions of internet globalisation."},{"t":"p","zh":"费孝通先生所提出的差序格局，是中国传统人际交往、社会结构和文化心理的一把重要的钥匙，有关系网络松散，以个体为中心，强调亲别等特征。有三个条件是差序格局所依赖的：稳定的附近、非完全可替代的角色、行动与关系的长期回馈。","en":"The differential mode of association proposed by Fei Xiaotong is an important key to traditional Chinese interpersonal relations, social structure and cultural psychology, characterised by loose relational networks, centring on the individual, and emphasis on degrees of closeness. The differential mode of association depends on three conditions: a stable vicinity, roles that are not fully replaceable, and long-term reciprocity between action and relationship."},{"t":"p","zh":"在当下的一些学术分析中，很多人将社会格局的变动归纳于差序格局之中。比如在《“差序格局”的形成及其变迁机制——一项基于行动者建模的研究》一文中，研究者指出：“伴随着互联网浪潮所带来的社交网络革命，个体可以超越传统先赋性的血缘、地缘、亲缘等因素来建立社会关系，个体的社会关系与社会网络呈现出新的面貌。”","en":"In some current academic analyses, many attribute changes in the social pattern to the differential mode of association. For example, in the article “The Formation of the ‘Differential Mode of Association’ and Its Mechanism of Change: A Study Based on Agent-Based Modelling,” the researchers note: “With the social-network revolution brought by the internet wave, individuals can transcend traditional ascribed factors such as blood, locality and kinship in building social relations, and individuals’ social relations and social networks take on a new appearance.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"但实际上对于青年人，尤其是互联网一代，逻辑恰好相反，由于与世界相接触的根本结构的改变、新自由主义框架下成长的社会背景、以及个体经验所被安置的“教育结构本身”逻辑中的主体可替换性的特征等等。“差序格局”所依赖的条件正在慢慢被抽空、失效。并不是差序格局被互联网丰富了新的内涵，而是这种格局本身所成立的条件就是被消解了的。而这并不仅限定于网络社交结构，在现实生活结构中：“技术环境和制度环境的改变造成了“人情式微”的局面，传统社会功能性互助关系萎缩，社会关系理性化趋势明显，现代社会市场交换体系逐渐确立并日益占据主导地位。”（《“任人唯亲”何以打破?社会信任与管理团队差序格局》2024）","en":"But in fact, for young people, especially the internet generation, the logic is exactly the opposite, owing to changes in the fundamental structure of contact with the world, the social background of growing up within a neoliberal framework, and the characteristic replaceability of the subject in the logic of the “educational structure itself” in which individual experience is placed, and so on. The conditions on which the “differential mode of association” depends are slowly being hollowed out and are ceasing to function. It is not that the internet has enriched the differential mode of association with new content, but that the very conditions under which this pattern holds have been dissolved. And this is not limited to the structure of online social life; in the structure of real life: “Changes in the technological and institutional environment have produced a situation of ‘declining renqing (human favour)’; the functional mutual-aid relations of traditional society have shrunk, the rationalisation of social relations is evident, and the market exchange system of modern society has gradually been established and increasingly dominates.” (“How Can ‘Cronyism’ Be Broken? Social Trust and the Differential Mode of Association in Management Teams,” 2024)"},{"t":"p","zh":"围绕差序格局展开的这几个讨论仅是作为本文引用的一个具体现象，本文真正想透过这个分析强调的是，这种”先入为主的将过去结构的框架继续安在现有状况“的思维框架普遍存在。这使叙事成为自我指涉、内部重复的空壳。","en":"These several discussions around the differential mode of association serve only as a concrete phenomenon cited in this essay; what this essay really wishes to emphasise through the analysis is that the mode of thinking that “preconceives and continues to impose the frameworks of past structures onto present conditions” is pervasive. It turns narrative into a self-referential, internally repetitive empty shell."},{"t":"p","zh":"总得来讲，当代中国青年：作为现代人，“行动（action）”本身消失，而作为儒家意识形态的中国人，过去延续的人生叙事失效。这是从“行动和意义”的角度出发，如果放在前文的主体性分析中，历史层层叠加在现实中，青年人还面临着更多的“脱链”和代际性冲突。","en":"On the whole, for contemporary Chinese youth: as modern people, “action” itself has disappeared; and as Chinese people of Confucian ideology, the life narratives continued from the past have failed. This is from the perspective of “action and meaning”; placed within the earlier analysis of subjectivity, with history layered upon reality, young people also face further “de-linking” and intergenerational conflict."},{"t":"h","zh":"三.文化焦虑","en":"III. Cultural Anxiety"},{"t":"p","zh":"如果说前文讨论的是行动与结构层面的断裂，那么“文化焦虑”则更多发生在意识形态与代际关系的中介层。虽称之为文化焦虑，但在本文中，它并非单纯的被用作描述心理状态，而是指一种在话语权结构中被持续生产、转移并承接的社会机制。","en":"If what was discussed above is rupture at the level of action and structure, then “cultural anxiety” occurs more in the intermediate layer of ideology and intergenerational relations. Although called cultural anxiety, in this essay it is not used merely to describe a psychological state, but refers to a social mechanism continuously produced, transferred and taken on within the structure of discursive power."},{"t":"h","zh":"1.被延续与转嫁的文化焦虑","en":"1. Cultural anxiety prolonged and passed on"},{"t":"p","zh":"当下青年所面对的文化焦虑，不仅是西方文化霸权语境下的必然状态；其中还有要被继承的“历史遗留问题”。近代以来，中国的社会长期处于一种频繁更迭状态之中，而文化性的问题如“传统如何安放”、“文化如何作传播转译”、“思想文化如何作衔接”等，相比高速发展的经济，并未与其同步，而是一直以悬而未决的形式被不断推延、以少数人微薄的力量缓慢推行。","en":"The cultural anxiety faced by today’s youth is not only the inevitable condition in a context of Western cultural hegemony; it also includes “problems left over from history” that must be inherited. Since modern times Chinese society has long been in a state of frequent upheaval, while cultural questions such as “how to place tradition,” “how culture is to be transmitted and translated,” and “how thought and culture are to be connected” have not kept pace with the rapidly developing economy, but have been continually deferred in unresolved form, slowly pushed forward by the meagre strength of a few."},{"t":"p","zh":"在这一过程中，前几代人所承载的文化焦虑，并未通过系统性的反思被消化，而更多是通过话语、教育与“道统”式期待向下传递。年轻一代作为话语权结构中的被动接收者，常在一个个具体情境中被要求在尚未完成的“文化连续性”问题上承担时代责任，这使得青年人成为尚未被解决的文化断裂问题的承载者：继承传统的同时要继续完成现代化；要寻找文化主体性；要在传统文化本身的内部衔接、构建没有完成的情况下，同时在全球竞争中证明自身价值。","en":"In this process, the cultural anxiety carried by previous generations has not been digested through systematic reflection, but has been passed downward mostly through discourse, education and “daotong”-style expectations. The younger generation, as passive recipients in the structure of discursive power, are often required in specific situations to shoulder the responsibility of the era on the unfinished question of “cultural continuity.” This makes young people the bearers of the unresolved problem of cultural rupture: they must inherit tradition while continuing to complete modernisation; they must seek cultural subjectivity; and, while the internal connection and construction of traditional culture itself remain unfinished, they must at the same time prove their own worth in global competition."},{"t":"h","zh":"2.道统的断裂","en":"2. The rupture of the daotong"},{"t":"p","zh":"“道统”是指儒家经学传统中一种能够为权威提供正当性来源、并将其行动纳入可解释秩序的结构性装置。","en":"“Daotong” 道统 (the orthodox transmission of the Way) refers to a structural device in the Confucian classical tradition that can provide a source of legitimacy for authority and bring its actions into an explicable order."},{"t":"p","zh":"进入20世纪，随着帝制崩溃和儒家思想的官方地位瓦解，“道统”在制度上已彻底断裂。但其思维模式和深层影响犹在。尤其在文化心理上体现为一种对“正统”和“传承”的执着，以及知识分子或文化精英应承担“为往圣继绝学，为万世开太平”的使命感。（这也是青年人仍有文化焦虑的原因，这是一种儒生潜意识里的使命感，也正因如此，说明这一文化心理并未随意义枯竭而完全消失。）","en":"Entering the twentieth century, with the collapse of the imperial system and the disintegration of Confucianism’s official status, the “daotong” was completely severed institutionally. But its mode of thinking and deep influence remain. Especially in cultural psychology, they show themselves as an attachment to “orthodoxy” and “transmission,” and a sense of mission that intellectuals or cultural elites should take on “continuing the lost learning of past sages and opening an age of peace for all generations.” (This is also why young people still have cultural anxiety: it is a sense of mission in the Confucian scholar’s unconscious, and precisely for this reason it shows that this cultural psychology has not entirely vanished with the drying-up of meaning.)"},{"t":"p","zh":"前文提到的“将过去结构的框架继续安在这一代年轻人身上的思路”，实际上来自于“道统”的思维结构。当下时兴的一些代际冲突和亚文化，并不能被简单地全部归因于在前文所被分析过的“结构性的主体性危机和伦理位置缺席”。实际上这一代际冲突还有一个常被忽视的原因——权威背后的道统的结构性错位与失效。权威虽然结构性占有解释权，但实际并不再在道统逻辑里天然具备合法性——不能提供普遍理解与内化的解释框架；与此同时权威者自身亦陷入主体性危机。也就是说我们过去赖以沟通的话语机制及话语权结构的本身，存在的前提早已经不在了。","en":"The “approach of continuing to impose the frameworks of past structures on this generation of young people” mentioned earlier actually comes from the thinking structure of the “daotong.” Some currently fashionable intergenerational conflicts and subcultures cannot simply be attributed entirely to the “structural crisis of subjectivity and absence of ethical positions” analysed above. In fact this intergenerational conflict has another, often overlooked cause—the structural misalignment and failure of the daotong behind authority. Although authority structurally holds the power of interpretation, it no longer naturally possesses legitimacy within the logic of the daotong—it cannot provide an interpretive framework that is universally understood and internalised; at the same time, those in authority have themselves fallen into a crisis of subjectivity. That is, the very premises of the discursive mechanisms and structure of discursive power on which we once relied to communicate have long since ceased to exist."},{"t":"p","zh":"在这种情况下，当下的代际关系里发生了一种结构性转移：权威无法自洽其合法性，只得运用“权威”本身进行话语重复。因此，年轻一代与其失去沟通与理解的基础。同时，对于推陈出新的未竟事业，青年人还要承担其结构性位置所被投射的期待——既要继承文化，又要为其失败负责；既被要求创新和批判性继承，又要服从规范。当下的文化冲突常常以“代际对立”的形式出现，但实则这种“对立”本身，来源于“理解的错位”。","en":"Under these circumstances a structural shift has occurred in present intergenerational relations: authority, unable to make its legitimacy self-consistent, can only use “authority” itself to repeat its discourse. The younger generation thus loses the basis for communication and understanding with it. At the same time, for the unfinished work of bringing forth the new from the old, young people must also bear the expectations projected onto their structural position—they must both inherit culture and answer for its failure; they are required both to innovate and to inherit critically, and to obey norms. Today’s cultural conflicts often appear in the form of “generational opposition,” but in fact this “opposition” itself originates in a “misalignment of understanding.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"将这一节与前文结合，把文化焦虑和道统断裂嵌入在更大的结构之中，我们又会看到：在行动层面，两者加剧了行动的不确定性；而由于代际结构中各种位置中的话语错位，又进一步加重了普遍的身份焦虑。","en":"Combining this section with the foregoing, and embedding cultural anxiety and the rupture of the daotong within the larger structure, we see again: at the level of action, both intensify the uncertainty of action; and the discursive misalignments among the various positions in the intergenerational structure further aggravate a general anxiety of identity."},{"t":"h","zh":"五.结尾","en":"V. Conclusion"},{"t":"p","zh":"通过上述对行动机制、伦理位置、社会结构与话语结构的分析，在这里，作为一个青年人，我想指出，当下我们所经验到的“意义缺失”与“身份断裂”，并非单一维度的问题，也仅无法通过个体内部调节或心理干预加以根本性缓解。它更倾向一种被延迟、被转移、并在特定代际位置上集中显化的结构性结果。这一困境并不意味着“青年失去了信念”，也不意味着传统资源已经耗尽，而是表明：过去赖以协调行动、权威与理解的结构本身，需要梳理、有所再次建构。只有在这一层面上重新理解当下青年的经验，才能避免将结构性问题不断回收为个体的心理或道德问题。不把结果当原因，而是分析结果呈现的现象，从而在较大范围内寻找普遍性与转折的方向。","en":"Through the above analysis of the mechanisms of action, ethical positions, social structure and discursive structure, I want here, as a young person, to point out that the “lack of meaning” and “rupture of identity” we currently experience are not one-dimensional problems, nor can they be fundamentally relieved merely through the individual’s internal adjustment or psychological intervention. They are better seen as a structural outcome that has been deferred, transferred, and made concentratedly visible in a particular generational position. This predicament does not mean that “youth have lost their convictions,” nor that the resources of tradition are exhausted; rather, it shows that the very structures on which we once relied to coordinate action, authority and understanding need to be sorted out and in some measure reconstructed. Only by re-understanding the experience of today’s youth at this level can we avoid continually recycling structural problems into individual psychological or moral problems. Not taking results for causes, but analysing the phenomena in which results appear, so as to look, across a wider range, for what is universal and for directions of change."}]},{"id":"W-2026-01","n":18,"title":{"zh":"中西思想体系融合时的错位","en":"Misalignments in the Fusion of Chinese and Western Systems of Thought"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2026-01-06","genre":"随笔","summary":{"zh":"我想了一下，要是想追溯中国的传统，像之前一样沿着儒家这一脉络顺藤摸瓜，是很不足够的。","en":"Thinking it over, I realised that if I want to trace Chinese tradition, simply following the Confucian lineage step by step as I did before is far from enough."},"words":2125,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"我想了一下，要是想追溯中国的传统，像之前一样沿着儒家这一脉络顺藤摸瓜，是很不足够的。我从想要追溯“中国传统”开始，就有非目的性的与西方作对比。这其实一开始还是带着那种敌我二分的情绪和前设的，因为我认为要找到一个传统的断裂点，而所谓传统的断裂点，我将其归咎于鸦片战争以来的远离传统、转向西方现代性。然后又想从这个节点里重新拾起些什么。但是这种单线的摸索与梳理其实是非常表面的，它只是“看上去像是那么回事”。实际上，从魏晋一直到清，传统在不同时期也有着新的断裂与重组，“传统”这一词在不同时期背后的思想体系也要被梳理。因此我又通过对传统的线性梳理-从王弼三书合流到宋明理学再到明末清初新儒家又做了轴心文明层面的信息整理。而对于神话，关于对文明原初点的故事性构建，也还是顺着前辈们对于中西比较的轴线，找到了一些考据与新的构建的尝试（如鲁迅《故事新编》）。由此，对于中国的那种“敞开”式的人与世界的关系，我找到了一个极为重叠对应并利于理解的词语“感兴”；并由此联想到了反柏拉图主义、注重生命意志与力的尼采一脉，想将二者作一些对应和主客关系的重构——有些东西我们本来就有、博大精深。并且，如果一定要参照西方的思想概念，尤其是现代以来的一些词语，他们在词语的使用与交织中想要重新构建或者说重新找到的东西。对我们来说是自然发生的，本就在其原位的。在思想史层，在中国，它一直暗含着、涌动着；而西方是先设定一个最高理念遮蔽它再去反掉遮蔽。我认为我们不应该是：“引进西方、同在现代的语境下，将西方的那个‘理念’、‘太一’、‘绝对精神’给反掉，然后建立主体性。在我们的语境中，我们如果用西方的理论来去反那个“至高存在”是根本就错位了的：西方反的是他们的思想框架的终点，他们想要解开的那个架空一切的设定，这落实到的是每个人与世界关系的这一层的；而中国人在思考框架本身就不是柏拉图主义的、不是宗教性的，而是理、气，一种发生中的生成与把握，最开始就没有要将人与世界隔开一个距离。我们从最开始反的那个“至高”就不是“人与世界的关系”这一层的——因为那里根本没什么可以反！我们实际上一直反的是一个具体的权威代表者、是一直以来的道统继承模式、是“人”。","en":"Thinking it over, I realised that if I want to trace Chinese tradition, simply following the Confucian lineage step by step as I did before is far from enough. From the moment I set out to trace “Chinese tradition,” I was already, without any particular aim, comparing it with the West. At first this actually carried a kind of us-versus-them emotion and presupposition, because I thought I had to find a point where tradition broke, and I blamed that break on the turn away from tradition and toward Western modernity since the Opium War. Then I wanted to pick something back up from that juncture. But this single-line groping and sorting is in fact very superficial; it only “looks about right.” In reality, from the Wei-Jin period all the way to the Qing, tradition underwent new ruptures and reorganisations in different periods, and the systems of thought behind the word “tradition” in each period also need to be sorted out. So, alongside a linear sorting of tradition—from Wang Bi’s confluence of the three books, to Song-Ming Neo-Confucianism, to the new Confucians of the late Ming and early Qing—I also organised material at the level of the Axial civilisations. As for myth, the narrative construction of a civilisation’s point of origin, I again followed the axis of Sino-Western comparison laid down by earlier scholars and found some textual research and some attempts at new constructions (such as Lu Xun’s Old Tales Retold). Through this, for the “open” relationship between person and world in China, I found a word that overlaps with it closely and helps one understand it: ganxing 感兴 (being stirred by things and responding). From there I thought of the line of Nietzsche, anti-Platonist and focused on the will to life and on force, and wanted to set up some correspondences between the two and reconstruct the subject-object relation—some things we already have, and they are vast and profound. Moreover, if we must refer to Western concepts, especially certain words of the modern period, what they seek to rebuild, or rediscover, through the use and interweaving of those words is something that for us happens naturally, that has always been in its proper place. At the level of intellectual history, in China it has always been implicit, always surging beneath; whereas the West first posits a highest Idea that conceals it and then works to undo that concealment. I believe we should not be: “importing the West and, likewise within a modern context, overturning the Western ‘Idea,’ ‘the One,’ ‘Absolute Spirit,’ and then establishing subjectivity.” In our context, using Western theory to overturn that “supreme being” is fundamentally misaligned: what the West overturns is the endpoint of its own framework of thought, the overarching premise that hollows everything out, and this lands on the level of each person’s relationship to the world; whereas the Chinese framework of thinking was never Platonist, never religious, but was li 理 (principle) and qi 气 (vital energy), a generation and grasping in the midst of happening, which from the very beginning never sought to set a distance between person and world. The “supreme” that we set out to overturn was never at the level of “the relationship between person and world”—because there was nothing there to overturn! What we have actually been overturning all along is a concrete representative of authority, the mode of inheriting the daotong 道统 (the orthodox transmission of the Way), that is, “people.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"所以矛头是错的，一开始就是错位的、不是一一对应的。我们当时不应该如此激进地推翻我们博大精深的传统、我们的“气”、“理”、“道”、“感兴”.....","en":"So the spearhead was aimed wrongly; it was misaligned from the start, not a one-to-one correspondence. We should not, back then, have overthrown so radically our vast and profound tradition, our “qi,” “li,” “dao 道 (the Way),” and “ganxing”....."},{"t":"p","zh":"上面是关于“转换”的错位。而对于中西思想碰撞的过程来说，对于西方的思想进入中国，如丁耕老师所分析，本就是中国知识份子所主观作的内容选择之后所进行的翻译与传播。也就是说，我们从一开始，就是顺着那些知识分子（有的是留学而归的）将西方的理论和写作者 “安”在了我们自己的认识框架中。我们反掉了自己的权威，但与西方反掉思想框架不同，我们是将新的权威嫁接进了已经有的框架中了。也就是说，看似换了新的讨论框架和内容，但仍是在过去的“平面”上，而这种将新权威替换成西方来源的情况，是让我们内部扭曲的——","en":"The above concerns the misalignment of “conversion.” As for the process of collision between Chinese and Western thought, the entry of Western thought into China was, as Professor Ding Geng has analysed, from the outset a matter of translation and dissemination carried out after Chinese intellectuals had subjectively selected the content. In other words, from the very beginning we followed those intellectuals (some of them returned from study abroad) in “installing” Western theories and writers into our own framework of understanding. We overturned our own authority, but unlike the West overturning its framework of thought, we grafted a new authority into the framework that already existed. That is, it seems we changed to a new framework and new content for discussion, yet we remain on the old “plane,” and this replacement of authority with a Western source is what twists us from within—"},{"t":"p","zh":"我们的思想框架中，权威、道统一直都在，但那个对我们产生“震慑”与“约束”的却是与我们人种、世界观、地理位置完全不同的“洋人”。因此要解开我们的文化焦虑，不可避免的要去纠正这些错位。","en":"In our framework of thought, authority and the daotong have always been there, but what now “awes” and “constrains” us is the “foreigner,” utterly different from us in race, worldview and geographical position. Therefore, to untie our cultural anxiety, we inevitably have to correct these misalignments."},{"t":"p","zh":"而我们要直面嵌入我们生活我们的思想框架，在公众领域，我曾经就“名言滥用”的一个现象作了分析，指出西哲在话语结构中被赋予了一种终极的合法性位置。同理，在理论与深思更集中的场域，我们也要作这种斟酌与思量。以期在创造新事物时也带着这种文化主体意识，对新的文化创造进行“洗牌”。","en":"And we must face squarely the framework of thought embedded in our lives. In the public sphere, I once analysed the phenomenon of the “abuse of famous quotations,” pointing out that Western philosophers have been given a position of ultimate legitimacy within the structure of discourse. Likewise, in fields where theory and deep reflection are more concentrated, we must exercise the same deliberation and weighing, in the hope that when creating new things we will also carry this awareness of cultural subjectivity, and “reshuffle” new cultural creation."},{"t":"p","zh":"“中国”的“传统”，“中国”一词也要溯源，我之前一直盯着传统不放。在《尼布楚条约》，“中国”一词第一次被在国际上被指称中国。但是知道了这个信息又如何？在网上随便一搜就能搜出来，为什么还要正襟危坐一样的插入到文本中？重要的不是信息的罗列，而是带着目的和立场来去选择信息，来用这些特定的信息组成新的叙述。虽然对于“动员”、“宏大叙事”我们要一直保有警惕，但是做一种系统的、可被共同进入的理解框架是必要的。","en":"“China’s” “tradition”: the word “China” too needs to be traced to its source; until now I had kept my eyes fixed on tradition. In the Treaty of Nerchinsk, the word “Zhongguo” (China) was used for the first time internationally to designate China. But what of it, knowing this? A quick online search turns it up, so why insert it into the text with such solemnity? What matters is not listing information, but selecting information with a purpose and a standpoint, and using that particular information to compose a new narrative. Although we must always remain wary of “mobilisation” and “grand narratives,” building a systematic framework of understanding that people can enter together is necessary."},{"t":"p","zh":"难道说要作一种可进入可随时抽身的框架/平面吗？这个平面并不是不存在，而是仅在某一部分人中间保有一定的短暂开启。泛滥的开启等于没有开启，改革不可能、也没有必要。对于中国来说，要建立起主体性、文化认同，是当下以及下一步要做的，而同时，要建立起社群。当经济慢慢好转的时候，我们要为有空闲时间的人提供一种或多种文化艺术层面的设计、一种填补空余时间的补充，一种协调、共同创建创造的平台。我们要建立起的是进入这个平台的天然的兴趣，但同时有一个问题也要被考虑到，那就是这个从工作中分离出来的空地和空余时间与工作本身的关系。消费的逻辑不可避免，但是我们可以在此之上建立一种新的，并且与消费的逻辑不相悖、还可以让消费的逻辑为其助力的运行框架。文化和艺术要成为一种“电子游戏”一样令人上瘾的东西，但不同的是，人的素质和教养会在这个基础上提高；这像是马克思所做的共产主义的对人的生活的设想。写到这里我突然发现自己还不太了解马克思及其思想。我不想仅仅是一个设想，因为AI的出现以及历史周期一般的旧世界瓦解让我觉得要去建构起新的东西。但是不想让它一上来就那么宏大","en":"Should we, then, make a framework or plane that one can enter and leave at any time? Such a plane is not non-existent; it merely stays open briefly among a certain group of people. An opening that is everywhere is no opening at all; reform is neither possible nor necessary. For China, establishing subjectivity and cultural identity is what must be done now and next, and at the same time, community must be built. As the economy gradually improves, we should provide those who have free time with one or more designs at the level of culture and art, a supplement to fill spare time, a platform for coordination and joint creation. What we need to build is a natural interest in entering this platform, but one problem must also be considered: the relationship between this open ground and free time, separated off from work, and work itself. The logic of consumption is unavoidable, but on top of it we can build a new operating framework that does not run counter to the logic of consumption and can even harness it. Culture and art should become something as addictive as a “video game,” but with the difference that people’s quality and cultivation will rise on this basis; this resembles Marx’s communist vision of human life. Writing this, I suddenly realise that I still don’t know Marx and his thought very well. I don’t want this to be merely a vision, because the arrival of AI and the collapse of the old world, like a historical cycle, make me feel that something new must be built. But I don’t want it to be so grand right from the start"},{"t":"p","zh":"为什么要作一种","en":"Why should we make a kind of"}]},{"id":"W-2026-02","n":16,"title":{"zh":"越后妻有","en":"Echigo-Tsumari"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2026-02-06","genre":"评论","summary":{"zh":"1994，乡村振兴战略，用艺术激发地域魅力、促进人口交流活动。北川弗拉姆担任总监。","en":"1994: a rural revitalization strategy, using art to bring out the region’s appeal and promote exchange between people. Fram Kitagawa served as director."},"words":1724,"blocks":[{"t":"h","zh":"发展历程","en":"Development History"},{"t":"p","zh":"1. 1994，乡村振兴战略，用艺术激发地域魅力、促进人口交流活动。北川弗拉姆担任总监。该计划于2000年启动，完全由地方政府财政支持并主导运作。","en":"1. 1994: a rural revitalization strategy, using art to bring out the region’s appeal and promote exchange between people. Fram Kitagawa served as director. The program was launched in 2000, entirely funded and run by the local government."},{"t":"p","zh":"十日町的市长担任执行委员长。","en":"The mayor of Tokamachi served as chair of the executive committee."},{"t":"p","zh":"第一届的规模：","en":"Scale of the first edition:"},{"t":"img","src":"e16-01.png"},{"t":"p","zh":"2. 2003年，主办方从“越后妻有大地艺术节执行委员会”更改为“大地艺术节・花之道路执行委员会”。","en":"2. In 2003, the organizer changed from the “Echigo-Tsumari Art Triennale Executive Committee” to the “Art Triennale · Flower Road Executive Committee.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"初衷是用国家-地方行政体系推动公共政策型艺术项目，核心是为：①基础设施建设②地域形象塑造③旅游拉动④公共投资回报。","en":"The original intention was to use the national–local administrative system to drive a public-policy-type art project, centered on: ① infrastructure construction ② shaping the regional image ③ boosting tourism ④ returns on public investment."},{"t":"p","zh":"但公共投入的成本巨大，从 2003 年开始，NPO 法人“越后妻有里山协动机构”逐渐成为实际执行主体，负责：","en":"But the cost of public investment was enormous, and from 2003 the NPO corporation “Echigo-Tsumari Satoyama Collaborative Organization” gradually became the actual executing body, responsible for:"},{"t":"p","zh":"社区动员、农田认养计划、空屋改造、志愿者系统、城市—乡村交流机制、农业品牌重建。也就是艺术节由 政府主导 变为 NPO 主导 + 政府支持。事件的内核从艺术旅游业慢慢变为“艺术构建生活”","en":"community mobilization, a farmland adoption program, renovation of vacant houses, a volunteer system, urban–rural exchange mechanisms, and rebuilding agricultural brands. That is, the festival shifted from being government-led to being NPO-led with government support. The core of the event slowly changed from art tourism to “art building life.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"（典型标志是：“松代梯田银行”计划启动，城市居民参与农业生产，艺术节开始深度介入 农业、社区治理、地方产业链）","en":"(A typical marker: the launch of the “Matsudai Terraced Rice Field Bank” program, in which city residents took part in agricultural production, and the festival began to engage deeply with agriculture, community governance and local industrial chains.)"},{"t":"p","zh":"本届规模：","en":"Scale of this edition:"},{"t":"img","src":"e16-02.png"},{"t":"h","zh":"3. 2006年","en":"3. 2006"},{"t":"p","zh":"主办方又重新更改回了大地艺术节执行委员会。这一届的范围规模和国际影响力都相比提高，举办理念除了第一届的“艺术品激活旅游业”、第二届的“渗入生活及长期执行”，还需要考虑到它的“标杆”位置。因此需要考虑可以将其：制度化、结构化、可推广、可治理、可协调.....因此要套上“制度性外壳”","en":"The organizer changed back again to the Art Triennale Executive Committee. This edition grew in both scope and international influence. Besides the first edition’s “artworks revitalizing tourism” and the second edition’s “permeating life and long-term implementation,” its organizing philosophy also had to take into account its position as a “benchmark.” It therefore had to consider how it could be: institutionalized, structured, replicable, governable, coordinable..... and so it had to be fitted with an “institutional shell.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"本届规模：","en":"Scale of this edition:"},{"t":"img","src":"e16-03.png"},{"t":"h","zh":"4. 2009","en":"4. 2009"},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术项目开始：进入农业生产过程、身体劳动、老龄化与照护议题。从空间治理 转变为 生命治理，也就是说艺术不再只是：“景观介入”而是“生活干预”。","en":"The art projects began to enter agricultural production processes, bodily labor, and issues of aging and care. They shifted from the governance of space to the governance of life; that is, art was no longer just “intervention in the landscape” but “intervention in life.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"本届规模：","en":"Scale of this edition:"},{"t":"img","src":"e16-04.png"},{"t":"h","zh":"5. 2012","en":"5. 2012"},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术项目开始常态运行，去节庆化 ，有了更稳定的生活结构。（365 天开放、农业—艺术—教育融合、空屋成为长期居住与创作空间）","en":"The art projects began to run on a regular basis, moving away from the festival format, and gained a more stable structure of life. (Open 365 days a year; integration of agriculture, art and education; vacant houses became spaces for long-term residence and creative work.)"},{"t":"p","zh":"本届规模：","en":"Scale of this edition:"},{"t":"img","src":"e16-05.png"},{"t":"h","zh":"6. 2015","en":"6. 2015"},{"t":"p","zh":"规模更加庞大，这时越后妻有大地艺术节已经有了相当的知名度，从支持者结构的赞助规模就可以看出，它的商业性成功。","en":"The scale grew even larger. By this time the Echigo-Tsumari Art Triennale had become quite well known, and its commercial success can be seen from the scale of sponsorship in its structure of supporters."},{"t":"p","zh":"同时，越后妻有成为“模板”：国际艺术节系统开始广泛借鉴，中国、东南亚乡村艺术项目大量模仿.","en":"At the same time, Echigo-Tsumari became a “template”: the international art festival system began to borrow from it widely, and rural art projects in China and Southeast Asia imitated it in large numbers."},{"t":"img","src":"e16-06.png"},{"t":"h","zh":"7. 2018","en":"7. 2018"},{"t":"p","zh":"2018 年越后妻有大地艺术节在亚洲文化圈的迅速扩展、中国馆与香港馆的设立、清津峡隧道的地标化改造以及海外访客与文化资本的涌入，共同将这一地方性艺术节推向全球化扩张的顶峰。然而，这一阶段亦导致里山生活伦理与观光资本逻辑之间的深层张力。","en":"In 2018, the rapid expansion of the Echigo-Tsumari Art Triennale within the Asian cultural sphere, the establishment of the China Pavilion and the Hong Kong Pavilion, the transformation of the Kiyotsu Gorge Tunnel into a landmark, and the influx of overseas visitors and cultural capital together pushed this local art festival to the peak of its global expansion. However, this stage also produced a deep tension between the ethics of satoyama life and the logic of tourism capital."},{"t":"h","zh":"8. 2022","en":"8. 2022"},{"t":"p","zh":"2020 年后新冠疫情所引发的全球流动中断，使这一张力骤然显现，并迫使艺术节在 2022 年进行系统性重构：从以国际传播与流量增长为导向，转向以地方生存系统修复、社区协作与日常生活重建为核心目标，标志着其由“全球文化节点”向“在地社会系统”的再地方化转型。","en":"After 2020, the interruption of global mobility caused by the COVID-19 pandemic brought this tension suddenly to the surface and forced the festival to undergo a systematic restructuring in 2022: shifting from an orientation toward international dissemination and traffic growth to core goals of repairing local systems of livelihood, community collaboration and rebuilding everyday life. This marked its re-localizing transformation from a “global cultural node” into a “locally rooted social system.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"2009年以后，当越后妻有大地艺术节开始介入到生活的时候，最初用艺术带动地方经济的目标可以说是达到了彼岸。若剖面分析，则，其实是将一个较为边缘、与主流较隔离的地方，划入了大逻辑里（可以说是新自由主义的逻辑、也可以说是现代社会的逻辑、消费社会的逻辑）。大机器有其运行的大模式，若是加入这套逻辑，效果则是显著高效的，但由于它过于的高速、在“安全模板”中，每个因素作为部件，人也与对空间的直接感知的联系也逐渐被转变和规范。也就是说艺术实践是商业实践的外壳。到了15年，这套成功的商业模式病毒一般地被复制到了周边地区。所以，如何长期发展、减少被商业逻辑完全吞噬的可能，应该是对艺术项目的要求之一。这在具体情况也是艺术项目在发展中要时刻校准、调整的。","en":"After 2009, when the Echigo-Tsumari Art Triennale began to intervene in life, the original goal of using art to drive the local economy can be said to have reached the other shore. Analyzed in cross-section, however, what actually happened is that a fairly marginal place, relatively isolated from the mainstream, was drawn into the big logic (call it the logic of neoliberalism, or the logic of modern society, or the logic of consumer society). The big machine has its own big pattern of operation; once you join this logic, the results are markedly efficient. But because it moves so fast, within a “safe template” every factor becomes a component, and people’s connection with their direct perception of space is also gradually transformed and standardized. In other words, artistic practice is the shell of commercial practice. By 2015, this successful business model had been copied, like a virus, into the surrounding regions. So how to develop over the long term and reduce the possibility of being completely swallowed by commercial logic should be one of the requirements for art projects. In concrete situations, this is also something an art project must constantly calibrate and adjust as it develops."},{"t":"p","zh":"这是对“越后妻有”发展的批判角度，诚然，越后妻有有着其巨大的成功、在艺术实践上也带来启发与反思。从地域性项目的角度来去思考这种艺术打造城市形象的实践，越后妻有无疑是成功的，它的模式可以复制，但其成功性不能被复制。在中国，若想发起这种艺术项目，就以青岛这座城市为例。与越后妻有的“乡村”、大量农田和自然景观不同，若想在青岛这种中型的、商业破坏极严重、工业景观的、各种功能逻辑零散拼凑出的城市中发起艺术项目，很容易让原本的眼花缭乱更加目不暇接。","en":"This is a critical angle on the development of “Echigo-Tsumari.” Admittedly, Echigo-Tsumari has achieved enormous success and has also brought inspiration and reflection to artistic practice. Thinking about this practice of using art to build a city’s image from the standpoint of regional projects, Echigo-Tsumari is undoubtedly a success: its model can be copied, but its success cannot. In China, if one wanted to launch such an art project, take the city of Qingdao as an example. Unlike Echigo-Tsumari’s “countryside,” with its expanses of farmland and natural landscape, launching an art project in a city like Qingdao—medium-sized, severely damaged by commerce, a landscape of industry, pieced together from scattered fragments of various functional logics—could easily make what is already a dazzling jumble even more overwhelming."},{"t":"p","zh":"其实，过去、地域性都是“壳”，重要的是建立新的东西（符号、标杆、历史记忆）。在埃菲尔铁塔建立之前是没有埃菲尔铁塔的。哪怕会被吞入大逻辑，但如果这个“符号/地标”自身可以经受时间的检验，那么它带来的身份认同、以及对城市发展、定位的影响是同步发生的。","en":"In fact, the past and locality are both “shells”; what matters is building something new (a symbol, a benchmark, a historical memory). Before the Eiffel Tower was built, there was no Eiffel Tower. Even if it is swallowed into the big logic, if this “symbol/landmark” can itself stand the test of time, then the sense of identity it brings and its influence on the city’s development and positioning will arise together."}]},{"id":"W-2026-03","n":4,"title":{"zh":"水性材料与时间结构：文人画的“感兴”机制的再思考","en":"Water-Based Materials and Temporal Structure: Rethinking the Mechanism of Ganxing in Literati Painting"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2026-03-16","genre":"论文","summary":{"zh":"以水性绘画材料的物理属性为切入点，探讨其在艺术实践中所生成的时间结构，并进一步分析这一结构如何塑造中国传统文人画中的“感兴”机制。","en":"Taking the physical properties of water-based painting materials as its point of departure, this paper examines the temporal structure they generate in artistic practice, and further analyses how this structure has shaped the mechanism of ganxing (stirred response) in traditional Chinese literati painting."},"words":5057,"blocks":[{"t":"label","zh":"摘要","en":"Abstract"},{"t":"p","zh":"以水性绘画材料的物理属性为切入点，探讨其在艺术实践中所生成的时间结构，并进一步分析这一结构如何塑造中国传统文人画中的“感兴”机制。文章通过对比水性媒介与古典油画在创作过程中“不可逆生成”与“可回溯逼近”两种行动逻辑，指出材料条件不仅影响图像呈现方式，更在长期实践中训练出不同的主体行动模式。研究结合绘画理论、诗学传统与思想史文本，以王夫之“事—势—几”的历史观为中介，揭示“感兴”作为一种在行动中生成意义的机制，其内在关联于时间的不可回撤性与情境判断的即时性。文章进一步将该机制置于现代生成哲学与当代人工智能语境中，提出“感兴”不仅是艺术经验，更构成一种以身体性与责任承担为核心的人类主体性形式。本文的创新在于从材料时间结构出发，打通艺术实践、思想史与当代技术问题之间的关联，为重新理解中国绘画传统提供一种生成论路径。","en":"Taking the physical properties of water-based painting materials as its point of departure, this paper examines the temporal structure they generate in artistic practice, and further analyses how this structure has shaped the mechanism of ganxing (stirred response) in traditional Chinese literati painting. By comparing two logics of action in the creative process of water-based media and classical oil painting, “irreversible generation” and “retraceable approximation”, the paper argues that material conditions not only affect the way images are presented but, through long practice, also train different modes of subjective action. Drawing on painting theory, the poetic tradition and texts from intellectual history, and taking Wang Fuzhi’s historical view of shi–shi–ji (events, momentum and incipience) as a mediating framework, it shows that ganxing is a mechanism by which meaning is generated in action, intrinsically bound up with the irreversibility of time and the immediacy of situational judgement. The paper further places this mechanism in the context of modern philosophies of becoming and contemporary artificial intelligence, proposing that ganxing is not merely an aesthetic experience but constitutes a form of human subjectivity centred on embodiment and the bearing of responsibility. Its contribution lies in starting from the temporal structure of materials to connect artistic practice, intellectual history and contemporary technological questions, offering a generative approach to re-understanding the tradition of Chinese painting."},{"t":"p","zh":"关键词：水性材料；时间结构；感兴；王夫之；","en":"Keywords: water-based materials; temporal structure; ganxing; Wang Fuzhi"},{"t":"h","zh":"一、问题的提出","en":"1. Posing the Question"},{"t":"p","zh":"在关于中国绘画的讨论中，常出现一种非正式的说法：“中国人的文化气质似乎自带水性”。这一表述往往被用来指涉中国绘画与水墨媒介之间的深层关联。然而，在多数情况下，这一说法仅停留在文化气质或审美偏好的描述层面，没有对其形成机制的进一步分析。","en":"In discussions of Chinese painting, one often hears an informal saying: “The cultural temperament of the Chinese seems to be inherently water-like.” The phrase is usually used to point to a deep connection between Chinese painting and the medium of ink and water. In most cases, however, the saying stays at the level of describing a cultural temperament or aesthetic preference, without any further analysis of how it came about."},{"t":"p","zh":"本文并不为某种民族性或文化身份建立本质性的界定，讨论的也并不是整个中国绘画史的普遍规律，而是一种在特定笔墨传统中被反复训练的行动结构。因此，提出一个实践层面的问题：在漫长的历史过程中，以水性材料为主导的绘画实践，是否在一定程度上塑造了特定的行动方式及受其影响的意义生成结构？","en":"This paper does not seek to establish an essentialist definition of any national character or cultural identity, nor does it discuss universal laws of the whole history of Chinese painting; its subject is a structure of action repeatedly trained within a particular tradition of brush and ink. It therefore poses a question at the level of practice: over a long historical process, did painting practice dominated by water-based materials, to some extent, shape particular ways of acting and the structures of meaning-making influenced by them?"},{"t":"p","zh":"“绘画是一门‘物质的炼金术’，颜料不仅是颜料，更是创作者思维的延伸。”如果说绘画不仅是一种图像生产方式，同时也是一种身体与时间经验的实践，那么材料本身所规定的操作条件，或许也会在长期实践中反过来影响创作者的思维方式与行动逻辑。","en":"“Painting is a ‘material alchemy’; pigment is not only pigment but an extension of the painter’s thinking.” If painting is not only a way of producing images but also a practice of bodily and temporal experience, then the operating conditions dictated by the material itself may, over long practice, in turn affect the painter’s way of thinking and logic of action."},{"t":"p","zh":"基于这一问题，下文以水性材料绘画与古典油画技法之间的对照为分析框架，讨论不同的材料及其物质属性如何在创作过程中形成不同的时间结构，并由此理解中国文化语境中“感兴”所指向的一种意义生成机制。","en":"Building on this question, what follows takes the contrast between water-based painting and classical oil painting technique as its analytical framework, discussing how different materials and their physical properties form different temporal structures in the creative process, and through this seeks to understand the mechanism of meaning-making to which ganxing points in the Chinese cultural context."},{"t":"h","zh":"二、从材料到行动：两种不同的发生结构","en":"2. From Material to Action: Two Different Structures of Occurrence"},{"t":"p","zh":"在中国文人画的实践中，水不仅是颜料的溶剂，更是时间的加速器。水性材料在宣纸上的物理表现——即迅速的毛细作用导致的渗透与纤维间的固着——造成了一种“时间的坍缩”。在古典油画中，由于油性介质干燥迟缓且具有遮盖力，时间被“空间化”了：艺术家可以在画布上进行反复的覆盖、涂抹与修改。这种逻辑本质上是“逼近（Approximation）”，即画面作为某种先验理念（Idea）的摹本，允许行动者在回溯中纠偏。","en":"In the practice of Chinese literati painting, water is not only a solvent for pigment but an accelerator of time. The physical behaviour of water-based materials on xuan paper, namely the penetration caused by rapid capillary action and the fixing among the fibres, produces a kind of “collapse of time”. In classical oil painting, because the oil medium dries slowly and has covering power, time is “spatialised”: the artist can repeatedly cover, apply and revise on the canvas. This logic is in essence one of “approximation”, in which the picture is a copy of some a priori Idea, and the actor is allowed to correct course by going back."},{"t":"p","zh":"从材料层面来看，水性材料、传统油画颜料与两者的支撑物在物理性质上都存在显著差异。水墨或其他水性颜料在纸面上的干燥速度较快，笔触一旦形成，往往难以被完全撤回或修正。绘画行为因此呈现出较强的即时性与不可逆性。创作者在落笔之前并不能对画面最终的呈现效果有着掌控式的规划，而是仅对整体气势与结构先进行初步预判。一旦进入操作过程，每一笔绘画的行动都需要承接并顺应已有画面之势、并进行引导或使其衍生。这个过程在持续推进的时间中展开。","en":"At the level of material, water-based materials, traditional oil paints and their respective supports differ markedly in physical properties. Ink or other water-based pigments dry quickly on paper, and once a brushstroke is made it is often hard to withdraw or correct completely. The act of painting therefore takes on a strong immediacy and irreversibility. Before putting brush to paper, the painter cannot plan the final appearance of the picture in a controlling way, but can only make a preliminary forecast of its overall momentum and structure. Once the process is under way, each stroke has to take up and follow the momentum of what is already on the paper, guiding it or letting it develop further. This process unfolds in continuously advancing time."},{"t":"p","zh":"相比之下，古典油画技法则允许更为复杂的修订过程。由于油性颜料干燥缓慢，画面在初步完成之后仍可以通过覆盖、刮除或重新塑形等方式进行反复调整。达·芬奇（Leonardo da Vinci）曾强调绘画是通过“增加与减少”来完善的。油性媒介的延展性（Malleability）允许创作者在空间维度上进行层累式的堆叠。在这一技术条件下，绘画更接近一种逐步逼近既定形式的过程。创作者在早期阶段所作出的判断并不具有终极性，它可以被暂时悬置，以便在后续工作中不断修正，为最终画面的呈现效果而服务。这种“空间化”的处理方式，实质上将时间转化为一种可以反复“回溯”的过程。","en":"By contrast, classical oil painting technique allows a more complex process of revision. Because oil paint dries slowly, the picture can still be adjusted again and again after its initial completion by covering, scraping or reshaping. Leonardo da Vinci stressed that painting is perfected through “adding and taking away”. The malleability of the oil medium allows the painter to build up layer upon layer in the spatial dimension. Under these technical conditions, painting is closer to a process of gradually approaching a predetermined form. The judgements a painter makes at an early stage are not final; they can be temporarily suspended so as to be corrected continually in later work, in service of the final appearance of the picture. This “spatialised” way of working in effect turns time into a process that can be repeatedly “retraced”."},{"t":"p","zh":"水性媒介在宣纸上的那种“干结”过程，更接近海德格尔（Martin Heidegger）所言的“真理的发生”——它不是对预设对象的再现，而是存在本身在特定瞬间的闪现。每一次落笔都是一次“去蔽”，其结果具有本体论意义上的终极性。需要在此说明的是，这种对比并非意在为两种媒介建立本质性的区分。水性材料内部同样存在可以反复调整的技法、洗掉部分笔墨，而油画传统中也包含大量一次完成的实践方式。本文所强调的，是在中西艺术史中较为典型的两种工作模式：一种以不可回撤的行动为特征，另一种则允许持续修订。正是在这一差异中，可以看到材料条件如何在实践层面塑造不同的行动结构。","en":"The process by which a water-based medium “sets” on xuan paper is closer to what Martin Heidegger called “the happening of truth”: it is not the representation of a preset object but the flashing forth of Being itself at a particular moment. Each stroke is an act of “unconcealment”, and its result has an ontological finality. It should be noted here that this comparison is not intended to establish an essential distinction between the two media. Within water-based materials there are also techniques that allow repeated adjustment, or washing away part of the ink, and the oil painting tradition also includes many practices completed in a single pass. What this paper emphasises are two working modes that are fairly typical in Chinese and Western art history: one characterised by irrevocable action, the other allowing continual revision. It is precisely in this difference that we can see how material conditions shape different structures of action at the level of practice."},{"t":"h","zh":"三、行动的时间结构：逼近理念与生成过程","en":"3. The Temporal Structure of Action: Approaching the Idea and the Process of Generation"},{"t":"p","zh":"如果进一步从时间经验的角度理解上述差异，可以发现两种绘画实践分别对应着不同的生成逻辑。","en":"If we understand the difference described above further from the angle of temporal experience, we find that the two painting practices correspond to different logics of generation."},{"t":"p","zh":"在允许反复修订的绘画过程中，创作往往呈现为一种逐步逼近既定目标的时间结构。艺术家在创作之初可以设想某种理想的画面形式，而具体的操作则通过不断调整与完善逐渐接近这一目标。在思想结构上，这种模式与西方形而上学传统中的“理念—摹本”逻辑具有某种可比性。在摄影术出现之前，这种“理念-摹本”的图解式功能一直主宰着西方绘画的呈现形态。","en":"In a painting process that permits repeated revision, creation often takes the form of a temporal structure that gradually approaches a set goal. At the outset the artist can envisage an ideal pictorial form, and the actual work approaches that goal through continuous adjustment and refinement. In terms of its structure of thought, this mode bears a certain comparability with the “Idea–copy” logic of the Western metaphysical tradition. Before the invention of photography, this illustrative “Idea–copy” function long dominated the forms in which Western painting presented itself."},{"t":"p","zh":"与之相对，在水性材料绘画中，由于行动具有较强的不可回撤性，创作更接近一种在时间中展开的生成过程。创作者在落笔之前或许拥有某种整体意图，但画面的最终形态并不会完全按照预设蓝本展开，而是在行动与材料的互动中逐渐显现。意义并不是对既有理念的再现，而是在行动过程中被不断触发与修正。","en":"In water-based painting, by contrast, because action is to a large degree irrevocable, creation is closer to a process of generation that unfolds in time. The painter may have some overall intention before the brush touches the paper, but the final form of the picture does not unfold entirely according to a preset blueprint; it gradually emerges through the interaction of action and material. Meaning is not the representation of a pre-existing Idea, but is continually triggered and revised in the course of action."},{"t":"p","zh":"这种结构与中国传统诗学中的“兴”具有某种相似性。自 《诗经》 以来，“兴”常被理解为一种由情境触发而生发意义的机制。在《文心雕龙》中，刘勰言：“兴者，起也。”“因物起兴。”学者叶嘉莹亦指出，“兴是诗人心灵在外物触动之下自然引发的感发活动”。在这一状态中，主体在面临某事时被内在触动，并与外部发生相融。人的情感、所处的环境与场域、文学或艺术表达，三者并非彼此分离，而是在某种尚未完全分化的状态中同时出现。因而在特定语言与形式尚未定型之前，对其选择与运用就已然开始。","en":"This structure bears a certain resemblance to xing (stirring, evocation) in traditional Chinese poetics. Since the Book of Songs (Shijing), xing has often been understood as a mechanism by which meaning arises when triggered by a situation. In The Literary Mind and the Carving of Dragons (Wenxin Diaolong), Liu Xie says: “Xing means to rise,” and “xing is raised in response to things.” The scholar Florence Chia-ying Yeh likewise points out that “xing is the activity of being stirred that arises naturally in the poet’s heart when moved by external things.” In this state, the subject facing some matter is moved inwardly and merges with what is outside. A person’s feelings, the surroundings and field in which they find themselves, and literary or artistic expression are not separate from one another, but appear at the same time in a state not yet fully differentiated. Thus, before a particular language or form has taken shape, the choice and use of it has already begun."},{"t":"p","zh":"墨绘画的逻辑是“生成（Emergence）”。一旦水滴触碰纸面，物理化学反应立即发生，这种不可逆转性迫使创作者进入一种“决战式”的临场状态。每一笔不仅是空间的占据，更是时间的质押。这种材料规定的“一次性”，使得文人画的创作过程变成了一种对他者的、对偶然性的极度开放。正如石涛所言“一画者，众有之本，万象之根”，这一笔下去，不存在回撤，只能顺势而为。这种承担后果的行动逻辑，是水性材料赋予艺术实践的伦理底色。","en":"The logic of ink painting is “emergence”. As soon as a drop of water touches the paper, a physical and chemical reaction takes place at once, and this irreversibility forces the painter into a state of presence as though in a decisive battle. Each stroke is not only the occupation of space but also a pledge of time. This “once-only” quality dictated by the material turns the creative process of literati painting into an extreme openness to the other and to chance. As Shitao said, “The One Stroke is the origin of all that exists, the root of the myriad phenomena”: once the stroke is laid down there is no withdrawing it; one can only follow the momentum. This logic of action that bears its consequences is the ethical ground that water-based materials give to artistic practice."},{"t":"h","zh":"四、“感兴”的中国绘画实践","en":"4. Ganxing in Chinese Painting Practice"},{"t":"p","zh":"王夫之的哲学体系为这种绘画实践提供了一个宏大的形而上学支撑。王氏反对宋儒将“理”视为超越万物的静止律令，他主张“理在气中”，即真理是在事物的演进过程（气化）中显现出来的。","en":"Wang Fuzhi’s philosophical system provides a grand metaphysical support for this kind of painting practice. Wang opposed the Song Confucians’ view of li (principle) as a static law transcending all things; he held that “principle lies within qi”, that is, truth reveals itself in the evolving process of things (the transformations of qi)."},{"t":"p","zh":"将此观点映射到文人画实践，我们可以发现一种同构性：","en":"Mapping this view onto the practice of literati painting, we can discern a kind of isomorphism:"},{"t":"p","zh":"“势”的推移： 作画者并非依仗一份精确的草图，而是根据第一笔落下的“势”来推导第二笔。","en":"The shifting of shi (momentum): the painter does not rely on a precise preliminary sketch, but works out the second stroke from the shi set in motion by the first."},{"t":"p","zh":"“几”的把握： 王夫之强调在变动不居中把握微小的契机（几），这正对应了水墨创作中对洇散、枯润等偶然效果的瞬间捕捉。","en":"Grasping ji (incipience): Wang Fuzhi stressed grasping the minute opportunity (ji) amid constant change, which corresponds exactly to the instantaneous capture of chance effects such as bleeding and spreading, dryness and moisture, in ink painting."},{"t":"p","zh":"主体的训练： 水性材料的不可撤回性，训练了一种“在流动中承担历史后果”的主体。这种主体的责任不是被外化给一个外在理念，而是一个嵌入流变时间、与客体共同生成的参与者。","en":"The training of the subject: the irrevocability of water-based materials trains a subject who “bears the historical consequences within the flow”. This subject’s responsibility is not externalised onto some outside Idea; it is that of a participant embedded in flowing time, coming into being together with the object."},{"t":"p","zh":"“兴”字所暗示的感兴之意，也包含了外物对内心的感发作用。“感兴”一词并不是一个在古典文献中被严格界定的哲学术语，而是由“兴”的诗学传统与中国思想中的感应观念长期叠合而形成的一种经验结构。它并非指向某种明确的概念体系，而是描述一种意义在行动过程尚未被完全概念化之前的生成状态。","en":"The sense of ganxing implied by the character xing also includes the stirring effect of external things on the heart. The term ganxing is not a philosophical concept strictly defined in the classical literature, but a structure of experience formed by the long overlapping of the poetic tradition of xing with the idea of ganying (sympathetic resonance) in Chinese thought. It does not point to any explicit conceptual system; rather it describes a state in which meaning is being generated in the course of action, before it has been fully conceptualised."},{"t":"p","zh":"在中国以笔墨书写为核心的文人绘画实践传统中，这种状态往往通过身体行动得以呈现。“皴”、“擦”、“勾”、“描”...这些我们耳熟能详的绘画技法，放在实践过程的语境中，实则是作画者的呼吸节律、身体重心的游动以及手腕握笔带来的笔触节奏，通过水与墨的流动在纸面之上所留下的痕迹。在绘画的整体上，进一步形成了我们常言的“气”“势”“迹”。这些痕迹既是物质性的，同时又承载着作画者行动发生时的时间经验。这些痕迹进一步以人的视觉为载体，通过人与人之间相同的身体构造和呼吸节律，进一步构建出一种作画者与观画者可共同交流的世界。","en":"In the tradition of literati painting centred on brush-and-ink writing in China, this state is often made manifest through bodily action. Cun (texture strokes), ca (rubbing), gou (outlining), miao (tracing)... these painting techniques so familiar to us are, in the context of the practice, really the traces left on the paper, through the flow of water and ink, by the painter’s rhythm of breathing, the shifting of the body’s centre of gravity, and the rhythm of strokes produced by the wrist holding the brush. Across the painting as a whole, they go on to form what we commonly call qi (vital energy), shi (momentum) and ji (trace). These traces are material, and at the same time they carry the temporal experience of the painter at the moment the action took place. Taking human vision as their carrier, and through the bodily structure and rhythm of breathing that people share, these traces further build a world in which painter and viewer can communicate with each other."},{"t":"cap","zh":"图 1 元 王蒙 松下著书图（局部）|纸本水墨","en":"Fig. 1 Wang Meng (Yuan dynasty), Writing Books under the Pines (detail) | ink on paper"},{"t":"img","src":"e04-01.webp"},{"t":"cap","zh":"266.7x70.5厘米 克利夫兰艺术博物馆藏","en":"266.7 × 70.5 cm, Cleveland Museum of Art"},{"t":"p","zh":"值得注意的是，在中国历史语境中，从事绘画实践的人往往同时也是政治与文化领域的精英阶层。文人士大夫并非仅以雇主的形式参与到艺术文化的发展与建设中，他们同时还以职业手工艺人的身份进行绘画，将绘画视为修身与表达的一种方式。因此，在绘画实践中形成的行动逻辑——例如对不可回撤行为的承担、对整体趋势的判断以及对偶然性的包容——并不会局限于艺术领域，而是通过书写、治理与日常交往逐渐扩散到更广泛的社会生活之中。","en":"It is worth noting that in the Chinese historical context, those who practised painting were often also members of the political and cultural elite. Literati-officials did not take part in the development and building of art and culture only as patrons; they also painted as practising craftsmen, regarding painting as a means of self-cultivation and expression. Hence the logic of action formed in painting practice, such as taking responsibility for irrevocable acts, judging the overall trend and accommodating chance, was not confined to the field of art, but gradually spread through writing, governance and everyday interaction into wider social life."},{"t":"p","zh":"从这一角度来看，与其说中国人的文化“基因里带水”，不如说在长期以水性材料为主导的图像传统中，创作者在实践中被持续训练为一种在流动时间中承担行动后果的主体。","en":"Seen from this angle, rather than saying that Chinese culture “has water in its genes”, it would be better to say that within a long image tradition dominated by water-based materials, painters were continually trained through practice to become subjects who bear the consequences of their actions in flowing time."},{"t":"p","zh":"如果从思想史角度进一步考察这一问题，可以将其与明清之际思想家 王夫之 的历史观进行对话。","en":"If we examine this question further from the perspective of intellectual history, we can bring it into dialogue with the historical view of Wang Fuzhi, the thinker of the Ming–Qing transition."},{"t":"p","zh":"王夫之强调“事”“势”“几”的展开性。他在《读通鉴论》中指出：“势之所趋，人不得不然。”他认为人的行动始终处于不断变化的情势之中。“几者，动之微也。”行动的合理性并不能在事前被完全确定，而只能在事件展开的过程中得到检验。在其“理在事中”“理随气化”的理解中，牟宗三认为“理在气中展开，而非超越气而存在。”人并非依据某种先验理念行事，而是在具体情境中作出判断并承担其后果。","en":"Wang Fuzhi emphasised the unfolding character of shi (events), shi (momentum) and ji (incipience). In his Commentary on Reading the Comprehensive Mirror (Du Tongjian Lun) he wrote: “Where momentum tends, people cannot but follow.” He held that human action always takes place within ever-changing circumstances. “Ji is the subtle beginning of movement.” The rightness of an action cannot be fully determined in advance, but can only be tested as the event unfolds. Regarding his understanding that “principle lies within events” and “principle follows the transformations of qi”, Mou Zongsan held that “principle unfolds within qi, rather than existing beyond qi.” People do not act according to some a priori Idea, but make judgements in concrete situations and bear their consequences."},{"t":"p","zh":"这种对时间与行动关系的理解，与文人画中主体的实践经验形成了有趣的呼应：意义与判断并非在事先被提前设定，也不是在事后被当作理念一样地回溯，而是在行动展开的当下，被迫承担并持续修正，并在不可回撤的行动过程中逐渐显现。因此，文人士大夫的绘画实践不是仅停留在了艺术实践内部，还与其在生活和参与政治治理的观念之间，相互渗透、相互影响，同时交织了一种关于行动、时间与责任的生命形态.....","en":"This understanding of the relation between time and action forms an interesting echo with the practical experience of the subject in literati painting: meaning and judgement are neither set in advance nor retraced afterwards as though they were Ideas; rather, in the present moment of unfolding action, they must be borne and continually revised, and they gradually emerge in the course of irrevocable action. The painting practice of the literati-officials therefore did not remain only within artistic practice; it interpenetrated and influenced their ideas about life and participation in political governance, weaving together a form of life concerned with action, time and responsibility....."},{"t":"h","zh":"五、现代绘画中的再发现","en":"5. Rediscovery in Modern Painting"},{"t":"p","zh":"现代社会起源于理性主义和基督教传统的西方。在希伯来-希腊轴心文明中，两者分别以“理念”或“上帝”作为追问源头，意义是提前成立的。而关于直接的、神话式、混乱的“人与世界的关系”长期被悬置于讨论范围之外。自从尼采宣布，“上帝死了”，“存在问题”就从至高理念的解散中脱胎而出。而西方现代艺术也开始重视起瞬间、身体与行动，回溯那天地混沌的“狄奥尼索斯精神”。十九世纪以来，人们逐渐开始反思、推翻传统绘画的创作方式，许多艺术家通过强调行动、书写与身体经验，重新将时间的即时性引入绘画实践。哲学家们如 Gilles Deleuze 对“生成”与“事件”的强调、Henri Bergson 关于“绵延”的时间理论，也在思想层面讨论了行动与时间的开放性。","en":"Modern society originated in the West, out of rationalism and the Christian tradition. In the Hebrew–Greek axial civilisations, the two took the “Idea” and “God” respectively as the source of inquiry, and meaning was established in advance. The direct, mythic, chaotic “relationship between human beings and the world” was long suspended outside the scope of discussion. Ever since Nietzsche proclaimed that “God is dead”, the “question of Being” has emerged from the dissolution of the supreme Idea. Western modern art, too, began to value the instant, the body and action, turning back to the “Dionysian spirit” of the primordial chaos of heaven and earth. Since the nineteenth century, people gradually began to reflect on and overturn the traditional ways of making paintings, and many artists, by emphasising action, writing and bodily experience, reintroduced the immediacy of time into painting practice. Philosophers such as Gilles Deleuze, with his emphasis on “becoming” and the “event”, and Henri Bergson, with his theory of time as “duration”, also discussed the openness of action and time at the level of thought."},{"t":"p","zh":"有如 Cy Twombly 和纽曼的绘画，他们通过近似书写的线条与痕迹，使绘画再次成为行动发生的记录。正如德勒兹在《意义的逻辑》之中所开宗明义：“事件并不是事物，也不是实体，而是在事物之中发生的生成。”","en":"In the paintings of Cy Twombly and Barnett Newman, for example, lines and traces akin to writing make painting once again a record of action taking place. As Deleuze states at the very outset of The Logic of Sense: “The event is not a thing, nor a substance, but a becoming that happens within things.”"},{"t":"cap","zh":"图 2[美] Cy Twombly Untitled|布面综合绘画","en":"Fig. 2 [USA] Cy Twombly, Untitled | mixed media on canvas"},{"t":"img","src":"e04-02.jpeg"},{"t":"cap","zh":"2.4×2米 1985都灵现代和当代艺术市民画廊藏","en":"2.4 × 2 m, 1985, collection of the Galleria Civica d’Arte Moderna e Contemporanea, Turin"},{"t":"p","zh":"也就是，说对于“感兴”的讨论并不意味着水性材料绘画具有某种文化上的独占性。事实上，在宇宙观与艺术实践相结合的结构上，现代社会再一次与来自遥远过去的“感兴”相遇了。","en":"That is to say, the discussion of ganxing does not imply that water-based painting enjoys some kind of cultural exclusivity. In fact, in the way cosmology and artistic practice are bound together, modern society has once again encountered the ganxing of the distant past."},{"t":"h","zh":"结语","en":"Conclusion"},{"t":"p","zh":"在一幅绘画作品中所留下的笔墨痕迹，可以成为不同时间、空间之间人类经验、身体得以相互连接的通道。","en":"The traces of brush and ink left in a painting can become a channel through which human experience and bodies across different times and places are connected to one another."},{"t":"p","zh":"而从材料实践的角度重新审视中国绘画传统，可以看到水性材料不仅是一种技术媒介，同时也是一种时间经验的训练方式。在长期实践中，它促成了一种以行动生成意义的创作结构。","en":"Re-examining the Chinese painting tradition from the standpoint of material practice, we can see that water-based materials are not only a technical medium but also a way of training temporal experience. Over long practice, they fostered a creative structure in which meaning is generated through action."},{"t":"p","zh":"“感兴”并不只是文学或诗学中的概念，它的发生，来自于一个文明的童年时空，是一种意义的生成机制。在这种机制中，意义与行为的最终目标并非被观念预先安排，而是在行动、事况与感受尚未分离的状态中交织并逐渐显现。","en":"Ganxing is not merely a concept of literature or poetics; its occurrence comes from the childhood of a civilisation, and it is a mechanism for generating meaning. In this mechanism, the ultimate aims of meaning and conduct are not arranged in advance by ideas, but interweave and gradually emerge in a state in which action, circumstance and feeling have not yet separated."},{"t":"p","zh":"如今，在这个文化日益趋于扁平与同质化的世界。追溯本土的传统文化，深挖其可能性与启发性，对于本国文化主体性的建立和在全球语境下对文化多元性的追求，都有重大意义。","en":"Today we live in a world whose culture is becoming ever flatter and more homogeneous. Tracing native traditional culture back to its sources and digging into its possibilities and insights is of great significance both for building the cultural subjectivity of one’s own country and for the pursuit of cultural diversity in a global context."},{"t":"p","zh":"人工智能科技革命正在传统价值体系不断受到挑战的当代社会情境中如火如荼的进行。对艺术创作而言，守护人的尊严、保留人之为人的情感、维系人与人之间带有温度的交流，已经是其不可推免与延迟的责任。“感兴”的这种强调‘临场决断’与‘身体热度’的行动机制，以及与其观念相交织的伦理态度，可以带来更多启发。","en":"The technological revolution of artificial intelligence is in full swing in a contemporary society whose traditional value systems are constantly being challenged. For artistic creation, safeguarding human dignity, preserving the emotions that make us human, and sustaining warm exchange between people have become responsibilities that cannot be shirked or postponed. Ganxing, as a mechanism of action that emphasises “decision in the moment” and “bodily warmth”, together with the ethical attitude intertwined with its ideas, can offer further inspiration."}]},{"id":"W-2026-04","n":14,"title":{"zh":"申请艺术驻地时的随记","en":"Notes Written While Applying for Art Residencies"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2026-03-28","genre":"随笔","summary":{"zh":"在申请艺术驻地项目的过程中，我根据项目主题比如二战集中营和force labour、当地馆藏艺术品研究、致敬艺术品无用这些，做了一些proposal，也逐渐发现了在做艺术公共项目时，我的一些观念、立场。我会聚焦于行动、劳动与公共性的讨论。","en":"In the process of applying for art residency programmes, I wrote a number of proposals in response to project themes such as Second World War concentration camps and forced labour, research on local museum collections, and paying tribute to the uselessness of art, and along the way I gradually discovered some of my own ideas and positions on public art projects. I focus on questions of action, labour and publicness."},"words":3780,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"在申请艺术驻地项目的过程中，我根据项目主题比如二战集中营和force labour、当地馆藏艺术品研究、致敬艺术品无用这些，做了一些proposal，也逐渐发现了在做艺术公共项目时，我的一些观念、立场。我会聚焦于行动、劳动与公共性的讨论。历史往往被制度化为抽象的语言系统，与真实的生命感知相分离。因此，记忆沦为了信息档案，而其感官、身体及政治维度的意义，正逐渐从公共话语和集体意识中退场。","en":"In the process of applying for art residency programmes, I wrote a number of proposals in response to project themes such as Second World War concentration camps and forced labour, research on local museum collections, and paying tribute to the uselessness of art, and along the way I gradually discovered some of my own ideas and positions on public art projects. I focus on questions of action, labour and publicness. History is often institutionalised into an abstract system of language, cut off from real, lived perception. Memory has thus been reduced to an information archive, while its sensory, bodily and political meanings are gradually withdrawing from public discourse and collective consciousness."},{"t":"p","zh":"与此同时，我希望可以引入儒家的“关系”伦理。记得大历史学家许倬云先生临终前不久曾做过一个结论，主要的意思是，当今世界的一些困境，可以向儒家文化吸取营养。","en":"At the same time, I hope to bring in the Confucian ethics of “relationship”. I remember that not long before he died, the great historian Hsu Cho-yun drew a conclusion, the gist of which was that for some of the predicaments of today’s world, we can draw nourishment from Confucian culture."},{"t":"p","zh":"就像是大一的时候学黑格尔的艺术终结论，那时我才刚开始走我的艺术道路，怎么艺术几百年前就终结了？学到丹托，艺术还是终结的。我没懂。我当时知识信息储备量不足，理解概念理念也无法将其归于某个框架，所以，我只是在心里埋了这个疑惑，一直在去寻找这个答案，希望某天可以明白。而今天终于找到答案：艺术真的终结了。","en":"It’s like when I studied Hegel’s thesis of the end of art in my first year of university. I had only just set out on my path as an artist—how could art have ended centuries ago? Then we got to Arthur Danto, and art was still over. I didn’t get it. At the time I didn’t have enough knowledge, and even when I understood the concepts and ideas I couldn’t place them in any framework. So I just buried the question in my heart and kept looking for the answer, hoping that one day I would understand. And today I have finally found the answer: art really has ended."},{"t":"p","zh":"许先生的话也是如此，在我的心里埋下一个疑惑。许先生自幼接受中国精英教育，后又移居美国数十载接受西方精英教育并逐渐成为博学的历史学家。这样的人，说出这句话，一定是有原因的，说不定他真的看到了一些潜在可能的联结，这条路真的走得通？于是，我将很多时间放在研习新儒家的资料上，我要找到这个答案，我希望真的可以有行得通的，就算行不通，我也要知道具体为什么行不通。","en":"Mr Hsu’s words were the same: they planted a question in my heart. Mr Hsu received an elite Chinese education from childhood, then moved to the United States, where over several decades he received an elite Western education and gradually became an erudite historian. When someone like that says something like this, there must be a reason. Maybe he really saw some latent connections—could this road really lead somewhere? So I have spent a great deal of time studying New Confucian writings. I want to find the answer. I hope there really is something that works, and even if it doesn’t, I want to know exactly why it doesn’t."},{"t":"p","zh":"从一月份开始写“空间伦理”这个论文，结合中西理论（主要是新儒家和现代、后现代理论），还有一些学科比如材料学、身体美学、心理学的一些“纤维”，发明了一个“空间行为压强模型”【P = (F × D × C) / (A × M)】。","en":"Since January I have been writing a paper on “spatial ethics”. Combining Chinese and Western theory (mainly New Confucianism and modern and postmodern theory) with some “fibres” from disciplines such as materials science, somaesthetics and psychology, I invented a “spatial behaviour pressure model” [P = (F × D × C) / (A × M)]."},{"t":"p","zh":"我觉得我找到了一个小口子，但不是说撕破新自由主义的逻辑，而是说，不冲突但也可以不被完全异化的一个小口子。打算这两天找完引用文献就去投刊。","en":"I feel I have found a small opening—not one that tears apart the logic of neoliberalism, but a small opening through which one need not be in conflict with it, and yet need not be completely alienated either. I plan to submit it to a journal as soon as I finish gathering the references in the next couple of days."},{"t":"h","zh":"Force labor","en":"Forced Labour"},{"t":"p","zh":"接着讲我的艺术驻地。","en":"Now, back to my art residencies."},{"t":"p","zh":"我在斯图加特的akademie solitude的网站上找到了关于二战强迫劳动的驻地，作了artistic concept的陈述、project proposal和public event 的设计。","en":"On the website of Akademie Solitude in Stuttgart I found a residency about forced labour in the Second World War, and I wrote an artistic concept statement, a project proposal and a design for a public event."},{"t":"p","zh":"Concept大概是这样的：中国人，我们经历了二战后剧烈的社会转型与政治动荡，社会形态的更迭极其迅猛。然而，通过制度惯性与代际传递，战前的某些社会结构与意识形态依然在潜移默化地发挥影响，编织进日常生活、空间形态及人际互动之中。同时，在全球化与数字媒介的冲击下，“信息爆炸”与“回声壁效应”加剧了群体间的认知隔阂。因此，在我的成长经历中，面对现代化的加速、集体创伤、尚未弥合的历史断裂、沟通的失效等等。我试图探寻一种艺术路径，在历史记忆与当下感知之间，在作者与观者之间重建桥梁。","en":"The concept went roughly like this: we Chinese went through drastic social transformation and political upheaval after the Second World War, and social forms changed with extreme speed. Yet through institutional inertia and intergenerational transmission, certain pre-war social structures and ideologies still exert a quiet influence, woven into daily life, spatial forms and interpersonal interaction. At the same time, under the impact of globalisation and digital media, the “information explosion” and the “echo-chamber effect” have deepened the cognitive divides between groups. So, growing up, I faced accelerating modernisation, collective trauma, historical ruptures not yet healed, the breakdown of communication, and so on. I am trying to find an artistic path that rebuilds bridges between historical memory and present perception, and between author and viewer."},{"t":"p","zh":"Project proposal是一个半透明绘画装置。艺术概念：“半透明”作为公共性的隐喻。","en":"The project proposal is a translucent painting installation. Artistic concept: “translucency” as a metaphor for publicness."},{"t":"p","zh":"绘画作为一种媒介，在呈现复杂的社会关系方面存在结构性的局限，也始终与观者、与真实世界隔着屏障。它于平面之上，平面留住它让它无法离开。基于此，我结合了半透明绘画作一种空间装置的实践方式。关于“公共性”的隐喻：“半透明性”的物理材料属性，既非完全敞开，也非完全封闭，而是在“揭示”与“遮蔽”之间保持一种动态平衡。在特定的场域（如岛屿或特定历史遗址）中，这种流动的边界具有特殊意义，它不仅指向空间，更指向历史与身份的塑造。绘画可以作为身体痕迹，被视为个体身体行动的留存，在个人维度上保留“此在”的“时间-空间-主体 ”的痕迹。","en":"As a medium, painting has structural limitations in presenting complex social relations, and it is always separated by a barrier from the viewer and from the real world. It lies on a flat surface, and the surface holds it and will not let it leave. On this basis, I have brought in translucent painting as a practice of spatial installation. As for the metaphor of “publicness”: translucency, as a physical property of the material, is neither fully open nor fully closed, but keeps a dynamic balance between “revealing” and “concealing”. In a particular site (such as an island or a specific historical site), this fluid boundary takes on special meaning: it points not only to space but also to the shaping of history and identity. Painting can serve as a bodily trace, regarded as what remains of an individual’s bodily action, preserving at the personal level the traces of the “time–space–subject” of Dasein (“being-there”)."},{"t":"p","zh":"与此同时，借助支撑介质的半透明特性，营造一种流动的空间状态。光线、湿度以及观众的移动都将积极参与到视觉经验的生成中。","en":"At the same time, the translucency of the supporting medium is used to create a fluid spatial state. Light, humidity and the movement of the audience will all take an active part in generating the visual experience."},{"t":"p","zh":"而作品在被艺术家完成之后并非终点，而是处于一种持续形成的状态——通过无数观察者的介入与互动，在不同的光线、时间下，作品与不同的观者产生的不同链接方式，总是在使场域改变着。过去与当下的人与人就这样将生命体验相互融合，在永远不会重复的数个“当下”。","en":"And the work’s completion by the artist is not its end point; it remains in a state of continual formation. Through the intervention and interaction of countless observers, under different light and at different times, the different ways the work connects with different viewers keep changing the site. In this way people of the past and the present merge their life experiences with one another, across several “presents” that will never repeat."},{"t":"p","zh":"Public event作为“活态档案（living archive）”的感知实验社会互动与参与。","en":"The public event as a perceptual experiment of a “living archive”: social interaction and participation."},{"t":"p","zh":"这侧重于通过视觉与空间的实验，建立一个连接人的平台，让人们通过艺术品重新审视历史。","en":"This focuses on using visual and spatial experiments to build a platform that connects people, so that they can re-examine history through the artwork."},{"t":"p","zh":"感知实验（空间共存实验室）：邀请参与者在装置介入前进入特定场域。重点不在于知识的单向传递，而在于观察历史叙事（如关于强迫劳动的碎片）如何调制个体的身体存在感、空间定位以及伦理敏感度。在地调研与视觉转化完成后，再次邀请公众进入空间。此时，艺术装置作为一个“反射触发器”，促使参与者重新定位自己在【历史（也可以说是世界或者公共领域、人类社会...总之是一个非线性时间的、一个较大的范围）】中的角色。","en":"Perceptual experiment (a laboratory of spatial coexistence): participants are invited into a specific site before the installation intervenes. The emphasis is not on one-way transmission of knowledge but on observing how historical narratives (such as fragments about forced labour) modulate an individual’s sense of bodily presence, spatial orientation and ethical sensitivity. Once the on-site research and visual transformation are complete, the public is invited into the space again. At this point the art installation acts as a “reflective trigger”, prompting participants to reposition their own role within [history (one could also say the world, or the public sphere, human society... in short, a larger scope, one of non-linear time)]."},{"t":"h","zh":"去作者化的跨文化对话","en":"De-authored Cross-Cultural Dialogue"},{"t":"p","zh":"我觉得在一件艺术品中，让人产生身体上的物理介入至关重要。我不希望将个人观点强加于听者，我不赞同让华丽的辞藻为艺术品做壳，我认为不应该作为一个艺术品的制造者而居高临下，因此我觉得，比起陈述，我们应该更关注参与的过程。这两次public events的设置，在艺术品完成的前后都令观者介入——作品既是与他们共同完成的，也是为他们而作的。让装置成为关于移动、伦理感知与空间记忆的“活态档案”。这不仅是一次关于“去作者化”的实验，也是可以跨文化的、人本主义的对话。","en":"I think it is crucial for an artwork to bring people into physical, bodily involvement. I don’t want to impose my personal views on the listener; I don’t approve of using ornate language as a shell for an artwork; and I don’t think one should look down on others from the position of the maker of an artwork. So I think that, rather than statements, we should pay more attention to the process of participation. These two public events bring viewers in both before and after the artwork is finished—the work is both made together with them and made for them. Let the installation become a “living archive” of movement, ethical perception and spatial memory. This is not only an experiment in “de-authorship” but also a dialogue that can be cross-cultural and humanist."},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术圈的人们总会重复别人的话。他们用知名学者的观点，来去阐释自己观画的感受。比如，丹托曾说，艺术灭亡、艺术走向观念。作为策展人、艺术品dealer、藏家、艺术家自己.....这些人就将这句话变成接力棒，在不同的人嘴里传来传去，他们不会去真的走到这个话语的内部——他们并不知道自己在说什么，他们只是知道，这是公认学者说过的话，因此重复是安全的。一开始或许是为掩盖自己“不懂”的局促，后来，发现自己不需要真的懂，只需要put it on act，就可以在安全区。人们倡导个人表达、个性，可自己却将自己囚禁在这些滚过来覆过去的话语中。","en":"People in the art world are always repeating what others have said. They use the views of well-known scholars to explain their own feelings about looking at paintings. For example, Danto once said that art has died, that art has turned into ideas. Curators, art dealers, collectors, artists themselves..... these people turn the sentence into a relay baton passed from mouth to mouth. They never really step inside the statement—they don’t know what they are saying; all they know is that a recognised scholar said it, so repeating it is safe. At first it may be to cover the awkwardness of “not understanding”; later they find they don’t need to really understand, they just need to put it on as an act, and they can stay in the safe zone. People champion personal expression and individuality, yet they imprison themselves in these phrases that get rolled back and forth over and over."},{"t":"p","zh":"当套话说多了，人自己也会变得麻木。而艺术家由于常常泡在这锅迷魂汤中，也会从一开始的疑惑、惊讶、兴奋、怀疑，到后来自己也信以为真，以为自己真的是像包装话术一样去创作的，从此以后、换汤不换药地产出那同质的、自以为是的商品。所我觉得个人主义是有毒的。而“去作者化”，可以让“语言”不必必然的汇聚于一个个体上，可以让解释、对话的平台与通道多一些可能。","en":"When you say stock phrases often enough, you go numb yourself. And because artists are so often steeped in this bewitching brew, they too go from initial puzzlement, surprise, excitement and doubt to eventually believing it themselves, thinking they really do create the way the packaging rhetoric says, and from then on they keep turning out the same homogeneous, self-satisfied commodities—new bottles, same old wine. So I think individualism is toxic. “De-authorship”, on the other hand, means that “language” need not necessarily converge on a single individual, and it can open up more possibilities for platforms and channels of interpretation and dialogue."},{"t":"h","zh":"还有一个日本的岛屿驻地","en":"And a Residency on a Japanese Island"},{"t":"p","zh":"Project proposal谷歌直接翻译过来是这样的：","en":"Put straight through Google Translate, the project proposal reads like this:"},{"t":"quote","zh":"“我的理论研究聚焦于关于行动、劳动与公共性的探讨，并将其放在儒家语境中；这使我意识到，作为一种媒介，绘画在呈现社会关系方面具有某种结构性的局限。","en":"“My theoretical research focuses on the discussion of action, labour and publicness, and places it within a Confucian context; this has made me aware that, as a medium, painting has a certain structural limitation in presenting social relations."},{"t":"quote","zh":"在驻留期间，我将以当地的环境为研究基石，探索将其转化为艺术表达的潜在路径。最终呈现的作品将体现一种由环境、材料与身体三者相互作用所生成的结构。","en":"During the residency, I will take the local environment as the cornerstone of my research and explore potential ways of transforming it into artistic expression. The work finally presented will embody a structure generated by the interaction of environment, material and body."},{"t":"quote","zh":"基于这一洞察，我将构建一种融合了绘画与半透明空间装置的创作实践。","en":"Based on this insight, I will build a creative practice that combines painting with translucent spatial installation."},{"t":"quote","zh":"其中的绘画作品将作为身体行动留下的痕迹，在个体层面保留一种时间性的感知；","en":"The paintings within it will serve as traces left by bodily action, preserving a temporal perception at the individual level;"},{"t":"quote","zh":"与此同时，其载体材料所具备的半透明特质将营造出一种流动的空间状态，使光线、湿度以及观者的移动能够积极地参与到视觉体验的生成过程之中。","en":"at the same time, the translucent quality of the supporting material will create a fluid spatial state, allowing light, humidity and the movement of viewers to take an active part in generating the visual experience."},{"t":"quote","zh":"通过这种方式，艺术作品即使在初步完成后，依然处于一种持续生成的状态——它在无数观者及其观看行为的互动中不断被重新生成。","en":"In this way, even after its initial completion, the artwork remains in a state of continual generation—it is constantly regenerated through interaction with countless viewers and their acts of looking."},{"t":"quote","zh":"在此，“半透明”不仅作为一种物质属性而存在，更作为“公共性”的一种隐喻：它既非全然敞开，亦非全然封闭，而是在显露与隐匿之间维持着一种动态的平衡。在岛屿这一特定的语境下，这些流动的边界被赋予了特殊的意义，其关联性不仅指向空间，更延伸至历史与身份认同的层面。作品的视觉参考图请参阅下方图像；最终的展览呈现形式将在完成现场勘察后予以确定。”","en":"Here, “translucency” exists not only as a material property but also as a metaphor for “publicness”: it is neither fully open nor fully closed, but maintains a dynamic balance between disclosure and concealment. In the specific context of an island, these fluid boundaries are given special meaning, their relevance pointing not only to space but extending to the levels of history and identity. For visual references for the work, please see the images below; the final form of the exhibition will be decided after the site survey is complete.”"},{"t":"h","zh":"感触和小结尾","en":"Thoughts, and a Short Ending"},{"t":"p","zh":"写了几个proposal，就发现，我自己的很多内容也是在自我重复。","en":"After writing a few proposals, I found that a lot of my own content is self-repetition too."},{"t":"p","zh":"抽象的理论循环中的价值虽然是合逻辑的，但在与真实世界的连接中，其并不能真实指向具体价值。Proposal中的作品在被完成之前就已经死了。","en":"The value inside the loop of abstract theory may be logical, but in its connection with the real world it cannot truly point to any concrete value. The work in a proposal is already dead before it is ever made."},{"t":"p","zh":"绘画在旧的世界死了。新的艺术家是已经去世的人。","en":"Painting died in the old world. The new artists are people who have already died."},{"t":"p","zh":"很多艺术事件也是由自我指涉和一个又一个套在一起的谎言构建起来的。Olafur将冰岛的冰搬到巴黎的市中心，以此引发人们对气候变暖的关注。这一“艺术”行为让冰岛的冰减少了，让巴黎的市中心多了一摊水，并在过程中调动大量人力物力去运输和清理。他还美名其曰，这是在宣传气候变暖。一堆人还在后面附和。这实在太搞笑了。只是一个案例，还有大量这样的例子。","en":"Many art events, too, are built out of self-reference and lies nested one inside another. Olafur moved ice from Iceland to the centre of Paris to draw people’s attention to global warming. This “art” action meant less ice in Iceland and an extra puddle of water in the centre of Paris, and along the way it mobilised a great deal of manpower and resources to transport and clean up. And he gave it the fine name of raising awareness about global warming. A whole crowd of people chimed in behind him. It’s just too ridiculous. That’s only one case; there are plenty of examples like it."},{"t":"p","zh":"当然这是带着主观和立场去看这件事，我这么去写并不客观。但这又不是论文，这是我自己的账号，我怎么想的我就怎么说。","en":"Of course, I’m looking at this subjectively and from a position, and writing it this way isn’t objective. But this isn’t a paper; this is my own account, and I say what I think."},{"t":"p","zh":"这段时间，我制定了两个任务，第一个任务是为传统文化找一些现代性转化，这件事情在时间上是有截止点的，因为个人的探索总是有限，总是会过时的，TA创造的价值也并不在时间上持续，并且这个的价值不具有普遍性，它不是对每个人都有效的。在社会结构上，它多是作为政治文化输出以及经济促进消费绩效的“工具”。第二条线是保护环境，人类和自然的关系是征服还是天人合一我想在这个时代答案已不证自明。人类只是地球的过客。而作为地球，对于地球上的所有生命来说，它是起源也是终点。因此对地球的保护是永恒的、无法被完成的任务。主体亦不需要从第二个任务中获得什么个人声誉，也不用被“想死后留下什么东西”这种念头所囚禁。只需要身心合一，让劳动工作和行动完美的协调，让自己所在的沙漠本身变成绿洲。","en":"During this period I have set myself two tasks. The first is to find some modern transformations for traditional culture. This task has a cut-off point in time, because an individual’s exploration is always limited and always goes out of date; the value it creates does not last over time, and that value is not universal—it does not hold for everyone. In terms of social structure, it mostly serves as a “tool” for political and cultural export and for boosting consumption and economic performance. The second line is protecting the environment. Whether the relationship between humans and nature is one of conquest or of tianren heyi (the unity of heaven and humankind)—I think in this era the answer is self-evident. Humans are only passing guests on the earth. And the earth, for all the life on it, is both origin and end. So protecting the earth is an eternal task that can never be completed. Nor does the subject need to gain any personal reputation from the second task, or be imprisoned by the thought of “wanting to leave something behind after death”. One need only unite body and mind, bring labour, work and action into perfect harmony, and let the very desert one stands in become an oasis."}]},{"id":"W-2026-05","n":2,"title":{"zh":"从场域到修身：新儒家伦理的空间生成路径","en":"From Field to Xiushen: The Spatial Generative Path of New Confucian Ethics"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2026-04-19","genre":"论文","summary":{"zh":"整体而言，本文尝试将新儒家伦理转化为可实践的空间机制，为公共艺术的探索新的思路。","en":"Overall, this paper attempts to translate New Confucian ethics into a practicable spatial mechanism, offering new ideas for the exploration of public art."},"words":11117,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"摘  要：围绕牟宗三“良知自我坎陷”命题，从分析传统儒家在面对科学与民主时的结构性张力，再到反思西方以冲突与妥协为基础的现代性逻辑所带来的工具理性扩张与伦理困境。首先将“冲突”的本体性前提转化为儒家的“时中”之关系。在此基础上，本文批判传统“修身—道德”的线性路径在新自由主义语境中的失效，提出“以道德反向引导修身”的路径倒置。通过构建“场域—身体—材料”三重结构，主张借助空间设计、感知触发与材料质感，在前反思层引导个体行为，形成低冲突的公共秩序；将公共空间之场域作为“抽象他者”，并作为个体反思和修身的入口。","en":"Abstract: Centring on Mou Zongsan’s proposition of the “self-negation of liangzhi” (liangzhi ziwo kanxian, the self-restriction of innate moral knowing), this paper moves from an analysis of the structural tension that traditional Confucianism faces when confronted with science and democracy to a reflection on the expansion of instrumental reason and the ethical dilemmas brought about by the Western logic of modernity, which is grounded in conflict and compromise. It first transforms the ontological premise of “conflict” into the Confucian relation of shizhong (timely centrality). On this basis, the paper criticizes the failure of the traditional linear path of “self-cultivation → morality” in the neoliberal context and proposes an inversion of that path: “using morality to guide self-cultivation in reverse.” By constructing a threefold structure of “field–body–material,” it argues for guiding individual behaviour at the pre-reflective level through spatial design, perceptual triggering and the texture of materials, so as to form a low-conflict public order; the field of public space is treated as an “abstract other” and as an entry point for individual reflection and self-cultivation."},{"t":"p","zh":"整体而言，本文尝试将新儒家伦理转化为可实践的空间机制，为公共艺术的探索新的思路。","en":"Overall, this paper attempts to translate New Confucian ethics into a practicable spatial mechanism, offering new ideas for the exploration of public art."},{"t":"p","zh":"关键词：新儒家；新自由主义；美学；空间伦理","en":"Keywords: New Confucianism; neoliberalism; aesthetics; spatial ethics"},{"t":"p","zh":"Abstract: AbstactTakes New Confucian responses to modernity as its theoretical background and explores pathways for reconstructing Confucian ethics in contemporary society. Centering on Mou Zongsan’s proposition of the “self-negation (self-retreat) of moral intuition,” it begins by analyzing the structural tension traditional Confucianism faces when encountering science and democracy, and then reflects on the ethical dilemmas and expansion of instrumental rationality produced by the Western modern logic grounded in conflict and compromise. The paper first transforms the ontological premise of “conflict” into the Confucian relational concept of timeliness and balance (shizhong).On this basis, it critiques the failure of the traditional linear path of “self-cultivation leading to morality” under neoliberal conditions, and proposes instead an inverted approach in which morality guides self-cultivation. By constructing a tripartite framework of “field–body–material,” the paper argues that spatial design, sensory activation, and material qualities can guide individual behavior at a pre-reflective level, thereby fostering a low-conflict public order. Public space is thus conceived as an “abstract other,” serving as an entry point for individual reflection and self-cultivation.Finally, the paper introduces an AI-based system for ethical generation in space, discussing its feasibility in dynamically facilitating the transformation from “space–behavior–ethics–morality,” while also addressing potential risks of alienation. Overall, the study seeks to translate New Confucian ethics into a practicable spatial mechanism, offering a new approach to the formation of public morality in contemporary contexts.","en":"Abstract: This paper takes New Confucian responses to modernity as its theoretical background and explores pathways for reconstructing Confucian ethics in contemporary society. Centering on Mou Zongsan’s proposition of the “self-negation (self-retreat) of moral intuition,” it begins by analyzing the structural tension traditional Confucianism faces when encountering science and democracy, and then reflects on the ethical dilemmas and expansion of instrumental rationality produced by the Western modern logic grounded in conflict and compromise. The paper first transforms the ontological premise of “conflict” into the Confucian relational concept of timeliness and balance (shizhong). On this basis, it critiques the failure of the traditional linear path of “self-cultivation leading to morality” under neoliberal conditions, and proposes instead an inverted approach in which morality guides self-cultivation. By constructing a tripartite framework of “field–body–material,” the paper argues that spatial design, sensory activation, and material qualities can guide individual behavior at a pre-reflective level, thereby fostering a low-conflict public order. Public space is thus conceived as an “abstract other,” serving as an entry point for individual reflection and self-cultivation. Finally, the paper introduces an AI-based system for ethical generation in space, discussing its feasibility in dynamically facilitating the transformation from “space–behavior–ethics–morality,” while also addressing potential risks of alienation. Overall, the study seeks to translate New Confucian ethics into a practicable spatial mechanism, offering a new approach to the formation of public morality in contemporary contexts."},{"t":"p","zh":"Key words: Confucianism; Neoliberalism; Aesthetic; Spatial Ethics","en":"Key words: Confucianism; Neoliberalism; Aesthetic; Spatial Ethics"},{"t":"h","zh":"一、 问题的提出：道统的延续与现代的撞击","en":"I. Raising the Problem: The Continuation of the Daotong and the Impact of Modernity"},{"t":"h","zh":"新儒家的基础坐标","en":"The Basic Coordinates of New Confucianism"},{"t":"p","zh":"“新儒家”非单一思想体系，而是一个横跨20世纪至今的思想谱系。20世纪初，中国传统文化面临“三千年未有之大变局”，儒学被认为是落后、守旧的代名词。而在这种“文化断裂”的危机下，中国的一些知识分子试图证明：儒家思想不仅没死，而且能救现代文明[1]。“新儒家”因此开启了是一场延续百年的思想运动。其核心关切在于：如何在现代性条件下重建儒家伦理的正当性与有效性。其理论脉络“可以看作是一个连续的、具有内在逻辑的三个阶段。“第一代致力于在文化激进主义中为儒家‘招魂’”[2]；第一代新儒家梁漱溟、熊十力、马一浮等学者主要致力于回应“文化危机”问题，证明儒学在现代依然有生命力。第二代则在花果飘零的境遇下通过哲学重构为儒家‘立命’；这一代人发布了著名的《为中国文化敬告世界人士宣言》唐君毅、牟宗三、徐复观等学者通过引入康德哲学，完成了儒学的形上学重建。“而第三代在‘全球化’与‘本土化’的双重张力中，实现儒学的‘创造性转化’。”杜维明、成中英、刘述先等学者将儒学推向国际，开展“文明对话”，探讨儒家伦理与现代化的关系。将儒学置于全球语境中，提出“文明对话”的可能性，强调“儒家伦理在现代社会中的公共意义”[3]","en":"“New Confucianism” is not a single system of thought but an intellectual lineage stretching from the twentieth century to the present. At the beginning of the twentieth century, traditional Chinese culture faced “a great transformation unseen in three thousand years,” and Confucianism came to be regarded as a byword for backwardness and conservatism. Amid this crisis of “cultural rupture,” some Chinese intellectuals tried to prove that Confucian thought was not only not dead but could even save modern civilization[1]. “New Confucianism” thus set off an intellectual movement that has lasted a century. Its core concern is how to rebuild the legitimacy and efficacy of Confucian ethics under the conditions of modernity. Its theoretical trajectory “can be seen as three continuous stages with an internal logic. ‘The first generation devoted itself to “summoning the soul” of Confucianism amid cultural radicalism’”[2]; the first-generation New Confucians—Liang Shuming, Xiong Shili, Ma Yifu and others—mainly sought to respond to the problem of “cultural crisis” and to prove that Confucianism still had vitality in the modern age. The second generation, in a situation of “flowers and fruit scattered and fallen” (huaguo piaoling, the dispersal of Chinese culture), sought to “establish the destiny” of Confucianism through philosophical reconstruction; this generation issued the famous “Manifesto on Behalf of Chinese Culture Respectfully Announced to the People of the World,” and Tang Junyi, Mou Zongsan, Xu Fuguan and others, by introducing Kantian philosophy, accomplished the metaphysical reconstruction of Confucianism. “The third generation, within the dual tension of ‘globalization’ and ‘localization,’ achieved the ‘creative transformation’ of Confucianism.” Tu Weiming, Cheng Chung-ying, Liu Shu-hsien and others carried Confucianism onto the international stage, engaging in “dialogue among civilizations” and exploring the relationship between Confucian ethics and modernization. They placed Confucianism in a global context, proposed the possibility of “dialogue among civilizations,” and emphasized “the public significance of Confucian ethics in modern society”[3]"},{"t":"h","zh":"现代性难题","en":"The Problem of Modernity"},{"t":"p","zh":"儒家与现代社会之结合，无法绕过科学民主制度和个人道德的关系问题。对此，牟宗三提出了命题——“良知自我坎陷”。他认为：“儒家传统里有极其深刻的道德精神（内圣），但缺乏科学和民主（外王）。为了长出科学和民主，儒家的道德主体必须‘自我退位’或‘自我否定’，给理性逻辑让路。”[4]而这个自我否定不是将儒学安置于西方知识座架之下，而是试图在本体论层面完成对康德知性逻辑的反向整合，将科学民主作为“内圣”的一个过程。那么，强调“道德修为”的学说（儒家），真的能通过自我调整，生发出讲求“客观逻辑”的科学和民主吗？还是说，这只是文人们的一厢情愿？","en":"Any union of Confucianism with modern society cannot bypass the question of the relationship between the institutions of science and democracy and personal morality. In response, Mou Zongsan put forward a proposition: the “self-negation of liangzhi” (liangzhi ziwo kanxian, the self-restriction of innate moral knowing). He held: “The Confucian tradition contains an extremely profound moral spirit (inner sageliness, neisheng) but lacks science and democracy (outer kingliness, waiwang). In order to grow science and democracy, the Confucian moral subject must ‘step down’ or ‘negate itself,’ making way for rational logic.”[4] This self-negation does not mean placing Confucianism under the framework of Western knowledge; it is an attempt to accomplish, at the ontological level, a reverse integration of Kant’s logic of the understanding, treating science and democracy as one process within “inner sageliness.” Can a doctrine that stresses “moral cultivation” (Confucianism) really, through self-adjustment, give rise to science and democracy, which demand “objective logic”? Or is this merely the wishful thinking of literati?"},{"t":"p","zh":"为了解决这个问题，牟宗三论证了人具有“智的直觉”，科学和民主作为“子集”嵌入到儒家的个人道德修为的自我调整框架中。","en":"To resolve this problem, Mou Zongsan argued that human beings possess “intellectual intuition,” and embedded science and democracy as “subsets” within the self-adjusting framework of Confucian personal moral cultivation."},{"t":"p","zh":"科学与民主是西方“对自然的恐惧与征服”[5]与“基于冲突而产生的妥协[6]”的产物。启蒙运动以来的民主科学思想走向了工具理性支配的现代社会；现代性走至极端以及其普遍平庸性产生了大屠杀与消费社会。[7]相较于此，以道德为追求的轴心文明的儒家社会秩序的合法性来自于“天”。天人合一意味着个人的内在修为与宇宙秩序是同构的。因此，“儒家的公共性不是通过讨价还价的‘妥协’达成的，而是每一个社会成员（尤其是精英）感受到的一种沉重的道德压力（Responsibility）。”[8]当然，这是双面的，对于统治和社会稳定来说，可以有稳定的一种“超稳态”：“儒家建立了一个高度统一的组织力量，通过意识形态（修身、齐家、治国、平天下）将国家与社会紧密结合。这种结构具有极强的自我修复能力，当社会因冲突而崩溃时，它总能通过‘大一统’逻辑重新回归原位，。”[9]而对于科学、征服与探索来说，这种观念就容易在其他并行文明如西方文明中“落伍”。比如，资本主义在中国萌芽了短暂的时间却又迅速被掐灭、比如要在一定程度上牺牲现代意义上的心理健康和经济自由。","en":"Science and democracy are products of the Western “fear and conquest of nature”[5] and of “compromise arising from conflict[6].” The democratic and scientific thought of the Enlightenment led to a modern society dominated by instrumental reason; modernity pushed to its extreme, together with its pervasive banality, produced the Holocaust and consumer society.[7] By contrast, the legitimacy of the social order of Confucian society—an Axial civilization oriented toward morality—comes from “Heaven” (tian). The unity of Heaven and humanity means that an individual’s inner cultivation is isomorphic with the cosmic order. Therefore, “Confucian publicness is not achieved through bargained ‘compromise’; it is a heavy moral pressure (Responsibility) felt by every member of society (especially the elite).”[8] This is, of course, double-edged. For rule and social stability it can provide a stable “ultrastability”: “Confucianism built a highly unified organizing force, binding state and society tightly together through ideology (cultivating the self, regulating the family, governing the state, bringing peace to all under Heaven). This structure has an extremely strong capacity for self-repair: when society collapses through conflict, it can always return to its original position through the logic of ‘great unification’.”[9] For science, conquest and exploration, however, this outlook easily “falls behind” other parallel civilizations such as the Western one. For example, capitalism sprouted in China for a short time only to be quickly snuffed out; and, to a certain degree, psychological health and economic freedom in the modern sense have to be sacrificed."},{"t":"p","zh":"若仅追求科学民主，是危险的，因为它们的起始点是对外的、帝国主义式侵略扩张的，结果是指向他者生命的，是一种掠夺性的“普世主义”[10]。“气候危机的紧迫性戳破了那个关于‘进步’的伟大神话：即人类可以通过科学与民主无限度地征服自然。”[11]生态危机便是对这种征服性意识形态的一种警示。而“中国文化以伦理本位为核心，其未来价值在于提供不同于西方理性主义的生活方式。”[12]","en":"Pursuing science and democracy alone is dangerous, because their starting point is outward-facing, an imperialist aggression and expansion, and their outcome is directed at the lives of others: a predatory “universalism”[10]. “The urgency of the climate crisis has punctured the great myth of ‘progress’: that humanity can conquer nature without limit through science and democracy.”[11] The ecological crisis is a warning against this ideology of conquest. And “Chinese culture takes ethics as its core; its future value lies in offering a way of life different from Western rationalism.”[12]"},{"t":"p","zh":"现代社会是西方希伯来宗教-希腊理性轴心文明的产物。科学和民主是现代社会的两大支柱。而当“上帝死了”，意义的最高终点也因此消散。在应对虚无主义和道德缺席时：自由主义指向个人主义，解决不了意义、消散了共识；马克思主义解决经济和社会结构，不解决心灵与德性；而尼采、海德格尔一脉的敞开性，在现实世界太形而上、太精英。","en":"Modern society is the product of the Western Axial civilization of Hebrew religion and Greek reason. Science and democracy are the two pillars of modern society. When “God is dead,” the highest endpoint of meaning dissipates with him. In responding to nihilism and the absence of morality, liberalism points toward individualism, fails to resolve the question of meaning and dissolves consensus; Marxism deals with economic and social structures but not with the heart and virtue; and the openness of the Nietzsche–Heidegger line is too metaphysical and too elitist for the real world."},{"t":"p","zh":"只有儒家，刚好补上所有缺口：它是敞开的、也是有指向的。既讲个体修身（内圣）、又讲社会秩序（外王）；既重德性、又重关系；既讲共同体、又不排斥个体。","en":"Only Confucianism happens to fill all the gaps: it is open, and it also has a direction. It speaks both of individual self-cultivation (inner sageliness) and of social order (outer kingliness); it values both virtue and relationships; it speaks of community without excluding the individual."},{"t":"h","zh":"一、 “对立和冲突”的本体论转变","en":"I. The Ontological Transformation of “Opposition and Conflict”"},{"t":"p","zh":"扩张——是向外的、无止境的。但对自我，却总有些余地和可达到的结果。","en":"Expansion is outward and endless. Toward the self, however, there is always some leeway and a result that can be reached."},{"t":"p","zh":"牟宗三主张的“统摄”——将民主科学统摄入到了个人“修身”的框架中。“修身”的范畴是广泛的，除了理性的、科学的，伦理的、责任的，还有艺术人文、身体素质等，它超越了单一的理性逻辑，横跨生命多个领域。这种非穷尽性是一种基于自律的“留白”。正因为每一个维度都是可被开启的，行动才是展开的、可持续的。正如中国画，不靠线条把空间占满，而是通过对确定性线条的克制和留白让“万物并育而不相害”，为生命各要素的自发涌现腾挪出空间。","en":"Mou Zongsan’s “comprehension” (tongshe, gathering under one governance) brings democracy and science into the framework of individual “self-cultivation” (xiushen). The scope of self-cultivation is broad: besides the rational and the scientific, the ethical and the responsible, it also includes the arts and humanities, physical fitness and more; it goes beyond a single rational logic and spans many domains of life. This non-exhaustiveness is a kind of “blank space” (liubai) grounded in self-discipline. Precisely because every dimension can be opened, action unfolds and can be sustained. It is like Chinese painting, which does not fill the space with lines but, through restraint in determinate lines and the leaving of blank space, lets “all things be nourished together without harming one another,” making room for the spontaneous emergence of the various elements of life."},{"t":"p","zh":"自我是一个“开放的中心”[13]，修身本身并非线性累积，行动和道德实在交互之中彼此嵌入的。这种嵌入将对科学和民主的追求纳入修身齐家治国平天下的轨道，由此达到一种“非共识性的共同操作意识”。“绕过冲突”，向内收缩式地去形成一种反思式的“修身”。“绕过冲突”并非指有一个冲突的存在而后绕开它，而是指冲突本身就是建构起来的，当把这些乱麻理顺，人看到的就不再是不可调和的对立，而是“时中”[14]的可能性。这并不意味着设定明确的自我边界和“绿洲式的隔离”（汉娜阿伦特1961），而是划定了一种在关系与交互中人类个人的、作为个体的“活动边界”，从而在公共领域无需压抑自己进行妥协就能达到共识。","en":"The self is an “open centre”[13]; self-cultivation is not a linear accumulation, and action and moral reality are embedded in each other through interaction. This embedding brings the pursuit of science and democracy onto the track of cultivating the self, regulating the family, governing the state and bringing peace to all under Heaven, and thereby achieves a kind of “non-consensual shared operational awareness.” “Bypassing conflict” means contracting inward to form a reflective “self-cultivation.” “Bypassing conflict” does not mean that a conflict exists and is then circumvented; it means that conflict itself is constructed: once this tangle is straightened out, what one sees is no longer irreconcilable opposition but the possibility of shizhong (timely centrality)[14]. This does not mean setting clear boundaries of the self and an “oasis-like isolation” (Hannah Arendt, 1961); rather, it marks out, within relationships and interactions, a personal “boundary of activity” for the human being as an individual, so that consensus can be reached in the public realm without suppressing oneself in compromise."},{"t":"p","zh":"相较之下，西方那种认为对立是真实且本质的观念，使其在社会秩序中也始终潜伏着“敌我划分”的逻辑。制度并非消解冲突，而往往只是对冲突进行延迟与管理。冲突仍然在，只是被延迟了。","en":"By contrast, the Western view that opposition is real and essential means that a logic of “friend–enemy distinction” always lurks within its social order. Institutions do not dissolve conflict; often they merely defer and manage it. The conflict is still there, only postponed."},{"t":"p","zh":"若是转变问题的本体，在儒家框架中，“冲突”的位置不是本质和必然，而是错位，是可转化的。那么在这种前提下，行动的重点便不是冲突-妥协，而是“时中”——在变动的中轴线中去寻找平衡点。","en":"If we transform the ontology of the problem, then within the Confucian framework “conflict” is not essential or necessary but a misalignment, something that can be transformed. Under this premise, the focus of action is no longer conflict–compromise but shizhong: seeking the point of balance along a shifting central axis."},{"t":"h","zh":"二、 新自由主义视域下“修身”的路径倒置与场域重建","en":"II. The Inversion of the Path of “Self-Cultivation” and the Reconstruction of the Field from the Perspective of Neoliberalism"},{"t":"h","zh":"应对新自由主义的“个体边界刚性”","en":"Responding to Neoliberalism’s “Rigidity of Individual Boundaries”"},{"t":"p","zh":"布朗指出：“新自由主义不仅是一种经济政策，更是一种“规范性的理性制度”。它“扩张”的方式是把所有人类活动——包括那些原本属于政治、法律或伦理领域的活动——全部转化为经济活动。”[15]新自由主义将所有进入到其机器的经济、政治、社会与国家治理的整体性制度范式与意识形态体系都纳入到它自己的机械中高速运转。同时，它使人自我监控、自我剥削[16]，从而“格式化”个体内在。上文我们将问题的本体论转向了儒家的框架。那么在新自由主义中，“修身”如何区别于自我剥削？","en":"Brown points out: “Neoliberalism is not only an economic policy but a ‘normative order of reason.’ It ‘expands’ by converting all human activity—including activities that originally belonged to the political, legal or ethical spheres—into economic activity.”[15] Neoliberalism takes the whole institutional paradigm and ideological system of economy, politics, society and state governance that enters its machine and sets it all running at high speed within its own machinery. At the same time, it makes people monitor and exploit themselves[16], thereby “formatting” the individual’s interior. Above, we shifted the ontology of the problem into the Confucian framework. How, then, does “self-cultivation” under neoliberalism differ from self-exploitation?"},{"t":"p","zh":"儒家的“修身”不应仅向内收缩，当外部的扩张性力量主动撞击个体的边界时，“修身”框架里还应具备一种“防御性的刚性”。这种刚性来源于对个人时间的整合：“当代的社会结构使权力不再依赖外部强制，而通过‘自我优化’机制运行。”[17]修身并不比成为自我企业家更轻松。而修身的持续努力和投入所指向的，也并非个人主义式的自我优化，而是对“圣贤与澄明”的持续自律。比起自我经营和自我剥削，它指向的是自我外部，是一种佛家式的到达彼岸的自洽，是对道德追求。","en":"Confucian “self-cultivation” should not merely contract inward; when expansive external forces actively strike the boundaries of the individual, the framework of self-cultivation should also possess a “defensive rigidity.” This rigidity comes from the integration of one’s personal time: “In contemporary social structures, power no longer depends on external coercion but operates through the mechanism of ‘self-optimization’.”[17] Self-cultivation is no easier than becoming an entrepreneur of the self. But what the sustained effort and investment of self-cultivation point toward is not individualistic self-optimization but continuous self-discipline toward “sagehood and clarity.” Compared with self-management and self-exploitation, it points beyond the self: a Buddhist-like self-coherence of reaching the other shore, a pursuit of morality."},{"t":"p","zh":"在如今意义虚无、个人时间碎片化的时代，“主体必须通过‘自我技术’达成一种自足状态，否则其行动将仅仅是对外部刺激或他者意志的被动反应。”[18] 传统的“修身”认为要格物、慎独。一个有修身工夫的人，其行为之间存在一条“道”、一个逻辑主线。因此通过修身，主体可以将无数个零散的时刻锚定在一个恒定的价值坐标上，整合成时间上连贯的叙事，整合出自我。","en":"In today’s era of meaninglessness and fragmented personal time, “the subject must attain a state of self-sufficiency through ‘technologies of the self’; otherwise its actions will be merely passive reactions to external stimuli or to the will of others.”[18] Traditional “self-cultivation” calls for gewu (investigating things) and shendu (vigilance in solitude). A person with the gongfu (practised effort) of self-cultivation has a “Way,” a logical main thread, running through their conduct. Through self-cultivation, therefore, the subject can anchor countless scattered moments to a constant coordinate of value, integrate them into a temporally coherent narrative, and integrate a self."},{"t":"h","zh":"传统修身的不可行性","en":"The Impracticability of Traditional Self-Cultivation"},{"t":"p","zh":"“儒学之本质，即在确立一价值主体……‘天道’之意义，实由‘心性’之自觉而显现。若无主体之自觉，则宇宙秩序仅为盲目之自然，而非道德之秩序。”[19]在儒家传统中，如果世界不通过“心”来彰显，它就没有道德意义。新儒家也是“从天（宇宙秩序）到心（内在直觉、良知）”的路线。如果没有“心”，道德会变成一种“结构性的存在”[20]。个体可以承认它的存在，但无法解释：为什么“我”要对它负责？如果没有“心”的主动性，主体的边界要么来自社会，要么来自“天的秩序”。","en":"“The essence of Confucianism lies in establishing a subject of value… The meaning of ‘the Way of Heaven’ is in fact manifested through the self-awareness of ‘mind and nature.’ Without the self-awareness of the subject, the cosmic order would be merely blind nature, not a moral order.”[19] In the Confucian tradition, if the world is not made manifest through the “mind” (xin), it has no moral meaning. New Confucianism also follows the route “from Heaven (cosmic order) to mind (inner intuition, liangzhi).” Without the “mind,” morality becomes a “structural existence”[20]. The individual can acknowledge that it exists but cannot explain why “I” should be responsible for it. Without the initiative of the “mind,” the boundaries of the subject come either from society or from the “order of Heaven.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"“天”代表了宇宙的普遍法则、客观物理规律，以及社会运行的深层结构。正如现象学认为“世界”是所有经验的先行视域，儒家的“天”也是所有伦理行为和身体感知的先行场域。它是一个“大场域”。[21]","en":"“Heaven” stands for the universal laws of the cosmos, objective physical laws and the deep structure of how society operates. Just as phenomenology holds that the “world” is the prior horizon of all experience, the Confucian “Heaven” is the prior field of all ethical conduct and bodily perception. It is a “great field.”[21]"},{"t":"p","zh":"“心”是宇宙法则在个体身上的投射，没有“心”的自觉，宇宙只是盲目的物质运动。“‘天道’作为一种本体论的实存，必须通过‘心’的自觉（Intellectual Intuition）才得以从‘盲目的自然秩序’转化为‘道德的意义世界’”[22]","en":"The “mind” is the projection of cosmic law onto the individual; without the self-awareness of the “mind,” the cosmos is merely blind material motion. “The ‘Way of Heaven,’ as an ontological reality, must pass through the self-awareness of the ‘mind’ (Intellectual Intuition) in order to be transformed from a ‘blind natural order’ into a ‘moral world of meaning’”[22]"},{"t":"p","zh":"道德是“天”通过“心”翻译出的语言，它是秩序的人格化表现。这三者的路径是“由内向外”的：映射着天理的“心”的主体以修身来实现道德并洞察宇宙的普遍法则。修身是实现道德的实践方式，有了修身的累积才能使道德显化。而道德得以发生，离不开“天”作为发生场域与“心”作为主体自觉。","en":"Morality is the language into which “Heaven” is translated through the “mind”; it is the personified expression of order. The path among these three runs “from inside out”: the subject of the “mind,” which reflects the principle of Heaven, realizes morality through self-cultivation and discerns the universal laws of the cosmos. Self-cultivation is the practical way of realizing morality; only with the accumulation of self-cultivation can morality become manifest. And for morality to occur at all, it depends on “Heaven” as the field in which it occurs and on the “mind” as the self-awareness of the subject."},{"t":"p","zh":"新自由主义统摄了世界，“天”是被遮蔽的——宇宙法则并不是敞开的，而是明确指向经济的。一切路径都被纳入新自由主义的逻辑中。上文指出，“修身”是指向主体内部的道德与澄明，而不是自我优化以在个体与整体中取得收益最大化。也就是说它的目的并非是与新自由主义同轨的-通过修身而达到道德的传统路径是与新自由主义相冲突的，因此，这一传统由于不符合它的逻辑会被格式化、被边缘化。也就是说，按照传统的“存天理、致良知”的顺序和关系，是无法实现让道德在修身实践中被转化出来的。","en":"Neoliberalism has taken hold of the world, and “Heaven” is obscured: the laws of the cosmos are not open but explicitly directed toward the economy. Every path is absorbed into the logic of neoliberalism. As noted above, “self-cultivation” points toward morality and clarity within the subject, not toward self-optimization for maximizing gains for the individual and the whole. That is to say, its aim does not run on the same track as neoliberalism—the traditional path of reaching morality through self-cultivation conflicts with neoliberalism, and so this tradition, not conforming to its logic, is formatted and marginalized. In other words, following the traditional order and relationship of “preserving the principle of Heaven and extending liangzhi,” it is impossible to have morality transformed out of the practice of self-cultivation."},{"t":"h","zh":"道德与修身的路径倒置","en":"Inverting the Path of Morality and Self-Cultivation"},{"t":"p","zh":"传统儒家是内圣外王向上扩充，修身治国平天下。修身在先、道德在后，通过修身达到道德。上文已经论述，这个路线在现代社会无法实现。现在让我们改变这一顺序，以道德带修身，对这一传统路径的目的与过程进行倒置：直接将道德设置为先行目的。","en":"Traditional Confucianism extends upward from inner sageliness to outer kingliness: cultivating the self, governing the state, bringing peace to all under Heaven. Self-cultivation comes first and morality after; morality is reached through self-cultivation. As argued above, this route cannot be realized in modern society. Let us now change this order and let morality lead self-cultivation, inverting the aim and the process of the traditional path: morality is set directly as the prior aim."},{"t":"p","zh":"这个目的不是个体的目的，而是在公共领域中，瞬间的和谐状态。传统的修身-道德可以找到在自我与他者之间的平衡点，这种和谐状态是其结果和目的地。既如此，我们可以在指定空间先提前设置这一和谐状态的场域形态，计算预测平衡点发生所需条件，从而让主体在身体前反思层发出行动（这个行动不是主动的修身带来的，而是心理学范畴的条件反射）从而在这种场域中形成无需思考的惯习，进一步让惯习带出伦理形态，反向带动个体生命状态。以开启“修身”的通口。","en":"This aim is not the aim of an individual but a momentary state of harmony in the public realm. The traditional path of self-cultivation to morality can find a point of balance between self and other; this state of harmony is its result and destination. That being so, we can set up in advance, in a designated space, the field form of this state of harmony, calculating and predicting the conditions needed for the point of balance to occur, so that subjects act at the pre-reflective level of the body (this action is not brought about by active self-cultivation but is a conditioned reflex in the psychological sense), thereby forming in this field an unthinking habitus, which in turn brings forth an ethical form and drives back the individual’s state of life—so as to open the gateway to “self-cultivation.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"本体论和目的论是在儒家内部的，达成方式是现代的手段，发生的逻辑是在身体层而不是行动层的——无需对抗新自由主义。","en":"The ontology and the teleology remain within Confucianism; the means of achieving them are modern; and the logic of occurrence lies at the level of the body rather than the level of action—there is no need to confront neoliberalism."},{"t":"h","zh":"三、 基于“场域—身体—材料”的主体复归","en":"III. The Return of the Subject Based on “Field–Body–Material”"},{"t":"h","zh":"和谐状态的场域形态","en":"The Field Form of the State of Harmony"},{"t":"p","zh":"场域是各种关系力波的交织，“本质上是一种关系网络，其内部始终处于力量的流动与再分配之中。[23]”在这一维度下“空间即道德”-“道德不再位于主体内部，而弥散于空间结构之中。[24]”。不是行为在空间中发生，而是在其实践过程中不断“生成”了空间本身。在这一场域空间的意义上，人们不是先有道德再行动，而是在行动中确认自我位置。比如，在一个公共空间里，“捡起地上的垃圾扔进垃圾桶”并不仅是一种公共行为，它同时是一个微小的存在宣言：我属于这个空间、我对这个空间负责并在共同体中占有某种位置。“个体的行为倾向依赖于其对群体归属的确认”[25]，而当一个人不确定自己是否属于环境时，行为就会被抑制。捡起垃圾的瞬间，个体通过身体动作将一个“荒凉的公共地带”转化为“有归属感的共同体场域”。反之，如果不知道自己是否属于环境，“捡垃圾”这种行为就会在犹豫与“保守策略”[26]中无法发生。","en":"A field is an interweaving of relational force-waves, “essentially a network of relations, within which forces are constantly flowing and being redistributed.[23]” In this dimension, “space is morality”—“morality is no longer located within the subject but is diffused throughout spatial structures.[24]” It is not that behaviour takes place in space; rather, space itself is continually “generated” in the course of practice. In the sense of this field-space, people do not first have morality and then act; they confirm their own position in action. For example, in a public space, “picking up litter from the ground and throwing it into a bin” is not only a public act; it is also a small declaration of existence: I belong to this space, I am responsible for this space, and I hold a certain position in the community. “An individual’s behavioural tendencies depend on the confirmation of their group belonging”[25], and when a person is unsure whether they belong to an environment, behaviour is inhibited. In the moment of picking up the litter, the individual, through a bodily movement, turns a “desolate public zone” into a “community field with a sense of belonging.” Conversely, if one does not know whether one belongs to the environment, an act such as “picking up litter” will fail to happen amid hesitation and a “conservative strategy”[26]."},{"t":"p","zh":"我们借由他人目光确认自身与世界的关系。而“公共领域是主体相互确认、经验互通的空间。”[27]罗森塔尔效应揭示，行为表现会在外在期待的微妙牵引下被重新分布（Rosenthal & Jacobson ，1968) 。现代社会，行为不再只受熟人社会中的“身边人”调节；现代场域的观看者是抽象的、泛化的[28]。通过提前设计场域，调节其审美阈值，营造出一种无形的“审美压强”。在这种场域形态下，冲突行为会产生巨大的“审美违和感”，这种违和感使冲突主体成为空间异物，迫使其行为向和谐状态对位。换言之，场域形态的目标是制造一个“抽象他者”，一个“时空对位事件”。它不要求长久的契约，只是在个体进入场域的瞬间，通过空间的留白与秩序，引导出一种自发的、和谐的临时性共处伦理。","en":"We confirm our relation to ourselves and to the world through the gaze of others. And “the public sphere is a space in which subjects mutually recognize one another and share experience.”[27] The Rosenthal effect shows that behaviour is redistributed under the subtle pull of external expectations (Rosenthal & Jacobson, 1968). In modern society, behaviour is no longer regulated only by the “people around us” in a society of acquaintances; the onlooker in the modern field is abstract and generalized[28]. By designing the field in advance and adjusting its aesthetic threshold, an invisible “aesthetic pressure” can be created. In this field form, conflictual behaviour produces a strong “aesthetic incongruity,” which turns the conflicting subject into a foreign body in the space and compels its behaviour to align with the state of harmony. In other words, the goal of the field form is to create an “abstract other,” a “spatio-temporal alignment event.” It demands no lasting contract; only at the moment the individual enters the field does it, through the blank space and order of the space, draw out a spontaneous, harmonious, temporary ethics of coexistence."},{"t":"h","zh":"前反思的身体","en":"The Pre-Reflective Body"},{"t":"p","zh":"“此在（Dasein）在常人的喧嚣中是麻木的。”[29]孟子的“性善论”并不是说人性天然具备完整的道德体系，而更指向一种可被触发的伦理结构。《孟子·公孙丑上》提出“恻隐、羞恶、恭敬、是非”四端，作为道德的初始形态；在“孺子将入井”的论述中，孟子进一步表明，道德反应并非源于理性判断，而是在特定情境中被瞬时激发[30]。“良知的呼唤具有召唤的性质”[31]，结合身体现象学的视角，身体作为人与世界发生关系的中介，可以使这种“召回”通过感知层面被激活。孟子的“四端”在现代语境下可被视为一种“前置的感官算法”：“身体与感知结构在认知之前发挥作用。”“人性善”指向的是：人具有“可被触发的道德结构”。[32]恻隐之心，人皆有之，“情感是决策的前提机制”[33]。因此反推，我们可以通过身体感官（如视觉平衡、触觉质感等）直接唤醒主体对生命质感的自觉，实现从“沉沦”到“在场”的那个非线性的时刻（Augenblick）[34]瞬时“发生”：通过对某一环境、关系、情境的设定来诱发道德反应。当在这一特定空间的场域具备“道德感”时，“身体”会自动过滤掉侵略性动作。侧身让行、放轻脚步...这些动作在思维意识到“我要讲文明”之前，就已经由处在“道德气氛[35]”空间的前反思身体完成了。","en":"“Dasein is numb amid the clamour of the They.”[29] Mencius’s “theory of the goodness of human nature” does not say that human nature is naturally equipped with a complete moral system; it points rather to an ethical structure that can be triggered. In “Gongsun Chou I” of the Mencius, the “four sprouts” (siduan)—commiseration, shame, deference, and the sense of right and wrong—are put forward as the initial forms of morality; in the passage on “a child about to fall into a well,” Mencius further shows that moral responses do not arise from rational judgment but are aroused instantaneously in a particular situation[30]. “The call of conscience has the character of a summons”[31]; combined with the perspective of bodily phenomenology, in which the body is the medium through which human beings relate to the world, this “recall” can be activated at the level of perception. In a modern context, Mencius’s “four sprouts” can be seen as a kind of “pre-installed sensory algorithm”: “the body and perceptual structures operate before cognition.” “Human nature is good” points to the fact that human beings possess “a moral structure that can be triggered.”[32] All people have a heart of commiseration; “emotion is a precondition mechanism of decision-making”[33]. Reasoning backwards, then, we can directly awaken the subject’s self-awareness of the texture of life through the bodily senses (such as visual balance and tactile texture), so that the non-linear moment (Augenblick)[34] of passing from “fallenness” to “presence” “occurs” instantaneously: moral responses are induced by setting up a certain environment, relationship or situation. When the field of this particular space has a “moral sense,” the “body” automatically filters out aggressive movements. Stepping aside to let someone pass, lightening one’s footsteps… these movements are already completed by the pre-reflective body in a space of “moral atmosphere[35]” before thought becomes aware that “I should behave in a civilized way.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在这个意义上，人只需要被“触发”。前文场域设计的功能就是担任这个“触发装置”。","en":"In this sense, people only need to be “triggered.” The function of the field design described above is to serve as this “triggering device.”"},{"t":"h","zh":"材料","en":"Material"},{"t":"p","zh":"在场域形态与身体美学的交汇点上，材料（Materiality）并非被动的物理填充，而是伦理感应的实质载体。如果说“场域”提供了公共空间的秩序视域，“身体”提供了感知的可能，那么“材料”则提供了两者发生共振的客观物理条件。","en":"At the point where field form and bodily aesthetics meet, material (Materiality) is not passive physical filler but the substantive carrier of ethical resonance. If the “field” provides the ordering horizon of public space and the “body” provides the possibility of perception, then “material” provides the objective physical conditions under which the two resonate."},{"t":"p","zh":"“材料本身具有一种存在的质量，它不仅是技术性实体，同时也是意义的载体。”[36]在哈洛的恒河猴依恋实验[37]中，触觉的柔软与温暖（情感安全感）在行为生成中具有先于物质满足（食物）的优先性。材料的质感直接锚定了主体的心理安全边界。","en":"“Material itself has a quality of being; it is not only a technical entity but also a carrier of meaning.”[36] In Harlow’s rhesus monkey attachment experiments[37], the softness and warmth of touch (emotional security) took precedence over material satisfaction (food) in the generation of behaviour. The texture of materials directly anchors the subject’s boundary of psychological safety."},{"t":"p","zh":"进一步，“材料不是惰性的，它们能与人的触觉，身体的重量感、重力与时间产生共鸣。[38]”材料不仅是祖姆托（Zumthor, 2011）笔下的“建筑组成”，更是塞内特（Sennett, 2008）所言的“自我话语”。材料的粗糙、平滑、致密或通透，和材料的组合方式，影响甚至规定了身体在空间中的移动逻辑和摩擦系数。主体的触觉、身体运动在与材料的直接交互中[39]，完成了一次非概念性的审美跃迁——从机械的物理感知升华为具有主体性的秩序维护。","en":"Further, “materials are not inert; they resonate with human touch, with the body’s sense of weight, with gravity and with time.[38]” Materials are not only the “composition of architecture” described by Zumthor (Zumthor, 2011) but also what Sennett (Sennett, 2008) calls a “discourse of the self.” The roughness, smoothness, density or translucency of materials, and the ways in which they are combined, influence and even dictate the logic of movement and the coefficient of friction of the body in space. Through direct interaction with materials[39], the subject’s touch and bodily movement accomplish a non-conceptual aesthetic leap: from mechanical physical perception to a subjective upholding of order."},{"t":"p","zh":"一个由冷硬、反光、工业化材料堆砌的空间，往往诱发主体的疏离感与防御性行为，从而激发冲突。而具有“温暖、柔软质感”的场域，则能通过视觉、触觉的反馈反向建立主体的责任感。这种情感导向的材料性质，构成了公共空间中“瞬间和谐”的物理底座。","en":"A space piled up with cold, hard, reflective, industrial materials tends to induce estrangement and defensive behaviour in the subject and thus to provoke conflict. A field with a “warm, soft texture,” by contrast, can build up the subject’s sense of responsibility in return through visual and tactile feedback. This emotionally oriented quality of materials forms the physical foundation of “momentary harmony” in public space."},{"t":"p","zh":"材料的效力在于这种“不说理但有感受”的特征。材料的“质感先于语言”[40]，诱发了身体的“共同感”（Sensus Communis）[41]，使个体在无须概念介入的情况下，直觉地捕获到场域内“无概念的目的性”[42]：一种“本该如此”的秩序感。其产生的道德趋向并非源于对某种教条的认知，而是一种纯粹的审美经验和惯习。从而在公共领域形成文章第一部分所说的“非共识性的共同操作意识”。","en":"The efficacy of material lies in this quality of “not reasoning, yet being felt.” The “texture of material precedes language”[40]; it induces the body’s “common sense” (Sensus Communis)[41], allowing individuals, without the intervention of concepts, to grasp intuitively the “purposiveness without concept”[42] within the field: a sense of order that things are “as they should be.” The moral tendency it produces does not come from knowledge of some doctrine; it is a purely aesthetic experience and habitus. It thereby forms in the public realm the “non-consensual shared operational awareness” spoken of in the first part of this paper."},{"t":"h","zh":"四、 三层级道德与其政治合法性","en":"IV. Three-Tier Morality and Its Political Legitimacy"},{"t":"h","zh":"三层级道德入口","en":"Three Tiers of Entry into Morality"},{"t":"p","zh":"在孟子的“性善论”中道德不是一次性达到的，而是“可被唤起的层级结构”，德性是由内而外的感化。孟子不是要求所有人成圣，而是从“恻隐之心”开始。也就是说：先从最低层级“情感触发”，中层“行为调整”再到最高层“自觉修身”。在此将“低-中-高”替换为“一-二-三”：这一替换是为了剥离传统伦理学中对“高尚”与“平庸”的静态价值判断，转而聚焦于从“外部场域感应”到“内部主体自觉”的动态转化过程和行为发生的逻辑次序。","en":"In Mencius’s “theory of the goodness of human nature,” morality is not attained all at once but is “a hierarchical structure that can be awakened”; virtue is a transforming influence from the inside out. Mencius does not demand that everyone become a sage; he begins with “the heart of commiseration.” That is to say: first the lowest tier, “emotional triggering,” then the middle tier, “behavioural adjustment,” and finally the highest tier, “conscious self-cultivation.” Here “low–middle–high” is replaced with “one–two–three”: this replacement is meant to strip away the static value judgments of “noble” and “mediocre” in traditional ethics, and to focus instead on the dynamic process of transformation from “external field resonance” to “internal subjective self-awareness” and on the logical order in which behaviour occurs."},{"t":"p","zh":"第一层（公共空间层）：通过公共空间形态设计、身体美学、环境与材料诱发。也就是说不需要自觉修身，但可以体验到：“我是有尊严的”，“我属于这个空间、在其中我有归属感”“我与他人的关系是和谐的”。在这个空间中“让冲突显得格格不入”：“君子之德风，小人之德草，草上之风，必偃”。","en":"Tier One (the public-space tier): induced through the design of public-space form, bodily aesthetics, environment and materials. That is, no conscious self-cultivation is required, yet one can experience “I have dignity,” “I belong to this space and have a sense of belonging in it,” “my relationship with others is harmonious.” In this space “conflict is made to seem out of place”: “The virtue of the gentleman is like the wind; the virtue of the petty person is like the grass. When the wind blows over the grass, it is sure to bend.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"第二层（过渡层）：与第一层的环境引导人做出瞬间的条件反射不同，在这一层中，反思开始出现，个体对行为产生“自我解释”，开始有“选择感”。","en":"Tier Two (the transitional tier): unlike the first tier, where the environment leads people to make momentary conditioned reflexes, in this tier reflection begins to appear; the individual produces a “self-explanation” for their behaviour and begins to have a “sense of choice.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"第三层（道德层）：这一层发生在个体内部，也就是说，到达这一层，个体主动修身、自我约束甚至进入“澄明状态”","en":"Tier Three (the moral tier): this tier takes place within the individual; that is, on reaching this tier the individual actively cultivates the self, exercises self-restraint and may even enter a “state of clarity”"},{"t":"p","zh":"诚然，基于条件反射的看似“道德”的行为，不能称之为道德本身，道德需具备可反思性、规范意识和责任承担。从第一层到第二层再到第三层的跃迁都并非是必然发生的：个体的道德本身是不可以也无法被量化的。无法设计具有广泛普遍性的交往框架，各情境是即时生发的，不同主体的判断、主观能动性也是无普世规律的。简言之，功夫论和心性都在个体内部私人空间的领域。","en":"Admittedly, seemingly “moral” behaviour based on conditioned reflexes cannot be called morality itself; morality requires reflexivity, normative awareness and the taking on of responsibility. None of the leaps from the first tier to the second and then to the third happens necessarily: individual morality itself must not and cannot be quantified. No framework of interaction with broad universality can be designed; every situation arises in the moment, and the judgments and agency of different subjects follow no universal law. In short, gongfu theory (the theory of practised effort) and xinxing (mind and nature) both belong to the domain of the individual’s inner private space."},{"t":"p","zh":"因此在这里首先要强调的是，本文对“空间伦理”的设计仅在第一层的公共空间设计出发，通过空间结构设计降低行为冲突，使“有序”、“礼让”的行为在公共领域成为“无需思考的自然结果”。","en":"It must therefore be stressed first that this paper’s design of “spatial ethics” proceeds only from the first tier, the design of public space: through the design of spatial structure it reduces behavioural conflict, so that “orderly” and “courteous” behaviour becomes an “unthinking natural outcome” in the public realm."},{"t":"p","zh":"其次，这种“有序”、“礼让”的公共空间形态的设计与组织，是为了对场域形态进行引导——制造抽象它者。","en":"Second, the design and organization of this “orderly” and “courteous” public-space form is meant to guide the field form—to create an abstract other."},{"t":"p","zh":"“‘有序’、‘礼让’的行为在公共领域成为‘无需思考的自然结果’”是第一层的结果，它并没有结束，而是旨在为道德反思层打开入口。","en":"“‘Orderly’ and ‘courteous’ behaviour becoming an ‘unthinking natural outcome’ in the public realm” is the result of the first tier; it does not end there, but aims to open an entrance to the tier of moral reflection."},{"t":"p","zh":"想要打开这个入口，不用追求宏大意义、也无需先格物致知成为圣人。只从空间、城市设计、日常生活出发，让人在环境里自然养成道德、习惯道德、愿意道德。不是靠内心觉悟，而是靠身体在空间里被引导的形态。","en":"To open this entrance, one need not pursue grand meaning, nor first investigate things and extend knowledge to become a sage. Starting simply from space, urban design and everyday life, people can be allowed, within their environment, to grow into morality naturally, to become used to morality and to be willing to be moral. This relies not on inner awakening but on the forms through which the body is guided in space."},{"t":"h","zh":"政治合法性的补充","en":"A Supplement on Political Legitimacy"},{"t":"p","zh":"假如说这是一个有普遍性的大框架，那么可能会引发一个争议——这个框架（精英 + 技术 + 引导）中的精英，也即框架设计者，他们如何被约束？其实这就又到了西方的语境框架中。我们可以引入阿甘本的例外状态来说明这个问题：统治者特权，框架内外的统治者位置问题。[43]","en":"If this is a large framework with universality, it may provoke a controversy: how are the elites in this framework (elite + technology + guidance), that is, the designers of the framework, to be constrained? This in fact brings us back into the Western frame of reference. We can bring in Agamben’s state of exception to illustrate the problem: the prerogative of the sovereign, and the question of the ruler’s position inside and outside the framework.[43]"},{"t":"p","zh":"而在儒家框架中，根据这个问题我们进一步提出疑问：是否设计“他人行为”的权力，本身也必须被纳入“修身”之中？","en":"Within the Confucian framework, this question leads us to ask further: must the power to design “the behaviour of others” itself also be brought within “self-cultivation”?"},{"t":"p","zh":"如果“是”，那如何保证“设计者”不会滥用这种能力？","en":"If “yes,” how can we ensure that the “designers” do not abuse this ability?"},{"t":"p","zh":"如果“否”，那就是在承认：这是一个结构性不对称系统（精英控制大众）。","en":"If “no,” then we are admitting that this is a structurally asymmetrical system (elites controlling the masses)."},{"t":"p","zh":"这个问题无法直接被回答，因为这个问题有一个前提：它把精英和大众对立起来或者说放入了统治——被统治的框架。而个体的差异是平等的基础[44]，精英-大众是政治学的范畴，而在我们讨论的范畴中，两者的位置是框架设计者和被动接受者。这是在试图超越莫斯卡等人所描述的“精英理论[45]”，转而构建一种基于关系本体论的“共在”模式。也就是说，两者不是对立关系，而是在其位，同样面对修身问题。","en":"This question cannot be answered directly, because it rests on a premise: it sets elites and masses against each other, or places them in a framework of ruling and being ruled. Yet individual difference is the basis of equality[44]; elite and masses are categories of political science, whereas within the scope of our discussion the two positions are those of framework designer and passive recipient. This is an attempt to go beyond the “elite theory[45]” described by Mosca and others and to construct instead a mode of “being-with” grounded in a relational ontology. That is to say, the two are not in opposition; each stands in its own place and each equally faces the question of self-cultivation."},{"t":"p","zh":"所以我们继续将讨论的重点放在“修身”中，并做一个清晰的区分：这种提前设计的理论基础是人具有“智的直觉”，手段虽是“算法”式的，但与福柯式的治理术有着本质的区别。","en":"So we keep the focus of our discussion on “self-cultivation” and draw a clear distinction: the theoretical basis of this advance design is that human beings possess “intellectual intuition”; although the means are “algorithmic,” they differ essentially from Foucauldian governmentality."},{"t":"p","zh":"相比福柯的“治理术”——主体是被权力话语建构出来的产物。“在规训中，个体的独特性被“全景敞视”的监控消解，从而将主体转换为数据和档案[46]”。这种对场域的设计与治理，目标是主体的“复归”，其目的是唤醒主体对自己生命质感的自觉，让人在瞬间的和谐中感受到“作为一个有尊严的人”的存在。这里的空间起到“社会润滑剂”的作用，将冲突消纳在发生之前，而非依赖事后的制度惩罚。在这里，权力的作用是“感应性”的。它不提供具体的指令或标准化的操练，而是提供一个“留白”的、具有审美尊严的场域。当个体通过场域的诱导开启了“修身”的通口，产生自觉后，这套技术装置就完成了使命，它不是为了永久地接管个体的意志，它只是其所是的在那里。","en":"In Foucault’s “governmentality,” the subject is a product constructed by discourses of power. “In discipline, the individual’s uniqueness is dissolved by the surveillance of ‘panopticism,’ converting the subject into data and files[46].” The design and governance of the field proposed here aim at the “return” of the subject; their purpose is to awaken the subject’s self-awareness of the texture of their own life, letting people feel, in a moment of harmony, their existence “as a human being with dignity.” Space here acts as a “social lubricant,” absorbing conflict before it happens rather than relying on institutional punishment after the fact. Here the action of power is “resonant.” It offers no specific instructions or standardized drills, but a field with “blank space” and aesthetic dignity. Once the individual, induced by the field, has opened the gateway to “self-cultivation” and become self-aware, this technical apparatus has fulfilled its mission; it is not meant to take over the individual’s will permanently—it is simply there, being what it is."},{"t":"p","zh":"简言之，将新儒家问题下放到公共领域，为空间建设设立“礼”的标准，而后以礼带反思、带修身，再带身份认同和主体性的整合。","en":"In short: bring the New Confucian question down into the public realm, set a standard of li (ritual propriety) for spatial construction, and then let li lead to reflection, to self-cultivation, and further to identity and the integration of subjectivity."},{"t":"h","zh":"五、 AI所做的系统化尝试","en":"V. A Systematic Attempt with AI"},{"t":"h","zh":"空间伦理系统的落地：基于AI算法的微行为生成匹配系统","en":"Putting the Spatial Ethics System into Practice: An AI-Algorithm-Based System for Generating and Matching Micro-Behaviours"},{"t":"h","zh":"空间作为“动态调节系统”","en":"Space as a “Dynamic Regulation System”"},{"t":"p","zh":"基于“空间伦理生成”理论：在一个空间中，“道德”的发生是“流动的”，是在人与空间的互动行为中生成的，场域的形态也是会因此流动的。这个系统旨在借助AI实时感知空间状态，动态调节光、路径提示、节奏等因素，使空间具备 “自我调节能力”。以此引导此空间内部人群进入低冲突、可协作的行为状态。","en":"Based on the theory of “spatial ethical generation”: in a space, the occurrence of “morality” is “fluid”; it is generated in the interactive behaviour between people and space, and the form of the field flows accordingly. This system aims to use AI to sense the state of a space in real time and to adjust factors such as light, path cues and rhythm dynamically, giving the space a “capacity for self-regulation.” In this way it guides the people in the space into a low-conflict, cooperative behavioural state."},{"t":"p","zh":"这个系统最初的试点和作为数据收集的基地，可以以“项目”形式落地，比如“公共艺术装置”形式的公益方式。在空间现存状态的基础上，嵌入行为引导与数据反馈，严密计算空间压强。而作为广泛性的衔接点，在后期可与社区治理体系对接、嵌入城市更新与公共艺术项目、作为未来“智慧社区”的基础模块。","en":"The system’s initial pilot, which would also serve as a base for data collection, could be implemented as a “project,” for example as a non-profit initiative in the form of a “public art installation.” Building on the existing state of the space, behavioural guidance and data feedback would be embedded and the spatial pressure carefully calculated. As points of wider connection, it could later be linked to community governance systems, embedded in urban renewal and public art projects, and serve as a basic module for future “smart communities.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"人工智能技术的深度应用，在全球范围内的一些顶尖研究机构例如MIT感知城市实验室、慕尼黑工业大学等，已经有了成熟的体系，有广泛的技术和已有数据可运用到我们的模型中训练。在本系统中，可以运用AI技术的方面包括但不限于：计算机视觉（遥感影像分割、目标检测、要素提取），图神经网络（交通网络、区域交互、空间结构建模），人口流动时序预测、时序遥感监测，空间模式挖掘、多源数据融合，人口流动的联合建模.....","en":"The deep application of artificial intelligence already has mature systems at leading research institutions around the world, such as the MIT Senseable City Lab and the Technical University of Munich, with extensive technologies and existing data that can be used to train our model. In this system, AI technology can be applied in areas including but not limited to: computer vision (remote-sensing image segmentation, object detection, feature extraction), graph neural networks (modelling of transport networks, regional interaction and spatial structure), time-series prediction of population flows, time-series remote-sensing monitoring, spatial pattern mining, multi-source data fusion, joint modelling of population flows....."},{"t":"h","zh":"结语","en":"Conclusion"},{"t":"p","zh":"图像可以被复制，商业模式可以被照搬，同质将走向终止。但若有组织地来进行长期的统筹规划,流动式的空间设计，则要被考虑进其中的就不仅是“视觉、触觉”等简单要素，而是场域及空间本身。","en":"Images can be copied and business models can be replicated; sameness leads to an end. But if long-term, overall planning and fluid spatial design are carried out in an organized way, then what must be taken into account is not only simple elements such as “sight and touch” but the field and space themselves."},{"t":"p","zh":"空间设计，是为个体进入三层级的道德打开入口，而若要入口持续打开，则需要从局部地区入手，再散点式分布，最后统筹整体式连接。","en":"Spatial design opens an entrance for individuals into the three tiers of morality; for that entrance to stay open, one must start from local areas, then spread out in scattered points, and finally connect the whole in a coordinated way."},{"t":"p","zh":"从实际效果来看，这个系统可以呈现“降低社会摩擦成本，提升群体共存质量”的形态。不过，“在某一特定的区域弱化社会冲突成本、提升个体相处和谐度.....”这些若只作为目的，是无法长期持续的。道德本身是流动的，因此，使用人工智能进行统筹规划，并非传统“内圣”与“外王”的逻辑，而是实时大数据计算-道德流动的逻辑。这一系统的本体论是新儒家的倒置路径：这一和谐形态只是起点和入口，真正的目的是引导个体修身、是去激活现代人的主体自觉。","en":"In terms of practical effect, this system can take the form of “reducing the cost of social friction and improving the quality of group coexistence.” However, if “weakening the cost of social conflict and raising the harmony of individual coexistence in a particular area.....” is taken merely as the goal, it cannot be sustained in the long run. Morality itself is fluid; therefore, using artificial intelligence for overall planning follows not the traditional logic of “inner sageliness” and “outer kingliness” but a logic of real-time big-data computation and moral flow. The ontology of this system is the inverted New Confucian path: this harmonious form is only the starting point and the entrance; the true purpose is to guide individuals toward self-cultivation and to activate the subjective self-awareness of modern people."},{"t":"p","zh":"空间伦理学作为新兴交叉领域，已初步揭示空间秩序对人类行为与社会价值的塑造作用，但现有研究多基于本文第一部分所分析的西方“对立-冲突”的思想框架，聚焦空间正义与权利分配；而并不指向个体道德品格的日常养成。与此同时，儒家空间思想研究则多停留在传统礼制阐释，未能与现代城市设计形成有效对接。因此，以空间设计为载体、由外而内地培育个体公共道德，仍是一个具有开拓性的未竟方向。","en":"As an emerging interdisciplinary field, spatial ethics has begun to reveal how spatial order shapes human behaviour and social values, but existing research is mostly based on the Western “opposition–conflict” framework of thought analysed in the first part of this paper, focusing on spatial justice and the distribution of rights rather than on the everyday formation of individual moral character. Meanwhile, research on Confucian spatial thought mostly remains at the level of interpreting traditional ritual institutions and has not connected effectively with modern urban design. Cultivating individual public morality from the outside in, with spatial design as the vehicle, therefore remains a pioneering and unfinished direction."},{"t":"ref","zh":"杜维明：《儒家思想：以自我超越为中心的创造性转化》，北京大学出版社，2002年版。","en":"Tu Weiming, Confucian Thought: Creative Transformation Centred on Self-Transcendence, Peking University Press, 2002."},{"t":"ref","zh":"杜维明. 当代儒学发展的三个阶段[J]. 中国哲学史研究, 1986, (03): 9-19.","en":"Tu Weiming. The Three Stages of the Development of Contemporary Confucianism [J]. Studies in the History of Chinese Philosophy, 1986, (03): 9-19."},{"t":"ref","zh":"Tu, Weiming. Confucian Thought: Selfhood as Creative Transformation. SUNY Press, 1985, p. 62","en":"Tu, Weiming. Confucian Thought: Selfhood as Creative Transformation. SUNY Press, 1985, p. 62"},{"t":"ref","zh":"牟宗三：《心体与性体》（上册），台湾学生书局，2003（原著1968），第198–240页","en":"Mou Zongsan, Mind and Nature (Xinti yu xingti), Vol. 1, Taiwan Student Book Co., 2003 (original 1968), pp. 198–240"},{"t":"ref","zh":"霍克海默、阿多诺《启蒙辩证法—哲学断片》，渠敬东 曹卫东译，上海人民出版，2020，P22","en":"Max Horkheimer and Theodor W. Adorno, Dialectic of Enlightenment: Philosophical Fragments, trans. Qu Jingdong and Cao Weidong, Shanghai People’s Publishing House, 2020, p. 22"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Ibid P76","en":"Ibid., p. 76"},{"t":"ref","zh":"汉娜阿伦特：《艾希曼在耶路撒冷-一份关于平庸的恶的报告》安尼译，译林出版社，2017-01-01，P148-150）","en":"Hannah Arendt, Eichmann in Jerusalem: A Report on the Banality of Evil, trans. An Ni, Yilin Press, 2017-01-01, pp. 148-150)"},{"t":"ref","zh":"金观涛：《轴心文明与现代社会：从轴心文明到现代性》，中信出版集团，2020，第三章","en":"Jin Guantao, Axial Civilizations and Modern Society: From Axial Civilizations to Modernity, CITIC Press Group, 2020, Chapter 3"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Ibid p235-240","en":"Ibid., pp. 235-240"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Schmitt, Carl. The Concept of the Political. Expanded Edition. Translated by George Schwab. Chicago: University of Chicago Press, 2007.","en":"Schmitt, Carl. The Concept of the Political. Expanded Edition. Translated by George Schwab. Chicago: University of Chicago Press, 2007."},{"t":"ref","zh":"阿米塔夫高希：《大异常：气候变化与不可思议之事》 侯嘉星译，上海译文出版社, 2024","en":"Amitav Ghosh, The Great Derangement: Climate Change and the Unthinkable, trans. Hou Jiaxing, Shanghai Translation Publishing House, 2024"},{"t":"ref","zh":"梁漱溟：《中国文化要义》，上海人民出版社，2005（原著1949），第112–118页","en":"Liang Shuming, The Essential Features of Chinese Culture, Shanghai People’s Publishing House, 2005 (original 1949), pp. 112–118"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Tu Weiming, Confucian Thought: Self-Transformation as Creative Transformation ，Albany: State University of New York Press, 1985, p.113","en":"Tu Weiming, Confucian Thought: Self-Transformation as Creative Transformation, Albany: State University of New York Press, 1985, p.113"},{"t":"ref","zh":"孔子：《中庸》，指：因时制宜、随时而终。","en":"Confucius, The Doctrine of the Mean (Zhongyong); refers to acting as befits the time and concluding in accordance with the moment."},{"t":"ref","zh":"Wendy Brown，《废墟中的民主：新自由主义的隐形革命》，路国廷译，上海三联书店，2017，P31（英文原版为2015年，由Zone Books出版）","en":"Wendy Brown, Undoing the Demos: Neoliberalism’s Stealth Revolution (Chinese edition titled Democracy in Ruins: The Invisible Revolution of Neoliberalism), trans. Lu Guoting, Shanghai Joint Publishing, 2017, p. 31 (English original published by Zone Books in 2015)"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Byung-Chul Han, The Burnout Society, 2015, p. 9","en":"Byung-Chul Han, The Burnout Society, 2015, p. 9"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Byung-Chul Han, The Burnout Society, 2015, p.23","en":"Byung-Chul Han, The Burnout Society, 2015, p.23"},{"t":"ref","zh":"米歇尔福柯：《主体解释学：法兰西学院演讲录》佘碧平译，上海人民出版社, 2005","en":"Michel Foucault, The Hermeneutics of the Subject: Lectures at the Collège de France, trans. She Biping, Shanghai People’s Publishing House, 2005"},{"t":"ref","zh":"劳思光：《中国哲学史》三卷下，北京商务印书馆，2010，p340","en":"Lao Sze-kwang, A History of Chinese Philosophy, Vol. 3, Part 2, The Commercial Press, Beijing, 2010, p. 340"},{"t":"ref","zh":"沟口雄三:《中国前近代思想的演变》，阳海新译，中华书局，1997年。","en":"Mizoguchi Yūzō, The Evolution of Pre-Modern Chinese Thought, trans. Yang Haixin, Zhonghua Book Company, 1997."},{"t":"ref","zh":"张祥龙:《从现象学到孔夫子》，商务印书馆；《海德格尔思想与中国天道》，三联书店。","en":"Zhang Xianglong, From Phenomenology to Confucius, The Commercial Press; Heidegger’s Thought and the Chinese Way of Heaven, SDX Joint Publishing."},{"t":"ref","zh":"牟宗三：《心体与性体》（上册），上海古籍出版社2006，P18-22","en":"Mou Zongsan, Mind and Nature (Xinti yu xingti), Vol. 1, Shanghai Classics Publishing House, 2006, pp. 18-22"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Bourdieu Pierre & Wacquant Loïc，An Invitation to Reflexive Sociology.University of Chicago Press, 1992.","en":"Bourdieu Pierre & Wacquant Loïc, An Invitation to Reflexive Sociology. University of Chicago Press, 1992."},{"t":"ref","zh":"列斐伏尔：《空间的生产》，陆扬 朱志荣译，上海人民出版社，2001","en":"Henri Lefebvre, The Production of Space, trans. Lu Yang and Zhu Zhirong, Shanghai People’s Publishing House, 2001"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Tajfel H, Turner J，The Social Psychology of Intergroup Relations, 1979","en":"Tajfel H, Turner J, The Social Psychology of Intergroup Relations, 1979"},{"t":"ref","zh":"欧文戈夫曼：《日常生活中的自我呈现》，冯钢译，北京大学出版社, 2016","en":"Erving Goffman, The Presentation of Self in Everyday Life, trans. Feng Gang, Peking University Press, 2016"},{"t":"ref","zh":"哈贝马斯：《交往行为理论》李君如译，商务印书馆，2006 ，p62","en":"Jürgen Habermas, The Theory of Communicative Action, trans. Li Junru, The Commercial Press, 2006, p. 62"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Ibid ，p26-32","en":"Ibid., pp. 26-32"},{"t":"ref","zh":"海德格尔：《存在与时间》，陈嘉映 王庆节译，生活·读书·新知三联书店，2014","en":"Martin Heidegger, Being and Time, trans. Chen Jiaying and Wang Qingjie, SDX Joint Publishing, 2014"},{"t":"ref","zh":"杨伯峻：《孟子译注》，中华书局，2005","en":"Yang Bojun, The Mencius: Translated and Annotated, Zhonghua Book Company, 2005"},{"t":"ref","zh":"海德格尔：《存在与时间》，陈嘉映 王庆节译，生活·读书·新知三联书店，2014，p321","en":"Martin Heidegger, Being and Time, trans. Chen Jiaying and Wang Qingjie, SDX Joint Publishing, 2014, p. 321"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Gallagher Shaun，How the Body Shapes the Mind. Oxford, 2005，p19","en":"Gallagher Shaun, How the Body Shapes the Mind. Oxford, 2005, p19"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Damasio Antonio，Descartes’ Error. 1994，p174","en":"Damasio Antonio, Descartes’ Error. 1994, p174"},{"t":"ref","zh":"海德格尔：《存在与时间》，陈嘉映 王庆节译，生活·读书·新知三联书店，2014，p313","en":"Martin Heidegger, Being and Time, trans. Chen Jiaying and Wang Qingjie, SDX Joint Publishing, 2014, p. 313"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Böhme  Gernot，Atmosphere as the Fundamental Concept of a New Aesthetics, 1993","en":"Böhme Gernot, Atmosphere as the Fundamental Concept of a New Aesthetics, 1993"},{"t":"ref","zh":"诺伯格 舒尔茨：《建筑与存在的意义》，顾伟铭译，中国建筑工业出版，2012，p84","en":"Christian Norberg-Schulz, Architecture and the Meaning of Existence, trans. Gu Weiming, China Architecture & Building Press, 2012, p. 84"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Harlow, H. F. (1958). The nature of love. American Psychologist, 13(12), 673–685.","en":"Harlow, H. F. (1958). The nature of love. American Psychologist, 13(12), 673–685."},{"t":"ref","zh":"帕拉斯马：《感官的眼睛：建筑与感知》耶鲁大学出版社引进版，丁建中译，陕西师范大学出版社，2016，p75","en":"Juhani Pallasmaa, The Eyes of the Skin: Architecture and the Senses (licensed edition from Yale University Press), trans. Ding Jianzhong, Shaanxi Normal University Press, 2016, p. 75"},{"t":"ref","zh":"杨仁恺:《建筑感知与体验论》，同济大学出版社，2018","en":"Yang Renkai, On Architectural Perception and Experience, Tongji University Press, 2018"},{"t":"ref","zh":"帕拉斯马:《感官的眼睛：建筑与感知》，丁建中译，中国建筑工业出版社，2016","en":"Juhani Pallasmaa, The Eyes of the Skin: Architecture and the Senses, trans. Ding Jianzhong, China Architecture & Building Press, 2016"},{"t":"ref","zh":"康德:《判断力批判》李秋零译，中国人民大学出版社，2011","en":"Immanuel Kant, Critique of Judgment, trans. Li Qiuling, China Renmin University Press, 2011"},{"t":"ref","zh":"Ibid","en":"Ibid."},{"t":"ref","zh":"Homo Sacer: Sovereign Power and Bare Life. Agamben, Giorgio.Stanford University Press, 1998, p. 8","en":"Homo Sacer: Sovereign Power and Bare Life. Agamben, Giorgio. Stanford University Press, 1998, p. 8"},{"t":"ref","zh":"汉娜阿伦特:《人的境况》，王寅丽译，上海人民出版社，2009","en":"Hannah Arendt, The Human Condition, trans. Wang Yinli, Shanghai People’s Publishing House, 2009"},{"t":"ref","zh":"摩斯卡《统治阶级》：McGraw-Hill Book Company, Inc., 1939","en":"Gaetano Mosca, The Ruling Class: McGraw-Hill Book Company, Inc., 1939"},{"t":"ref","zh":"福柯《监视与惩罚：监狱的诞生》，陈嘉映译，生活·读书·新知三联书店，2018，p200-220","en":"Michel Foucault, Discipline and Punish: The Birth of the Prison, trans. Chen Jiaying, SDX Joint Publishing, 2018, pp. 200-220"}]},{"id":"W-2026-06","n":7,"title":{"zh":"感兴","en":"Ganxing (Stirred Response)"},"subtitle":{"zh":"水性材料的生发结果","en":"What Water-Based Materials Bring Forth"},"date":"2026-04-19","genre":"论文","summary":{"zh":"从材料本体的细微差异出发，分析中西绘画实践中不同的时间伦理与行动逻辑。","en":"Starting from subtle differences in the materials themselves, this paper analyses the different temporal ethics and logics of action in Chinese and Western painting practice."},"words":3231,"blocks":[{"t":"label","zh":"摘要","en":"Abstract"},{"t":"p","zh":"从材料本体的细微差异出发，分析中西绘画实践中不同的时间伦理与行动逻辑。古典油画以其油性介质的迟缓与覆盖力，构造出一种可回溯、可订正的“空间化时间”，其创作本质是向着先验理念反复修正的“逼近”。与之相对，中国水墨依托水性材料与宣纸的即时干结，造就了“时间的坍缩”与不可回撤的“生成”。这种“一次性”的创作机制，使绘画从单纯的再现转向了海德格尔意义上的“去蔽”与诗学意义上的“感兴”。借由王夫之“理在气中”的观念，揭示水墨创作中对“势”的推移与“几”的捕捉，实则是一种关于“临场决断”的生命演习。文人士大夫在不可逆的笔墨痕迹中，被训练为在流动时间中勇于承担后果的行动主体。","en":"Starting from subtle differences in the materials themselves, this paper analyses the different temporal ethics and logics of action in Chinese and Western painting practice. Classical oil painting, through the slowness and covering power of its oil-based medium, constructs a retraceable, correctable “spatialised time”; its creative essence is an “approximation” that corrects itself again and again toward an a priori idea. By contrast, Chinese ink painting, relying on the immediate drying and setting of water-based materials on xuan paper, produces a “collapse of time” and an irreversible “generation”. This “one-time” creative mechanism turns painting from mere representation toward “unconcealment” in Heidegger’s sense and ganxing (stirred response) in the poetic sense. Drawing on Wang Fuzhi’s idea that “principle lies within qi”, the paper shows that following the unfolding of shi (momentum) and seizing ji (the incipient moment) in ink painting are in fact a life-exercise in “decision on the spot”. Through irreversible traces of brush and ink, the literati-officials were trained to become acting subjects who dare to bear the consequences of their actions within flowing time."},{"t":"p","zh":"关键词： 水性材料；兴；生成逻辑；王夫之；势；主体性","en":"Keywords: water-based materials; xing (stirring response); generative logic; Wang Fuzhi; shi (momentum); subjectivity"},{"t":"label","zh":"Abstract","en":"Abstract"},{"t":"p","zh":"Drawing upon subtle distinctions inherent in the materials themselves, this analysis examines the divergent temporal ethics and logics of action embedded within the painting practices of the East and West. Classical oil painting—characterized by the viscosity and opacity of its oil-based medium—constructs a form of \"spatialized time\" that is both retrospective and amenable to revision; its creative essence lies in a process of iterative \"approximation\" toward a transcendental ideal. In contrast, Chinese ink painting—relying on the rapid drying properties of water-based media and “Xuan”paper—engenders a \"collapse of time\" and an irreversible process of \"generation.\" This \"one-shot\" creative mechanism shifts the focus of painting from mere representation toward \"unconcealment\" (in the Heideggerian sense) and \"poetic inspiration\" (“ganxing”). By invoking Wang Fuzhi’s concept that \"Principle resides within *Qi*,\" this study reveals that the manipulation of \"momentum\" (“shi”) and the capture of \"incipient moments\" (“ji”) in ink painting constitute, in essence, a vital exercise in \"situational decision-making.\" Through the medium of irreversible brushstrokes and ink traces, the literati-official is thus trained to emerge as an active subject—one prepared to courageously shoulder the consequences of their actions amidst the ceaseless flow of time.","en":"Drawing upon subtle distinctions inherent in the materials themselves, this analysis examines the divergent temporal ethics and logics of action embedded within the painting practices of the East and West. Classical oil painting—characterized by the viscosity and opacity of its oil-based medium—constructs a form of \"spatialized time\" that is both retrospective and amenable to revision; its creative essence lies in a process of iterative \"approximation\" toward a transcendental ideal. In contrast, Chinese ink painting—relying on the rapid drying properties of water-based media and “Xuan”paper—engenders a \"collapse of time\" and an irreversible process of \"generation.\" This \"one-shot\" creative mechanism shifts the focus of painting from mere representation toward \"unconcealment\" (in the Heideggerian sense) and \"poetic inspiration\" (“ganxing”). By invoking Wang Fuzhi’s concept that \"Principle resides within *Qi*,\" this study reveals that the manipulation of \"momentum\" (“shi”) and the capture of \"incipient moments\" (“ji”) in ink painting constitute, in essence, a vital exercise in \"situational decision-making.\" Through the medium of irreversible brushstrokes and ink traces, the literati-official is thus trained to emerge as an active subject—one prepared to courageously shoulder the consequences of their actions amidst the ceaseless flow of time."},{"t":"p","zh":"Keywords: Water-based materials; “Xing” (Inspiration); Generative logic; Wang Fuzhi; “Shi”(Momentum); Subjectivity","en":"Keywords: Water-based materials; “Xing” (Inspiration); Generative logic; Wang Fuzhi; “Shi”(Momentum); Subjectivity"},{"t":"h","zh":"引言","en":"Introduction"},{"t":"p","zh":"材料不仅是艺术表现的工具，更是思维逻辑的容器。在中国文人画的传统中，水性材料在宣纸上的物理表现——迅速的毛细渗透与纤维固着——不仅决定了画面的视觉肌理，更深层地重塑了创作的时间经验。本文试图论证，这种材料特性如何迫使创作者从“预设目标的完成者”转变为“流变过程的承担者”，并在此过程中完成一种独特的哲学主体的建构。","en":"Materials are not only tools of artistic expression; they are also containers of a logic of thought. In the tradition of Chinese literati painting, the physical behaviour of water-based materials on xuan paper—rapid capillary penetration and fixation in the fibres—not only determines the visual texture of the picture but, at a deeper level, reshapes the temporal experience of creation. This paper attempts to show how this property of the material forces the creator to change from “one who completes a preset goal” into “one who bears a process of flux”, and how, in this process, a distinctive philosophical subject is constructed."},{"t":"h","zh":"“时间的形态”在中西古典绘画技法的差异：逼近与生成","en":"“The Form of Time” in the Differing Techniques of Classical Chinese and Western Painting: Approximation and Generation"},{"t":"p","zh":"油性介质干燥迟缓且具有遮盖力，时间因此被“空间化”了：艺术家可以在画布上进行反复的覆盖、涂抹与修改。这种古典油画的技法在逻辑的本质上是“逼近”。达·芬奇在《论绘画》中曾强调绘画是通过“增加与减少”来完善的。由于油性介质干燥迟缓且具备遮盖力，时间被转化为一种可回溯的空间维度：艺术家可以在画布上反复覆盖、刮除、修正。在这种逻辑下，画面是某种先验“理念（Idea）”的摹本，创作过程是向着既定终点的逐步靠拢。","en":"Oil-based media dry slowly and have covering power, and so time is “spatialised”: the artist can cover, smear and revise on the canvas again and again. In its logical essence, the technique of classical oil painting is “approximation”. In his Treatise on Painting, Leonardo da Vinci stressed that painting is perfected through “adding and taking away”. Because the oil-based medium dries slowly and has covering power, time is turned into a retraceable spatial dimension: the artist can repeatedly cover, scrape away and correct on the canvas. Under this logic, the picture is a copy of some a priori “Idea”, and the creative process is a gradual approach toward a fixed endpoint."},{"t":"p","zh":"与之相对，水墨绘画，一旦水墨触碰纸面，水墨的分子就会沁入到纸纤维的缝隙中，并随着墨汁的干燥而永久地和纸面融为一体。这种不可逆转性使得创作者在创作时需一笔成型、一笔定性。石涛在《苦瓜和尚画语录》中云：“一画者，众有之本，万象之根。”这一笔下去，不存在回撤，只能顺势而为。绘画行为因此从“空间堆垒”转向了一种“生成”：时间是不可回撤的、有方向绵延的。","en":"In ink painting, by contrast, once the ink touches the paper its molecules seep into the gaps between the paper fibres and, as the ink dries, become permanently one with the paper surface. This irreversibility requires the creator to give each stroke its form, and settle its character, in a single movement. In his Sayings on Painting by the Monk Bitter Melon, Shitao writes: “The single stroke is the origin of all that exists and the root of the myriad phenomena.” Once this stroke is laid down there is no taking it back; one can only follow its momentum. The act of painting thus turns from “spatial accumulation” to a kind of “generation”: time is irreversible, a duration with a direction."},{"t":"h","zh":"“兴”与“去蔽”：画面意义的动态发生","en":"Xing and “Unconcealment”: The Dynamic Emergence of Pictorial Meaning"},{"t":"p","zh":"水性媒介的这种“干结”过程，接近于海德格尔意义上的真理发生。它不是对对象的再现，而是存在本身在特定瞬间的“去蔽”。每一次落笔都具有本体论上的终极性。海德格尔的真理发生与中国诗学的“兴”，在深层中是同构的：它们共同指向了“意义并非由于事先的设计，而是在行动或遭遇的当下瞬间‘跃出’”的这一特征。刘勰在《文心雕龙》中谓：“兴者，起也。”叶嘉莹先生亦指出，兴是诗人心灵在外物触动之下自然引发的感发活动。","en":"This “drying and setting” process of the water-based medium comes close to the happening of truth in Heidegger’s sense. It is not a representation of an object but the “unconcealment” of being itself at a particular instant. Every stroke carries an ontological finality. Heidegger’s happening of truth and xing (stirring response) in Chinese poetics are isomorphic at a deep level: both point to the same feature, that “meaning does not come from prior design but ‘leaps out’ in the present instant of action or encounter.” Liu Xie writes in The Literary Mind and the Carving of Dragons: “Xing means to arise.” Ye Jiaying likewise points out that xing is the activity of feeling that arises naturally in the poet’s mind when it is touched by external things."},{"t":"p","zh":"在水墨创作中，创作者并非依循一份精确的草图，而是在“因物起兴”的过程中，让手腕的呼吸节律、墨色的洇散与内在的情感共同交织。这种发生形态所导致的是，意义不再来源于提前设定的先验理念，而是在行动与材料的剧烈互动中被不断触发、修正并最终成形的痕迹。","en":"In ink painting, the creator does not follow a precise sketch; instead, in the process of “being stirred by things”, the breathing rhythm of the wrist, the spreading of the ink and inner emotion are woven together. What this mode of emergence brings about is that meaning no longer derives from an a priori idea set in advance; it is a trace that is continually triggered, revised and finally given form in the intense interaction between action and material."},{"t":"p","zh":"与古典油画作对比我们则可以发现，西方油画式的“逼近”逻辑，赋予了主体一种掌控全局的、可以反复试验的上帝视角；而水墨绘画的“生成”逻辑，则迫使主体进入一种临场的感受与决断。这种临场取消了“草稿”与“正稿”的界限。意义并非预设，也不是事后的追认，而是在每一个当下瞬间显现。","en":"Comparing this with classical oil painting, we find that the Western oil-painting logic of “approximation” grants the subject a God’s-eye view that commands the whole and can experiment again and again, whereas the “generative” logic of ink painting forces the subject into feeling and deciding on the spot. Being on the spot in this way abolishes the boundary between “draft” and “final version”. Meaning is neither preset nor ratified after the fact; it appears in each present instant."},{"t":"p","zh":"这一逻辑的发展，导向了明清之际王夫之对“势”与“几”的精微讨论：当行动者意识到每一步都不可回撤时，他必须在历史的流动中捕捉那最微妙的动向。","en":"This logic, as it develops, leads to Wang Fuzhi’s subtle discussion of shi (momentum) and ji (incipience) at the turn of the Ming and Qing dynasties: when the actor realises that no step can be taken back, he must catch the most subtle tendencies within the flow of history."},{"t":"h","zh":"王夫之视域下的“势”与“几”","en":"Shi and Ji from Wang Fuzhi’s Perspective"},{"t":"p","zh":"若从思想史角度考察，文人画的这种行动逻辑与明清之际思想家王夫之的历史观高度契合。王夫之反对静止的“理”，主张“理在气中”，即真理存在于事物的演进过程之中。“势之所趋，人不得不然。”文人画作画者不依仗草图，而是根据第一笔落下的“势”来推导第二笔。“几者，动之微也。”在动与静的交界处。这件事已经“动”了，但还没有显现出来；它在萌芽状态，尚未形成无可挽回的定局。在水墨创作中，水滴触碰纸面的那一微秒，墨汁尚未完全洇散，但纤维的渗透方向已经由纸张的疏密、笔锋的残存压力决定了。在这个时刻，结果尚未显现，但因果方向已经落位。","en":"Examined from the standpoint of intellectual history, this logic of action in literati painting accords closely with the view of history of Wang Fuzhi, the thinker of the Ming–Qing transition. Wang Fuzhi opposed a static li (principle) and held that “principle lies within qi (vital energy)”, that is, truth exists within the process by which things unfold. “Where momentum tends, people cannot but follow.” The literati painter does not rely on a sketch but derives the second stroke from the shi of the first stroke laid down. “Ji is the minute beginning of movement.” It lies at the border between movement and stillness. The matter has already “moved” but has not yet become manifest; it is in a germinal state and has not yet hardened into an irreversible outcome. In ink painting, in the microsecond when a drop of water touches the paper, the ink has not yet fully spread, but the direction in which it will penetrate the fibres has already been determined by the density of the paper and the residual pressure of the brush tip. At this moment the result has not yet appeared, but the direction of cause and effect is already in place."},{"t":"h","zh":"结论：塑造“在流动中承担后果”的主体","en":"Conclusion: Shaping a Subject Who “Bears the Consequences Amid Flux”"},{"t":"p","zh":"与西方传统不同，文人士大夫并非仅以雇主的形式参与到艺术文化的发展与建设中，他们同时还以职业手工艺人的身份进行绘画，将绘画视为修身与表达的一种方式。因此，在绘画实践中形成的行动逻辑——例如对不可回撤行为的承担、对整体趋势的判断以及对偶然性的包容——并不会局限于艺术领域，而是通过书写、治理与日常交往逐渐扩散到更广泛的社会生活之中。","en":"Unlike in the Western tradition, the literati-officials did not take part in the development and building of artistic culture only as patrons; they also painted in the capacity of professional craftsmen, treating painting as a means of self-cultivation and expression. Therefore the logic of action formed in painting practice—bearing responsibility for acts that cannot be undone, judging overall tendencies, accommodating chance—did not remain confined to the field of art, but gradually spread, through writing, governance and everyday social interaction, into the wider life of society."},{"t":"p","zh":"中国文人画塑造的主体是一个嵌入流变时间、与客体共同生成的参与者。他们习惯于在不可控的偶然性中寻找秩序，在不可撤回的行动中承担责任。","en":"The subject shaped by Chinese literati painting is a participant embedded in changing time, coming into being together with the object. Such subjects are accustomed to seeking order within uncontrollable contingency and to taking responsibility within actions that cannot be withdrawn."},{"t":"h","zh":"参考文献 (References)","en":"References"},{"t":"ref","zh":"[唐] 张彦远，《历代名画记》.","en":"[Tang] Zhang Yanyuan, Record of Famous Painters of Successive Dynasties (Lidai minghua ji)."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[清] 石涛，《苦瓜和尚画语录》.","en":"[Qing] Shitao, Sayings on Painting by the Monk Bitter Melon (Kugua heshang huayu lu)."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[德] 海德格尔，《艺术作品的本源》.","en":"[Germany] Heidegger, The Origin of the Work of Art."},{"t":"ref","zh":"(意) 达·芬奇，《 达·芬奇论绘画 》戴勉译， 北京: 人民美术出版社, 1979.P22-24","en":"(Italy) Leonardo da Vinci, Leonardo da Vinci on Painting, trans. Dai Mian, Beijing: People’s Fine Arts Publishing House, 1979. pp. 22–24"},{"t":"ref","zh":"(德) 海德格尔，《林中路》 孙周兴译， 上海: 上海译文出版社, 2004. P39","en":"(Germany) Heidegger, Off the Beaten Track (Holzwege), trans. Sun Zhouxing, Shanghai: Shanghai Translation Publishing House, 2004. p. 39"},{"t":"ref","zh":"(法) 吉尔·德勒兹，《感觉的逻辑》，董强译，广西师范大学出版社2007版P158 (梁)刘勰，《文心雕龙》，中华书局，2012，第283页。","en":"(France) Gilles Deleuze, Francis Bacon: The Logic of Sensation, trans. Dong Qiang, Guangxi Normal University Press, 2007 edition, p. 158 (Liang) Liu Xie, The Literary Mind and the Carving of Dragons, Zhonghua Book Company, 2012, p. 283."},{"t":"ref","zh":"叶嘉莹，《迦陵论诗丛稿》，中华书局，2014，第72页。","en":"Ye Jiaying, Collected Essays on Poetry by Jialing (Jialing lunshi conggao), Zhonghua Book Company, 2014, p. 72."},{"t":"ref","zh":"(清) 王国维、叶嘉莹，《人间词话：叶嘉莹讲评本》，万卷出版公司，2021 .P9","en":"(Qing) Wang Guowei and Ye Jiaying, Remarks on Lyrics in the Human World: With Lectures and Commentary by Ye Jiaying, Wanjuan Publishing Company, 2021. p. 9"},{"t":"ref","zh":"(清) 王夫之，《读通鉴论》，北京: 中华书局, 1975 P1112","en":"(Qing) Wang Fuzhi, On Reading the Comprehensive Mirror (Du Tongjian lun), Beijing: Zhonghua Book Company, 1975, p. 1112"},{"t":"ref","zh":"(清) 王夫之，《周易外传》，中华书局，2010，P32。意为：行动必须在变化中把握契机。","en":"(Qing) Wang Fuzhi, Outer Commentary on the Book of Changes (Zhouyi waizhuan), Zhonghua Book Company, 2010, p. 32. Meaning: action must seize the opportune moment amid change."},{"t":"ref","zh":"牟宗三. 《政道与治道》 台北: 学生书局, 1991.P58","en":"Mou Zongsan. The Way of Politics and the Way of Governance (Zhengdao yu zhidao). Taipei: Student Book Co., 1991. p. 58"},{"t":"ref","zh":"(法) 亨利·柏格森，《时间与自由意志》吴士栋译， 商务印书馆1958.P75-78","en":"(France) Henri Bergson, Time and Free Will, trans. Wu Shidong, The Commercial Press, 1958. pp. 75–78"},{"t":"ref","zh":"(法) 吉尔·德勒兹，《意义的逻辑》董强译. 上海: 上海译文出版社, 2011.P9","en":"(France) Gilles Deleuze, The Logic of Sense, trans. Dong Qiang. Shanghai: Shanghai Translation Publishing House, 2011. p. 9"}]},{"id":"W-2026-07","n":6,"title":{"zh":"现代性视角下当代青年“内卷”与“躺平”的成因及演变研究","en":"The Causes and Evolution of “Involution” and “Lying Flat” among Contemporary Youth: A Study from the Perspective of Modernity"},"subtitle":null,"date":"2026-06-11","genre":"论文","summary":{"zh":"本文立足于现代性视角，探讨当代青年群体中“内卷”与“躺平”现象的深层成因与历史演变。","en":"From the perspective of modernity, this paper explores the deep causes and historical evolution of the phenomena of “involution” (neijuan) and “lying flat” (tang ping) among contemporary young people."},"words":2266,"blocks":[{"t":"label","zh":"摘要","en":"Abstract"},{"t":"p","zh":"本文立足于现代性视角，探讨当代青年群体中“内卷”与“躺平”现象的深层成因与历史演变。研究认为，“内卷”与“躺平”并非个体主动选择的人生态度，而是青年面对社会结构困境时，因缺乏稳定意义感而产生的消极防御。文章梳理了改革开放以来我国个体“主体性”演变的四个阶段，指出在宏观体制重构与微观绩效社会的双重压力下，个体由于“努力—回报”机制失效而陷入“自我管理与自我剥削”的倦怠悖论，进而生发出向往地理迁移的“彼岸幻想”。研究表明，青年意义感的缺失是一种被延迟、被转移的结构性结果，单纯依靠个体心理调适难以根本解决。缓解该困境亟需在宏观和微观层面重新理顺和重构支撑个体行动的社会机制。","en":"From the perspective of modernity, this paper explores the deep causes and historical evolution of the phenomena of “involution” (neijuan) and “lying flat” (tang ping) among contemporary young people. It argues that “involution” and “lying flat” are not attitudes toward life that individuals actively choose, but a passive defense that arises when young people, confronting the predicament of the social structure, lack a stable sense of meaning. The paper traces four stages in the evolution of individual “subjectivity” in China since the Reform and Opening-up, and points out that under the double pressure of macro-level institutional restructuring and the micro-level performance society, individuals—because the “effort–reward” mechanism has failed—fall into the burnout paradox of “self-management and self-exploitation,” which in turn gives rise to an “other-shore fantasy” of longing for geographical relocation. The study shows that young people’s loss of a sense of meaning is a deferred and displaced structural outcome, one that can hardly be fundamentally resolved by individual psychological adjustment alone. Alleviating this predicament urgently requires straightening out and reconstructing, at both the macro and micro levels, the social mechanisms that support individual action."},{"t":"p","zh":"关键词：青年群体；主体性危机；内卷；","en":"Keywords: youth; crisis of subjectivity; involution;"},{"t":"h","zh":"一、 引言：“内卷”与“躺平”的现象审视","en":"1. Introduction: Examining the Phenomena of “Involution” and “Lying Flat”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在今天的公共讨论中，“内卷”与“躺平”已经从网络热词演变成了年轻人的常态化生活标签。对于这一问题的归因，通常包括但不限于以下几种：①指向全球范围共有的人类所面临的现代性危机；②溯源至五四、改革开放...作“中-西、传统-现代”或“过去、当下”的二元对立从而指向身份认同危机；③互联网时代以来的新的社会结构、人与人之间相处方式的改变，由此所加深的身份与身体的分离.....与此同时，许多评论习惯于将这一现象扁平化地诊断为“年轻人失去了意义感”，并顺理成章地开出“改变心态从而解决问题”的药方。然而，内卷与躺平绝非年轻人主动选择的“人生态度”，而是面对同一种社会结构困境时，因缺乏稳定意义感而产生的消极防御。","en":"In today’s public discussion, “involution” and “lying flat” have evolved from internet buzzwords into routine labels for young people’s lives. Explanations of this problem usually include, but are not limited to, the following: ① pointing to the crisis of modernity shared by humanity worldwide; ② tracing it back to the May Fourth Movement, the Reform and Opening-up..., setting up binary oppositions of “China–West, tradition–modernity” or “past–present” and thus pointing to a crisis of identity; ③ the new social structures and changed ways people relate to one another since the advent of the internet age, and the resulting deepening separation of identity from the body..... At the same time, many commentators habitually give this phenomenon the flattened diagnosis that “young people have lost their sense of meaning,” and, as a matter of course, prescribe the remedy of “changing one’s mindset to solve the problem.” However, involution and lying flat are by no means “attitudes toward life” that young people actively choose; they are a passive defense that arises, in the face of the same structural social predicament, from the lack of a stable sense of meaning."},{"t":"h","zh":"二、 宏观结构视域下的现代性危机与中西方差异","en":"2. The Crisis of Modernity and Sino-Western Differences from a Macro-Structural Perspective"},{"t":"p","zh":"当代人常因“我是谁”、“我为什么而活”的终极困惑而感到焦虑。福柯认为：“自20世纪60年代以来，主体性、身份认同和个体性构成了一个重大的政治问题”；因此，我们必须首先改变“我们的主体性，我们与自身的关系。”这种斗争不再是针对剥削或宏观经济结构，而是针对个人与自身结合的斗争。关于对现代性危机的分析，从马克斯韦伯到今天，这些对断裂的讨论在西方已经延续了相当长的时间，主体性的问题在西方，从传统社会“宗教”到现代“世俗伦理”、“职业精神”、“公民身份”的转变形态是层层递进的。而相比之下，在中国，自改革开放以来，传统社会结构的宗族、道德、伦理秩序并非“循序渐进地过渡到当今全球化的现代社会形态”，而是在战争后高度加速的政治—制度重构中被切断。费孝通先生基于血缘和地缘的熟人社会伦理提出的“差序格局”，在快速城市化中土崩瓦解。人们从被国家全面包裹的“单位、公社体制”，被抛入到讲究契约和利益的“全球化市场体制”中。这也是为什么当代中国在经历了经济奇迹的同时，常常伴随着道德焦虑、信任危机和伦理失范的原因——因为我们跳过了建立现代公共精神和契约道德的“循序渐进”阶段。这是放在宏观结构作讨论，那么对于微观的数个个体而言：个人与自身结合的斗争”又是怎样发生的？","en":"People today often feel anxious over the ultimate questions of “Who am I?” and “What am I living for?” Foucault held that “since the 1960s, subjectivity, identity and individuality have constituted a major political problem”; we must therefore first change “our subjectivity, our relationship to ourselves.” This struggle is no longer directed against exploitation or macroeconomic structures, but is a struggle concerning the individual’s bond with the self. As for the analysis of the crisis of modernity, from Max Weber to the present these discussions of rupture have continued in the West for a considerable time; there, the question of subjectivity has evolved step by step, from “religion” in traditional society to the modern forms of “secular ethics,” “professional ethos” and “citizenship.” By contrast, in China since the Reform and Opening-up, the clan, moral and ethical order of the traditional social structure did not “transition gradually into today’s globalized form of modern society,” but was severed amid the highly accelerated political and institutional restructuring after the war. The “differential mode of association” that Fei Xiaotong proposed, based on the ethics of an acquaintance society rooted in kinship and locality, collapsed amid rapid urbanization. People were thrown out of the “work-unit and commune system,” in which the state enveloped them completely, into a “globalized market system” governed by contracts and interests. This is also why contemporary China, while experiencing an economic miracle, has often been accompanied by moral anxiety, a crisis of trust and ethical anomie—because we skipped the “gradual” stage of building a modern public spirit and contractual morality. This is the discussion at the level of macro structure; then, for the many individuals at the micro level, how does “the struggle concerning the individual’s bond with the self” take place?"},{"t":"h","zh":"三、 改革开放以来青年主体性演变的历史脉络","en":"3. The Historical Trajectory of the Evolution of Youth Subjectivity since the Reform and Opening-up"},{"t":"p","zh":"在改革开放初期（1980s-1990s），“个人”概念大量涌现，但当时的目标高度外在化——为了生存、为了改善家庭命运。此时，人虽在行动，但不需要反思“我是谁”，因为“活下去、改变命运”本身就是最明确的答案。","en":"In the early period of the Reform and Opening-up (1980s–1990s), the concept of the “individual” emerged on a large scale, but the goals of the time were highly externalized—to survive, to improve the family’s fortunes. At this stage, although people were acting, they did not need to reflect on “who am I,” because “staying alive and changing one’s fate” was itself the clearest answer."},{"t":"p","zh":"到了上世纪90年代末至2000年前后，随着教育、就业的制度化和绩效化，“努力—回报”变成了可量化的路径。社会开始要求个人用“结果”来证明自己的价值，“成功”成为正当主体的唯一标准。尽管此时意义已被高度功利化，但由于社会流动性依然存在，未来仍被想象为是“敞开的”。","en":"From the late 1990s to around 2000, as education and employment became institutionalized and performance-based, “effort–reward” turned into a quantifiable path. Society began to require individuals to prove their worth through “results,” and “success” became the sole criterion of a legitimate subject. Although meaning had by then become highly utilitarian, because social mobility still existed, the future was still imagined as “open.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"真正的危机在近年来全面显化。随着上升路径变窄，成功标准进一步单一化，个体却被要求为包括结构性失败在内的一切结果负责。行动仍被强烈要求，但行动的结果却不再指向明确的未来。尤其是社交媒体的盛行，更让年轻人陷入了“自我管理—自我剥削”的恶性循环——呈现出高度自律、持续自我优化，却又由于缺乏精神锚点而极度倦怠的悖论形态。","en":"The real crisis has become fully manifest in recent years. As the paths upward narrow and the standard of success becomes still more uniform, individuals are nonetheless required to take responsibility for every outcome, including structural failure. Action is still strongly demanded, but its results no longer point toward a clear future. The prevalence of social media in particular has trapped young people in a vicious circle of “self-management—self-exploitation”—a paradoxical condition of high self-discipline and continuous self-optimization combined with extreme burnout due to the lack of a spiritual anchor."},{"t":"h","zh":"四、 绩效社会下青年的行为响应机制","en":"4. Young People’s Behavioral Response Mechanisms in the Performance Society"},{"t":"h","zh":"（一） “内卷”与“躺平”：同质化的精神退缩","en":"(1) “Involution” and “Lying Flat”: A Homogeneous Spiritual Retreat"},{"t":"p","zh":"在这种背景下，无论是与之同步的“内卷”还是滞留原地的“躺平”，其实都是“消极”的行动疲惫与精神退缩。绩效社会的高效数据使得整体看上去“积极”，但实则对于青年人来说，无论是选择在系统中加速对抗的内卷，还是选择在原地停滞的躺平，其背后无法避免的都是行动空间的压缩、精神的退缩以及道德的冷却。","en":"Against this background, whether it is “involution,” which keeps pace with the system, or “lying flat,” which stays put, both are in fact “passive” exhaustion of action and spiritual retreat. The efficient data of the performance society make the whole look “positive,” but in reality, for young people, whether they choose involution—accelerating their struggle within the system—or lying flat—standing still where they are—what lies unavoidably behind both is the compression of the space for action, spiritual retreat and the cooling of morality."},{"t":"h","zh":"（二） “彼岸幻想”：空间迁移作为唯一有效的想象行动","en":"(2) The “Other-Shore Fantasy”: Spatial Relocation as the Only Effective Imagined Action"},{"t":"p","zh":"近年来被频繁提起的第三种选择，是设定一个地理位置上的迁移（如大理、阿勒泰或海外）——一个理想的彼岸。需要指出的是，这种理想状态并不真实存在，只是一种象征。比如，将未来的目标设定为地理位置上的迁移。这是一种广泛的状态设定：退出既定评价体系、暂停持续比较、逃离熟人社会的期待与羞耻。哪怕这是一种幻想的“彼岸”设定，在现实中并不更轻松，但它至少更陌生、可以远离“断裂的主要承受者”的结构性位置。当“改变这里”不可实现时，只剩“离开这里”。因为“离开”会成为唯一被想象为有效的行动。这是行动空间被压缩后的自然反应，而旅游业和全球化则为这一幻想提供了可被想象的理想目的地。","en":"A third option frequently raised in recent years is to set oneself a geographical relocation (such as to Dali, Altay or overseas)—an ideal other shore. It should be pointed out that this ideal state does not really exist; it is only a symbol. For example, one sets one’s future goal as a geographical relocation. This is a widespread setting of one’s state: withdrawing from the established evaluation system, suspending constant comparison, escaping the expectations and shame of the acquaintance society. Even though this is a fantasized “other shore” that is not actually easier in reality, it is at least more unfamiliar, and it allows one to move away from the structural position of being “the main bearer of the rupture.” When “changing this place” cannot be achieved, only “leaving this place” remains, because “leaving” becomes the only action imagined to be effective. This is a natural reaction once the space for action has been compressed, and tourism and globalization supply this fantasy with imaginable ideal destinations."},{"t":"p","zh":"绩效社会的高效数据使得整体看上去“积极”。但实则对于青年人来说，无论是与之同步的“内卷”还是滞留原地的“躺平”，“消极”的行动疲惫、精神退缩、道德冷却，都是两者无法避免的情况。","en":"The efficient data of the performance society make the whole look “positive.” But in reality, for young people, whether it is “involution,” which keeps pace with the system, or “lying flat,” which stays put, “passive” exhaustion of action, spiritual retreat and moral cooling are unavoidable in both."},{"t":"h","zh":"五、 结论","en":"5. Conclusion"},{"t":"p","zh":"总而言之，将内卷与躺平简单归结为个体的心理或道德问题，既不合逻辑也无法解决问题。这是一种被延迟、被转移的结构性结果，青年人并非失去了信念，而是过去赖以支撑行动的社会机制，亟待在宏观和微观层面得到重构与理顺。","en":"In sum, simply attributing involution and lying flat to individuals’ psychological or moral problems is both illogical and incapable of solving the problem. This is a deferred and displaced structural outcome: young people have not lost their convictions; rather, the social mechanisms that once supported their action urgently need to be reconstructed and straightened out at both the macro and micro levels."}]},{"id":"W-2026-08","n":8,"title":{"zh":"见证与转化的伦理","en":"The Ethics of Witness and Transformation"},"subtitle":{"zh":"——塞巴斯蒂安·萨尔加多纪实摄影中的本真性问题兼论对本真系列肖像绘画的创作启示","en":"— The Question of Authenticity in Sebastião Salgado’s Documentary Photography, with Reflections on Its Implications for the Authenticity Series of Portrait Paintings"},"date":"2026-07-15","genre":"论文","summary":{"zh":"塞巴斯蒂安·萨尔加多（Sebastião Salgado）的纪实摄影在当代视觉文化中占据着特殊位置：他的作品既以宏大的美学力量震撼观者，又因将苦难高度美学化而持续引发伦理争议。","en":"Sebastião Salgado’s documentary photography occupies a special place in contemporary visual culture: his work overwhelms viewers with its grand aesthetic power, yet continually provokes ethical controversy for aestheticising suffering to such a high degree."},"words":8946,"blocks":[{"t":"p","zh":"摘要：塞巴斯蒂安·萨尔加多（Sebastião Salgado）的纪实摄影在当代视觉文化中占据着特殊位置：他的作品既以宏大的美学力量震撼观者，又因将苦难高度美学化而持续引发伦理争议。本文以\"本真性\"（authenticity）为核心分析框架，考察萨尔加多摄影实践中苦难呈现与美学转化之间的张力结构。论文首先梳理萨尔加多的艺术道路与核心关切，进而从图像学、政治哲学与接受美学三个维度分析其作品中的\"本真性悖论\"——即苦难在被摄影转化为艺术对象的过程中，究竟是被见证、被传播，还是被过滤、被消费。在此基础上，本文引入海德格尔关于\"本真性存在\"的论述及本雅明的\"灵韵\"概念，提出萨尔加多摄影中\"本真性见证\"得以可能的三个结构性条件：时间性承诺、非剥削的观看姿态、以及图像的政治责任承担。最后，本文将上述分析延伸至个人肖像绘画创作实践——\"人物本真系列\"，阐述萨尔加多的方法论如何启发一种以捕捉功能性交流之外的本真性流露为目标的当代肖像绘画路径。","en":"Abstract: Sebastião Salgado’s documentary photography occupies a special place in contemporary visual culture: his work overwhelms viewers with its grand aesthetic power, yet continually provokes ethical controversy for aestheticising suffering to such a high degree. Taking “authenticity” as its core analytical framework, this paper examines the structure of tension between the presentation of suffering and its aesthetic transformation in Salgado’s photographic practice. It first traces Salgado’s artistic path and central concerns, then analyses the “paradox of authenticity” in his work from three dimensions, iconology, political philosophy and reception aesthetics: namely, whether suffering, in the process of being turned by photography into an art object, is witnessed and disseminated, or filtered and consumed. On this basis, the paper draws on Heidegger’s account of “authentic existence” and Benjamin’s concept of “aura” to propose three structural conditions that make “authentic testimony” possible in Salgado’s photography: a temporal commitment, a non-exploitative stance of looking, and the assumption of political responsibility by the image. Finally, the paper extends this analysis to my own practice of portrait painting, the “Authenticity Series of Figures”, setting out how Salgado’s methodology inspires a path for contemporary portrait painting that aims to capture authentic expression beyond functional communication."},{"t":"p","zh":"关键词：塞巴斯蒂安·萨尔加多；本真性；纪实摄影；苦难美学；肖像绘画；海德格尔","en":"Keywords: Sebastião Salgado; authenticity; documentary photography; aesthetics of suffering; portrait painting; Heidegger"},{"t":"h","zh":"一、引言","en":"1. Introduction"},{"t":"p","zh":"在最初筹备硕士毕业论文时，塞巴斯蒂安·萨尔加多（Sebastião Salgado）是我想要深入研究的艺术家之一。大约两三年前，我第一次观看了由维姆·文德斯（Wim Wenders）执导的纪录片《地球之盐》（The Salt of the Earth），此后又反复观看多次。纪录片铺设了多条线索：主线是萨尔加多摄影作品的几个重要系列——塞拉佩拉达金矿（Serra Pelada）、移民（Migrations）、劳动者（Workers）、创世纪（Genesis）；副线则包括他的人生轨迹与社会实践。文德斯在片中说，他最初看到萨尔加多的摄影作品时，被其中传达出的\"艺术家对人类的爱\"深深感动。这句话至今仍是我理解萨尔加多的起点。","en":"When I first began preparing my master’s thesis, Sebastião Salgado was one of the artists I wanted to study in depth. About two or three years ago I first watched The Salt of the Earth, the documentary directed by Wim Wenders, and I have watched it many times since. The film lays out several threads: the main one follows several major series of Salgado’s photographs, Serra Pelada, Migrations, Workers and Genesis; the secondary threads include the course of his life and his social engagement. In the film Wenders says that when he first saw Salgado’s photographs, he was deeply moved by the “artist’s love for humanity” they conveyed. That sentence is still the starting point of my understanding of Salgado."},{"t":"p","zh":"我也被这位艺术家的作品深深打动，十七八岁时甚至选择了几张他所摄制的人物形象画了下来。那时曾有一段时间很想做战地记者，而这部纪录片重新燃起了那个热情：我希望将战争、非洲挨饿的孩子们、瘦骨嶙峋的死亡——这些通过绘画、摄影或文字记录下来、传播出去。两三年后重燃这个想法时，有了更复杂的考虑。当时就已经意识到苦难美学化所带来的伦理问题。如今，这个问题在我这里的状态可能仍是pending，但通过这篇论文，我希望进行一次系统的梳理与回应。","en":"I was deeply moved by this artist’s work too, and at seventeen or eighteen I even chose a few of the figures he photographed and drew them. For a time back then I very much wanted to be a war correspondent, and this documentary rekindled that passion: I wanted to record and spread, through painting, photography or writing, war, the starving children of Africa, skeletal death. When the idea came back two or three years later, my thinking had become more complicated. I was already aware then of the ethical problems that the aestheticisation of suffering brings. Today the question may still be “pending” for me, but through this paper I hope to work through it systematically and respond to it."},{"t":"p","zh":"\"艺术表达、展示、传递苦难\"这件事情，本身具有深刻的\"双刃\"性质。一方面，带着爱的视角与情感的传播以及苦难本身，会在观者心中激起涟漪——我们因同情、因看见，而对这个议题投入更多关注与行动，也会由此引发个人层面的深刻反思。而另一方面，当我们在这个场所展示苦难时，呈现的始终是一种被过滤、被\"艺术化\"了的苦难。当我们对这个审美对象倾注情感时，对苦难本身的关注在大多数情况下会被悬置——大多数人只是在做一种\"良心安慰\"式的自我感动。苦难所带来的情感幅度，在此过程中被转化为消费逻辑的标价。","en":"The act of “expressing, exhibiting and conveying suffering through art” is in itself deeply “double-edged”. On the one hand, the dissemination of a loving perspective and of emotion, and suffering itself, send ripples through viewers’ hearts: because we sympathise, because we see, we give the issue more attention and action, and it can also prompt profound personal reflection. On the other hand, when we display suffering in this setting, what is presented is always a filtered, “artified” suffering. When we pour our feelings into this aesthetic object, attention to the suffering itself is in most cases suspended; most people are merely indulging in a self-congratulatory emotion that “soothes the conscience”. In this process, the emotional amplitude that suffering produces is converted into a price tag under the logic of consumption."},{"t":"p","zh":"萨尔加多的摄影实践之所以值得深入研究，不仅因为他在纪实摄影领域取得的卓越成就，更因为他的作品将上述伦理张力推向了极致：他的影像一方面具有几近崇高的美学品质，另一方面又以长周期、大规模的田野工作为根基。在这种近乎矛盾的实践中，是否蕴含着一种使\"本真性见证\"成为可能的方法？如果存在，这种方法又能否超越摄影这一特定媒介，为当代肖像绘画提供启示？本文将循着这些问题展开。","en":"Salgado’s photographic practice deserves close study not only because of his outstanding achievements in documentary photography, but because his work pushes the ethical tension described above to its extreme: his images have an almost sublime aesthetic quality, yet they are grounded in long-term, large-scale fieldwork. Within this near-contradictory practice, is there a method that makes “authentic testimony” possible? If so, can this method go beyond the particular medium of photography and offer insights for contemporary portrait painting? This paper follows these questions."},{"t":"h","zh":"二、萨尔加多的艺术道路：从经济学博士到纪实摄影大师","en":"2. Salgado’s Artistic Path: From Doctor of Economics to Master of Documentary Photography"},{"t":"p","zh":"塞巴斯蒂安·萨尔加多于1944年出生在巴西米纳斯吉拉斯州的一个农场。与大多数摄影师不同，萨尔加多的学术背景是经济学——他在巴西取得经济学硕士学位后，又在巴黎大学获得经济学博士学位。这段经历对于理解他的摄影实践至关重要：经济学的训练赋予他一种结构性的、全球性的观察方式，使他习惯于将个体命运置于宏观经济和政治结构的框架中审视。","en":"Sebastião Salgado was born in 1944 on a farm in the state of Minas Gerais, Brazil. Unlike most photographers, Salgado’s academic background is in economics: after earning a master’s degree in economics in Brazil, he received a doctorate in economics from the University of Paris. This experience is crucial to understanding his photographic practice: his training in economics gave him a structural, global way of observing, accustoming him to viewing individual fates within the framework of macroeconomic and political structures."},{"t":"p","zh":"1970年代，萨尔加多在伦敦国际咖啡组织担任经济学家期间，开始使用摄影记录工作现场。1973年，他彻底放弃了经济学家的职业，转向全职摄影。这一转变看似突兀，实则有其内在逻辑：经济学为他提供了理解世界结构的概念工具，而摄影则成为他介入这些结构的方式。正如萨尔加多本人所言，他不是在拍摄\"贫困\"，而是在拍摄\"被全球经济体系边缘化的人群\"。这种来自经济学的结构性视角，使他的镜头天然地带有一种从全球政治经济结构出发的观察维度——这恰恰是许多纪实摄影师所缺乏的。","en":"In the 1970s, while working as an economist for the International Coffee Organization in London, Salgado began using photography to document work sites. In 1973 he gave up his career as an economist entirely and turned to photography full time. The change seems abrupt, but it has its own inner logic: economics gave him the conceptual tools to understand the structure of the world, and photography became his way of intervening in those structures. As Salgado himself put it, he was not photographing “poverty” but “people marginalised by the global economic system”. This structural perspective drawn from economics gives his lens a built-in dimension of observation rooted in the structures of the global political economy, precisely what many documentary photographers lack."},{"t":"p","zh":"萨尔加多的主要作品系列构成了一条清晰的叙事线索。《劳动者》（Workers, 1986—1992）记录了全球范围内体力劳动者的生存状态，从巴西塞拉佩拉达金矿五万名矿工如蚂蚁般攀爬木梯的史诗场景，到印度煤矿中满脸煤灰的矿工肖像，萨尔加多在此系列中确立了\"纪念碑式纪实\"的个人风格。《移民》（Migrations, 1993—1999）则转向战争、饥荒与自然灾害所导致的大规模人口流动，拍摄了卢旺达种族灭绝后的难民营、南苏丹饥荒中的儿童，将镜头对准了人类苦难的极限。而《创世纪》（Genesis, 2004—2011）是一次彻底的转向——萨尔加多耗时八年，深入全球尚未被现代文明触及的原始地貌与族群，拍摄地球\"未被污染\"的面貌。","en":"Salgado’s major series form a clear narrative line. Workers (1986–1992) documents the living conditions of manual labourers around the world, from the epic scene of fifty thousand miners climbing wooden ladders like ants at the Serra Pelada gold mine in Brazil to portraits of coal-blackened miners in India; with this series Salgado established his personal style of “monumental documentary”. Migrations (1993–1999) turns to the mass movements of people caused by war, famine and natural disaster, photographing refugee camps after the Rwandan genocide and children in the famine in South Sudan, training the lens on the limits of human suffering. Genesis (2004–2011) marks a complete turn: Salgado spent eight years travelling deep into landscapes and peoples around the globe not yet touched by modern civilisation, photographing the “unpolluted” face of the earth."},{"t":"p","zh":"这一从\"劳动者\"到\"移民\"再到\"创世纪\"的轨迹，本身就是一种意味深长的叙事：从人类劳动的尊严，到人类苦难的极限，再到地球原初状态的回望。它暗示着一条从社会批判到存在性叩问的精神路径。值得特别指出的是，萨尔加多的巴西出身—法国工作的跨文化背景，以及他作为\"全球南方\"知识分子在欧洲文化场域中的位置，构成了理解其作品政治维度不可忽视的上下文。这种身份的双重性使他既能在西方艺术体制内获得话语权，又保持着对殖民历史和全球不平等的切身敏感。","en":"This trajectory, from Workers to Migrations to Genesis, is itself a deeply meaningful narrative: from the dignity of human labour, to the limits of human suffering, to a look back at the earth’s original state. It suggests a spiritual path from social critique to existential questioning. It should be particularly noted that Salgado’s cross-cultural background, Brazilian-born and working in France, and his position as an intellectual of the “Global South” within the European cultural field, form a context that cannot be ignored in understanding the political dimension of his work. This dual identity allows him both to gain a voice within the Western art system and to retain a personal sensitivity to colonial history and global inequality."},{"t":"h","zh":"三、苦难美学的伦理张力：萨尔加多摄影的诗学与政治","en":"3. The Ethical Tension of the Aesthetics of Suffering: The Poetics and Politics of Salgado’s Photography"},{"t":"h","zh":"（一）美学形式与苦难内容的矛盾","en":"(1) The Contradiction between Aesthetic Form and the Content of Suffering"},{"t":"p","zh":"萨尔加多的摄影作品之所以引发持续争议，核心在于其美学品质与拍摄对象之间的巨大反差。他的影像往往具有极强的形式美感：精心控制的影调、戏剧性的光影、纪念碑式的构图——这些形式特征将苦难转化为一种具有崇高感的审美对象。批评者指出，这种美学化处理在某种意义上\"美化\"了苦难，使得观者在震撼之余获得一种审美愉悦，而这种愉悦与拍摄对象的真实处境之间存在伦理上的错位。","en":"The core reason Salgado’s photographs provoke lasting controversy lies in the enormous contrast between their aesthetic quality and their subjects. His images often have a very strong formal beauty: carefully controlled tonality, dramatic light and shadow, monumental composition. These formal features turn suffering into an aesthetic object with a sense of the sublime. Critics point out that this aesthetic treatment in some sense “beautifies” suffering, so that viewers, besides being shaken, gain a kind of aesthetic pleasure, and that this pleasure stands in an ethical misalignment with the real situation of the people photographed."},{"t":"p","zh":"苏珊·桑塔格（Susan Sontag）在《关于他人的痛苦》（Regarding the Pain of Others, 2003）中对此类问题有过深刻讨论：苦难的影像在反复传播中会逐渐丧失其刺痛力，观者变得麻木，苦难沦为一种视觉消费品。萨尔加多的作品面临着同样的危险——当巴西金矿的矿工群像被装裱在画廊的白墙上，当饥荒中儿童的面孔成为摄影集铜版纸上的印刷品，苦难是否已被转化为一种\"精致的痛苦\"（exquisite suffering）？这一质疑触及了纪实摄影的根本伦理困境：当苦难成为可供凝视的审美对象时，它是否已经丧失了其作为\"苦难\"的本真性？","en":"Susan Sontag discussed such problems profoundly in Regarding the Pain of Others (2003): images of suffering gradually lose their sting through repeated circulation, viewers grow numb, and suffering is reduced to a visual commodity. Salgado’s work faces the same danger. When the group portraits of miners at the Brazilian gold mine are framed on the white walls of a gallery, when the faces of children in famine become prints on the coated paper of a photobook, has suffering already been turned into “exquisite suffering”? This doubt touches the fundamental ethical dilemma of documentary photography: when suffering becomes an aesthetic object available to the gaze, has it already lost its authenticity as “suffering”?"},{"t":"h","zh":"（二）\"美与和谐是解药\"——观看的政治","en":"(2) “Beauty and Harmony Are the Antidote”: The Politics of Looking"},{"t":"p","zh":"在流媒体上，我曾看到一场关于韩国画家姜明姬（Myonghi Kang）在南法画展开幕午餐会的记录。举办者、法国前总理德维尔潘（Dominique de Villepin）在祝酒词中表达了这样的观点：\"在这样一个美丽的地方，人们是不会去想到苦难、战争的，美与和谐就是我们的解药。\"先不论这段发言背后可能存在的偷换概念与\"何不食肉糜\"的姿态，单就这个观点本身而言，它恰恰提出了一个与萨尔加多实践构成尖锐对位的问题：视觉艺术究竟应该呈现什么？","en":"On a streaming platform I once saw a recording of the opening luncheon of an exhibition by the Korean painter Myonghi Kang in the south of France. The host, former French Prime Minister Dominique de Villepin, expressed this view in his toast: “In such a beautiful place, people will not think of suffering or war; beauty and harmony are our antidote.” Leaving aside the possible sleight of hand behind this speech and its “let them eat cake” posture, the view itself raises precisely a question that stands in sharp counterpoint to Salgado’s practice: what, in the end, should visual art present?"},{"t":"p","zh":"德维尔潘的发言揭示了一个关键的权力结构问题。站在欧洲南法的阳光庭院中说\"美是解药\"的人，与那些生活在苦难中的人，处于截然不同的位置。他的发言恰恰暴露了\"美\"可以被用作遮蔽现实的意识形态工具——美与和谐不是解药，而是特权者回避他者苦难的屏障。这一案例使我意识到，艺术家在创办展览时面临的不仅是美学选择，更是政治选择：在哪里办展、说什么语言、发言讲什么话、讲给谁听——这些都是需要精心构建的。欧洲白人男性外交政治家与亚洲黄人女艺术家之间的权力关系，使得\"姜明姬从济州岛出生，付出了很多努力和运气才能到南法举办展览\"这样看似客观的陈述，也暗含了先入为主的高姿态和对后者文化及国力的隐晦蔑视。","en":"De Villepin’s remarks reveal a key problem of power structure. The person who stands in a sunlit courtyard in the south of France and says “beauty is the antidote” occupies an utterly different position from those who live in suffering. His remarks expose precisely how “beauty” can be used as an ideological tool to screen out reality: beauty and harmony are not an antidote but a barrier behind which the privileged avoid the suffering of others. This case made me realise that when artists mount an exhibition, they face not only aesthetic choices but political ones: where to exhibit, in what language, what to say in a speech and to whom; all of this needs to be carefully constructed. The power relation between a white European male diplomat-politician and an Asian woman artist meant that even a seemingly objective statement such as “Myonghi Kang, born on Jeju Island, needed a great deal of effort and luck to hold an exhibition in the south of France” carried an implicit air of preconceived superiority and a veiled contempt for her culture and her country’s standing."},{"t":"p","zh":"正是在这一背景下，萨尔加多的实践呈现出截然不同的立场。他来自巴西——一个经历了殖民历史、经济依附与政治动荡的\"全球南方\"国家。他的经济学训练使他能够从结构性视角理解自己拍摄的对象：那些金矿工人、难民、饥荒中的农民并非\"不幸的个体\"，而是全球经济体系的结构性产物。当萨尔加多带着这种自觉进行拍摄时，他的镜头姿态就不是居高临下的\"关怀\"，而是从内部出发的\"见证\"。这种立场的自觉选择——为谁发言、立场是什么——是\"本真性\"得以可能的第一重条件。","en":"It is against this background that Salgado’s practice presents an entirely different stance. He comes from Brazil, a “Global South” country that has gone through colonial history, economic dependency and political turmoil. His training in economics enables him to understand his subjects from a structural perspective: the gold miners, refugees and famine-stricken farmers are not “unfortunate individuals” but structural products of the global economic system. When Salgado photographs with this awareness, the stance of his lens is not condescending “concern” but “witness” from the inside. This conscious choice of position, for whom one speaks and where one stands, is the first condition that makes “authenticity” possible."},{"t":"h","zh":"（三）苦难呈现的\"双刃\"结构与转化的可能性","en":"(3) The “Double-Edged” Structure of Presenting Suffering and the Possibility of Transformation"},{"t":"p","zh":"萨尔加多的实践揭示了一个基本的结构性事实：苦难的视觉呈现始终处于\"见证\"与\"消费\"的双重可能性之间。美的形式使苦难得以进入公共话语、引发情感共振与行动可能；但与此同时，美的形式也可能使苦难被消费、被\"净化\"为一种安全的情感体验。这一矛盾并非萨尔加多个人的困境，而是所有涉及苦难呈现的艺术实践都必须面对的结构性问题。","en":"Salgado’s practice reveals a basic structural fact: the visual presentation of suffering always lies between the dual possibilities of “witness” and “consumption”. Beautiful form allows suffering to enter public discourse and to provoke emotional resonance and the possibility of action; but at the same time beautiful form may also allow suffering to be consumed, “purified” into a safe emotional experience. This contradiction is not Salgado’s personal predicament but a structural problem that every artistic practice involving the presentation of suffering must face."},{"t":"p","zh":"那么，是否存在一种方式，使苦难的视觉呈现既保有其情感力量，又不被消费逻辑所吞噬？我认为，回答这一问题的关键在于重新理解\"本真性\"这一概念——不是将其等同于\"真实\"或\"未经加工\"，而是在哲学层面考察本真性发生的结构性条件。","en":"Is there, then, a way for the visual presentation of suffering to retain its emotional force without being swallowed by the logic of consumption? I believe the key to answering this question lies in re-understanding the concept of “authenticity”: not equating it with “the real” or “the unprocessed”, but examining, at a philosophical level, the structural conditions under which authenticity occurs."},{"t":"h","zh":"四、本真性的哲学维度：海德格尔、本雅明与纪实摄影","en":"4. The Philosophical Dimensions of Authenticity: Heidegger, Benjamin and Documentary Photography"},{"t":"h","zh":"（一）海德格尔的\"本真性存在\"与艺术创作","en":"(1) Heidegger’s “Authentic Existence” and Artistic Creation"},{"t":"p","zh":"在马丁·海德格尔（Martin Heidegger）的《存在与时间》（Sein und Zeit, 1927）中，\"本真性\"（Eigentlichkeit）并非指某种静态的品质或属性，而是此在（Dasein）与世界相遇的一种方式。海德格尔写道：\"随着丧失于常人之中的境况，此在切近的实际能在——诸种任务、规则、措施、操劳在世和操持在世的紧迫性与广度——总已被决定好了。常人总已经从此在那里取走了对那种种存在可能性的掌握……由于它的耽搁，此在曾丧失于非本真状态中。从常人中收回（Zurückholen）选择，这种收回使常人转变为本真的自身存在。\"","en":"In Martin Heidegger’s Being and Time (Sein und Zeit, 1927), “authenticity” (Eigentlichkeit) does not refer to some static quality or attribute, but to a way in which Dasein encounters the world. Heidegger writes: “With Dasein’s lostness in the ‘they’, that factical potentiality-for-Being which is closest to it (the tasks, rules and standards, the urgency and extent, of concernful and solicitous Being-in-the-world) has already been decided upon. The ‘they’ has always kept Dasein from taking hold of these possibilities of Being... Because of this neglect, Dasein has been lost in inauthenticity. Taking the choice back (Zurückholen) from the ‘they’: this taking back transforms the ‘they’ into authentic Being-one’s-Self.”"},{"t":"p","zh":"本真性在海德格尔意义上不是一种可被\"拥有\"的东西，而是一种\"收回\"——从常人的规定中收回自身存在的可能性。这一理解对于思考纪实摄影中的本真性问题具有深远的启示：重要的不是被拍摄对象是否\"真实\"，而是拍摄者和观者是否在与影像的相遇中从惯常的观看方式中\"收回\"自身，进入一种本真的领会。","en":"Authenticity in Heidegger’s sense is not something that can be “possessed” but a “taking back”: taking back the possibilities of one’s own Being from what the “they” prescribes. This understanding has far-reaching implications for thinking about authenticity in documentary photography: what matters is not whether the photographed subject is “real”, but whether the photographer and viewer, in their encounter with the image, “take themselves back” from habitual ways of looking and enter an authentic understanding."},{"t":"p","zh":"在艺术创作的语境中，这一点具有特殊的意义。艺术作品中的真理性存在与创作过程中创作者的\"去主体化\"密切相关——也就是说，这一过程是借由艺术家本人，但却不是有意所流露出来的本真性存在。这是一种并不直接显现出重量的轻盈。对此，米兰·昆德拉（Milan Kundera）在《生命不可承受之轻》中提供了一个有力的文学参照：当特蕾莎返回捷克时，托马斯感受到了一种\"存在性的眩晕\"。个体的存在因个体存在之外的存在而展开意义。当特蕾莎离开时，对于托马斯来说，这不仅是他的伴侣离开了——他的责任、意义的锚点也离开了。存在的重量从他身上抽离，他如行尸走肉般四处消磨时间，躲避生命处于自由之轻的虚无。最终他放弃了在匈牙利的一切，回到了正处在战争中的祖国、特蕾莎的身边。而对于萨比娜，她一生都在逃离、追寻无媚俗的自由。可我们不是超人，媚俗避无可避。人活着需要一个有确定性的锚点、一个生命之重。","en":"In the context of artistic creation this has a special significance. The truth that exists in a work of art is closely tied to the creator’s “de-subjectivation” in the creative process; that is, it is an authentic existence that comes forth through the artist, yet is not deliberately expressed. It is a lightness that does not directly show its weight. Milan Kundera’s The Unbearable Lightness of Being offers a powerful literary reference here: when Tereza returns to Czechoslovakia, Tomas feels a kind of “existential vertigo”. An individual’s existence unfolds its meaning through an existence beyond itself. When Tereza leaves, for Tomas it is not only his partner who leaves; his responsibility, his anchor of meaning, leaves too. The weight of existence is drawn out of him, and he wanders about like a walking corpse killing time, fleeing the nothingness of a life in the lightness of freedom. In the end he gives up everything in Hungary and returns to his homeland, then in the midst of war, to Tereza’s side. As for Sabina, all her life she flees, pursuing a freedom without kitsch. But we are not supermen; kitsch cannot be escaped. To live, a person needs an anchor of certainty, a weight of life."},{"t":"p","zh":"艺术也是如此。它可以允许有更多\"未定、悬置\"的存在，它给予事情发生方向敞开的可能性；但当它真正发生的时候，也需要有意义的锚点。萨尔加多的摄影之所以具有那种打动人心的力量，正是因为他的每一张照片都承载着这样一个\"锚点\"——不是在形式上的刻意追求，而是在与被摄者真实的、长时间的相遇中自然生成的存在重量。","en":"Art is the same. It can allow more “undetermined, suspended” existence, opening up possibilities for the direction in which things happen; but when it truly happens, it also needs an anchor of meaning. The reason Salgado’s photographs have such power to move people is precisely that every one of them carries such an “anchor”: not something deliberately pursued in form, but a weight of existence that grows naturally out of real, long encounters with the people photographed."},{"t":"h","zh":"（二）本雅明的\"灵韵\"与机械复制时代的苦难影像","en":"(2) Benjamin’s “Aura” and Images of Suffering in the Age of Mechanical Reproduction"},{"t":"p","zh":"瓦尔特·本雅明（Walter Benjamin）在《机械复制时代的艺术作品》（1936）中提出，本真性是物性与事性的统一，两者缺一不可。机械复制导致了事性的丧失，也就是灵韵（Aura）的丧失。人的心灵无法栖息在这种只有物性而没有事性的商品上。这或许也是现代社会倦怠感的来源之一——人们如同普罗米修斯般被秃鹰日日啄食，倦怠而心灵无处安放。","en":"In The Work of Art in the Age of Mechanical Reproduction (1936), Walter Benjamin proposed that authenticity is the unity of a thing’s materiality and its eventhood, and that neither can be missing. Mechanical reproduction leads to the loss of eventhood, that is, the loss of aura. The human soul cannot dwell in commodities that have only materiality and no eventhood. This may also be one source of the weariness of modern society: like Prometheus, people are pecked at day after day by the vulture, exhausted, with nowhere for the soul to rest."},{"t":"p","zh":"萨尔加多的摄影实践面临着本雅明所诊断困境的极端版本：他的作品通过摄影集、展览和纪录片在全球范围内被大规模复制和传播，但它们所呈现的恰恰是那些最不可被复制的东西——苦难的身体经验、生死的切近、人与土地之间的原初关联。这种矛盾并非萨尔加多实践的失败信号，而是揭示了当代视觉文化中的一个根本性张力：在最彻底的复制媒介中，是否仍可能保存某种\"灵韵\"式的存在品质？","en":"Salgado’s photographic practice faces an extreme version of the predicament Benjamin diagnosed: his work is reproduced and circulated on a massive global scale through photobooks, exhibitions and documentaries, yet what it presents is precisely what is least reproducible: the bodily experience of suffering, the nearness of life and death, the primal bond between people and the land. This contradiction is not a sign of failure in Salgado’s practice; rather, it reveals a fundamental tension in contemporary visual culture: within the most thoroughly reproductive medium, is it still possible to preserve an existential quality akin to “aura”?"},{"t":"p","zh":"值得注意的是，本雅明自己对此问题并非完全悲观。他认为灵韵的消散同时也意味着艺术从仪式性的膜拜价值中解放出来，获得了政治实践的可能性。从这个角度看，萨尔加多摄影的广泛传播恰恰是其政治效力得以实现的条件——它使那些被遮蔽的苦难进入了公共可见性的领域。问题的关键不在于阻止复制，而在于如何在复制的洪流中保持图像的政治指向性。","en":"It is worth noting that Benjamin himself was not entirely pessimistic on this question. He held that the dissipation of the aura also meant the liberation of art from the cult value of ritual, gaining the possibility of political practice. From this angle, the wide circulation of Salgado’s photographs is precisely the condition for their political efficacy: it brings hidden suffering into the realm of public visibility. The crux lies not in preventing reproduction, but in how to keep the image’s political orientation amid the flood of reproduction."},{"t":"h","zh":"（三）\"本真性见证\"的三个结构性条件","en":"(3) Three Structural Conditions of “Authentic Testimony”"},{"t":"p","zh":"综合海德格尔和本雅明的理论资源，并结合萨尔加多的具体实践，我提出理解其摄影中本真性的一个核心框架——\"本真性见证\"（authentic testimony），它包含三个相互关联的结构性条件：","en":"Drawing together the theoretical resources of Heidegger and Benjamin, and in light of Salgado’s concrete practice, I propose a core framework for understanding the authenticity of his photography, “authentic testimony”, which comprises three interrelated structural conditions:"},{"t":"p","zh":"第一，时间性的在场。萨尔加多的拍摄不是快门瞬间的攫取，而是长周期的陪伴与等待。他在塞拉佩拉达金矿停留数周，与矿工一同生活；他在非洲难民营中不是以记者身份短暂造访，而是以同行者的身份长期驻留。这种时间性的投入，使他的影像带有一种无法被单张快照所捕捉的时间厚度——它承载的不仅是\"那一刻\"的视觉事实，更是\"那一段生命\"的存在质地。在当代影像生产的加速逻辑中，这种以\"慢\"对抗\"快\"的时间伦理本身就是一种政治姿态。","en":"First, temporal presence. Salgado’s photography is not a grab in the instant of the shutter, but long-term companionship and waiting. He stayed for weeks at the Serra Pelada gold mine, living alongside the miners; in African refugee camps he did not make brief visits as a journalist but stayed for long periods as a fellow traveller. This investment of time gives his images a temporal thickness that no single snapshot can capture: they carry not only the visual fact of “that moment” but the existential texture of “that stretch of life”. Within the accelerating logic of contemporary image production, this ethic of time that pits “slow” against “fast” is in itself a political stance."},{"t":"p","zh":"第二，结构性的自觉。萨尔加多的经济学训练使他能够从结构性视角理解拍摄对象。他拍摄的不是孤立的\"受难者\"，而是在特定政治经济结构中被迫承受苦难的群体。这种自觉使他的影像超越了个体苦难的奇观化展示，而指向了苦难得以产生的结构条件——这是图像政治责任的具体承担方式。正如我在对艺术与\"牛虻\"传统的思考中所意识到的：艺术家的位置有些特殊，不能因市场运用的\"个人崇拜\"叙事就沉浸其中、顺着单一逻辑维护\"个人品牌\"。艺术家首先要意识到自己在社会结构中的位置——为谁发言、立场是什么。","en":"Second, structural awareness. Salgado’s training in economics enables him to understand his subjects from a structural perspective. What he photographs are not isolated “victims” but groups forced to bear suffering within specific political and economic structures. This awareness lets his images go beyond the spectacularised display of individual suffering and point to the structural conditions that produce suffering; this is the concrete way in which the image takes on political responsibility. As I came to realise in thinking about art and the tradition of “the gadfly”: the artist’s position is somewhat special; one must not become absorbed in the “personality cult” narrative used by the market, maintaining a “personal brand” along a single logic. The artist must first be aware of his or her position in the social structure: for whom one speaks, and where one stands."},{"t":"p","zh":"第三，姿态的非剥削性。萨尔加多不使用长焦偷拍，不追求猎奇效果。他的肖像往往以正面、平视、纪念碑式的构图呈现被摄者。这种拍摄姿态不是在\"捕捉\"对象的苦难，而是在\"承接\"对象的存在。被摄者不是被动的受害者，而是以尊严的主体形象出现在画面中。这恰恰是桑塔格所批评的那种\"剥削性观看\"的反面——萨尔加多的镜头不是侵入性的，而是承接性的。","en":"Third, a non-exploitative stance. Salgado does not take covert shots with a telephoto lens and does not chase sensational effects. His portraits usually present their subjects frontally, at eye level, in monumental compositions. This way of photographing does not “capture” the subject’s suffering but “receives” the subject’s existence. The people photographed appear in the picture not as passive victims but as subjects with dignity. This is precisely the opposite of the “exploitative looking” Sontag criticised: Salgado’s lens is not intrusive but receptive."},{"t":"p","zh":"这三个条件共同构成了萨尔加多摄影中\"本真性见证\"的可能性：通过时间性承诺、结构性自觉和非剥削的观看姿态，苦难的呈现得以同时保有情感力量和伦理严肃性，而不至于滑入消费逻辑的陷阱。如果借用本雅明的术语，我们可以说：萨尔加多的实践在机械复制时代的内部，重新创造了一种\"灵韵\"得以闪现的条件——不是通过怀旧式的返回仪式传统，而是通过一种高度自觉的、政治性的观看伦理。","en":"Together these three conditions constitute the possibility of “authentic testimony” in Salgado’s photography: through temporal commitment, structural awareness and a non-exploitative stance of looking, the presentation of suffering can retain both emotional force and ethical seriousness without sliding into the trap of the logic of consumption. To borrow Benjamin’s terms, we might say that Salgado’s practice, from within the age of mechanical reproduction, recreates the conditions under which “aura” can flash forth, not through a nostalgic return to ritual tradition, but through a highly self-aware, political ethics of looking."},{"t":"h","zh":"五、从镜头到画布：萨尔加多方法论对当代肖像绘画的启示","en":"5. From Lens to Canvas: What Salgado’s Methodology Offers Contemporary Portrait Painting"},{"t":"h","zh":"（一）媒介转换中的方法论迁移","en":"(1) Methodological Transfer across Media"},{"t":"p","zh":"萨尔加多的实践虽然是摄影，但其方法论内核——时间性的在场、结构性的自觉、非剥削的观看姿态——完全可以被迁移到肖像绘画的创作实践中。绘画与摄影在媒介属性上有着根本差异：摄影以其索引性（indexicality）与被摄对象保持着物理性的光化学关联，而绘画则是通过手工劳作逐步建构图像。这一差异使得绘画在呈现\"本真性\"时面临更复杂的挑战：绘画无法依赖媒介的索引性来保证\"真实\"，它必须通过其他路径抵达本真。","en":"Although Salgado’s practice is photography, the core of his methodology, temporal presence, structural awareness and a non-exploitative stance of looking, can be transferred entirely to the practice of portrait painting. Painting and photography differ fundamentally as media: photography, through its indexicality, maintains a physical, photochemical connection with its subject, whereas painting builds up the image gradually through manual labour. This difference means that painting faces more complex challenges in presenting “authenticity”: it cannot rely on the indexicality of the medium to guarantee “truth”, and must reach authenticity by other paths."},{"t":"p","zh":"然而，绘画也有其独特的优势：它的时间性不是快门的瞬间冻结，而是创作过程的缓慢绵延。在绘画中，艺术家与被描绘者的关系不是瞬间的\"捕捉\"，而是通过长时间的手工劳动进行的\"承接\"。这一过程本身就具有一种海德格尔意义上的\"操劳\"（Besorgen）结构——艺术家在绘画的行动中与对象建立了一种时间性的、身体性的关系。正如我在创作阐释中所强调的：绘画不是艺术家用绘画工具在承载物上描绘、堆叠的一个\"目的—结果\"的线性累加，而是每一个动作和各个零碎的落在平面上的结果都打破了时间、相互抓扣与影响的生成事件。","en":"Yet painting also has its own advantages: its temporality is not the instantaneous freeze of the shutter, but the slow duration of the creative process. In painting, the relationship between artist and sitter is not an instantaneous “capture” but a “receiving” carried out through long hours of manual labour. This process itself has the structure of “concern” (Besorgen) in Heidegger’s sense: in the act of painting, the artist establishes a temporal, bodily relationship with the subject. As I have stressed in my statements on my work: painting is not a linear “purpose–result” accumulation in which the artist uses painting tools to depict and pile up on a support; rather, every movement and each fragmentary result falling on the plane is a generative event that breaks through time, in which they catch hold of and affect one another."},{"t":"h","zh":"（二）\"人物本真系列\"的创作实践","en":"(2) The Creative Practice of the “Authenticity Series of Figures”"},{"t":"p","zh":"我的\"人物本真系列\"肖像绘画，正是以这种方式回应萨尔加多方法论所带来的启示。该系列聚焦于捕捉人物在\"功能性交流之外\"的本真性流露——那些在社会角色的间隙中闪现的脆弱、恻隐、犹疑与温柔。在摄影和影像实践中，我延续的是同一套创作内核：摄影呈现上主要有对权力结构情景的\"叙事性捕捉\"和对人物功能性交流之外的本真性流露的捕捉这两个主题；而在影像中采取的是一种采访式的、引发被采访人思考的方式，其主题是\"你什么时候感到了内疚\"。","en":"My “Authenticity Series of Figures”, a series of portrait paintings, responds in exactly this way to the insights offered by Salgado’s methodology. The series focuses on capturing people’s authentic expression “beyond functional communication”: the fragility, compassion, hesitation and tenderness that flash out in the gaps between social roles. In my photography and video work I continue the same creative core: in photography there are two main themes, the “narrative capture” of situations of power structure and the capture of people’s authentic expression beyond functional communication; in video I take an interview-like approach that prompts the interviewee to reflect, on the theme “When did you feel guilty?”"},{"t":"p","zh":"在创作实践中，我从以下几个方面借鉴并转化了萨尔加多的方法论：","en":"In my practice, I have drawn on and transformed Salgado’s methodology in the following respects:"},{"t":"p","zh":"其一，以时间换深度。与萨尔加多在拍摄地的长期驻留相似，我在绘制肖像前与对象进行充分的相处与对话。肖像不是对一张照片的临摹，而是对一段相处的沉淀。画布上的每一笔都不只是形状的描摹，而是时间在身体动作中留下的痕迹。这种以\"慢\"为方法的创作伦理，直接回应了萨尔加多的工作方式。","en":"First, trading time for depth. Much as Salgado stays for long periods where he photographs, before painting a portrait I spend ample time with the sitter in conversation. A portrait is not a copy of a photograph but the sediment of a period spent together. Every stroke on the canvas is not merely the tracing of a shape but a trace left by time in the movement of the body. This creative ethic that takes “slowness” as its method responds directly to Salgado’s way of working."},{"t":"p","zh":"其二，自觉于权力结构。摄影中的拍摄姿态决定了观看的政治——是俯视、平视还是仰视，是偷拍还是正面对峙。在绘画中，这一问题转化为：我在画布上以何种方式\"安置\"被描绘者？我的\"人物本真系列\"追求一种平视的、不带侵略性的观看——让被描绘者以其自身的节奏和姿态存在于画布空间中，而非被强加某种叙事或意义。这与我受马克思主义影响的底层关切一脉相承：苦难使我想要改变，但现实政治的层层相扣使低回报的事情难以被实现；而通过艺术，可以使一些事情借着\"艺术的壳\"得以进行。","en":"Second, awareness of power structures. In photography, the stance from which one shoots determines the politics of looking: looking down, at eye level or up; covert shooting or frontal confrontation. In painting, the question becomes: in what way do I “place” the sitter on the canvas? My “Authenticity Series of Figures” seeks a level, non-aggressive way of looking, letting sitters exist in the space of the canvas with their own rhythm and posture rather than having a narrative or meaning imposed on them. This is of a piece with my concern for those at the bottom of society, shaped by Marxism: suffering makes me want to change things, but the interlocking layers of real politics make low-return work hard to achieve; through art, some things can be carried out under “the shell of art”."},{"t":"p","zh":"其三，让绘画本身成为事件。借鉴海德格尔对本真性的理解，本真系列不以\"准确地再现\"为目标，而是让绘画过程中的笔触、材料的物质性、身体的气息节律共同参与意义的生成。正如罗伯特·莱曼（Robert Ryman）所言：\"我不认为我的绘画是抽象绘画，因为我不对一个具体的东西进行抽象。\"对于具体的画面本身来说，每个笔触都是实实在在存在着的。它在画布上单独成立或与其他笔触相融合——这并不抽象。就算仅仅只有白色，每一个白色的形状、厚薄和画面上被光线所捕捉到的细微色差也都是十分具象的。颜料本身就已经是颜料，是一个此在的物。画面中未被完全\"完成\"的部分，恰如萨尔加多影像中那些拒绝被简化为符号的面孔——它们保留了一种不可被完全消费的剩余，这正是本真性得以驻留的裂隙。","en":"Third, letting painting itself become an event. Drawing on Heidegger’s understanding of authenticity, the Authenticity Series does not aim at “accurate representation”, but lets the brushstrokes of the painting process, the materiality of the materials and the rhythm of the body’s breath all take part in the generation of meaning. As Robert Ryman said: “I don’t think of my paintings as abstract, because I’m not abstracting from anything concrete.” For the picture itself, every brushstroke really and concretely exists. It stands on its own on the canvas or merges with other strokes, and this is not abstract. Even if there is only white, each white shape, its thickness, and the subtle differences of colour caught by light on the surface are all thoroughly concrete. The paint is already paint, a thing that is here (da-seiend). The parts of the picture that are not fully “finished” are like the faces in Salgado’s images that refuse to be reduced to symbols: they keep a remainder that cannot be completely consumed, and this is exactly the fissure in which authenticity can dwell."},{"t":"h","zh":"（三）从\"见证\"到\"承接\"","en":"(3) From “Witness” to “Receiving”"},{"t":"p","zh":"萨尔加多在《创世纪》中完成了一次重要的转向：从\"苦难的见证\"到\"生命本源的呈现\"。这一转向对于我的本真系列创作同样具有启示意义。如果说早期的肖像实践更多关注个体在社会结构中的伤痕与脆弱——这一点与萨尔加多《劳动者》和《移民》系列的精神相通——那么后续的创作则逐渐转向对人物本真性在场的\"承接\"：不是在画布上\"展示\"对象，而是让对象的存在在绘画的行动中自行显现。","en":"In Genesis, Salgado made an important turn: from “witnessing suffering” to “presenting the origins of life”. This turn is equally instructive for my Authenticity Series. If my earlier portrait practice was concerned more with the scars and fragility of individuals within social structures, in a spirit close to Salgado’s Workers and Migrations series, my later work has gradually turned towards “receiving” the authentic presence of the people I paint: not “displaying” the subject on canvas, but letting the subject’s existence reveal itself in the act of painting."},{"t":"p","zh":"这种转化对应着一种更深刻的艺术观念转变。艺术的批判性如何建设性地介入社会生活？这是我时常纠结的问题，也是对于\"艺术无用\"的无奈与不甘。经过长期思考，我逐渐意识到：艺术不能直接解决社会问题，它只能在限定的范围内作探索。但这并不意味着放弃批判——而是将批判的路径从\"大声疾呼\"转向\"在场的承接\"。正如萨尔加多在《创世纪》中所做的那样，他不去拍摄被破坏的地球，而是拍摄仍然完好的一切，以此为\"本应如此\"的生命状态提供一个可见的参照。在本真系列肖像中，我也尝试类似的做法：不去描绘被异化的人的面孔，而是承接那些尚未被异化吞噬的瞬间——那些脆弱、恻隐、温柔的时刻。这些时刻不是对现实的逃避，而是一种政治性的在场：它们以\"存在\"的方式证明，另一种感知世界的方式是可能的。","en":"This transformation corresponds to a deeper shift in my idea of art. How can the critical force of art intervene constructively in social life? This is a question I often wrestle with, and it is also my helplessness and refusal to accept that “art is useless”. After long reflection, I gradually came to realise that art cannot solve social problems directly; it can only explore within limited bounds. But this does not mean giving up critique; rather, it means shifting the path of critique from “crying out loud” to “receiving in presence”. Just as Salgado did in Genesis, photographing not the ravaged earth but everything that remains intact, so as to offer a visible reference for the state of life as “it ought to be”, in the Authenticity Series portraits I try something similar: not painting the faces of alienated people, but receiving those moments not yet swallowed by alienation, moments of fragility, compassion and tenderness. These moments are not an escape from reality but a political presence: by way of “existence” they prove that another way of perceiving the world is possible."},{"t":"h","zh":"六、结语","en":"6. Conclusion"},{"t":"p","zh":"塞巴斯蒂安·萨尔加多的纪实摄影实践，为我们提供了一个思考\"苦难呈现的伦理\"与\"艺术本真性\"之间关系的经典案例。本文通过对萨尔加多艺术道路、作品伦理张力及哲学理论资源的系统性分析，论证了：在视觉艺术中呈现苦难并非必然导向苦难的消费化——关键在于\"如何呈现\"。萨尔加多的实践揭示了一种\"本真性见证\"的可能路径，其结构性条件包括时间性的在场承诺、对自身观看位置的结构性自觉、以及非剥削性的观看姿态。","en":"Sebastião Salgado’s documentary photography offers us a classic case for thinking about the relationship between “the ethics of presenting suffering” and “artistic authenticity”. Through a systematic analysis of Salgado’s artistic path, the ethical tensions of his work and the relevant philosophical resources, this paper has argued that presenting suffering in visual art does not necessarily lead to the consumption of suffering; the key lies in “how it is presented”. Salgado’s practice reveals a possible path of “authentic testimony”, whose structural conditions include a commitment to temporal presence, structural awareness of one’s own position as viewer, and a non-exploitative stance of looking."},{"t":"p","zh":"这些条件同样适用于肖像绘画的创作实践。在我的\"人物本真系列\"创作中，萨尔加多的方法论被转化为一种以\"承接\"而非\"捕捉\"为核心的绘画路径：通过长时间的相处换取深度，通过平视的姿态尊重对象的主体性，通过让绘画过程本身成为意义生成的事件来保存本真性。这种路径不仅是对萨尔加多艺术遗产的个人回应，也是在当代视觉文化的高度消费化语境中，对绘画如何可能承载\"本真性在场\"的一次探索。","en":"These conditions apply equally to the practice of portrait painting. In my “Authenticity Series of Figures”, Salgado’s methodology has been transformed into a path of painting centred on “receiving” rather than “capturing”: gaining depth through long periods spent together, respecting the subjectivity of the sitter through a level gaze, and preserving authenticity by letting the painting process itself become an event in which meaning is generated. This path is not only a personal response to Salgado’s artistic legacy, but also an exploration, within the highly consumerised context of contemporary visual culture, of how painting might carry an “authentic presence”."},{"t":"p","zh":"回到文德斯的那句话——萨尔加多的作品中传达着\"艺术家对人类的爱\"。这句话的力量不在于其诗意，而在于它指向了一种具体的实践方式：爱不是空洞的情感，而是投入时间、承担政治责任、以平等的目光承接他者存在的行动。在萨尔加多的影像中，每一张脸孔都是一个不容被消费的存在——它们不是在\"被看\"，而是在\"在\"（Da-sein）。这正是海德格尔意义上的本真性：不是一种被拥有的品质，而是一种被承接的存在方式。","en":"To return to Wenders’s words: Salgado’s work conveys “the artist’s love for humanity”. The power of this sentence lies not in its poetry but in the fact that it points to a concrete way of practice: love is not empty emotion but action, investing time, taking on political responsibility, and receiving the existence of others with an equal gaze. In Salgado’s images, every face is an existence that must not be consumed: they are not “being looked at”; they are “being there” (Da-sein). This is precisely authenticity in Heidegger’s sense: not a quality that is possessed, but a way of being that is received."},{"t":"p","zh":"作为艺术家，我们无须发表海阔天空的大言论，但在具体的人与人交往的权力微型博弈中，在被记录的每一次相遇中，都要谨慎、放下个人，拾起背后的身份与责任。\"相比艺术品本身，它所承接的人与人的社会关系更为重要。\"这是我从萨尔加多那里学到的最重要的一课，也是我的\"人物本真系列\"肖像绘画所试图践行的伦理。","en":"As artists, we need not make grand, sweeping pronouncements; but in the micro-games of power in concrete human interactions, in every encounter that is recorded, we must be careful, set ourselves aside, and take up the identity and responsibility that lie behind us. “More important than the artwork itself are the social relations between people that it receives.” This is the most important lesson I have learned from Salgado, and it is the ethic that my “Authenticity Series of Figures” portrait paintings try to put into practice."},{"t":"h","zh":"参考文献","en":"References"},{"t":"ref","zh":"[1] Benjamin, W. The Work of Art in the Age of Its Technological Reproducibility, and Other Writings on Media [M]. Cambridge: Harvard University Press, 2008.","en":"[1] Benjamin, W. The Work of Art in the Age of Its Technological Reproducibility, and Other Writings on Media [M]. Cambridge: Harvard University Press, 2008."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[2] Heidegger, M. Being and Time [M]. Trans. John Macquarrie & Edward Robinson. New York: Harper & Row, 1962.","en":"[2] Heidegger, M. Being and Time [M]. Trans. John Macquarrie & Edward Robinson. New York: Harper & Row, 1962."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[3] Kundera, M. The Unbearable Lightness of Being [M]. New York: Harper & Row, 1984.","en":"[3] Kundera, M. The Unbearable Lightness of Being [M]. New York: Harper & Row, 1984."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[4] Salgado, S. Workers: An Archaeology of the Industrial Age [M]. New York: Aperture, 1993.","en":"[4] Salgado, S. Workers: An Archaeology of the Industrial Age [M]. New York: Aperture, 1993."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[5] Salgado, S. Migrations: Humanity in Transition [M]. New York: Aperture, 2000.","en":"[5] Salgado, S. Migrations: Humanity in Transition [M]. New York: Aperture, 2000."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[6] Salgado, S. Genesis [M]. Cologne: Taschen, 2013.","en":"[6] Salgado, S. Genesis [M]. Cologne: Taschen, 2013."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[7] Sontag, S. Regarding the Pain of Others [M]. New York: Farrar, Straus and Giroux, 2003.","en":"[7] Sontag, S. Regarding the Pain of Others [M]. New York: Farrar, Straus and Giroux, 2003."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[8] Wenders, W. & Salgado, J. R. The Salt of the Earth [Documentary]. Decia Films, 2014.","en":"[8] Wenders, W. & Salgado, J. R. The Salt of the Earth [Documentary]. Decia Films, 2014."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[9] Rancière, J. The Emancipated Spectator [M]. London: Verso, 2009.","en":"[9] Rancière, J. The Emancipated Spectator [M]. London: Verso, 2009."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[10] Azoulay, A. The Civil Contract of Photography [M]. New York: Zone Books, 2008.","en":"[10] Azoulay, A. The Civil Contract of Photography [M]. New York: Zone Books, 2008."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[11] 汉娜·阿伦特. 《人的境况》上海: 上海人民出版社, 2017.","en":"[11] Hannah Arendt. The Human Condition. Shanghai: Shanghai People’s Publishing House, 2017."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[12] 金观涛. ，《轴心文明与现代社会》 北京: 法律出版社, 2019.","en":"[12] Jin Guantao. Axial Civilizations and Modern Society. Beijing: Law Press, 2019."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[13] 瓦尔特·本雅明.《 机械复制时代的艺术》作品 王才勇译. 北京: 中国城市出版社, 2002.","en":"[13] Walter Benjamin. The Work of Art in the Age of Mechanical Reproduction. Trans. Wang Caiyong. Beijing: China City Press, 2002."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[14] 米兰·昆德拉. 《生命不可承受之轻》  许钧译. 上海: 上海译文出版社, 2003.","en":"[14] Milan Kundera. The Unbearable Lightness of Being. Trans. Xu Jun. Shanghai: Shanghai Translation Publishing House, 2003."},{"t":"ref","zh":"[15] 马丁·海德格尔. 《存在与时间》. 陈嘉映, 王庆节译. 北京: 生活·读书·新知三联书店, 2014.","en":"[15] Martin Heidegger. Being and Time. Trans. Chen Jiaying, Wang Qingjie. Beijing: SDX Joint Publishing, 2014."}]}];
